var e=JSON.parse(`[["@purpurabog/ui","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/","Components that follow IBM's Carbon Design System, made for forms in Thai and English: fields, lists, dates (Buddhist era), overlays, data tables and the UI shell. This site is built with them. The same components come in three forms. Pick the one that fits your app: You build with Use You get Any framework, or plain HTML Lit web components (<ui-date-picker>) Carbon's look and behaviour, styled with tokens and ::part() React + Tailwind Components copied into your app with shadcn (npx shadcn add) Carbon's look as Tailwind classes you can edit line by line React, your own design Unstyled parts (@purpurabog/ui/headless) Carbon's keyboard, focus and ARIA with no classes at all All three share one core, so the behaviour is the same everywhere: every component is tested against Carbon in Chrome and WebKit, with axe and with the keyboard."],["@purpurabog/ui","Try it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/#try-it","Change the theme or the language in the settings at the top right: the components follow the page's data-theme and lang."],["@purpurabog/ui","What next","/kanok-ui-docs/en/#what-next","Install the package or copy components with shadcn. Browse every element, its attributes, slots, parts and events in the Storybook."],["Installation","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/","The package is public on npm. Pick the way that fits your app; you can mix them."],["Installation","Choose a style","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#choose-a-style","The components come in two styles. Both use the same JavaScript: a style is only a stylesheet. Style Load On the page Carbon (the default) tokens.css nothing to add Kanok (our own design) tokens.css, then kanok.css data-design=\\"kanok\\" on <html> or on your app's root element Both, switchable the same two files set or remove data-design at run time Kanok uses the Bai Jamjuree font (Thai and Latin, SIL Open Font License). Install it with npm i @fontsource/bai-jamjuree, then import the weights 400, 500, 600 and 700 (import '@fontsource/bai-jamjuree/400.css'; and so on). To see the whole site in Kanok, open Settings (the gear in the header) and choose Kanok under Style, or share a link ending in ?design=kanok. More in Kanok design."],["Installation","Web components (any framework)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#web-components-any-framework","Load the design tokens once per page, then the components you use:"],["Installation","React","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#react","React wrappers with typed props and events come with the package. They need @lit/react too (an optional peer dependency, only for @purpurabog/ui/react): Load the tokens once (import '@purpurabog/ui/tokens.css';), then import the wrappers you use from @purpurabog/ui/react."],["Installation","React + Tailwind with shadcn","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#react-tailwind-with-shadcn","Copy a component into your app and edit its classes. Its behaviour (keyboard, focus, ARIA) comes from @purpurabog/ui/headless, which the CLI installs for you. Your app needs Tailwind v4 and a components.json. If you already use shadcn, add only the registries part: Pin the version in the URL (@purpurabog/ui@0.82.0 instead of @latest) so every copy in your app comes from the same release. Add components: Import the tokens and the theme after Tailwind in your main CSS: The files land in components/ui/ (under src/ when your app has one)."],["Installation","Unstyled React (headless)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#unstyled-react-headless","For your own design system: the behaviour without a single class. State shows as data-* attributes (data-open, data-selected, data-highlighted …) to style on. The parts have their own section: start at Headless."],["Installation","Use your first component","/kanok-ui-docs/en/installation/#use-your-first-component","The same dropdown as a web component, with the React wrapper and with React + Tailwind. Every example on this site comes in these tabs: pick yours once and the other pages follow. The headless version is in Headless. lang on the element or any ancestor sets the language of the built-in text of the web components and the React wrappers (Thai and English are included)."],["Migrating to 1.0","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/","1.0 replaces the data-driven web component <ui-data-table> with a family of elements that follow Carbon web components (cds-table): <ui-table>, <ui-table-head>, <ui-table-header-row>, <ui-table-header-cell>, <ui-table-body>, <ui-table-row>, <ui-table-cell> and the toolbar, batch-action and skeleton elements around them. This page lists what to change."],["Migrating to 1.0","What changed and why","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#what-changed-and-why","Markup instead of data. <ui-data-table> took headers and rows as properties and drew the table itself. <ui-table> is written as elements, as Carbon's cds-table is: each header, row and cell is an element you write or render. What a cell shows is whatever you put in it, so renderCell is gone. Carbon web components names. Attributes, events, slots and parts now follow cds-table: is-sortable, is-selectable, use-zebra-styles, ui-table-header-cell-sort, ui-table-row-selected and so on. Features Carbon doesn't have (paging, column settings, pinned and resized columns, CSV, inline editing, loading and empty states) keep working with the same behaviour and get names in the same style. The toolbar is elements too. The search, the batch actions, the Columns button and the Export CSV button are <ui-table-toolbar-search>, <ui-table-batch-actions>, <ui-table-column-settings> and <ui-table-csv-export> inside a <ui-table-toolbar>, instead of switches on the table. New entry point. Import @purpurabog/ui/table instead of @purpurabog/ui/data-table. Unchanged: the React + Tailwind DataTable (tw-data-table, data-driven with headers and rows, including DataTableSkeleton) and the headless useDataTable hook and its parts. Code that uses them needs no change."],["Migrating to 1.0","Before and after","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#before-and-after",""],["Migrating to 1.0","Attributes and properties","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#attributes-and-properties","<ui-data-table> 1.0 headers ({ key, header }[]) <ui-table-header-cell>s in a <ui-table-head> › <ui-table-header-row>; key → column, header → the cell's content rows ({ id, … }[]) <ui-table-row>s of <ui-table-cell>s in a <ui-table-body>; keep the id yourself (data-id, a React key) renderCell(row, header) Write the content into the <ui-table-cell> size size (unchanged) zebra use-zebra-styles static-width use-static-width sortable is-sortable on the table (every header) or on single headers sort-key + sort-direction sort-direction on that <ui-table-header-cell> manual-sorting preventDefault() on ui-table-header-cell-sort, then sort the data and set sort-direction sortRow(a, b, context) sort-value on cells; customSortRow(lhs, rhs, collator) on the table compares two cells' values heading <ui-table-header-title slot=\\"title\\"> description <ui-table-header-description slot=\\"description\\"> label aria-label on <ui-table> selectable is-selectable radio radio (unchanged) selectedIds selected on <ui-table-row>; selectedRows (the row elements) on the table searchable <ui-table-toolbar-search> in <ui-table-toolbar-content> search-persistent persistent on <ui-table-toolbar-search> search-label, search-placeholder label, placeholder on <ui-table-toolbar-search> filter-text No attribute: set the search's value and dispatch an input event from it filterRows(row, text, headers) (true keeps the row) filterRows(rowText, searchString) on the table — true now leaves the row out, as in Carbon manual-filtering filterRows = () => false, and listen for input on the search renderExpandedRow(row) expandable on the table and a <ui-table-expanded-row> right after the row expandedIds expanded on <ui-table-row> expand-all batch-expansion (with expandable) sticky-header sticky-header (unchanged) resizable resizable on the table (every header) or on single headers columnWidths width on each header; columnWidths on the table is now read-only loading, loading-rows Unchanged page-size, page, page-sizes Unchanged total-selected selected-rows-count on <ui-table-batch-actions> (set it in your ui-table-row-selected listener) total-count total-rows-count on <ui-table-batch-actions> column-settings <ui-table-column-settings> in <ui-table-toolbar-content> hiddenColumns column-hidden on headers, setColumnHidden(column, hidden) and resetColumns(); hiddenColumns on the table is now read-only csv-export <ui-table-csv-export> in <ui-table-toolbar-content> csv-file-name file-name on <ui-table-csv-export> Host data-has-selection selected on <ui-table-header-row> while any row is chosen (ui-table:has(ui-table-header-row[selected])) Header fields: DataTableHeader <ui-table-header-cell> key column header The cell's content sortable: false Leave is-sortable off the table and put it on the headers that sort align No attribute: style the cells, e.g. style=\\"text-align: end\\" on <ui-table-cell> editable, options editable, options (a property, or JSON in the attribute) validate(value, row) validate(value, cell) (a property) resizable: false Leave resizable off the table and put it on the headers that resize width, minWidth, maxWidth width, min-width, max-width hideable: false hideable=\\"false\\" hidden: true column-hidden pinned pinned Row fields: id is yours to keep (data-id); disabled: true → disabled on <ui-table-row>."],["Migrating to 1.0","Methods","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#methods","<ui-data-table> 1.0 toCsv({ scope }), downloadCsv({ scope, fileName }) Unchanged on <ui-table> focus() Unchanged selectedRows selectedRows returns the <ui-table-row> elements sortBy(key, direction) None: click the header, or sort the data yourself and set sort-direction filteredRows, visibleRows, shownRows None: table.querySelectorAll('ui-table-row:not([filtered])'); rows on other pages also have paged-out pageCount None: Math.ceil(rows / pageSize) visibleHeaders table.columns.filter((header) => !header.columnHidden)"],["Migrating to 1.0","Events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#events","<ui-data-table> 1.0 ui-sort { key, direction } ui-table-header-cell-sort { oldSortDirection, sortDirection } from the header, cancelable, before the rows move; ui-table-sorted { sortedHeader } after ui-select { selected, rows } ui-table-row-selected { selectedRow, selectedRows }; ui-table-row-all-selected { selectedRows } after select-all or Cancel ui-filter { value } ui-table-filtered { unfilteredRows }; input on <ui-table-toolbar-search> for the text ui-cell-edit { rowId, key, value, previous, row }, after the save ui-table-cell-edit { row, cell, column, value, previous } from the cell, cancelable, before the value is written ui-page-change ui-table-page-change (same detail) ui-select-all { totalCount } ui-table-batch-actions-select-all-clicked from <ui-table-batch-actions> ui-column-resize { key, width, widths } ui-table-column-resize { column, width } from the header; read columnWidths on the table for all ui-expand { expandedIds, expanded, id } ui-table-row-expando-toggled { expanded } from the row (cancelable ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled before) ui-csv-export { csv, rows, fileName } ui-table-csv-export { csv, rows, fileName } from <ui-table-csv-export>, cancelable; rows are now the row elements ui-columns-change { hiddenColumns, key, hidden } ui-table-columns-change { hiddenColumns, column, hidden }"],["Migrating to 1.0","Slots","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#slots","<ui-data-table> 1.0 toolbar Your controls go in <ui-table-toolbar-content>, inside <ui-table-toolbar slot=\\"toolbar\\"> batch-actions The children of <ui-table-batch-actions> empty, no-results Unchanged — New: title, description"],["Migrating to 1.0","CSS parts and custom property","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#css-parts-and-custom-property","<ui-data-table> 1.0 base None: style ui-table header, content, table, pagination, empty Unchanged on ui-table title, description Style ui-table-header-title, ui-table-header-description toolbar, toolbar-content, search Style ui-table-toolbar, ui-table-toolbar-content, ui-table-toolbar-search batch-actions Style ui-table-batch-actions batch-summary, cancel-button, select-all-button ui-table-batch-actions::part(…), same names sort-button, resizer ui-table-header-cell::part(sort-button), ::part(resizer) columns-button, columns-panel ui-table-column-settings::part(button), ::part(panel) export-button ui-table-csv-export::part(button) expand-button ui-table-row::part(expand-button) (ui-table-header-row for expand-all) expanded-row ui-table-expanded-row::part(cell) --ui-data-table-max-height --ui-table-max-height React + Tailwind's DataTable still reads --ui-data-table-max-height."],["Migrating to 1.0","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#skeleton","<ui-data-table-skeleton> (UiDataTableSkeleton) becomes <ui-table-skeleton> (UiTableSkeleton), as Carbon's cds-table-skeleton: headers is a list of strings instead of { header } objects, hide-header becomes show-header=\\"false\\" and hide-toolbar becomes show-toolbar=\\"false\\". row-count, column-count and zebra are unchanged; there is no size."],["Migrating to 1.0","Screen reader announcements","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#screen-reader-announcements","<ui-data-table> said \\"Sorted by Contract, ascending\\" after a sort and \\"3 of 12 rows\\" when typing paused. <ui-table> says only \\"Loading data\\" while loading, as Carbon's table says nothing; the batch bar's count is still a status. The React + Tailwind DataTable keeps both announcements."],["Migrating to 1.0","React","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#react","UiDataTable and UiDataTableSkeleton are gone from @purpurabog/ui/react. Pick one of: The UiTable* wrappers (UiTable, UiTableHead, UiTableHeaderRow, UiTableHeaderCell, UiTableBody, UiTableRow, UiTableCell, UiTableExpandedRow, UiTableHeaderTitle, UiTableHeaderDescription, UiTableToolbar, UiTableToolbarContent, UiTableToolbarSearch, UiTableBatchActions, UiTableColumnSettings, UiTableCsvExport, UiTableSkeleton): map your data into them. Events are onUiTable… props, such as onUiTableRowSelected. The React + Tailwind DataTable: still data-driven with headers and rows, closest to the old UiDataTable props. The table sorts by moving its rows in the DOM, and saves an edit by writing into the cell. Rows React renders belong to React, so sort and save through your state: The same goes for Vue, Angular and any framework that renders the rows. See Data table for every feature in HTML and React."],["Migrating to 1.0","Types","/kanok-ui-docs/en/migration-1-0/#types","The DataTable… types of the web component (DataTableHeader, DataTableRow, DataTableSortDetail …) are gone from @purpurabog/ui; the new ones are UiTable, UiTableRow, UiTableHeaderCell …, TableSortDirection and the event details (TableSortedDetail, TableRowSelectedDetail, TableCellEditDetail …). React + Tailwind's own types (DataTableSort …) are unchanged."],["Themes and layers","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/","Every color comes from Carbon's four themes, generated from @carbon/themes into tokens.css. You pick a theme with one attribute, data-theme, on the whole page or on any part of it. Inside a theme, <ui-layer> moves fields and menus one step along Carbon's layering model so they stay visible on the surface below them. Theme Look white Light, white background (the default) g10 Light, gray 10 background g90 Dark, gray 90 background g100 Dark, gray 100 background data-theme and the tokens work the same for the web components, the React wrappers and React + Tailwind, whose classes read the same tokens. Headless parts have no colors of their own."],["Themes and layers","Switch the theme of the page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#switch-the-theme-of-the-page","Put data-theme on <html>. Without it the page is white. The dark themes (g90, g100) also set color-scheme: dark, so scrollbars and the browser's own controls turn dark too."],["Themes and layers","Make a zone dark","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#make-a-zone-dark","data-theme works on any element: everything inside it uses that theme, the rest of the page doesn't. Zones can nest. A zone only changes the tokens. To paint the zone itself, give it the theme's background and text color: The field inside the layer uses the next layer's color, so it still stands out from the surface it sits on."],["Themes and layers","Follow the system setting","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#follow-the-system-setting","data-theme=\\"auto\\" shows white, or g100 when the system asks for dark (prefers-color-scheme: dark). It's opt-in: Carbon itself never switches on its own. auto works on <html> or on a zone: an auto zone inside another theme still shows white or g100 by the system setting."],["Themes and layers","Let people pick light, dark or system","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#let-people-pick-light-dark-or-system","<ui-theme-switcher> is an icon content switcher with three choices: light, dark and system. It has no Carbon counterpart. The one under Settings at the top right of this site is this element. To draw your own control in React with no styles, use the useThemeMode hook: see Headless. What it does: Shows the choice on <html data-theme>. Light becomes light-theme (white by default), dark becomes dark-theme (g100 by default), and system follows the OS, also while it changes. Remembers it in localStorage under storage-key (ui-theme by default; storage-key=\\"\\" doesn't remember). Starts on the remembered choice, else value, else what <html data-theme> already shows, else light. Keeps every switcher in step: all switchers on the page (Lit and React) and in other tabs follow each other. Attribute Values Default value light, dark, system the remembered choice light-theme white, g10 white dark-theme g90, g100 g100 storage-key any key; \\"\\" = don't remember ui-theme size sm, md, lg md low-contrast boolean off tooltip-placement where the icon tooltips show top label names the group \\"Theme\\", translated In React and React + Tailwind the props are camelCase (lightTheme, darkTheme, storageKey, lowContrast, tooltipPlacement), and the Tailwind switcher takes aria-label instead of label. On the web component, its parts are switcher (the content switcher) and item (each choice)."],["Themes and layers","Save the choice to a user's profile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#save-the-choice-to-a-user-s-profile","Picking a choice fires ui-theme-change with { mode, theme } (onUiThemeChange on the React wrapper, onChange on the React + Tailwind switcher). Store the mode on your server, and set value when the profile loads: the switcher shows it and remembers it."],["Themes and layers","Paint the remembered theme on the first frame","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#paint-the-remembered-theme-on-the-first-frame","The switcher only runs once its script has loaded, so on a reload the page would first paint the default theme and then switch. themeScript() returns a small script for <head> that sets the remembered theme before anything is painted. Render it on the server, or write it into index.html in a build step: Give it the same storageKey, lightTheme and darkTheme as your switcher, whichever of the four it is. When nothing is remembered it does nothing, so your own <html data-theme> stays the default. On the server useThemeMode, and so the React + Tailwind switcher, returns defaultValue (or light), so add themeScript() to <head> there too."],["Themes and layers","Put fields on a tile: <ui-layer>","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#put-fields-on-a-tile-ui-layer","Carbon colors surfaces in layers: a field on a gray tile must not be the same gray as the tile. <ui-layer> is Carbon's Layer. Inside it, components use the theme's next layer set: field, tile and menu backgrounds, and selected rows borders and dividers hover and active fills level Uses 0 The page's own set, as outside any layer 1 The second set 2 The third set (the deepest) Without level, a layer works it out like Carbon's cds-layer: a layer outside any other is level 0, and a nested one is its parent's level + 1, up to 2. Set level to choose one yourself. with-background paints the layer with Carbon's layer background, the color its content sits on. Carbon React's <Layer> starts at level 1, not 0. The React + Tailwind Layer follows Carbon React, so it needs no level here. The React wrapper renders <ui-layer> and starts at 0 like the element: write level=\\"1\\" (level={1}) for the same result."],["Themes and layers","Use themes inside a shadow root (micro apps)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#use-themes-inside-a-shadow-root-micro-apps","This section is for the web components in a Lit app; for a React + Tailwind app in a shadow root, see Frameworks. Tokens are CSS custom properties, which inherit through shadow roots: a theme on <html> reaches every component, wherever it is. The [data-theme] rules, though, live in tokens.css at document level. If your app renders inside a shadow root of its own and puts data-theme on an element in there, load tokens.css into that shadow root too. The file also names :host, so data-theme on your app's host element works like it does on <html>: The theme switcher only changes <html>. In a micro app, set data-theme on your own host instead. <ui-layer> needs nothing extra: its rules are part of the element, so it works in any shadow root."],["Themes and layers","What next","/kanok-ui-docs/en/themes/#what-next","Customize the look: tokens, ::part(), states and slots."],["Kanok design","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/","Kanok (กนก, after the flame-like Thai motif lai kanok) is the library's own style, next to Carbon. It is meant for internal business tools: clean and calm, surfaces set apart by their fill rather than lines, with a Thai-craft identity in its colours and one recurring detail. Every component keeps the same HTML, JavaScript and accessibility; only the stylesheet changes."],["Kanok design","What it looks like","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#what-it-looks-like","Colour. Blue for actions (#0068d6; dark: khram indigo #5563db), chad vermilion for danger, cool near-neutral greys on white (theme paper) and a violet-warm black (theme lacquer). Every colour is generated and checked against WCAG 2.2 contrast when the package is built. You are here. A blue line marks the selected tab, the current page in the header and a chosen table row (--ui-border-interactive: the primary on paper, a lighter indigo on lacquer so it stays visible); in the side nav, a tree and vertical tabs the chosen row is tinted, with no bar. No lines where a fill will do. Cards and tiles have no border: a soft grey sets them apart from the page, one step off whatever they sit on, in a layer too. Notifications and toasts have no coloured bar; the icon tells the kind. Focus. One light ring everywhere: solid blue (a light indigo on lacquer), 2px, with rounded corners, shown for the keyboard only. A click on a button, a checkbox or a toggle shows none; Tab does, 2px outside a control and inside a highlighted row. An input box (a text field, a dropdown, a select) shows its focus either way, as Pixiv's soft 4px blue halo outside the box, with no line on its edge; an invalid one has a red halo (Carbon: 2px, square, a click too). Shape. Pill-shaped buttons; 6px corners on fields, a soft grey fill with no edge (or an edge: see Outlined fields); 12px on cards, tiles and dialogs (a card's footer buttons sit 8px in) (a card clips its image to them); 8px on menus, notifications and code snippets. Tags have small 4px corners, so a status never reads as a button. No ink blocks. Secondary buttons are a soft grey fill with no border. Chosen things are the primary colour, never black: a selected tag, a chosen tile, the slider, the multi-select count. Density. Buttons and fields 40px tall by default (sm 32px, lg 48px, as Carbon's fields), so a button lines up with the field beside it; menu rows 32px, table rows 40px. The large button sizes stay pills: xl is 48px and 2xl 56px, label centred (Carbon's 64 / 80px with the label at the top). Select. A native select, as in Carbon: it opens the browser's own list, and a phone's own picker. For a list in the menu look, use a dropdown (or set --ui-select-appearance: base-select for Chrome 135+'s customizable select). Type. Bai Jamjuree for Thai and Latin, semibold labels and headings, and taller lines so stacked Thai vowels and tone marks never collide."],["Kanok design","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#use-it","Load kanok.css after tokens.css (see Installation), then mark where Kanok applies: data-design works on any element, not only <html>. An app that runs inside another product's frame (a portal with its own header and side bar) puts it on its own root element, so the host page is left alone:"],["Kanok design","React + Tailwind","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#react-tailwind","The React + Tailwind components read the same settings, so they follow Kanok too. Copy kanok.css next to the tokens (npx shadcn@4 add @kanok-ui/kanok) and import it after them: Then set data-design as above. In a micro app (React in a shadow root) put data-design and data-theme on the host element."],["Kanok design","Outlined fields","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#outlined-fields","Kanok's fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. For fields with an edge, say a long form with many fields close together, or a form on a grey surface (a tile, a layer) where the soft fill is hard to see, use the outlined look. To use it: Turn Kanok on as in Use it (kanok.css and data-design=\\"kanok\\"). Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the fields: a <form>, a <section>, or <html> for the whole app. Every field inside follows; there's nothing to set per field and no component code to change. It works the same for the web components, the React wrappers and React + Tailwind, since it's a plain HTML attribute. Below, filled (left) and outlined (right) side by side: The whole app outlined: State filled (default) outlined Rest soft grey fill, no edge 1px edge, no fill Focus 4px blue halo the same edge + 4px blue halo Invalid red halo the same edge + red halo Disabled soft grey fill, faint text faint edge, faint text The edge follows the theme (paper / lacquer) and is set by --ui-field-outline-color; a theme zone nested inside stays outlined. Keep one look per form."],["Kanok design","Light and dark","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#light-and-dark","Kanok has two themes: paper (light) and lacquer (dark). data-theme=\\"auto\\" follows the system setting. You don't need to change anything for <ui-theme-switcher> or useThemeMode: on a Kanok page their light / dark choice becomes paper / lacquer. The core functions are in @purpurabog/ui/core: Function Does applyDesign('kanok') sets data-design on <html> and moves the theme to the same mode in Kanok designScript() a <head> script that paints the remembered style (or ?design= from the URL) on the first frame; put it before themeScript() themeIn('kanok', 'g100') the theme a design shows for a mode: lacquer"],["Kanok design","Adjust it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#adjust-it","Kanok is a set of values for public CSS custom properties: colours (--ui-primary, --ui-border-interactive, …) and shape settings (--ui-button-radius, --ui-field-border, --ui-card-radius, --ui-menu-item-radius, …). Override any of them on a zone, as in Customizing. Each element's settings are listed in its API reference."],["Kanok design","Status","/kanok-ui-docs/en/kanok/#status","Kanok is new. These components have their Kanok shape: button, the form fields (text input, text area, number, select, search, dropdown, combobox, multi-select, date and time pickers), checkbox, radio, toggle, tags, tabs, tiles, cards, tables (with a mark on a chosen row), menus, notifications, modals, button sets, code snippets, contained tabs (as a segmented control), the calendar, the header, the side nav, the content switcher, pagination, the slider, the file uploader, tooltips, popovers, toggletips, overflow menus, side panels and tearsheets. Every other component already takes Kanok's colours, font and sizes, and gets its shape in the next releases. The React + Tailwind components follow Kanok as well."],["Customize the look","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/","Start from the shallowest layer and go deeper only when it isn't enough: Design tokens (--ui-*) for sizes and colors Theme zones (data-theme, see Themes and layers) ::part() for one piece of an element Slots for markup in labels and help text A derived class as the last resort The shallower layers survive upgrades better, because they don't depend on how an element is built inside. Attributes, properties, events, slots, parts and --ui-* tokens listed in api.md are not removed or renamed before the next major version. Selectors inside the shadow DOM are not part of that promise."],["Customize the look","Change sizes and colors with tokens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#change-sizes-and-colors-with-tokens","Every component reads CSS custom properties named --ui-* from tokens.css (loaded once per page). Set them on :root to change the whole app, or on any element to change only what's inside it. You don't touch the shadow DOM: The React + Tailwind classes read the same tokens (see below), so a token set on a wrapper changes them too. Headless parts have no look, so tokens don't apply to them. The public tokens that components read: Token Changes --ui-field-height-sm, -md, -lg Field height per size (32 / 40 / 48px): text input, select, dropdown, combobox, multi-select, date picker, button --ui-menu-max-rows Rows a dropdown, combobox or multi-select menu shows before it scrolls (5.5) --ui-calendar-width Width of the date picker's calendar (288px) --ui-sheet-radius Top corners of the date picker's bottom sheet on phones (the menu radius) --ui-available-height, --ui-available-width Written on an open list or menu while it is open: the room left beside its field. Its max-height takes it, so a long list scrolls inside the screen. Read it in your own popup's CSS; don't set it --ui-highlight Color of the selected days in a range picker --ui-surface-1, --ui-surface-2, --ui-hairline, --ui-ink-subtle, --ui-ghost-hover, --ui-ghost-active Layer tokens: they point at the current layer's set, and <ui-layer> moves them --ui-primary, --ui-ink, --ui-canvas, --ui-focus, … Theme colors, each made from the Carbon token named at the end of its line in tokens.css Each element's own list is under \\"Design tokens\\" in api.md and in the CSS custom properties table of its Storybook page."],["Customize the look","Change one piece of an element with ::part()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#change-one-piece-of-an-element-with-part","::part(name) styles a piece an element exposes. Part names are the same words across components: base, label, input, menu, option, helper-text, error-text, … The date picker passes on the parts of the fields inside it; in range mode they get start- and end- in front: Every element's parts are listed in api.md. ::part() is for the web components and the React wrappers, which render them. React + Tailwind and headless have no shadow DOM: give the pieces classes instead (the last two sections). A few elements have no pieces inside: ui-toaster, ui-fluid-form, ui-button-set, ui-badge-indicator and ui-stack are the box you see. Style them with plain CSS on the element, e.g. ui-stack { row-gap: 24px; } or ui-badge-indicator { background: var(--ui-info); }: page CSS wins over their own. ui-button-set also has the part button-set (as in Carbon), but its layout is on the element."],["Customize the look","Style by state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#style-by-state","You can read every state that changes the look from the element itself, and combine it with ::part(): Properties you or the user change are reflected as attributes: open, checked, selected, expanded, invalid, warn, size, kind, … States the element works out itself are set as data-* attributes on the element: Attribute Means On data-open The list or calendar is open ui-dropdown, ui-combobox, ui-multi-select, ui-date-picker data-show-error, data-show-warn The error or warning is actually showing (an error replaces a warning) every form field data-has-value There is text or a selection ui-combobox, ui-multi-select, ui-search data-placeholder The placeholder is showing ui-dropdown, ui-select data-password-visible The password is shown ui-text-input type=\\"password\\" data-editing In edit mode ui-edit-in-place data-drag-over A file is dragged over the drop zone ui-file-uploader data-shown The spinner or overlay really shows (after delay) ui-loading data-overflowing The text is cut off ui-truncated-text Each of these is also a custom state, as on native and Web Awesome elements: ui-dropdown:state(open) matches exactly when ui-dropdown[data-open] does (:state(show-error), :state(has-value), …). Use whichever you prefer; the attribute works in older browsers too. Each element's states are listed in its API reference. Click into the email field and leave it empty, then open the dropdown: Use [data-show-error] rather than [invalid] to style the error the user actually sees. invalid is the value you set: it stays on a disabled field, which shows no error, and it doesn't include errors from the user's own input. The data-* states are set after the first render in the browser, so HTML rendered on a server doesn't have them yet. The headless parts show their state with data-* attributes of their own: see Headless."],["Customize the look","Put markup in labels and help text with slots","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#put-markup-in-labels-and-help-text-with-slots","When text needs a link, bold text or an icon, use a slot instead of the attribute of the same name. The attribute still works as plain-text fallback. Every field takes the label, helper-text, warn-text and invalid-text slots. data-description on an <option> adds a second line in a dropdown, combobox or multi-select. Other elements have their own, such as header-actions on ui-modal and end on ui-tabs; api.md lists them all. React + Tailwind has no slots: label, helperText, warnText and invalidText take markup, and an item's description is its second line."],["Customize the look","Change the shape with a derived class","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#change-the-shape-with-a-derived-class","The last resort, for what tokens, parts and slots can't do, and only for the web components. Extend the element's class and add your styles after its own. You keep all its behavior (forms, keyboard, accessibility): Internal selectors are not public API. Select by [part=…], as above: it survives upgrades better than internal class names."],["Customize the look","React + Tailwind: edit the copied classes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#react-tailwind-edit-the-copied-classes","With shadcn the component's source is copied into your app, so you change its look where it is written. Each file keeps its classes in plain Tailwind (cva variants for kinds and sizes). For example, in components/ui/react-tw/button.tsx: For one place only, pass className. Classes are merged with tailwind-merge, so the ones you pass win: The classes (bg-primary, text-ink, h-field-md, rounded-pill, …) come from theme.css, which maps the --ui-* tokens into Tailwind's theme. Tokens and data-theme zones therefore work here exactly as for the web components. The behavior (keyboard, focus, ARIA) comes from @purpurabog/ui/headless and keeps updating with the package."],["Customize the look","Headless","/kanok-ui-docs/en/customizing/#headless","The headless parts render no classes and read no tokens: you style them on their data-* state attributes. See Headless."],["Icons","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/","The components don't ship icons; they take yours in a slot or an icon prop and size and color them. Use Carbon's icons, the set this design system is drawn with: browse them in the IBM UI icon library and install the package for your stack."],["Icons","Install","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#install","Carbon publishes the icons as two packages, both under the Apache-2.0 license. Install the one for your stack; @purpurabog/ui doesn't depend on either."],["Icons","Find an icon's name","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#find-an-icon-s-name","The library shows each icon's name in lowercase with hyphens, such as trash-can. Each package spells it its own way: In the library React (@carbon/icons-react) Others (@carbon/icons) add Add @carbon/icons/es/add/16.js trash-can TrashCan @carbon/icons/es/trash-can/16.js overflow-menu--horizontal OverflowMenuHorizontal @carbon/icons/es/overflow-menu--horizontal/16.js chevron--right ChevronRight @carbon/icons/es/chevron--right/16.js @carbon/icons has a file for each size: 16.js, 20.js, 24.js and 32.js. Some icons are drawn differently at 16px, so pick the size the component shows (see Size and color)."],["Icons","Put an icon in a component","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#put-an-icon-in-a-component","In React, an icon is a component that renders an <svg> and passes other props, such as slot, to it. Without a bundler or in another framework, turn the icon's data into an <svg> with toString from @carbon/icon-helpers. For a static HTML page, use Download SVG in the library and paste the <svg>, as the HTML examples on this site do."],["Icons","Where the components take an icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#where-the-components-take-an-icon","Component Web component / React wrapper React + Tailwind Button prefix or suffix slot icon (after the text) Icon button the default slot children Menu item icon slot icon Overflow menu trigger icon slot (in place of ⋮) icon Tabs icon slot of ui-tab icon Content switcher icon slot icon Tag icon slot icon Link icon slot icon Tile icon slot of a linked tile icon Contained list item icon slot icon Tree view node icon slot icon User avatar icon slot icon Toggletip trigger trigger slot (in place of ⓘ) icon UI shell header global action: the default slot; side nav link and menu: icon slot children / icon Page header icon slot of the breadcrumb bar and of the content icon"],["Icons","Size and color","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#size-and-color","The component sets the icon's size: 16px in buttons, menus, tags and the side nav, 20px in the header and in large icon-only tabs, 32px before a page header's title. The width and height an icon comes with don't matter there. Use the icon's own size (size={20} in React, 20.js in @carbon/icons) when the component shows it at 20px or more, so you get the drawing made for that size. Carbon's icons fill with currentColor, so they take the component's text color, also on hover, when disabled and in every theme. Don't set a fill of your own."],["Icons","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#accessibility","An icon inside a control is decoration: both packages add aria-hidden=\\"true\\" to an icon without an aria-label. The control carries the name, such as the label of an icon button, which is also its tooltip. Don't give the icon a label as well, or screen readers read the name twice. An icon that stands alone and means something (a status, for example) needs its own name: pass aria-label (React) or add it to attrs; the icon then gets role=\\"img\\". For status, the status indicator already has the right icons and names."],["Icons","Names that clash","/kanok-ui-docs/en/icons/#names-that-clash","Some icon names are also component names, such as Search, Notification or Copy. Rename the icon when you import it. The examples on this site use an Icon suffix:"],["Forms and validation","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/","Every field is a form-associated custom element: it takes part in a plain <form> the way <input> does. You get submit, FormData, reset and the browser's constraint validation without any glue code. The React wrappers from @purpurabog/ui/react render the same elements, so everything on this page applies to them too. The React + Tailwind components copied with shadcn work like Carbon React: validation is your app's, and they show what you pass in invalid and invalidText (going over maxCount is still an error by itself). For the wrappers, events and the rest of the setup, see Using it with frameworks. Press Submit with the fields empty: each one shows its error and the first gets focus. (method=\\"dialog\\" only keeps this demo on the page; your form posts as usual.)"],["Forms and validation","Submit with a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#submit-with-a-form","Give each field a name. Fields submit under that name, so FormData reads them like native inputs: <ui-button type=\\"submit\\"> submits the form it sits in, and type=\\"reset\\" resets it. The default type is button, which does neither. Enter in a text box submits the form as a native text input does: through the form's first submit button, and not at all while that button is disabled. A form without a submit button submits on Enter only when it has a single text field. A <fieldset disabled> or <ui-form-group disabled> disables every field and <ui-button> inside it: they are not submitted, don't block the form and can't submit it. A field without a label of its own is named by an aria-label or aria-labelledby on it, or by a <label for> that points at it, as a native control is. submit only fires when every field is valid. Reset puts each field back to the value it started with and hides its error again."],["Forms and validation","Mark a field as required","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#mark-a-field-as-required","Add required. The form won't submit while the field is empty. Every field brings its own message, translated to the page language (Thai and English are built in): Field Message when empty ui-dropdown, ui-combobox, ui-multi-select Built in: \\"Please select an option.\\" ui-radio-group Built in: \\"Please select an option.\\" (required-text to change it) ui-checkbox-group Built in: \\"Select at least one option.\\" (required-text to change it) ui-date-picker Built in: \\"Please enter a date.\\", plus messages for a wrong format, an impossible date and dates outside min / max ui-file-uploader Built in: \\"Add at least one file.\\" (required-text to change it) ui-text-input, ui-text-area, ui-number-input Built in: \\"Fill out this field.\\" ui-select Built in: \\"Please select an option.\\" Other browser checks, such as a wrong email address or a pattern, still use the browser's message, in the browser's language. On every field in this table except the file uploader, invalid-text replaces the built-in or browser message, whatever made the field invalid. Set it when you want your own words, or one language everywhere:"],["Forms and validation","When errors show","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#when-errors-show","Errors wait until the user is done with the field. Nobody sees \\"required\\" while they're still typing. A field shows its error after the user leaves it. Trying to submit shows the error on every invalid field at once and moves focus to the first one. The browser's own bubble doesn't appear. reportValidity() (the form's or a field's) does the same. checkValidity() stays silent, as on native controls: an app that checks the form on every keystroke (to enable its Save button, say) shows no errors and doesn't move the focus. Going over a max-count limit, and invalid set by your code, show right away. A disabled or read-only field shows no error."],["Forms and validation","Show an error from your validator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#show-an-error-from-your-validator","Set invalid and invalid-text for errors only your app or server knows about. The error shows right away. When your form library owns validation, pass its result to invalid and invalidText: On the web component and its React wrapper, invalid also makes the field invalid for the form, so the form won't submit again until you clear it. The React + Tailwind example uses React Hook Form; add zodResolver from @hookform/resolvers for a Zod schema."],["Forms and validation","Check a rule with custom validity","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#check-a-rule-with-custom-validity","setCustomValidity() works like on <input>: a message makes the field invalid, and '' clears it. Unlike invalid, the message waits for the user to leave the field, like the built-in checks: Fields also have checkValidity(), reportValidity(), validity, validationMessage, willValidate and form, as native controls do. These are methods of the elements: in React, call them on the wrapper's ref. In React + Tailwind, such a rule is part of your own validation."],["Forms and validation","Add helper text and warnings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#add-helper-text-and-warnings","helper-text is a hint under the field. warn with warn-text is a warning that doesn't block submit. One line shows at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats helper text. To put a link or bold text in a message, use the slot of the same name (helper-text, warn-text, invalid-text). In React + Tailwind, pass the markup to helperText, warnText or invalidText:"],["Forms and validation","Style a field that shows an error","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#style-a-field-that-shows-an-error","While the error line is showing, the field has data-show-error on itself (data-show-warn for a warning). Unlike invalid, which you set, this attribute follows what the user actually sees. It is on the web components, so it works with the React wrappers too:"],["Forms and validation","Disable a field or a group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#disable-a-field-or-a-group","disabled greys the field out. A disabled field isn't submitted and isn't validated, as natively. readonly shows the value and submits it, but the user can't change it. A disabled <fieldset> disables every field inside. So does <ui-form-group disabled>, Carbon's fieldset with a label as its legend:"],["Forms and validation","Dates: what users see and what you get","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#dates-what-users-see-and-what-you-get","The date picker shows dates the way the reader expects. Your code always gets the same ISO date: Page in Thai (lang=\\"th\\") Page in English The user sees and types 10/10/2569 (พ.ศ.) 10/10/2026 value and the submitted form 2026-10-10 2026-10-10 value, min and max are always yyyy-mm-dd in the Gregorian year (ค.ศ.). Thai pages show and take years in พ.ศ. Set era=\\"ce\\" to use ค.ศ. instead. Users may type Thai digits (๐–๙). They become 0–9. In พ.ศ., a year typed before 2400 (say 2026) gets a message asking for the พ.ศ. year. Nothing is converted behind the user's back. format sets the order: dd/mm/yyyy (default), mm/dd/yyyy or yyyy-mm-dd. The format shows as helper text until you set your own. The language comes from lang on the element or the closest ancestor. Set locale to override it for the date picker alone. A range picker submits two entries, name and end-name: To refuse single days (weekends, holidays), set isDateDisabled: a function that returns true, or a string to use as the message. On the web component it's a property, so set it in JavaScript; in React and React + Tailwind it's a prop:"],["Forms and validation","Count characters and words","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#count-characters-and-words","max-count adds a counter to ui-text-input and ui-text-area. It's a soft limit: users can paste and then trim. Going over turns the counter red, shows an error and blocks submit. Screen readers hear when the limit is near. On ui-text-area, counter-mode=\\"word\\" counts words instead. Thai has no spaces between words, so the count uses the browser's word segmenter for the field's language. \\"สวัสดีครับ ผมชื่อสมชาย\\" counts as 5 words. Change the messages with too-long-text ({max} becomes the limit) and near-limit-text. For a hard limit that stops typing, use maxlength instead."],["Forms and validation","Use a fluid form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/forms/#use-a-fluid-form","Inside <ui-fluid-form>, fields render as Carbon fluid fields: the label sits inside a 64px box and errors show inside the box. Fluid fields have no helper line. ui-fluid-form is not a form, so wrap it in your own <form>: To make one field fluid on its own, give it the fluid attribute (the fluid prop in React and React + Tailwind)."],["Using it with frameworks","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/","The components are standard custom elements (<ui-date-picker>, <ui-table> …), so any framework that renders HTML can use them. React gets typed wrappers on top. This page covers what changes from one framework to the next: passing data, listening to events, routing, server rendering and language."],["Using it with frameworks","Set up","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#set-up","HTML: load the tokens once per page and import the elements you use (Installation). React: install the package with Lit and @lit/react, which the wrappers are built on (React 19 or later). Load the tokens once, then import the wrappers you use. Vue: tell Vue's compiler that ui-* tags are custom elements. Angular: add CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA to the component that uses the elements."],["Using it with frameworks","Pass data and listen to events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#pass-data-and-listen-to-events","HTML: write attributes in the markup. Set arrays, objects and functions as properties from JavaScript, and listen with addEventListener. React: each wrapper renders the element with typed props. Props set the element's properties, so arrays, objects and functions pass straight through. Custom events become onUi… props with a typed detail. Vue: bind arrays and objects as properties with .prop; listen to custom events by their name. Angular: [name] binds a property, [attr.name] an attribute, and (event-name) listens to any event. Rows a framework renders: the table sorts by moving its rows, which the framework owns. Call preventDefault() on ui-table-header-cell-sort, sort the data and set the header's sort-direction, as above (Data table)."],["Using it with frameworks","input and change in React","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#input-and-change-in-react","Fields fire native input and change events, with DOM meaning: onInput on every keystroke, onChange when the user commits the value (leaves the field, presses Enter, picks a date). This differs from React's own <input onChange>, which fires on every keystroke. The prop follows the event the element really fires. The date picker fires change, so its prop is onChange; UiDatePicker has no onUiChange. Your editor's autocomplete lists the event props of each wrapper."],["Using it with frameworks","Attribute or property?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#attribute-or-property","Value How to pass it Text, numbers (label, max-count) Attribute or property On / off (required, disabled) Attribute present or absent, or a boolean property Arrays, objects, functions (rows, headers, isDateDisabled) Property only Attributes use dashes (invalid-text), properties camelCase (invalidText). The API reference lists both for every element."],["Using it with frameworks","Route links with your SPA router","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#route-links-with-your-spa-router","Links that a component draws itself sit in its shadow DOM, where client-side routers can't see them. So a plain click on one first fires a cancelable ui-navigate event with { href }. Cancel it and let your router change the page. One listener on document covers the whole app. These elements fire it: ui-header-name, ui-header-menu-item, ui-side-nav-link, ui-side-nav-menu-item, ui-switcher-item, ui-link, ui-breadcrumb-item, and ui-button, ui-icon-button, ui-tile, ui-card and ui-tree-node when they have an href. In React, call useUiNavigate() once in your root layout. To handle one link or one menu instead, the wrappers also have an onUiNavigate prop: on each link wrapper, and on UiHeader, UiSideNav, UiHeaderMenu and UiSideNavMenu, which the event bubbles through."],["Using it with frameworks","What the router doesn't get","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#what-the-router-doesn-t-get","Ctrl, ⌘, Shift or Alt clicks, middle clicks, target=\\"_blank\\", download and links to other sites don't fire ui-navigate. They act as normal links, so opening in a new tab still works. If nobody cancels the event, the link loads the page as usual. Adding the listener later breaks nothing. Mark the current page yourself, for example current on ui-side-nav-link. A ui-header-menu highlights itself when a link inside it is current."],["Using it with frameworks","Render on the server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#render-on-the-server","Every element renders on the server with Lit SSR (@lit-labs/ssr, or through @lit-labs/nextjs, @lit-labs/eleventy-plugin-lit or Astro's @astrojs/lit). The server HTML is the first paint. When the JavaScript loads, each element renders its shadow root again instead of hydrating, so there are no hydration mismatches. Import @lit-labs/ssr before the elements; it installs the DOM shim they need. The server can't see some things, so the first paint is incomplete until the JavaScript runs: Children in light DOM: a <ui-select> has no options yet, and ui-tabs shows every panel. Properties: rows, headers, files. Ancestors, including <html lang>: built-in text is English unless the element has its own lang. Put lang=\\"th\\" on the element for a Thai first paint. State attributes such as data-show-error and data-open, which are set in the browser. To paint the user's saved theme without a flash of the light theme, put the theme script in <head>, before your CSS: storageKey must match the storage-key of your <ui-theme-switcher> (default ui-theme). If the switcher sets light-theme or dark-theme, pass the same values as lightTheme and darkTheme (default white and g100)."],["Using it with frameworks","Run inside a shadow root (micro app)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#run-inside-a-shadow-root-micro-app","When your app is embedded in someone else's page, mount it in the shadow root of one custom element and keep all its CSS inside. Styles then can't leak in or out. The React + Tailwind components support this: app.css holds Tailwind, the tokens and the theme: tokens.css declares every token on both :root and :host, so it works inside a shadow root. The same file works for the web components. Switch the theme with data-theme on your host element (<contracts-app data-theme=\\"g100\\">). The theme switcher only changes <html>. For the Kanok design, import ./components/ui/primitives/kanok.css after the tokens and put data-design=\\"kanok\\" on the host element too. Declare fonts (@font-face) at document level: Chrome doesn't load @font-face inside a shadow root."],["Using it with frameworks","Type your event listeners","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#type-your-event-listeners","Every element has a Ui…EventMap, and addEventListener knows the detail of each event by name. document.querySelector('ui-table') returns the element's own type: The detail types are exported when you want to name them: ui-navigate is also declared on document, so the router listeners above are typed without casts. Listen on the element itself rather than a container: ui-* events bubble and cross shadow roots, so a container hears ui-toggle from every component inside it."],["Using it with frameworks","Thai and English text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/frameworks/#thai-and-english-text","Built-in text (button labels, required messages, counters, month names) follows the closest lang: the element's own, then the closest ancestor's, then <html>, then the browser's language. Thai and English are built in; any other language falls back to English. Changing lang on <html> or on the element itself re-renders it with the new language. To change a few messages, register a copy of a built-in translation with your changes: Add a language the same way, with a new $code (for example $code: 'ja') and every message translated. The English messages in src/core/translations/en.ts show every key. A text attribute on the element always wins over the translation, for example required-text, too-long-text or close-label. The React wrappers export registerTranslation and getTranslation too. For forms, validation and the date picker's Buddhist-era display, see Forms and validation."],["Use it with AI coding tools","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/","Claude, Cursor, Copilot and other AI tools write better code with these components when they can read the docs and the design rules. Give them three things: the docs index, the design file, and a short set of rules in your project."],["Use it with AI coding tools","Give it the docs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/#give-it-the-docs","The site publishes its pages in the llms.txt format, built from the same source as these pages (Installation and API sections included): File What's in it llms.txt Every page, one line each, with a link to its Markdown llms-full.txt All the pages in one file (large: give it to tools that index docs) en/<page>.md, e.g. en/select.md One page as Markdown, for a single component Add llms.txt (or llms-full.txt) as documentation in your tool, or paste the link of the page you're working on into the chat."],["Use it with AI coding tools","Give it the design","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/#give-it-the-design","DESIGN.md holds the design in the DESIGN.md format: the colors of all four themes, type, spacing, corners, motion, the main button, field and tile values, and the do's and don'ts. It is generated from tokens.css, so the values are the package's. The package ships it too, so your tool can read the copy that matches your installed version:"],["Use it with AI coding tools","Add the rules to your project","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/#add-the-rules-to-your-project","Put a few lines in the file your tool reads for project instructions (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .cursor/rules/, .github/copilot-instructions.md …): Keep it short: the tool reads the details from the docs and DESIGN.md when it needs them."],["Use it with AI coding tools","Autocomplete in the editor","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/#autocomplete-in-the-editor","custom-elements.json in the package lists every element with its attributes, events, slots and parts. Editors that read the Custom Elements Manifest give autocomplete and hover docs in HTML and templates. React gets the same from the wrappers' TypeScript types."],["Use it with AI coding tools","Check what it wrote","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ai/#check-what-it-wrote","AI tools still guess. Before you keep the code, check the usual slips: A plain <button>, <input> or <select> where a component exists. A hex color or a pixel value where a token exists. A field on a tile without a layer around the tile. Rounded corners or a box shadow on a surface. A React prop spelled like the HTML attribute (helper-text instead of helperText)."],["Button","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/","A button starts an action: save, submit, open a dialog. For going to another page, give it an href and it becomes a real link. Every example below comes in three versions: the web component (HTML, any framework), the React wrapper (@purpurabog/ui/react) and the React + Tailwind copy (shadcn). Pick a tab once and the whole site follows."],["Button","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Button","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#use-it",""],["Button","Pick a kind","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#pick-a-kind","Kind Use it for primary The one main action of a page or dialog secondary The action next to the primary one (Cancel, Back) tertiary A less important action that still needs a visible border ghost Quiet actions in toolbars, tables and next to other content danger, danger-tertiary, danger-ghost Actions that delete or can't be undone Use one primary button per area. kind is Carbon's name; variant works as an alias on the web component."],["Button","Danger buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#danger-buttons","Use a danger kind for an action that deletes something or can't be undone: danger for the main action of a confirm dialog, danger-tertiary and danger-ghost next to other content. Add a danger description: screen readers hear it after the name, so the warning isn't carried by the red colour alone."],["Button","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (the default), xl 64px, 2xl 80px. In forms, match the field height (md for 40px fields). On xl and 2xl the label stays at the top, as in Carbon."],["Button","Full width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#full-width","full-width stretches the button to the width of its container. Use it for the only action at the foot of a narrow form or a phone screen."],["Button","Button set","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#button-set","<ui-button-set> puts buttons side by side, each up to 196px wide, with a thin line between them: Carbon's footer of a form or side panel. Put the secondary button first. stacked gives each button its own row, for a narrow panel."],["Button","Icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#icons","The web component takes an icon in its prefix or suffix slot; the React + Tailwind button takes a trailing icon only. Carbon puts the icon at the end, and a ghost button that moves on to more detail often ends in a chevron. For a button with only an icon, see icon-only buttons."],["Button","Icon-only buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#icon-only-buttons","For a button that shows only an icon, use <ui-icon-button> (Carbon's IconButton). Its label is both its name and its tooltip, so the meaning shows on hover and on focus. It's ghost by default; tooltip-placement moves the tooltip (below by default). <ui-button icon-only label=\\"…\\"> also makes a square button, but without the tooltip."],["Button","Notification badge","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#notification-badge","badge-count puts Carbon's badge indicator in the corner of a ghost icon button: a number shows a count, and 0 shows a dot. Screen readers hear the count as the button's description. Use it for things waiting for the user, such as approvals."],["Button","Toggle buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#toggle-buttons","pressed makes a button that stays on or off, such as pinning a contract to the dashboard. Screen readers hear \\"pressed\\" or \\"not pressed\\". Flip it in your click handler; leave it unset on an ordinary button. It works on <ui-button> and <ui-icon-button>."],["Button","Loading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#loading","loading shows Carbon's small spinner, ignores clicks and keeps focus on the button, so keyboard users don't lose their place. The loading text replaces the label while it loads; the loading label is what screen readers hear. loading-position moves the spinner: end (the default) where a trailing icon goes, start in the label's place, center in the middle of the button."],["Button","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#skeleton","While the data behind a page loads, <ui-button-skeleton> keeps the button's place: a 150px bar at the button's size. Screen readers skip it, so say \\"loading\\" on the area around it (for example aria-busy=\\"true\\")."],["Button","Disabled, or disabled with a reason","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#disabled-or-disabled-with-a-reason","disabled removes the button from the Tab order, as Carbon does. If people need to learn why they can't use it, use disabled-focusable instead: it looks disabled and ignores clicks, but keyboard users can still reach it and read a tooltip."],["Button","Links that look like buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#links-that-look-like-buttons","With href the button renders an <a> and screen readers announce a link. On the web component a plain click fires a cancelable ui-navigate event, so a SPA router can take over (see Frameworks). In this preview the event is cancelled and its href shown instead."],["Button","Submit a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#submit-a-form","In a <form>, type=\\"submit\\" submits it and type=\\"reset\\" resets it, as a native button does. The default type is button, so other buttons never submit by accident. Set loading while the request runs, so nobody sends it twice."],["Button","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#accessibility","It renders a native <button>: Enter and Space press it, and type=\\"submit\\" / type=\\"reset\\" work in a <form>. Name icon-only buttons: label on the web component (an aria-label on the element does not reach the inner button), aria-label on the Tailwind button. pressed makes it a toggle button (aria-pressed); haspopup and expanded describe a button that opens a menu or dialog. Danger kinds can add a danger description, read after the name (\\"Deletes the contract for good\\")."],["Button","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Button","<ui-button> · React UiButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/button/#ui-button-react-uibutton","Attribute Property Type Default Description variant Same as kind, kept for teams used to variant (shadcn, MUI); kind is Carbon's name and the one in the docs kind kind ButtonKind 'primary' Carbon kind: primary, secondary, tertiary, ghost, danger, danger-tertiary, danger-ghost. size size ButtonSize 'lg' disabled disabled boolean false disabled-focusable disabledFocusable boolean false Disabled, but still focusable: aria-disabled, ignores clicks — so a tooltip can explain why. type type 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset' 'button' full-width fullWidth boolean false Stretch to the container width. icon-only iconOnly boolean false Square button (as wide as it is tall, no padding) with its content centred: put the icon in the prefix slot and leave the label empty — nothing is hidden for you. Set label for its name; it shows no tooltip (use <ui-icon-button> for one). label label string '' Accessible name; required when the button shows only an icon. description description string '' Accessible description (set by ui-tooltip). danger-description dangerDescription string '' Carbon dangerDescription: read after the name of a danger kind (danger, danger-tertiary, danger-ghost), e.g. \\"Deletes the contract for good\\". Empty by default, as Carbon v11 (React ButtonBase, WC cds-button). href href string '' Render as a link. target target '_self' | '_blank' '_self' loading loading boolean false Busy: looks disabled with a spinner, ignores clicks, keeps focus, announces loading-label. loading-label loadingLabel string '' What loading announces (default: loading-text, else the translation's \\"Loading\\"). loading-position loadingPosition ButtonLoadingPosition 'end' Where the spinner goes (MUI loadingPosition): end (Carbon ActionSet), start, center. loading-text loadingText string '' Shown in the label's place while loading, e.g. \\"Saving…\\" (Carbon Modal loadingDescription). pressed pressed boolean | undefined Toggle-button state; leave unset for a normal button. haspopup haspopup string '' The button opens a popup: rendered as aria-haspopup (e.g. menu, listbox, dialog). expanded expanded boolean | undefined Whether the popup / disclosed content is open (aria-expanded); left unset, only a haspopup button reports it. Property Type Description variant ButtonKind Same as kind (permanent alias for teams used to variant); a variant attribute works too. form (read-only) The <form> the button submits or resets, as a native button's form. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Label prefix Leading icon suffix Trailing icon (e.g. the ghost-button chevron) Part Description base The native button or link prefix The leading icon slot suffix The trailing icon slot loading The spinner's place: at the end, the start or the centre (loading only; not when it takes the label's place) Custom property Default Description --ui-button-align align-items of the content (ui-modal sets flex-start for its 64px footer buttons) --ui-button-padding-top Top padding of the content (ui-modal footer: 14px) --ui-button-padding-start Start padding (default 15px; ui-table-batch-actions: 16px) --ui-button-padding-end End padding (default 63px, Carbon's room for an icon; ui-table-batch-actions: 16px) --ui-button-height-lg Height of size=\\"lg\\", the default (default: --ui-field-height-lg, 48px; Kanok: 32px) --ui-button-radius Corner radius (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-button-justify justify-content of label and icon (default space-between, Carbon's label-start / icon-end; Kanok: center) --ui-button-gap Gap between label and icon (default 32px; Kanok: 8px) --ui-button-ghost-justify justify-content of the ghost kinds (default flex-start) --ui-button-ghost-padding-end End padding of the ghost kinds (default 15px) --ui-button-secondary Fill of kind=\\"secondary\\" (default --ui-secondary); also --ui-button-secondary-hover, --ui-button-secondary-active --ui-on-button-secondary Text of kind=\\"secondary\\" (default --ui-on-primary) --ui-button-secondary-border Border colour of kind=\\"secondary\\" (default transparent) --ui-button-height-xl Height of size=\\"xl\\" (default 64px; Kanok: 40px); also --ui-button-height-2xl (80px; Kanok: 48px) --ui-button-padding-xl Start and end padding of size=\\"xl\\" (default: the button's own); also --ui-button-padding-2xl --ui-button-tall-align align-items of xl / 2xl content (default flex-start, Carbon's label at the top; Kanok: center) --ui-button-tall-padding-top Top padding of xl / 2xl content (default 14px; Kanok: 0px); also --ui-button-tall-icon-offset (1px) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of the focus ring (default -2px, inside; Kanok: 2px, outside) --ui-focus-inset-width Width of the inner focus-inset line (default 2px; Kanok: 0) --ui-button-tertiary-hover / --ui-button-tertiary-active / --ui-button-tertiary-focus - Tertiary fills (default primary, its hover and active; Kanok: the highlight tint) --ui-button-tertiary-state-ink / --ui-button-tertiary-active-border - Tertiary text on those fills and the pressed border (default text-on-color, the button's border)"],["Text input","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/","A text input takes one line of text: a name, an email, a password, an ID number. For several lines, use a text area; for amounts, a number input."],["Text input","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Text input","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#use-it","The element fires native input on every keystroke and change when the user commits the value, so the React wrapper has onInput and onChange. The React + Tailwind onChange is React's own (every keystroke). Its second argument is the value without a mask's separators."],["Text input","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px."],["Text input","Passwords","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#passwords","type=\\"password\\" adds Carbon's show / hide button at the end of the field. Its tooltip is also its name and says what a press does next: \\"Show password\\", then \\"Hide password\\". Change the words with show-password-label and hide-password-label. Each press fires ui-toggle with detail.visible."],["Text input","Email, phone and web addresses","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#email-phone-and-web-addresses","type also takes email, tel, url, search and number, as on <input>. For the virtual keyboard alone, set inputmode (and enterkeyhint for its Enter key). Add autocomplete so the browser can fill the field in. The browser checks an email address; a mask keeps a phone number readable."],["Text input","Currency, units and masks","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#currency-units-and-masks","prefix-text and suffix-text put text inside the field, before or after the value: a currency, a unit. They aren't part of the value, and screen readers hear them as part of the field's description. mask formats the value as the user types: 0 is a digit, a a letter, * either, and any other character is a separator the field adds by itself. A mask of digits only brings up the numeric keyboard. Put the format in the helper text too, so people know it before they type. The element's value and the submitted form get the formatted text (1-2345-67890-12-3). Its rawValue property gives what was typed, without separators (1234567890123). In React + Tailwind, onChange gets that as its second argument. A value your code sets, raw or formatted, shows formatted. None of these has a Carbon counterpart (Carbon puts the unit or the format in the label or helper text); they follow USWDS."],["Text input","Read the value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#read-the-value","Listen to input to react on every keystroke, or to change once the user is done. With a mask, value is what the field shows and rawValue is what was typed."],["Text input","Character counter","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#character-counter","max-count shows a counter above the field. It's a soft limit: people can paste a long text and then trim it. Going over turns the counter red, shows an error at once and blocks the form. Screen readers hear when the limit is near, not on every keystroke. Change the messages with too-long-text ({max} becomes the limit) and near-limit-text. For a hard limit that stops typing, use maxlength. More in Forms and validation."],["Text input","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","One line shows under the field at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. On the element, required, pattern, minlength and the browser's checks work as on <input>, and their errors wait until the user leaves the field. The React + Tailwind field shows what you pass in invalid and invalidText; validation is your app's, as in Carbon React. To put a link in a message, use the slot of the same name (helper-text, warn-text, invalid-text). In React + Tailwind, pass the markup to helperText, warnText or invalidText. When errors show, custom validity and server errors: Forms and validation."],["Text input","Label and helper text with markup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#label-and-helper-text-with-markup","For a label or a message with markup, such as a link or an emphasis, use the label and helper-text slots (warn-text and invalid-text work the same way). The React + Tailwind field takes the markup in label and helperText."],["Text input","Label position, read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#label-position-read-only-and-disabled","hide-label keeps the label for screen readers but doesn't show it. Use it only where something else on screen names the field. inline puts the label before the field and the message after it, in one row (Carbon's inline text input). fluid, or a fluid form around the field, puts the label inside a 64px box (fluid forms). readonly shows and submits the value, but the user can't change it. disabled greys the field out; it isn't submitted."],["Text input","Fluid fields","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#fluid-fields","A fluid field puts its label inside a 64px box, and an error or a warning shows inside the box below a line; there is no helper text. Set fluid on a field, or put the fields in a <ui-fluid-form> (see fluid forms)."],["Text input","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Text input","Check it in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#check-it-in-a-form","In a <form>, the element checks required, type, pattern, minlength and the counter, as a native input does. A submit with a problem is blocked, every field with a problem shows its error, and the first one gets focus. Try sending this form empty."],["Text input","Errors from your own checks","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#errors-from-your-own-checks","setCustomValidity(message) makes the field invalid with your message, as on <input>. Use it for a check the browser can't do, such as a contract number that is already in use. The error shows once the user leaves the field; setCustomValidity('') clears it. More in Forms and validation."],["Text input","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#skeleton","While the data of a form loads, <ui-text-input-skeleton> keeps the field's place: a label bar and a field bar at its size, or a fluid box with fluid. Screen readers skip it, so say \\"loading\\" on the form (for example aria-busy=\\"true\\")."],["Text input","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#keyboard","Key What it does Enter Submits the form the field sits in, as a native text input does Enter or Space on the password button Shows or hides the password"],["Text input","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#accessibility","The label is a real <label> for the inner <input>, and the message line is its aria-describedby. aria-label on the element does not reach the input; use label (with hide-label if it must not show). An error sets aria-invalid on the input. On the element it waits until the user leaves the field, so nobody hears \\"required\\" while still typing. The password button has no aria-pressed: its name changes with what it does next, as in Carbon. The prefix and suffix are read as part of the field's description, so \\"฿\\" or \\"kg\\" isn't lost to screen reader users. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Text input."],["Text input","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Text input","<ui-text-input> · React UiTextInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-input/#ui-text-input-react-uitextinput","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Message shown when invalid. Falls back to the browser's validation message. invalid invalid boolean false Force the error state (e.g. a server-side error). warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. type type TextInputType 'text' size size TextInputSize 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). placeholder placeholder string '' autocomplete autocomplete string '' inputmode inputmode string '' Passed to the text box: the virtual keyboard to show (numeric, decimal, email, tel, url, search…). enterkeyhint enterkeyhint string '' Passed to the text box: the label of the virtual keyboard's Enter key (search, send, next, done…). pattern pattern string '' prefix-text prefixText string '' Text inside the field before the value, e.g. a currency (฿). Part of the field's description for screen readers. suffix-text suffixText string '' Text inside the field after the value, e.g. a unit (kg). Part of the field's description for screen readers. mask mask string '' Formats the value as the user types: 0 a digit, a a letter, * either; any other character is a separator added for the user (\\\\ makes a pattern character one). E.g. 0-0000-00000-00-0 (Thai citizen ID), 000-000-0000. value and the form get the formatted text, rawValue what was typed. Put the format in the helper text too (Carbon). minlength minlength number | undefined maxlength maxlength number | undefined max-count maxCount number | undefined Soft limit with a visible counter (unlike maxlength, extra text isn't blocked). too-long-text tooLongText string '' Error when over max-count; {max} is replaced with the limit. near-limit-text nearLimitText string '' Announced once when the remaining characters drop to 10% or less. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidTextInput: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. show-password-label showPasswordLabel string '' The password toggle's name and tooltip while the password is hidden (Carbon showPasswordLabel; default: the translation's \\"Show password\\"). hide-password-label hidePasswordLabel string '' The password toggle's name and tooltip while the password shows (Carbon hidePasswordLabel; default: the translation's \\"Hide password\\"). inline inline boolean false Carbon inline: the label before the field, the helper / error text after it (ignored while fluid). Property Type Description rawValue (read-only) The characters typed, without the mask's separators (value when there is no mask). willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change onChange Re-dispatched from the native input (native change is not composed) ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { visible } when the password toggle shows or hides the password (Carbon onTogglePasswordVisibility) input onInput Native input event (already composed, so it reaches the host) Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The field box around the input label The label input The native input prefix The text before the value suffix The text after the value password-toggle The show / hide password button password-tooltip The <ui-tooltip> around it (its name) counter The character counter status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Text area","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/","A text area takes text that runs over several lines: notes, a description, a reason. It has the same label, helper text and error line as the text input, plus a character or word counter and a field that can grow with its text."],["Text area","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Text area","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#use-it","The element fires native input on every keystroke and change when the user leaves the field, so the React wrapper has onInput and onChange. The React + Tailwind onChange is React's own (every keystroke)."],["Text area","Height","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#height","rows sets the starting height in lines, 4 by default as in Carbon. The user can drag the corner to make it taller (resize: vertical); a disabled field can't be resized."],["Text area","Grow with the text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#grow-with-the-text","auto-grow starts at rows and grows a line at a time as the user types, with no resize handle. max-rows caps it; past that, the field scrolls. Carbon has no auto-grow."],["Text area","Count characters or words","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#count-characters-or-words","max-count shows a counter above the field. As on the text input, it's a soft limit: going over turns the counter red, shows an error at once and blocks the form, but nothing is cut. Screen readers hear when the limit is near. counter-mode=\\"word\\" counts words instead (Carbon's counterMode). Thai has no spaces between words, so the field asks the browser's word segmenter for its language (lang on the field or the page): \\"สวัสดีครับ ผมชื่อสมชาย\\" is 5 words, where Carbon's count splits Thai at every vowel and tone mark. Numbers don't count as words. Change the messages with too-long-text ({max} becomes the limit) and near-limit-text. For a hard limit that stops typing, use maxlength. More in Forms and validation."],["Text area","Your own counter messages","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#your-own-counter-messages","too-long-text is the error once the text is over the limit, and near-limit-text is what screen readers hear once when 10% or less is left. Write them for the field, so people know what to cut. This text is already too long, so the error shows at once."],["Text area","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","Same as the text input: one line under the field, an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. The error and warning icons sit in the top-right corner of the field. required, minlength and maxlength work on the element as on <textarea>. In React + Tailwind, validation is your app's: pass invalid and invalidText. Everything else about errors: Forms and validation."],["Text area","Label and helper text with markup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#label-and-helper-text-with-markup","For a label or a message with markup, use the label and helper-text slots (warn-text and invalid-text work the same way). The React + Tailwind field takes the markup in label and helperText."],["Text area","Read-only, disabled and fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#read-only-disabled-and-fluid","readonly shows and submits the text, but the user can't change it. disabled greys it out; it isn't submitted. fluid, or a fluid form around it, puts the label inside the box (Carbon's FluidTextArea, see fluid forms)."],["Text area","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Text area","Check it in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#check-it-in-a-form","In a <form>, required and minlength block the submit until the text is long enough, and the field shows its error. Try sending this form with a short reason."],["Text area","Save a draft when the user leaves","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#save-a-draft-when-the-user-leaves","change fires once the user leaves the field after changing it, so it is the moment to save a draft without a request on every keystroke."],["Text area","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#skeleton","While the data of a form loads, <ui-text-area-skeleton> keeps the field's place: a label bar and a 100px field bar, or a fluid box with fluid. Screen readers skip it, so say \\"loading\\" on the form (for example aria-busy=\\"true\\")."],["Text area","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#accessibility","The label is a real <label> for the inner <textarea>, and the message line is its aria-describedby. aria-label on the element does not reach the textarea; use label (with hide-label if it must not show). Enter types a new line, as in any text area; it never submits the form. The counter is not read on every keystroke. Screen readers hear once when the limit is near and when it's passed. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Text area."],["Text area","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Text area","<ui-text-area> · React UiTextArea","/kanok-ui-docs/en/text-area/#ui-text-area-react-uitextarea","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. placeholder placeholder string '' rows rows number 4 Initial number of text rows (Carbon default 4); the user can still resize. minlength minlength number | undefined maxlength maxlength number | undefined autocomplete autocomplete string '' Passed to the textarea (off, or an autofill token). inputmode inputmode string '' Passed to the text box: the virtual keyboard to show (numeric, decimal, email, tel, url, search…). enterkeyhint enterkeyhint string '' Passed to the text box: the label of the virtual keyboard's Enter key (search, send, next, done…). max-count maxCount number | undefined Soft limit with a visible counter (unlike maxlength, extra text isn't blocked). counter-mode counterMode CounterMode 'character' What max-count counts: character (default) or word (Carbon counterMode). auto-grow autoGrow boolean false Grows with the text from rows (no Carbon counterpart); max-rows caps it, then it scrolls. max-rows maxRows number | undefined The most lines auto-grow shows before scrolling (default: no cap). too-long-text tooLongText string '' Error when over max-count; {max} is replaced with the limit (default: the translation's, for characters or words). near-limit-text nearLimitText string '' Announced once when what is left of the limit drops to 10% or less. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidTextArea: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change onChange Re-dispatched from the native textarea (native change is not composed) input onInput Native input event (already composed, so it reaches the host) Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The field box around the textarea label The label input The native textarea counter The character (or word) counter status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px)"],["Number input","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/","A number input takes a number: a quantity, an amount, a percentage. Carbon's − and + buttons sit at the end of the field, and ↑ / ↓ step from the keyboard."],["Number input","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Number input","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#use-it","The value is text, so the field can be empty: \\"12\\", \\"0.5\\", or \\"\\". The element's valueAsNumber gives the number (NaN while empty). The element fires input on every keystroke or step, and change when the value is committed (leaving the field, Enter, a step). The React wrapper has onInput and onChange. The React + Tailwind onChange gets the new value as text, not an event."],["Number input","Step, minimum and maximum","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#step-minimum-and-maximum","step (1 by default) is how far − / + and ↑ / ↓ move. A step stays within min and max, and the button at the end of the range turns off. A value typed outside the range is an error. From an empty field, the first step goes to step-start-value if you set one; otherwise to min when only a minimum is set, else to 1 or −1, as in Carbon."],["Number input","Decimals","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#decimals","A step rounds to the decimals of the value or of step, whichever has more, so 0.1 + 0.2 shows 0.3, not 0.30000000000000004. With the default type=\\"number\\", step is also the precision the browser accepts: with step=\\"0.01\\", 12.345 is an error."],["Number input","Currency, units and number formats","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#currency-units-and-number-formats","prefix-text and suffix-text put text inside the field, before or after the number: ฿, kg, baht a month. They stay in view while the user types and aren't part of the value. They have no Carbon counterpart. For Carbon's formatted field, set type=\\"text\\" with format-options, which takes any Intl.NumberFormat options: thousands separators, currency, percent, units. The text is free while the user types and is formatted when they leave. The value stays a plain number: ฿1,234.50 submits 1234.5, and a percent style gives the fraction (0.5 for 50%). The locale is the page language, or locale."],["Number input","Percent and units","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#percent-and-units","With format-options, the percent sign or the unit is part of the formatted text, which is Carbon's way. A percent style stores the fraction: 7.5% is 0.075, so give step, min and max as fractions too. locale picks the number format when it must not follow the page."],["Number input","Empty fields","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#empty-fields","As in Carbon, an empty number input counts as missing, even without required: the form won't submit until there is a number. Set allow-empty on a field that may stay empty."],["Number input","Steppers and the mouse wheel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#steppers-and-the-mouse-wheel","hide-steppers removes the − / + buttons; ↑ / ↓ still step. disable-wheel stops the mouse wheel from changing a focused field, which is easy to do by accident while scrolling a long form. decrement-label and increment-label rename the buttons for screen readers (\\"Decrement number\\" and \\"Increment number\\" by default, translated)."],["Number input","Sizes, messages, read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#sizes-messages-read-only-and-disabled","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. helper-text, warn + warn-text and invalid + invalid-text work as on the text input. A value outside min / max gets the browser's or the built-in message unless you set invalid-text. More in Forms and validation. readonly shows and submits the number, and the steppers turn off. disabled greys it out; it isn't submitted."],["Number input","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#fluid","fluid (Carbon's FluidNumberInput), or a <ui-fluid-form> around the field, puts the label inside a 64px box; an error or a warning shows inside the box, and there is no helper text. See fluid forms."],["Number input","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Number input","Work out a total","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#work-out-a-total","Listen to input to update a total on every keystroke and every step. valueAsNumber gives the number, or NaN while the field is empty."],["Number input","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#in-a-form","With a name, the field submits a plain number: the formatted rent ฿18,500.00 below submits 18500. A value outside min / max, or an empty field without allow-empty, blocks the submit and shows its error. Try 72 months."],["Number input","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#skeleton","While the data of a form loads, <ui-number-input-skeleton> keeps the field's place: a label bar and a field bar at its size, or a fluid box with fluid. Screen readers skip it, so say \\"loading\\" on the form (for example aria-busy=\\"true\\")."],["Number input","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#keyboard","Key What it does ↑ / ↓ One step up or down, within min / max Enter Commits the value and submits the form the field sits in The − / + buttons are out of the Tab order, as in Carbon: the arrow keys do the same from the field."],["Number input","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#accessibility","The label is a real <label> for the inner <input>; the prefix, the suffix and the message line are its description. The − / + buttons have names (\\"Decrement number\\", \\"Increment number\\") and turn off at the end of the range. inputmode=\\"decimal\\" brings up a keyboard with a decimal point on phones. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Number input."],["Number input","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Number input","<ui-number-input> · React UiNumberInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/number-input/#ui-number-input-react-uinumberinput","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. value value string '' The field text; valueAsNumber gives the parsed number (NaN while empty or invalid). name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. placeholder placeholder string '' prefix-text prefixText string '' Text inside the field before the value, e.g. a currency (฿); not part of value. Part of the field's description for screen readers. suffix-text suffixText string '' Text inside the field after the value, e.g. a unit (kg); not part of value. Part of the field's description for screen readers. min min number | undefined max max number | undefined step step number 1 Step of the ± buttons and ↑ / ↓; with type=\\"number\\" also the allowed precision. step-start-value stepStartValue number 0 Where the steppers start from an empty field (Carbon stepStartValue); 0 = Carbon's rule: ±1, or min when only a minimum is set. type type NumberInputType 'number' number: a native number field. text: a text field formatted for locale with format-options (Carbon type=\\"text\\"). locale locale string '' BCP 47 locale of the formatting with type=\\"text\\"; empty = the page language (lang on the element, an ancestor or <html>), as ui-date-picker. format-options formatOptions Intl.NumberFormatOptions {} Intl.NumberFormat options with type=\\"text\\", e.g. {\\"style\\":\\"currency\\",\\"currency\\":\\"THB\\"} or {\\"maximumFractionDigits\\":2}. allow-empty allowEmpty boolean false An empty field is valid (Carbon allowEmpty); otherwise empty counts as missing. hide-steppers hideSteppers boolean false Remove the − / + buttons (keyboard stepping still works). disable-wheel disableWheel boolean false Ignore mouse-wheel changes while focused (Carbon disableWheel). size size NumberInputSize 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidNumberInput: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. decrement-label decrementLabel string '' Accessible name of the − button. increment-label incrementLabel string '' Accessible name of the + button. Property Type Description valueAsNumber (read-only) The parsed value, NaN while empty or not a number. willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change onChange After a committed change (blur / Enter / stepper; with type=\\"text\\", on blur when the number changed) input onInput On every keystroke or stepper click Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The field box label The label input The native input prefix The text before the value suffix The text after the value controls The stepper group decrement-button The − button increment-button The + button status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Search","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/","A search field lets people find or filter content by typing. Carbon hides its label and shows a magnifier instead; a clear button appears once there is text."],["Search","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Search","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#use-it","The element fires input on every keystroke, change when the value is committed (leaving the field, Enter) or cleared, and ui-clear after the clear button or Esc emptied it. In React + Tailwind, clearing empties the field with a real input event, so your onChange sees it; onClear runs after. Always give it a label, even though it doesn't show: it names the search landmark and the field (\\"Search\\" when you leave it out)."],["Search","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. Match the height of what sits next to it, such as a table toolbar or a button."],["Search","Clear the text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#clear-the-text","The × button appears once there is text and empties the field, keeping focus in it. Esc does the same from the keyboard. On an empty field Esc does nothing, so a dialog around the search can still close on Esc. clear-label renames the button (\\"Clear search input\\" by default, translated)."],["Search","Filter a list as you type","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#filter-a-list-as-you-type","For a short list that is already on the page, filter it on input. It fires on every keystroke and when the field is cleared, so one listener keeps the list in step."],["Search","Expandable search","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#expandable-search","expandable (Carbon's ExpandableSearch) shows only the magnifier until someone clicks it or presses Enter or Space; then it opens to its full width with focus in the field. Leaving it empty, or Esc on an empty field, closes it again. expanded is the state: set it to open the search from your code. Each open or close fires ui-toggle with detail.expanded. The magnifier is a button named by the label, with the label as its tooltip. ExpandableSearch comes with the same tw-search file."],["Search","Open with an earlier search","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#open-with-an-earlier-search","An expandable search with text stays open: it closes only when it's empty. Set expanded and value together to show a search the user ran before, such as a table filter kept in the address. Clear it and leave the field, and it closes."],["Search","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#fluid","fluid (Carbon's FluidSearch), or a <ui-fluid-form> around it, shows the label inside a 64px box, so the search lines up with the other fluid fields of a form."],["Search","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Search","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly keeps the text, still submits it and hides the clear button: use it to show the search behind a saved report. disabled greys the field out, for a search that can't be used yet."],["Search","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#in-a-form","Give it a name and it submits like <input type=\\"search\\">. Enter submits the form it sits in. required, pattern, minlength and maxlength work as on a native search input. Carbon's search has no error line, so a failed check shows the browser's bubble. readonly keeps the text and hides the clear button. disabled greys the field out. fluid, or a fluid form around it, shows the label inside a 64px box (Carbon's FluidSearch). Type at least two characters and press Enter."],["Search","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#skeleton","While the results load, <ui-search-skeleton> keeps the search's place: one bar at its size, or a fluid box with fluid. Screen readers skip it, so say \\"loading\\" on the area around it (for example aria-busy=\\"true\\")."],["Search","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#keyboard","Key What it does Esc Clears the text and keeps focus in the field; on an empty expandable search, closes it and focuses the magnifier Enter Commits the value and submits the form the search sits in Enter or Space on the magnifier Opens an expandable search Tab Moves to the clear button while there is text (it's skipped when there is nothing to clear)"],["Search","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#accessibility","It's a role=\\"search\\" landmark named by its label, so screen reader users can jump to it. The label is hidden on screen, as in Carbon, but the field and the landmark use it. aria-label on the element doesn't reach the inner input; use label. Pressing the clear button keeps focus in the field, so keyboard users can type again right away. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Search."],["Search","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Search","<ui-search> · React UiSearch","/kanok-ui-docs/en/search/#ui-search-react-uisearch","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Accessible name of the field (visually hidden, as in Carbon). placeholder placeholder string '' value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size SearchSize 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. autocomplete autocomplete string 'off' inputmode inputmode string '' Passed to the text box: the virtual keyboard to show (numeric, decimal, email, tel, url, search…). enterkeyhint enterkeyhint string '' Passed to the text box: the label of the virtual keyboard's Enter key (search, send, next, done…). clear-label clearLabel string '' Accessible name of the clear button. required required boolean false Constraint validation like <input type=\\"search\\">: blocks submit and reports in the browser's bubble (Carbon Search has no error line). pattern pattern string '' minlength minlength number | undefined maxlength maxlength number | undefined readonly readonly boolean false Value can be selected and submitted but not changed; no clear button. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidSearch: the label inside a 64px box. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. expandable expandable boolean false Carbon ExpandableSearch: collapsed to its magnifier until opened. expanded expanded boolean false Whether an expandable search is open. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid until cleared with ''. clear() Empties the field, keeps focus in it and announces the change (input, change, ui-clear). Event React Description change onChange When the value is committed (blur / Enter) or cleared ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } when an expandable search opens or collapses input onInput On every keystroke ui-clear onUiClear After the clear button or Esc emptied the field Part Description base The role=search wrapper input The native search input label The label (visually hidden, as in Carbon; shown inside the box when fluid) magnifier The search icon clear-button The clear button magnifier-button The magnifier of an expandable search Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Select","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/","A select picks one option from a list. It wraps the browser's own <select>, so phones open their native picker and screen readers know it well."],["Select","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Select","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#use-it",""],["Select","Select, Dropdown, Combobox or MultiSelect?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#select-dropdown-combobox-or-multiselect","Component Use it when Select A plain form field. The browser draws the list: the native picker on phones, the most familiar control for screen readers. Options are one line of text. Dropdown The list must look the same in every browser, or options need a second line (data-description). Combobox The list is long and typing is faster than scrolling, the options come from a server search, or free text is allowed. Multi-select The user picks several values. For two to five options that should all stay visible, use a radio group (one choice) or checkboxes (several)."],["Select","Placeholder and starting value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#placeholder-and-starting-value","placeholder adds an empty first choice in a muted colour. With required, the user has to pick something else before the form submits. Without a placeholder, the select starts on value, else on the <option selected>, else on the first option, as a native select does. Reset goes back to that starting value. change fires when the user picks an option. React + Tailwind renders a native <select>, so its onChange is React's own and it also takes defaultValue."],["Select","Groups and disabled options","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#groups-and-disabled-options","Put options in <optgroup label> to group them. disabled on an option or an <optgroup> shows it but blocks it. The web component watches its children, so you can add or remove <option>s at any time."],["Select","Options that depend on another field","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#options-that-depend-on-another-field","An address form fills the district list from the chosen province. Replace the options when the first select changes: the web component picks up the new children by itself. Keep the second select disabled until there is something to choose. districts, province and district are the same in every React version."],["Select","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default, as in Carbon), lg 48px."],["Select","Inline","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#inline","inline puts the label beside a compact, borderless select. Use it in toolbars and above tables, not in forms."],["Select","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#fluid","fluid puts the label inside a 64px box (Carbon's FluidSelect). A fluid form around the field does the same for every field in it; see fluid forms. Fluid fields have no helper line."],["Select","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Select","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","One line shows under the field at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. warn is a non-blocking warning; invalid forces the error, for example after the server rejected the value."],["Select","A link in the helper text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#a-link-in-the-helper-text","The helper-text, warn-text and invalid-text attributes are plain text. For a link or bold text, put the markup in the slot of the same name. In React + Tailwind, pass the markup to helperText, warnText or invalidText."],["Select","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) shows the value and submits it, but neither the mouse nor the keyboard can change it. Tab still moves through. disabled greys the select out. It isn't submitted."],["Select","Required in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#required-in-a-form","With required and a placeholder, the form won't submit until the user picks an option. Press Submit without a choice to see the error. Without invalid-text, the built-in \\"Please select an option.\\" shows, in the page's language. The React + Tailwind select shows what you pass in invalid and invalidText; checking the value is your app's, as in Carbon React. More in Forms and validation."],["Select","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#skeleton","While the options load, show ui-select-skeleton in the field's place: a label bar and a field bar at the same size. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/select-skeleton."],["Select","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#accessibility","The control is a native <select>: the browser's own keys open and change it, and phones show the system picker. label is tied to the select. Use hide-label to keep it for screen readers only when the context already names the field. Helper, warning and error text are the select's description, so they are read when it gets focus. Options can't hold markup or a second line. If you need that, use a Dropdown. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Select."],["Select","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Select","<ui-select> · React UiSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/select/#ui-select-react-uiselect","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. placeholder placeholder string '' Shown as an empty first choice; with required the user must pick something else. value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidSelect: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. inline inline boolean false Label beside a compact, borderless select. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change none (use a ref) When the user picks an option Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The field box label The label input The native select chevron The arrow icon status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-inline-border-color Border colour of the inline variant (default: no underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-select-appearance base-select opens the list in the menu look of the dropdowns (--ui-menu-*) where the browser supports a customizable select (Chrome 135+); default none, the native list (Kanok: base-select) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px)"],["Dropdown","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/","A dropdown picks one option from a list that looks the same in every browser. Options can have a second line and sit in labelled groups."],["Dropdown","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Dropdown","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#use-it",""],["Dropdown","Select, Dropdown, Combobox or MultiSelect?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#select-dropdown-combobox-or-multiselect","Component Use it when Select A plain form field. The browser draws the list: the native picker on phones, the most familiar control for screen readers. Dropdown The list must look the same in every browser, or options need a second line. Combobox The list is long and typing is faster than scrolling, the options come from a server search, or free text is allowed. Multi-select The user picks several values."],["Dropdown","Options, groups and descriptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#options-groups-and-descriptions","The web component takes <option value> children, the same markup as Select: <optgroup label> makes a labelled group in the list. data-description on an option adds a second line under its label. Typing to jump to an option only searches the label. disabled shows an option but skips it. React + Tailwind takes the same as data in items: options { value, label, description?, disabled? } and groups { label, options }."],["Dropdown","Placeholder and value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#placeholder-and-value","placeholder is the text in the field while nothing is chosen (Carbon calls it label). The starting choice is value, else the <option selected>. Reset goes back to it. change fires when the user picks a different option. React + Tailwind also takes defaultValue when you don't need to hold the value yourself."],["Dropdown","Sizes and direction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#sizes-and-direction","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. The list opens below the field. direction=\\"top\\" prefers above; either way it flips when there is no room."],["Dropdown","Inline","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#inline","inline puts the label, a borderless field and any error or warning in one row, with no helper line. Use it in toolbars and above tables."],["Dropdown","Inline with an error or a warning","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#inline-with-an-error-or-a-warning","An inline dropdown shows its error or warning beside the field, in the same row, so a toolbar keeps its height."],["Dropdown","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#fluid","fluid puts the label inside a 64px box (Carbon's FluidDropdown); the open list keeps the usual row height. A fluid form around the field does the same for every field in it; see fluid forms."],["Dropdown","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Dropdown","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","One line shows under the field at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. warn doesn't block the form; invalid forces the error."],["Dropdown","Load the options when the list opens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#load-the-options-when-the-list-opens","loading shows one \\"Loading…\\" row instead of the options, and the keys pick nothing. Together with the event that fires after the list opens or closes, you can fetch the options the first time someone opens the list. Open the list below: the names arrive after a second. loadOwners, load and owners are the same in every React version."],["Dropdown","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) shows the value and submits it, but the list doesn't open. disabled greys the field out. It isn't submitted."],["Dropdown","Required in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#required-in-a-form","An empty required dropdown blocks the form and has a built-in message in Thai and English; invalid-text replaces it. The error waits until the user leaves the field or submits. Press Submit without a choice to see it. submit prevents the navigation and puts new FormData(form) into sent, as in the HTML. More on errors and when they show: Forms and validation."],["Dropdown","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#skeleton","While the options load, show ui-dropdown-skeleton in the field's place: a label bar and a field bar at the same size. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/dropdown-skeleton."],["Dropdown","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#keyboard","Key List closed List open ↓, Enter, Space ↓ / Enter / Space open the list on the chosen option (else the first) ↓ moves down; Enter and Space pick the highlighted option and close ↑ Does nothing Moves up (no wrap) Home / End Opens on the first / last option First / last option Page Up / Page Down Moves by 10 Letters Opens on the next option that starts with them Jumps to the next option that starts with them Alt+↑ Picks the highlighted option and closes Esc Closes without a change Tab Moves on Closes without a change and moves on"],["Dropdown","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#accessibility","It follows the WAI-ARIA select-only combobox pattern: the field is a button with role=\\"combobox\\", the list a listbox. Focus stays on the field and the highlighted option is announced through aria-activedescendant. The field is a Tab stop in every browser, Safari included. loading marks the list busy and announces \\"Loading…\\". Use hide-label only when the context already names the field. The label then stays for screen readers. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Dropdown."],["Dropdown","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Dropdown","<ui-dropdown> · React UiDropdown","/kanok-ui-docs/en/dropdown/#ui-dropdown-react-uidropdown","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. placeholder placeholder string '' Text shown in the field while nothing is selected (Carbon's label). value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). direction direction 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Preferred side for the list; it flips when there is no room. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. loading loading boolean false The options are on their way: the list shows \\"Loading…\\" and the keys pick nothing (no Carbon counterpart). fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidDropdown: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. inline inline boolean false Label beside a compact, borderless field. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after the list opens or closes (Carbon cds-dropdown-toggled) input onInput Whenever value changes, just before change (as ui-combobox and ui-multi-select) change onChange When the user picks a different option Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description option-description Second line of an option (<option data-description>) base The field box label The label input The field button (role=combobox) chevron The arrow icon status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) menu The floating list option Each row group-label An <optgroup> heading Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-inline-border-color Border colour of the inline variant (default: no underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-radius Corner radius of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-menu-border Border around the list (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-menu-shadow box-shadow of the list (default Carbon's 0 2px 6px) --ui-menu-padding Padding of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 4px, rows inset) --ui-menu-item-radius Corner radius of a row (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-menu-item-ink Text of a row at rest (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-divider Rule between rows (default --ui-row-divider; Kanok: none) --ui-menu-item-selected Fill of the chosen row (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: --ui-highlight) --ui-menu-item-selected-hover The chosen row under the pointer (default --ui-layer-selected-hover; Kanok: the highlight a shade deeper) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-field-open-background The box's fill while its list is open (default the field's hover fill; Kanok: transparent) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-menu-item-active-outline / --ui-menu-item-active-background - The keyboard-highlighted row: its ring and its fill (default focus, transparent) --ui-menu-item-pressed Fill of a pressed option (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: the 20% pressed tint)"],["Combobox","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/","A combobox is a text box with a list: people type to find an option instead of scrolling. Use it for long lists, server lookups, and fields that also take free text."],["Combobox","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Combobox","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#use-it","Not sure a combobox is the right field? See Select, Dropdown, Combobox or MultiSelect?"],["Combobox","How typing narrows the list","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#how-typing-narrows-the-list","Typing opens the list and highlights the first option whose label contains the text. filter decides whether the other options stay: filter The list while typing none (default, as Carbon) Every option stays; only the highlight moves contains Only options whose label contains the text, anywhere starts-with Only options whose label starts with the text Matching ignores case. When the filter leaves no option, the list shows \\"No matching items\\". Type \\"chiang\\" in both fields below to compare."],["Combobox","Free text or a listed option","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#free-text-or-a-listed-option","When the user leaves the field, text that exactly matches an option's label picks that option. Other text snaps back to the option chosen before, so the value is always one of the options. allow-custom-value keeps the typed text instead: it becomes the value and is submitted with the form. Use it when the list is only a suggestion, such as job titles."],["Combobox","Read the value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#read-the-value","The committed choice is value, and change fires when it changes. The text the user currently sees is inputValue on the web component. Type, pick, then leave the field to watch both. In React + Tailwind, onInputChange gets the text on every keystroke."],["Combobox","Search on a server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#search-on-a-server","Listen to the text as the user types, fetch the matches, replace the options, and set loading while the request runs. The list shows \\"Searching…\\" meanwhile. Keep filter=\\"none\\" (the default), as the server has already filtered. In the demo, a short timer stands in for the server. companies, loading, onText and search are the same in every React version."],["Combobox","Groups and descriptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#groups-and-descriptions","As in Dropdown: <optgroup label> groups options, data-description adds a second line, and disabled options are shown but can't be picked. React + Tailwind takes groups { label, options } and description in items. Typing only searches the labels, never the descriptions."],["Combobox","Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#clear","While the box holds text, × clears it along with the value. hide-clear removes the × (Carbon always shows it). Esc on a closed list still clears."],["Combobox","Sizes and direction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#sizes-and-direction","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. direction=\\"top\\" opens the list above when there is room."],["Combobox","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#fluid","fluid puts the label inside a 64px box (Carbon's FluidComboBox); the open list keeps the usual row height. A fluid form around the field does the same; see fluid forms."],["Combobox","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Combobox","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","One line shows under the field at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. warn doesn't block the form; invalid forces the error."],["Combobox","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) shows and submits the value but blocks changes. disabled greys the field out, and it isn't submitted."],["Combobox","Required in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#required-in-a-form","required blocks the form until a value is committed. The error waits until the user leaves the field or submits. Press Submit with the field empty to see it. submit prevents the navigation and puts new FormData(form) into sent, as in the HTML. More: Forms and validation."],["Combobox","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#keyboard","Key Does Typing Opens the list and highlights the first option containing the text ↓ / ↑ Opens the list on the chosen option (else the first / last); then moves the highlight (no wrap) Alt+↓ Opens the list without a highlight Alt+↑ Picks the highlighted option and closes Enter Picks the highlighted option. With no highlight, picks the first option containing the text (or keeps the text with allow-custom-value) Esc Closes the list; on a closed list, clears the field Tab Moves on without picking the highlight. The text is committed or snaps back, as described above"],["Combobox","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#accessibility","It follows the WAI-ARIA combobox pattern with list autocomplete: the text box has role=\\"combobox\\", the list is a listbox, and the highlight is announced through aria-activedescendant. The × and the chevron are not Tab stops (as in Carbon), so Tab goes straight to the next field. Esc clears from the keyboard. \\"Searching…\\" and \\"No matching items\\" are announced to screen readers. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Combobox."],["Combobox","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Combobox","<ui-combobox> · React UiCombobox","/kanok-ui-docs/en/combobox/#ui-combobox-react-uicombobox","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. placeholder placeholder string '' value value string '' Committed value: the chosen option's value, or free text with allow-custom-value. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). direction direction 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Preferred side for the list; it flips when there is no room. filter filter ComboboxFilter 'none' allow-custom-value allowCustomValue boolean false Keep text that matches no option as the value instead of snapping back. hide-clear hideClear boolean false No × button (Carbon always shows one while there is text); Escape on a closed list still clears. loading loading boolean false Shows a \\"Searching…\\" row while a server lookup is running. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidComboBox: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. Property Type Description inputValue What the user currently sees in the text box. willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after the list opens or closes input onInput Whenever value changes, as ui-dropdown and ui-multi-select; also native and composed as the user types, where value is unchanged (kept for compatibility: listen to ui-input for the typing) change onChange When the committed value changes ui-input onUiInput detail: { value } the typed text (inputValue), as the user types Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description option-description Second line of an option (<option data-description>) base The field box label The label input The text box (role=combobox) clear-button The × button toggle The chevron button status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) menu The floating list option Each row group-label An <optgroup> heading empty The \\"searching\\" / \\"no results\\" row Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-radius Corner radius of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-menu-border Border around the list (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-menu-shadow box-shadow of the list (default Carbon's 0 2px 6px) --ui-menu-padding Padding of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 4px, rows inset) --ui-menu-item-radius Corner radius of a row (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-menu-item-ink Text of a row at rest (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-divider Rule between rows (default --ui-row-divider; Kanok: none) --ui-menu-item-selected Fill of the chosen row (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: --ui-highlight) --ui-menu-item-selected-hover The chosen row under the pointer (default --ui-layer-selected-hover; Kanok: the highlight a shade deeper) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-menu-item-active-outline / --ui-menu-item-active-background - The keyboard-highlighted row: its ring and its fill (default focus, transparent) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-menu-item-pressed Fill of a pressed option (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: the 20% pressed tint)"],["Multi-select","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/","A multi-select picks several options from a list of checkbox rows. The list stays open while people choose, and a tag in the field shows how many are chosen."],["Multi-select","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Multi-select","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#use-it","Choosing one value from many? See Select, Dropdown, Combobox or MultiSelect?"],["Multi-select","Read and submit the value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#read-and-submit-the-value","value is the array of chosen values. Mark the starting choices with <option selected> (or defaultValue in React + Tailwind). The form gets one entry per chosen value under name, so read it with FormData.getAll(). change fires whenever the set of chosen values changes. With required, the form won't submit until at least one option is chosen. value is a property, not an attribute: in HTML, set it from JavaScript or use <option selected>. The placeholder stays in the field even after a choice (Carbon's label), next to the count tag."],["Multi-select","Select all","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#select-all","select-all adds a first row that checks or unchecks every enabled option. It shows a mixed state while only some are chosen."],["Multi-select","Where chosen options go","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#where-chosen-options-go","selection-feedback decides when chosen rows move to the top of the list: selection-feedback Chosen rows top-after-reopen (default) Move to the top the next time the list opens, so nothing jumps while choosing top Move to the top at once fixed Stay where they are Otherwise the order is yours (Carbon also sorts alphabetically; this library keeps your <option> order). With <optgroup>s, the groups stay as written and nothing moves. Choose the last rows in each field below, then close and reopen the lists."],["Multi-select","Filterable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#filterable","filterable turns the field into a text box that narrows the list as people type (Carbon's FilterableMultiSelect). filter is contains (the default, as Carbon) or starts-with. Choosing keeps the text and the list open; leaving the field clears the text. \\"Select all\\" then acts on the rows shown."],["Multi-select","Search on a server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#search-on-a-server","For a server search, set filter=\\"none\\", listen to the typed text, replace the options and set loading (the list shows \\"Searching…\\"). Keep the chosen options in the list so their rows stay. In the demo, a short timer stands in for the server. In the React versions, onText sets loading, calls search(), and puts the result in rows together with the chosen options. search() fetches the matches, as on Combobox."],["Multi-select","Load the options when the list opens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#load-the-options-when-the-list-opens","Without filterable, loading shows one \\"Loading…\\" row and the keys pick nothing. Use it with the open event to fetch the options on first open, exactly as on Dropdown: ui-toggle on the web component, onUiToggle in React, onMenuChange in React + Tailwind."],["Multi-select","Groups and descriptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#groups-and-descriptions","As in Dropdown: <optgroup label> groups options, data-description adds a second line (typing and filtering only search the labels), and disabled options can't be chosen. React + Tailwind takes groups { label, options } and description in items."],["Multi-select","Sizes and direction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#sizes-and-direction","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px; direction=\\"top\\" opens the list above."],["Multi-select","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#fluid","fluid puts the label inside a 64px box (Carbon's FluidMultiSelect); the open list keeps the usual row height. A fluid form around the field does the same; see fluid forms."],["Multi-select","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Multi-select","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","One line shows under the field at a time: an error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text. warn doesn't block the form; invalid forces the error."],["Multi-select","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) shows and submits the choice but blocks changes. disabled greys the field out, and it isn't submitted. Required fields, errors and warnings: Forms and validation."],["Multi-select","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#keyboard","Key List closed List open ↓, Enter, Space Open the list Enter and Space check or uncheck the highlighted row; the list stays open ↓ / ↑, Page Down / Page Up, Home / End ↑ does nothing; Home / End open on the first / last row Move the highlight Letters Open on the next option that starts with them Jump to the next option that starts with them Delete, Backspace, Esc Clear every choice Esc closes Tab Moves on Closes and moves on With filterable, the field is a text box: letters, Space, Home, End, Delete and Backspace edit the text, ↓ or Enter open the list, Enter checks the highlighted row, and Esc on a closed list clears the choices and the text."],["Multi-select","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#accessibility","The list is a listbox with aria-multiselectable; the highlight is announced through aria-activedescendant, so focus stays on the field. The × buttons are not Tab stops (as in Carbon). Delete, Backspace or Esc clear the choices from the keyboard. \\"Loading…\\", \\"Searching…\\" and \\"No matching items\\" are announced. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Multi-select."],["Multi-select","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Multi-select","<ui-multi-select> · React UiMultiSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/multi-select/#ui-multi-select-react-uimultiselect","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. placeholder placeholder string '' Text always shown in the field (Carbon's label), e.g. \\"Choose options\\". name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). direction direction 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Preferred side for the list; it flips when there is no room. selection-feedback selectionFeedback SelectionFeedback 'top-after-reopen' select-all selectAll boolean false Adds a \\"Select all\\" row. filterable filterable boolean false The field is a text box that narrows the list (Carbon FilterableMultiSelect / filterable). filter filter MultiSelectFilter 'contains' With filterable: contains (Carbon), starts-with, or none to leave the list to a server search. loading loading boolean false The options are on their way: \\"Searching…\\" with filterable (a server search), else \\"Loading…\\"; the keys pick nothing. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidMultiSelect: the label inside a 64px box, an error / warning inside it. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. Property Type Description value string[] Chosen option values. Initial choices can also come from <option selected>. inputValue With filterable, what the user typed; set it to search for something. willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after the list opens or closes (Carbon React onMenuChange) input onInput Whenever the set of chosen values changes, as ui-dropdown and ui-combobox; with filterable, also native and composed as the user types, where value is unchanged (kept for compatibility: listen to ui-input for the typing) ui-input onUiInput detail: { value } the typed text (inputValue) with filterable, as the user types or when the text is emptied change onChange Whenever the set of chosen values changes Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description option-description Second line of an option (<option data-description>) base The field box label The label input The field button, or the text box with filterable (role=combobox) toggle The chevron button (filterable) clear-filter-button The × that clears the text (filterable) empty The \\"searching\\" / \\"no results\\" row (filterable) tag The selected-count pill clear-button The × inside the pill chevron The arrow icon status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) menu The floating list option Each row select-all The \\"Select all\\" row checkbox The box drawn in each row group-label An <optgroup> heading Custom property Default Description --ui-count-tag-background The count pill's fill (default --ui-ink); also --ui-count-tag-ink (--ui-inverse-ink) and --ui-count-tag-hover (its ×, --ui-secondary-hover) --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-radius Corner radius of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-menu-border Border around the list (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-menu-shadow box-shadow of the list (default Carbon's 0 2px 6px) --ui-menu-padding Padding of the open list (default 0; Kanok: 4px, rows inset) --ui-menu-item-radius Corner radius of a row (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-menu-item-ink Text of a row at rest (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-divider Rule between rows (default --ui-row-divider; Kanok: none) --ui-menu-item-selected Fill of the chosen row (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: --ui-highlight) --ui-menu-item-selected-hover The chosen row under the pointer (default --ui-layer-selected-hover; Kanok: the highlight a shade deeper) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-field-open-background The box's fill while its list is open (default the field's hover fill; Kanok: transparent) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-menu-item-active-outline / --ui-menu-item-active-background - The keyboard-highlighted row: its ring and its fill (default focus, transparent) --ui-option-box-align / --ui-option-box-offset - A two-line row's checkbox: align-self and top margin (default auto, 0: centred; Kanok: beside the label line) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-menu-item-pressed Fill of a pressed option (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: the 20% pressed tint) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Checkbox","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/","A checkbox turns one option on or off. In a group, people can pick any number of options, including none."],["Checkbox","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Checkbox","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#use-it","The label is the element's content on the web component and the label prop in React + Tailwind. Import checkbox-group only when you use the group."],["Checkbox","One checkbox","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#one-checkbox","checked sets the state. change fires when the user toggles it. A checked box submits value (on by default) under name; an unchecked box submits nothing. required blocks submit until the box is checked, as for accepting terms."],["Checkbox","A group of checkboxes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#a-group-of-checkboxes","ui-checkbox-group labels a set of boxes and is announced as one group: required means \\"at least one\\": the form won't submit until a box is checked. orientation=\\"horizontal\\" puts the boxes in a row. disabled and readonly apply to every box, without overwriting each box's own setting. Each checkbox still submits its own name and value, so read them with FormData.getAll(). React + Tailwind has no checkbox group: use FormGroup (Carbon's fieldset), lay the boxes out yourself, and check \\"at least one\\" in your own validation. In the example, docsError comes from your own validation, such as \\"Select at least one option.\\""],["Checkbox","Helper text, warnings and errors on one box","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors-on-one-box","A single checkbox has its own message line under the label: helper-text, a non-blocking warn with warn-text, and invalid with invalid-text. An error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text."],["Checkbox","Warnings and errors on a group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#warnings-and-errors-on-a-group","On ui-checkbox-group, the message belongs to the whole group and shows once under it. An error also turns every enabled box red, and each box repeats the error for screen readers. React + Tailwind's FormGroup has invalid and message (the message turns red) but no warning state."],["Checkbox","Indeterminate","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#indeterminate","indeterminate shows a bar instead of a check: a parent box whose children are partly checked. The user's next click clears it. Keep the parent in step with its children in your code: all, chosen, some and pick are the same in every React version. On the web component, do the same in change listeners: set checked and indeterminate on the parent from its children."],["Checkbox","Hide the label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#hide-the-label","hide-label keeps the label for screen readers but doesn't show it, such as for a checkbox in a table row."],["Checkbox","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) keeps the state and submits it, but clicks and Space change nothing. disabled greys the box out, and it isn't submitted."],["Checkbox","Required in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#required-in-a-form","A required group needs at least one box; a required single box must be checked. The errors wait until the user has used the field or pressed Submit. Press Submit with nothing checked to see both. submit prevents the navigation and puts new FormData(form) into sent, as in the HTML. The group's message is built in, in Thai and English; required-text or invalid-text replaces it. More: Forms and validation."],["Checkbox","Selectable tiles","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#selectable-tiles","When each option needs a title and a description, use ui-selectable-tile: a checkbox drawn as a tile (Carbon's SelectableTile), from @purpurabog/ui/selection-tiles. It submits name and value like a checkbox, and Space toggles it. In a ui-checkbox-group the tiles are members like checkboxes: the group's required, disabled, readonly and error apply to them."],["Checkbox","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#skeleton","While the options load, show one ui-checkbox-skeleton per row: an empty box and a label bar. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/checkbox-skeleton."],["Checkbox","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#keyboard","Key Does Space Checks or unchecks the focused box Tab Moves to the next box: each checkbox is its own Tab stop"],["Checkbox","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#accessibility","Each box is a native checkbox inside a <label>, so the whole row is clickable and screen readers hear its state, \\"mixed\\" included. ui-checkbox-group is a role=\\"group\\" named by its label; its helper, warning or error text describes the group, and every box repeats the group's error so it is heard on the first box. Don't use a checkbox for a setting that applies at once; use a Toggle. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Checkbox."],["Checkbox","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Checkbox","<ui-checkbox> · React UiCheckbox","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#ui-checkbox-react-uicheckbox","Attribute Property Type Default Description checked checked boolean false indeterminate indeterminate boolean false Mixed state, e.g. a \\"select all\\" box with some children checked. Cleared on user toggle. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label text for screen readers but don't show it. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. value value string 'on' helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. Property Type Description groupDisabled boolean Set by ui-checkbox-group; kept apart from the author's own disabled / readonly. groupMessage string Error text of the owning ui-checkbox-group while the group is invalid. The group shows it once below the boxes; each box repeats it as its own accessible description and reports aria-invalid, so a screen reader landing on the first box hears why (an IDREF cannot cross the group's shadow root). willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change none (use a ref) When the user toggles the box Slot Description (default) Label text Part Description base The clickable row (label element) control The native checkbox input box The drawn 16px box label The text beside the box status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-checkbox-border Border of the box (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-checkbox-checked Fill and border when checked or mixed (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary) --ui-checkbox-mark Check mark colour (default --ui-icon-inverse; Kanok: --ui-on-primary)"],["Checkbox","<ui-checkbox-group> · React UiCheckboxGroup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#ui-checkbox-group-react-uicheckboxgroup","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the group label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. required-text requiredText string '' Error for an empty required group. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. orientation orientation 'vertical' | 'horizontal' 'vertical' Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Slot Description (default) <ui-checkbox> or <ui-selectable-tile> elements label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The group box holding the checkboxes label The group label status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot)"],["Checkbox","<ui-selectable-tile> · React UiSelectableTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/checkbox/#ui-selectable-tile-react-uiselectabletile","Attribute Property Type Default Description checked checked boolean false indeterminate indeterminate boolean false Mixed state, e.g. a \\"select all\\" box with some children checked. Cleared on user toggle. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label text for screen readers but don't show it. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. value value string 'on' helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. Property Type Description groupDisabled boolean Set by ui-checkbox-group; kept apart from the author's own disabled / readonly. groupMessage string Error text of the owning ui-checkbox-group while the group is invalid. The group shows it once below the boxes; each box repeats it as its own accessible description and reports aria-invalid, so a screen reader landing on the first box hears why (an IDREF cannot cross the group's shadow root). willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change none (use a ref) When the user toggles the box Slot Description (default) Tile content (title, description…) Part Description base The clickable row (label element) control The native checkbox input box The drawn 16px box label The text beside the box status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-tile-border-color Border of an unchosen tile (default transparent; Kanok: a hairline); --ui-card-radius its corners --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-tile-selected-border Border of the chosen tile (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: primary blue); --ui-tile-selected-mark its check mark (default --ui-icon-primary) --ui-tile-selected-background Fill of the chosen tile (default --ui-card-background; Kanok: soft highlight wash) --ui-tile-mark-space End padding kept clear for the mark (default 48px, Carbon's); e.g. 16px lets the content run under the mark in the top-end corner (beyond Carbon) --ui-checkbox-border Border of the box (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-checkbox-checked Fill and border when checked or mixed (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary) --ui-checkbox-mark Check mark colour (default --ui-icon-inverse; Kanok: --ui-on-primary)"],["Radio button","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/","Radio buttons pick exactly one option from a small set, with every option in view. Once one is picked, the user can change it but not clear it."],["Radio button","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Radio button","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#use-it","Radios always go in a group: the group holds the label, the name and the value, and submits the checked option's value. More than about five options, or not enough room? Use a Select or Dropdown."],["Radio button","Starting value and changes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#starting-value-and-changes","The group's value is the checked option. Without it, a <ui-radio checked> is the starting choice; with neither, nothing is checked. Reset goes back to the starting choice. change fires on the group when the user picks another option."],["Radio button","Orientation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#orientation","Groups are vertical by default. orientation=\\"horizontal\\" puts the options in a row; keep it for two or three short options."],["Radio button","Label position","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#label-position","label-position=\\"left\\" puts each option's text before its circle (Carbon labelPosition). A vertical group then lines the circles up at its end. Set it on one radio to move only that one."],["Radio button","Helper text, warnings and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#helper-text-warnings-and-errors","The group has one message line under its options: helper-text, a non-blocking warn with warn-text, and invalid with invalid-text. An error beats a warning, and a warning beats the helper text."],["Radio button","Disabled options, read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#disabled-options-read-only-and-disabled","disabled on one radio skips it; on the group, it disables every option and the group isn't submitted. readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) keeps the value and submits it. The arrow keys still move focus so people can read the options, but nothing changes."],["Radio button","Show more fields for one choice","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#show-more-fields-for-one-choice","A choice often needs details that only apply to it, such as a bank account for a transfer. Listen to change and show the extra field only for that option."],["Radio button","Required in a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#required-in-a-form","required on the group blocks submit until an option is picked, with a built-in message (required-text changes it). The rest: Forms and validation. Press Submit without a choice to see the message. submit prevents the navigation and puts new FormData(form) into sent, as in the HTML."],["Radio button","Radio tiles","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#radio-tiles","The same group also holds radio tiles (<ui-radio-tile>, from @purpurabog/ui/selection-tiles) when each option needs more room: a title and a line of description. The check mark shows only on the chosen tile."],["Radio button","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#skeleton","While the options load, show one ui-radio-skeleton per option: a label bar (Carbon draws no circle). It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/radio-skeleton."],["Radio button","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Enters the group on the checked option (else the first), and leaves it on the next Tab ↓ / → Moves to the next option and checks it; wraps from the last to the first ↑ / ← Moves to the previous option and checks it; wraps from the first to the last Space Checks the focused option"],["Radio button","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#accessibility","The group is a role=\\"radiogroup\\" named by its label, with one Tab stop, as the WAI-ARIA radio group pattern describes. Disabled options are skipped. The group's helper, warning or error text describes it, and each radio repeats the error so a screen reader hears it on the option it lands on. Use hide-label only when the context already names the group; the label then stays for screen readers. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Radio button."],["Radio button","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Radio button","<ui-radio-group> · React UiRadioGroup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#ui-radio-group-react-uiradiogroup","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Group label (rendered like a fieldset legend). hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the group label for screen readers but don't show it. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. value value string '' orientation orientation 'vertical' | 'horizontal' 'vertical' label-position labelPosition RadioLabelPosition 'right' Carbon labelPosition: left puts each radio's text before its circle (default right, after it). disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. required-text requiredText string '' Error text for an empty required group. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description input none (use a ref) change none (use a ref) When the user picks an option Slot Description (default) <ui-radio> options label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text Part Description base The group box holding the radios label The group label status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot)"],["Radio button","<ui-radio> · React UiRadio","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#ui-radio-react-uiradio","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' checked checked boolean false disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. label-position labelPosition RadioLabelPosition | undefined Carbon labelPosition: left puts the text before the circle; unset, the group's label-position applies. Slot Description (default) Label text Part Description circle The drawn radio circle label The text beside it Custom property Default Description --ui-radio-border Ring colour (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-radio-checked Ring and dot when chosen (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary)"],["Radio button","<ui-radio-tile> · React UiRadioTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/radio/#ui-radio-tile-react-uiradiotile","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' checked checked boolean false disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. label-position labelPosition RadioLabelPosition | undefined Carbon labelPosition: left puts the text before the circle; unset, the group's label-position applies. Slot Description (default) Tile content (title, description…) Part Description circle The drawn radio circle label The text beside it Custom property Default Description --ui-tile-border-color Border of an unchosen tile (default transparent; Kanok: a hairline); --ui-card-radius its corners --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-tile-selected-border Border of the chosen tile (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: primary blue); --ui-tile-selected-mark its check mark (default --ui-icon-primary) --ui-tile-selected-background Fill of the chosen tile (default --ui-card-background; Kanok: soft highlight wash) --ui-tile-mark-space End padding kept clear for the mark (default 48px, Carbon's); e.g. 16px lets the content run under the mark in the top-end corner (beyond Carbon) --ui-radio-border Ring colour (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-radio-checked Ring and dot when chosen (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary)"],["Toggle","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/","A toggle switches a setting on or off, and the change takes effect right away. The label sits above the switch and the state text beside it."],["Toggle","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Toggle","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#use-it",""],["Toggle","Toggle or checkbox?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#toggle-or-checkbox","Use a toggle when the change applies at once, such as a setting. In a form that the user submits later, or for agreeing to terms, use a Checkbox."],["Toggle","On and off","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#on-and-off","checked is the state. change fires after the user flips it, with checked already updated. saveSetting stands for your own code."],["Toggle","Labels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#labels","label is the text above the switch (the label slot takes markup). label-a and label-b are the state text beside it, for off and on. By default it reads \\"Off\\" / \\"On\\", translated to the page language. hide-label drops the label above; the label then replaces the state text beside the switch, as in Carbon."],["Toggle","Markup in the label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#markup-in-the-label","When part of the label needs weight, put it in the label slot; it replaces the label attribute. In React + Tailwind, label takes the markup itself."],["Toggle","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#sizes","size: md is a 48×24 track (the default); sm is 32×16, with a check mark in the knob when on."],["Toggle","A list of settings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#a-list-of-settings","For a list of related settings, put small toggles with hide-label in a form group, so each label sits beside its switch. When one setting turns the others off, disable the group: disabled on ui-form-group (FormGroup in React + Tailwind) disables every toggle inside."],["Toggle","State text in the page language","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#state-text-in-the-page-language","The default state text comes from the language of the page, or of the closest lang around the toggle. Set lang on the toggle, or on a part of the page, to change it there."],["Toggle","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#in-a-form","With a name, a toggle that is on submits value (on by default) with its form; off, it submits nothing. Form reset puts it back to its starting state. save stands for your own code."],["Toggle","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly (readOnly in React + Tailwind) shows the state and submits it, but clicks and keys don't flip it. disabled greys it out, and it isn't submitted."],["Toggle","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#skeleton","While the settings load, show <ui-toggle-skeleton> in the toggle's place, as Carbon's ToggleSkeleton. It has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/toggle-skeleton, and is hidden from screen readers."],["Toggle","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#keyboard","Key Does Space, Enter Flips the toggle Tab Moves to the next control"],["Toggle","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#accessibility","The switch is a <button role=\\"switch\\"> with aria-checked, named by the label above (or, with hide-label, by the label beside it). Screen readers hear \\"on\\" or \\"off\\" from the role, so the state text beside it is hidden from them. Clicking the track or the state text flips the switch, as in Carbon, and focus stays on it. Write the label as the setting (\\"Email alerts\\"), not as an action (\\"Turn on email alerts\\"). Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Toggle."],["Toggle","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Toggle","<ui-toggle> · React UiToggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggle/#ui-toggle-react-uitoggle","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Label above the switch; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Hide the label above; it then replaces the On / Off text beside the switch (Carbon hideLabel). label-a labelA string '' Side text while off (Carbon labelA). label-b labelB string '' Side text while on (Carbon labelB). checked checked boolean false value value string 'on' Submitted under name while checked. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size ToggleSize 'md' md: 48×24 track (default) · sm: 32×16 with a check mark in the knob. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the state but blocks toggling. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Event React Description input none (use a ref) change none (use a ref) After the user toggles it (checked already updated) Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback Part Description base The row holding the switch and the side text label The label above the switch switch The track handle The knob text The On / Off text beside the switch Custom property Default Description --ui-toggle-on Track colour when on (default --ui-success; Kanok: --ui-primary)"],["Date picker","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/","A date picker takes a date that users type or pick from a calendar. On a Thai page it shows the Buddhist era (พ.ศ.); your code always gets an ISO date in the Gregorian year."],["Date picker","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Date picker","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#use-it","UiDatePicker fires a native change, so its React prop is onChange (there is no onUiChange). The Tailwind DatePicker hands onChange the ISO string itself."],["Date picker","What users see, what you get","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#what-users-see-what-you-get","Users see and type the date in the page's language and era. Your code reads the same ISO date in every language. The two pickers below share one value: change either one. Page in Thai Page in English The user sees and types 10/10/2569 10/10/2026 value, change, the submitted form 2026-10-10 2026-10-10 value, min and max are always yyyy-mm-dd in the Gregorian year. A value that isn't a real date of that form becomes '', as with <input type=\\"date\\">. The element fires change when a value is committed: on leaving the field, on Enter, on a pick from the calendar and on clear. Read event.target.value (and endValue in a range). An empty field still submits name=, as a native date input does. A disabled picker submits nothing."],["Date picker","Type it or pick it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#type-it-or-pick-it","The calendar opens when the text box gets focus, by a click or by Tab, and focus stays in the box so users can keep typing. The calendar follows what they type. Text that already reads as a full date in the field's format, such as 10/10/2026, becomes the value at once; change fires when it is committed (blur, Enter), not while typing. Anything else is read on blur or Enter. The numbers are pulled out of what was typed, so s10/12/2026x becomes 10/12/2026. Nothing is guessed. An incomplete date (10/12), an impossible one (31/04/2026) or text with no date in it stays in the field with a message saying what's wrong, and value becomes ''. A full date outside min / max, or one isDateDisabled refuses, is kept and committed with its own message. The form won't submit until it's fixed. Try it: type a date that doesn't exist, or one outside the year, then leave the field. The messages come built in, in Thai and English. How and when errors show, and how to add your own, is in Forms and validation."],["Date picker","Buddhist era and Thai","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#buddhist-era-and-thai","The language comes from lang on the element or the closest ancestor, else <html lang>. A Thai language gives Thai labels and messages, Thai month names, and years in พ.ศ. (ค.ศ. + 543). locale overrides the language for this picker alone. era sets the year users see and type: be (พ.ศ., the default for Thai) or ce (ค.ศ., the default otherwise). Any language can use either. Typed years follow the same era. In พ.ศ., a year before 2400 (say 2026) gets a message asking for the พ.ศ. year; nothing is converted behind the user's back. Users may type Thai digits (๐–๙). They become 0–9 as they type. The placeholder and the default helper line show the format in the page's language: วว/ดด/ปปปป in Thai. React + Tailwind reads <html lang>, or its locale prop."],["Date picker","Formats","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#formats","format sets the order of day, month and year: dd/mm/yyyy (the default), mm/dd/yyyy or yyyy-mm-dd. Only what users see changes; value stays ISO. The format shows as helper text until you set helper-text (helperText in React + Tailwind). Screen readers still hear it after that."],["Date picker","Pick a range","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#pick-a-range","range gives two fields sharing one calendar: value / name / label for the start, end-value / end-name / end-label for the end. With both names the form gets two entries. Without end-name, ui-date-picker submits one name entry, start/end (2026-10-01/2026-10-05), as Carbon's cds-date-picker does; the React + Tailwind DatePicker submits the end only under endName. A pick keeps the calendar open for the end. The days in between are highlighted with a continuous ribbon, with a preview on either side of the start while the end is chosen (from the pointer or the keys; a day that can't be picked doesn't move it). Picking an end before the start swaps the two. With a whole range chosen, the next pick starts a new range (as Cally); change fires once both ends are picked. A typed end before the start is kept and reported, not swapped."],["Date picker","Two-month range view","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#two-month-range-view","Set months=\\"2\\" to display two side-by-side months in the calendar, ideal for flight/hotel booking and long booking ranges:"],["Date picker","Limit the dates","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#limit-the-dates","min and max take ISO dates. Days outside them are greyed out, and the month buttons stop at them. To refuse single days (weekends, holidays), set isDateDisabled: a function that returns true, or a string to show as the message. On the web component it's a property, so set it in JavaScript:"],["Date picker","Clear button and Today","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#clear-button-and-today","clearable adds a × inside the field while it has text. show-today adds a Today button under the calendar (Carbon has none; this one is opt-in). first-day sets the first day of the week, from 0 (Sunday, the default) to 6."],["Date picker","Sizes and fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#sizes-and-fluid","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default, as in Carbon), lg 48px, the same scale as the text input. fluid, or a fluid form around it (<ui-fluid-form>, FluidForm in React + Tailwind), gives Carbon's fluid field: a 64px box with the label inside. Both props have the same names in React and React + Tailwind."],["Date picker","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Date picker","Helper text, errors and warnings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#helper-text-errors-and-warnings","helper-text says what the date is for (the helper-text slot takes markup). warn with warn-text flags a date that is allowed but unusual; it doesn't block submit. invalid with invalid-text shows an error from your own check, such as one made on the server. In a range, the warning shows under the start field."],["Date picker","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly shows and submits the value but blocks typing and the calendar. disabled greys the field out; it isn't submitted or validated. A disabled <fieldset> around it does the same. The web component and its React wrapper spell it readonly; React + Tailwind uses readOnly."],["Date picker","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#in-a-form","With required, the form won't submit until the date is filled in; in a range, both dates are required. The form gets ISO dates under name (and end-name). Submit the empty form below to see the messages. send stands for your own code."],["Date picker","Phones and tablets","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#phones-and-tablets","On a phone (a touch screen narrower than 42rem), picker=\\"auto\\" (the default) opens the calendar in a bottom sheet: a dialog along the bottom edge of the screen, over a dimmed page. A tap on the box opens it with a day focused, so no on-screen keyboard comes up over it. Focus alone doesn't open it: after the sheet closes, a tap on the box types. Esc, the × button, a swipe down on its top bar or a tap on the dimmed page closes it. Typed text is committed and focus goes back to the box. While it is open the page behind can't be reached or scrolled, and the sheet's padding keeps clear of the phone's safe areas (the home indicator, a notch). On tablets and larger screens the calendar opens under the box as before. picker Opens auto (default) The bottom sheet on a phone, the calendar under the box everywhere else custom The calendar under the box on every device sheet The bottom sheet on every device native The OS date picker. It can't grey out isDateDisabled days, so its pick is checked like typed text Style the sheet with ::part(sheet) (its scrim with ::part(sheet)::backdrop), ::part(sheet-grip) and ::part(sheet-close); --ui-sheet-radius rounds its top corners (the menu radius by default). The prop has the same name in every variant."],["Date picker","The calendar on its own","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#the-calendar-on-its-own","The calendar inside the picker is its own element, ui-calendar, and it comes with the same import. It is a controlled view: it moves its own focus, but you keep the chosen day. Listen to ui-pick (detail { date }, a Date) and set value: The month shown follows the focusDate property (a Date, today by default). Like the picker, ui-calendar follows the page's language (the nearest lang) and shows พ.ศ. in Thai; locale and era override it. It takes min, max, isDateDisabled, range with end-value, first-day and show-today as the picker does. The React + Tailwind Calendar is controlled too: focusDate, onFocusDateChange and onPick are required."],["Date picker","Multiple dates (multi)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#multiple-dates-multi","<ui-calendar multi> allows selecting multiple arbitrary dates simultaneously (Cally style), toggled into values:"],["Date picker","Dual-month calendar (months=\\"2\\")","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#dual-month-calendar-months-2","<ui-calendar range months=\\"2\\"> renders two months side-by-side with a continuous cross-month range ribbon:"],["Date picker","Month and year selects (as Cally)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#month-and-year-selects-as-cally","The calendar's header has Cally's two native selects, <ui-calendar-select-month> and <ui-calendar-select-year>. A month wholly outside min / max is off, and the year list holds 20 years around the year shown, cut to min / max. On a Thai page the years are in พ.ศ. With several months the header has the year select only, because each grid has its month's name. Put your own content in the heading slot to replace them. Selects you put there, or inside what you put there, follow the calendar too: Element Attribute Does ui-calendar-select-month format-month Month names long (default) or short ui-calendar-select-year max-years How many years to offer around the year shown (default 20) Style the selects with ui-calendar::part(month-select) and ::part(year-select). The React + Tailwind Calendar has the same header; the headless parts are Calendar.MonthSelect and Calendar.YearSelect."],["Date picker","More calendar options (as Cally)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#more-calendar-options-as-cally","ui-calendar / ui-date-picker React + Tailwind Does months months 1 to 12 months side by side; 12 months show the calendar year from January page-by=\\"single\\" pageBy=\\"single\\" ‹ › move several months by one month (default: a whole page) show-week-numbers showWeekNumbers An ISO week number before each week; the picker's popover widens for it show-outside-days showOutsideDays Shows other months' days, in six weeks. By default they are blank and only the weeks the month needs show, as Cally (one month only) weekday-format weekdayFormat Weekday headings narrow or short (default: the translation's) today today The day marked as today, ISO; handy for tests and screenshots getDayParts (property, ui-calendar only) dayClassName Your own part names / classes for a day: holidays, events Style the parts that getDayParts returns with ::part(): ui-calendar also fires these events: ui-range-start and ui-range-end (detail { date }) for each end of a range. change waits until both ends are picked. ui-page-change (detail { start, end }) when the months on show change. The React + Tailwind Calendar has onPageChange for this. Other options: focus({ target: 'previous' | 'next' | 'day' }) moves focus to an arrow button or to the day. The previous and next slots replace the arrow icons, and heading the month and year selects. <ui-date-picker> takes show-outside-days, getDayParts (it exports the part names it returns, so ui-date-picker::part(holiday) works) and fires ui-range-start / ui-range-end; the React + Tailwind DatePicker has onRangeStart / onRangeEnd. Every day button has a part for each state it is in: selected, today, outside, disabled, disallowed, range-start, range-end, in-range and day-0 … day-6. The week numbers have the part weeknumber. In a right-to-left page, ← and → swap."],["Date picker","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#skeleton","While the page loads its data, show <ui-date-picker-skeleton> in the picker's place, as Carbon's DatePickerSkeleton; add range for two fields. It has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/date-picker-skeleton, and is hidden from screen readers."],["Date picker","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#keyboard","In the text box: Key Does Typing Enters the date; the open calendar follows a full date ↓ Opens the calendar and moves focus into it Tab Moves on to the next field (in a range, from the start to the end); what was typed is committed and the calendar closes once focus leaves the picker Shift + Tab From the start field: closes the calendar and moves back Enter Commits the typed text, closes the calendar and submits the form it's in Esc Closes the calendar In the calendar: Key Does ← / → Previous / next day ↑ / ↓ Same day of the previous / next week Home / End First / last day of the week Page Up / Page Down Previous / next month Shift + Page Up / Page Down Previous / next year Enter, Space Picks the day; the calendar closes (in a range, after the end) Esc Closes, focus back in the text box Tab Goes round the calendar's own controls: ‹, the month, the year, ›, the day (and Today), back to the first after the last; Esc or a pick leaves the calendar Shift + Tab The same, the other way round With a mouse, pick a month or a year from the selects in the calendar header."],["Date picker","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#accessibility","The text box is a combobox that opens a dialog (aria-haspopup=\\"dialog\\", aria-expanded). The calendar is a dialog named \\"Choose date\\" with a grid of day buttons, following the WAI-ARIA date picker dialog pattern. Each day is read as a full date (\\"Saturday, October 10, 2026\\"). Today has aria-current=\\"date\\", chosen days aria-pressed, refused days aria-disabled. Month changes are announced through a polite live region. The bottom sheet is a modal dialog with the same name: the page behind it is inert until it closes. The calendar icon is decorative, as in Carbon: it is not a Tab stop, and a click on it is a click in the text box. An error sets aria-invalid and is linked to the box with aria-describedby, as is the format hint. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Date picker."],["Date picker","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Date picker","<ui-date-picker> · React UiDatePicker","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#ui-date-picker-react-uidatepicker","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Visible label text; the label slot replaces it when markup is needed. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label for screen readers but don't show it. helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. value value string '' ISO yyyy-mm-dd (the start date in range mode). name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. range range boolean false Two fields sharing one calendar (Carbon datePickerType=\\"range\\"). end-value endValue string '' Range mode: the end date, ISO yyyy-mm-dd. end-name endName string '' Range mode: form entry name of the end date. Without it the range submits as one name entry start/end. end-label endLabel string '' Range mode: label of the end field. min min string '' Earliest selectable date, ISO yyyy-mm-dd. max max string '' Latest selectable date, ISO yyyy-mm-dd. format format DateFormat 'dd/mm/yyyy' locale locale string '' Locale for names, labels and messages. Defaults to the nearest lang: the element's own, an ancestor's, then <html>'s, else the browser language. era era Era | '' '' Year era shown and typed: be (พ.ศ.) or ce (ค.ศ.). Defaults to be for Thai locales. first-day firstDay number 0 0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidDatePicker: each date box is a 64px box with its label inside. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. picker picker 'auto' | 'custom' | 'sheet' | 'native' 'auto' Which picker opens: auto (default) = our calendar, in a bottom sheet on a phone; custom = our calendar as a popover on every device; sheet = in a bottom sheet on every device; native = the OS date picker. clearable clearable boolean false Shows a clear button inside the field while it has text. show-today showToday boolean false Adds a \\"Today\\" button under the calendar. months months number 1 Months to show side by side in the calendar, 1 to 12 (default 1, e.g. 2 for range picking). page-by pageBy 'months' | 'single' 'months' With more than one month, ‹ › turn a whole page (months) or one month (single): the calendar's page-by. show-outside-days showOutsideDays boolean false Show the days of the months before and after (by default they are blank): the calendar's show-outside-days. show-week-numbers showWeekNumbers boolean false A column of ISO week numbers in the calendar: its show-week-numbers. weekday-format weekdayFormat 'narrow' | 'short' | '' '' Weekday headings narrow or short: the calendar's weekday-format. today today string '' The day the calendar marks as today, ISO (default the real today). size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Field height, same scale as ui-text-input. Property Type Description getDayParts (date: Date) => string | undefined Extra part names for a calendar day, e.g. holiday: the calendar's getDayParts; the picker exports each name it returns, so ui-date-picker::part(holiday) styles those days. isDateDisabled (date: Date) => boolean | string | undefined Property only. Return true for days that can't be chosen (weekends, holidays…), or a string to show that reason instead of the generic message. willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change onChange When a committed value (start or end) changes: blur, Enter, a calendar pick or clear. ui-range-start onUiRangeStart Detail { date }, range: a calendar pick began a range (its start), as Cally's rangestart; change waits for the end ui-range-end onUiRangeEnd Detail { date }, range: a calendar pick finished a range (its end), as Cally's rangeend A typed date outside min/max is still committed, with the field reporting the range error. Slot Description label Label content with markup; the label attribute is the plain-text fallback helper-text Helper text with markup (links, bold); overrides helper-text warn-text Warning text shown while warn; overrides warn-text invalid-text Error text shown while invalid; overrides invalid-text end-label Label of the end field in range mode; overrides end-label Part Description base The field box (range: also start-base / end-base; same for every field part) label The label input The text box clear-button The × button toggle The calendar icon (decorative, as Carbon) status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) calendar The popover shell (in the bottom sheet: the sheet's panel) sheet The bottom sheet <dialog> on a phone (picker=\\"auto\\" / sheet; style its scrim with ::part(sheet)::backdrop) sheet-grip The sheet's top bar, which a swipe down closes sheet-close The sheet's × button header Calendar month / year row nav Previous / next month buttons heading The month and year selects' row month-select The month select (<ui-calendar-select-month>'s select) year-select The year select (<ui-calendar-select-year>'s select) month-title A month's name over its grid when several show grid The table of days day Each day button (its state also: selected, today, outside, disabled, disallowed, range-start, range-end, in-range, and the names getDayParts returns) weeknumber A week-number cell (show-week-numbers) today-button The optional \\"Today\\" button Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-menu-radius / --ui-menu-border / --ui-menu-shadow - Corners, border and shadow of the calendar (the menu settings) --ui-sheet-radius The bottom sheet's top corners (default: the menu radius) --ui-modal-scrim The bottom sheet's scrim, as the modal's (default Carbon's overlay) --ui-calendar-day-radius Corner radius of a day (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-calendar-today-dot-radius Corner radius of today's dot (default 0, a square; Kanok: 50%, a dot) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled) --ui-fluid-background / --ui-fluid-gap - A fluid box's fill and the space under it (default the layer's fill, 0: boxes that touch; Kanok: transparent, 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of the month arrows' and Today's focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Date picker","<ui-calendar> · React UiCalendar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/date-picker/#ui-calendar-react-uicalendar","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' Chosen day (start day in range mode), ISO yyyy-mm-dd. end-value endValue string '' Range mode: chosen end day, ISO yyyy-mm-dd. range range boolean false Whether range selection is enabled. multi multi boolean false Multi-date selection mode: select multiple individual dates (like Cally's calendar-multi). values values string[] | string [] Selected dates in multi mode (array or comma/space-separated ISO string). months months number 1 Months on show side by side, 1 to 12 (default 1; 12 paged by the page is a calendar year, from January). page-by pageBy 'months' | 'single' 'months' With more than one month, ‹ › and the keys turn a whole page (months, the default) or one month (single), as Cally's page-by. show-outside-days showOutsideDays boolean false Show the days of the months before and after, in six weeks (Cally show-outside-days); by default they are blank and only the weeks the month needs show. Several months never show them. show-week-numbers showWeekNumbers boolean false A column of ISO week numbers before the weeks (Cally show-week-numbers). weekday-format weekdayFormat 'narrow' | 'short' | '' '' Weekday headings narrow (S / อา) or short (Sun / อา.); by default narrow in Thai, short otherwise (Cally format-weekday). today today string '' The day marked as today, ISO (default the real today): for tests, demos and another time zone (Cally today). active-field activeField 'start' | 'end' 'start' Range mode: which end a pick will set; drives the preview highlight. min min string '' Minimum selectable ISO date. max max string '' Maximum selectable ISO date. locale locale string '' BCP 47 locale for names and labels. Defaults to the nearest lang. era era Era | '' '' Year era: be (พ.ศ.) or ce (ค.ศ.). Defaults to be for Thai locales. first-day firstDay number 0 0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday. show-today showToday boolean false Whether to display the \\"Today\\" footer shortcut button. Property Type Description getDayParts (date: Date) => string | undefined Extra part names for a day, e.g. holiday (Cally getDayParts). focusDate Day that holds the roving tab stop; its month is shown. isDateDisabled (date: Date) => boolean | string | undefined Callback to disable individual dates (e.g. weekends, holidays). multiValues string[] (read-only) Selected dates as clean ISO array in multi mode. Method Description focusDay() Puts DOM focus on the day that holds the roving tab stop. tabStops() The calendar's Tab stops in order: ‹, its own month and year selects (not when heading is slotted), ›, the day that holds the tab stop and Today. focus(options) Focus on the day with the tab stop, or with { target: 'previous' | 'next' } on a month arrow (Cally's focus()). Event React Description ui-page-change onUiPageChange Detail { start, end }, the first and last day shown after the months on show changed (Cally pagechange) ui-multi-pick onUiMultiPick Detail { date, values }, in multi mode when a day is toggled change none (use a ref) Detail { value, endValue, values }, native-like change event on a pick (with range, once both ends are picked) ui-pick onUiPick Detail { date }, when a day is activated ui-focus-change onUiFocusChange Detail { date }, when keyboard or navigation moves the focused date ui-range-start onUiRangeStart Detail { date }, with range: the first end was picked (Cally rangestart) ui-range-end onUiRangeEnd Detail { date }, with range: the second end was picked (Cally rangeend) Slot Description previous Replaces the previous button's arrow icon next Replaces the next button's arrow icon heading Replaces the month and year selects; <ui-calendar-select-month> / <ui-calendar-select-year> put here follow the calendar Part Description months Multi-month layout container month-view Container of a single month month-title A month's name above its grid when two months show (the header then has the year only) header Month / year row container nav Previous / next navigation buttons prev-button The previous month button next-button The next month button heading The month and year selects' row (the heading slot) month-select The default heading's month select (<ui-calendar-select-month>'s select) year-select The default heading's year select (<ui-calendar-select-year>'s select) grid The table grid of days table The table grid of days thead The table header row with weekday labels th Individual weekday heading cell (also day-N, 0 = Sunday; the week-number heading also weeknumber) weeknumber A week-number cell (show-week-numbers) tbody The table body of weeks row Each week table row cell Each day table cell day Each day button; its state adds day-N (0 = Sunday), selected, today, outside (another month), disabled (before min / after max), disallowed (refused by isDateDisabled), range-start, range-end, in-range, and the names getDayParts returns today-button The optional \\"Today\\" footer button footer The footer container Custom property Default Description --ui-calendar-day-radius Corner radius of a day button (default 9999px for circular days) --ui-calendar-today-dot-radius Corner radius of today's indicator dot (default 50%) --ui-calendar-day-focus The keyboard focus ring on a day --ui-calendar-selected-focus Focus ring on a selected day"],["Time picker","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/","A time picker takes a time as short hh:mm text, with optional selects beside it for AM / PM and the time zone."],["Time picker","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Time picker","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#use-it",""],["Time picker","12-hour or 24-hour","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#12-hour-or-24-hour","By default the box takes 12-hour time, h:mm or hh:mm (9:30, 09:30, 12:45), and at most 5 characters. Carbon's own pattern rejects a leading zero; this one accepts it, so typing what the hh:mm placeholder shows works. For 24-hour time, set your own pattern and leave out the AM / PM select: maxlength (maxLength in React) changes the length limit; placeholder the hint."],["Time picker","Start with a value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#start-with-a-value","To edit a time that is already saved, set value on the picker and on each select. A select without value starts on its <option selected>, else its first option, as a native select does."],["Time picker","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default, as in Carbon), lg 48px. The selects take the picker's size. The prop has the same name in React and React + Tailwind."],["Time picker","Fluid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#fluid","fluid, or a fluid form around it (<ui-fluid-form>, FluidForm in React + Tailwind), gives Carbon's fluid time picker: the box and each select as equal 64px columns with their labels inside. The prop has the same name in React and React + Tailwind."],["Time picker","Outlined (Kanok design)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#outlined-kanok-design","In the Kanok design, fields are filled by default: a soft grey fill, no edge. Put data-field-variant=\\"outlined\\" on an element around the field (a <form>, or <html> for the whole app) for a 1px edge on no fill; focus is still the soft blue halo. The attribute does nothing in the Carbon design, so the example below sits inside data-design=\\"kanok\\". See Kanok design for the details."],["Time picker","Errors and warnings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#errors-and-warnings","The web component checks the text against pattern after the user leaves the box or tries to submit, and shows the error under it. invalid-text replaces the browser's own message (\\"Please match the requested format\\"). Set invalid for an error from your own validation, or warn with warn-text for a warning that doesn't block submit: React + Tailwind follows Carbon React: pattern still takes part in the form's validation, but no message shows by itself. Set invalid and invalidText when your check fails. More in Forms and validation."],["Time picker","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly keeps every value and submits it: the box can't be edited, and a select still takes focus but doesn't open or change. disabled disables the box and every select inside. The web component and its React wrapper spell it readonly; React + Tailwind uses readOnly."],["Time picker","What the form gets","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#what-the-form-gets","Each part submits on its own: the time box under its name and each select under its own name. The time is the text as typed (9:30 or 09:30), and the select values are your <option> values. Nothing is converted: the time zone select is a plain choice, with no time zone arithmetic behind it. required blocks the submit while the box is empty. save stands for your own code."],["Time picker","Events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#events","The web component fires input while typing and change on commit; each select fires change. In React the wrapper props are onInput / onChange; the Tailwind TimePicker passes onChange to its <input>, as React does."],["Time picker","Check a time against another","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#check-a-time-against-another","Your own rules, such as a closing time after the opening time, go through invalid and invalid-text: check on change and set them. Here both boxes take 24-hour time."],["Time picker","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#skeleton","While the page loads its data, show <ui-time-picker-skeleton> in the picker's place. Carbon has only the fluid time picker skeleton, so this is that one: the box, the AM / PM select and the time zone select. is-only-two (isOnlyTwo in React + Tailwind) draws two equal parts instead. It has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/time-picker-skeleton, and is hidden from screen readers."],["Time picker","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#keyboard","Key Does Enter (in the time box) Submits the form it's in, as a native input does ↑ / ↓, Space (on a select) The browser's own select keys; ignored while read-only"],["Time picker","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#accessibility","The box is a native text input with a <label>; the selects are native <select> elements. Name each select with label. Without one, the web component and React + Tailwind fall back to \\"Open list of options\\", as Carbon does. An error sets aria-invalid on the box and is linked to it with aria-describedby. A read-only select has aria-readonly. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Time picker."],["Time picker","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Time picker","<ui-time-picker> · React UiTimePicker","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#ui-time-picker-react-uitimepicker","Attribute Property Type Default Description max-length Deprecated: use maxlength label label string '' hide-label hideLabel boolean false value value string '' name name string '' placeholder placeholder string 'hh:mm' pattern pattern String.raw\`(1[012]|0?[1-9]):[0-5][0-9](\\\\s)?\` 12-hour time with an optional trailing space. Carbon's default rejects a leading zero, so \\"09:30\\" typed as the hh:mm placeholder shows would fail; this one accepts \\"9:30\\" and \\"09:30\\". maxlength maxLength number 5 Like <input maxlength> (Carbon maxLength); the max-length attribute of 0.8 and earlier is still read. size size TimePickerSize 'md' disabled disabled boolean false readonly readonly boolean false fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidTimePicker: equal 64px columns with labels inside, an error / warning inside the box. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. required required boolean false invalid invalid boolean false invalid-text invalidText string '' warn warn boolean false warn-text warnText string '' Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change onChange Slot Description (default) <ui-time-picker-select> elements label Rich label invalid-text Rich error text warn-text Rich warning text Part Description label The label base Row with the input and the selects input The text input error-text Error text invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) warning-text Warning text warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled)"],["Time picker","<ui-time-picker-select> · React UiTimePickerSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/time-picker/#ui-time-picker-select-react-uitimepickerselect","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Accessible name of the select (Carbon default \\"open list of options\\"). value value string '' name name string '' size size TimePickerSize 'md' disabled disabled boolean false readonly readonly boolean false Property Type Description pickerDisabled boolean Set by the surrounding <ui-time-picker> when it is disabled. willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Event React Description change onChange When the user picks an option Slot Description (default) <option> elements Part Description input The native select Custom property Default Description --ui-field-readonly-background The box's fill when read-only (default transparent; Kanok: a faint ink tint, so read-only reads as set and never weaker than disabled)"],["Slider","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/","A slider picks a number, or a range between two numbers, from a scale. A number box beside the track lets users type the exact value."],["Slider","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Slider","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#use-it","The web component fires input while the value moves (dragging, keys, typing) and change when it is committed: the pointer released, a key handled, the number box left. In React those are onInput / onChange on UiSlider. The Tailwind Slider calls onChange(value) on every change and onRelease(value) on commits."],["Slider","Scale and step","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#scale-and-step","min and max set the ends (0 and 100 by default) and step the increment (1). Arrow keys move one step; with Shift they move step-multiplier steps (4 by default). min-label and max-label add a unit after the end numbers."],["Slider","Format the labels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#format-the-labels","For more control, the formatLabel property (a function (value, label) => string) formats the end labels and the value screen readers hear. It is a property on the web component and a prop in both React versions. With hide-text-input, the tooltip on the thumb uses it too, so money reads as money."],["Slider","Two handles: a range","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#two-handles-a-range","Set value-upper and the slider picks a range from value to value-upper. The two thumbs never pass each other, a press on the track moves the nearer one, and each has its own number box: the lower one before the track, the upper one after. The form gets both values: under name-upper for the upper one, or both under name when you leave name-upper out. The thumbs are named \\"Lower bound\\" and \\"Upper bound\\" after the slider's label; input-label and upper-input-label rename the number boxes."],["Slider","The number box","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#the-number-box","The box mirrors the value, and typing changes it: A number in range applies at once, snapped to the nearest step. On blur or Enter, a number outside min / max is clamped to the nearest end. Screen readers hear that it was corrected (corrected-text changes the words; {value} is the typed number). A box that holds no number (cleared, say) shows the error \\"Enter a number\\" and blocks submit until it is fixed. hide-text-input removes the box and shows the value in a tooltip on the thumb instead:"],["Slider","Errors and warnings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#errors-and-warnings","invalid with invalid-text shows an error from your own validation and blocks submit; warn with warn-text shows a warning that doesn't. The slider has no helper line. How errors show across fields: Forms and validation."],["Slider","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#read-only-and-disabled","readonly keeps the value and submits it; the thumb can't be moved and the number box can't be edited. A read-only thumb leaves the Tab order unless the box is hidden, so users still reach the value. disabled greys everything out and nothing is submitted. The web component and its React wrapper spell it readonly; React + Tailwind uses readOnly."],["Slider","Show the value as it moves","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#show-the-value-as-it-moves","Use input to update what depends on the value while the thumb moves, and change to save once it settles. In React + Tailwind those are onChange and onRelease. save stands for your own code."],["Slider","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#in-a-form","With a name, the slider submits its value with the form; a range also submits name-upper. Form reset puts the thumbs back where they started."],["Slider","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#skeleton","While the page loads its data, show <ui-slider-skeleton> in the slider's place, as Carbon's SliderSkeleton. two-handles (twoHandles in React + Tailwind) draws a range and hide-label leaves out the label bar. It has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/slider-skeleton, and is hidden from screen readers."],["Slider","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#keyboard","On a thumb: Key Does ← / ↓ One step down → / ↑ One step up Shift + arrow step-multiplier steps (4 by default) Home / End To min / max (in a range, as far as the other thumb allows) In the number box, Enter commits the typed number."],["Slider","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#accessibility","Each thumb is a role=\\"slider\\" with aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax, aria-valuenow and aria-valuetext, named by the label. In a range each thumb's bounds stop at the other thumb. A click on the label focuses the thumb, as a label focuses a native range input. The number box is a native number input with its own name (\\"Slider number input\\", or \\"Lower bound\\" / \\"Upper bound\\"; input-label and upper-input-label change them). An error sets aria-invalid and is linked with aria-describedby. A clamped number is announced in a polite live region. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Slider."],["Slider","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Slider","<ui-slider> · React UiSlider","/kanok-ui-docs/en/slider/#ui-slider-react-uislider","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' hide-label hideLabel boolean false value value number 0 value-upper valueUpper number | null null A second thumb: the slider picks the range value…value-upper (Carbon unstable_valueUpper). name-upper nameUpper string '' The name the upper value is submitted under (default: name, so the form gets both under one name). upper-input-label upperInputLabel string '' Accessible name of the upper number box (Carbon unstable_ariaLabelInputUpper; default \\"Upper bound\\"). min min number 0 max max number 100 step step number 1 step-multiplier stepMultiplier number 4 Shift + arrow moves by step × step-multiplier. min-label minLabel string '' Appended to the min / max numbers, e.g. \\"%\\" (Carbon minLabel / maxLabel). max-label maxLabel string '' input-label inputLabel string '' Accessible name of the number input (Carbon ariaLabelInput). hide-text-input hideTextInput boolean false name name string '' disabled disabled boolean false readonly readonly boolean false required required boolean false invalid invalid boolean false invalid-text invalidText string '' warn warn boolean false warn-text warnText string '' corrected-text correctedText string '' Announcement after an out-of-range number is clamped; {value} is the typed number (Carbon auto-correct message). Property Type Description formatLabel SliderFormatLabel Formats min / max labels and the value tooltip (Carbon formatLabel). willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. isRange (read-only) Two thumbs (value-upper set). Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. focus(options) Focus the handle. Event React Description input onInput change onChange Slot Description label Rich label (overrides label) invalid-text Rich error text warn-text Rich warning text Part Description label The label base Row with labels, track and input min-label Minimum label max-label Maximum label track The 2px track filled-track The filled part thumb The handle (role=slider) thumb-lower With value-upper: the lower handle (also thumb) thumb-upper With value-upper: the upper handle (also thumb) input The number input input-lower With value-upper: the lower bound's input (also input) input-upper With value-upper: the upper bound's input (also input) error-text Error text below invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) warning-text Warning text below warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-field-border / --ui-field-radius / --ui-field-background - The number box, as the other fields --ui-slider-fill The thumb, the filled track and the range handles (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: --ui-interactive) --ui-slider-handle-hover A range handle under the pointer (default --ui-ink-muted) --ui-slider-tick display of the mark at the middle of the track (default inline-block; Kanok: none) --ui-slider-range-handle-width / --ui-slider-range-handle-height / --ui-slider-range-lower-offset / --ui-slider-range-upper-offset - A range's handle box and where it sits on its value (default 16 × 24px, beside the value: Carbon's flags) --ui-slider-range-thumb / --ui-slider-range-thumb-hover / --ui-slider-range-thumb-inset / --ui-slider-range-thumb-radius / --ui-slider-range-focus-ring - A range thumb drawn in the handle (default none: the flag icons only; Kanok: a round dot) --ui-slider-range-gap / --ui-slider-range-icon-opacity - The gap where a flag meets the track and the flags' opacity (default the page colour, 1)"],["File uploader","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/","A file uploader lets people pick files from their device, with a button or by dropping them on a drop zone. The chosen files are listed under it, each with its state: ready, uploading, uploaded, or an error."],["File uploader","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["File uploader","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#use-it","Each file in the list is a FileItem: uuid, name, the File itself, and its status, invalid, errorSubject, errorBody, progress and retryable. The element fires ui-add right after a pick (refused files included), before files updates (as Carbon's onAddFiles), ui-change with addedFiles, removedFiles, currentFiles and action (add, remove or clear), and ui-delete when the user removes a file. In React these are onUiAdd, onUiChange and onUiDelete; in React + Tailwind, onAdd, onChange and onDelete. Without multiple, a new pick replaces the list."],["File uploader","Button or drop zone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#button-or-drop-zone","The default is Carbon's \\"Add file\\" button. drop shows the dashed drop zone instead (Carbon's FileUploaderDropContainer): people can drop files on it, or click it to open the file dialog. Folders dropped on it are skipped. button-label changes the button text, and button-kind its kind (primary by default). After a pick the button shows the file name, or \\"3 files\\"; keep-label keeps your text. drop-label changes the drop zone text. size (sm, md, lg) sizes the button and the rows."],["File uploader","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#sizes","size sets the height of the button and of every row: sm, md (the default) or lg. A row on its own takes size too."],["File uploader","Limit the files","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#limit-the-files","accept lists the file types: extensions and MIME types, comma-separated (.pdf,.jpg,image/png). max-file-size is the largest size of one file, in bytes (5 MB = 5000000). max-files is the most files in the list, and max-total-size the most bytes they may add up to. These two go beyond Carbon. A refused file still shows in the list, marked as an error with the reason, so people see what went wrong. It isn't submitted with the form, and the user removes it with ×. Set the error titles with invalid-type-text, too-large-text, too-many-text and total-too-large-text, and the line under them with invalid-body-text. The built-in texts are translated (\\"File type not supported\\", \\"File is too large\\", \\"Too many files\\"…). show-size shows each file's size in its row (\\"1.2 MB\\", in the page language). accept also filters the file dialog, but a dropped file is checked too."],["File uploader","File states","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#file-states","Each row shows one of these. A row also works on its own, for files that are already on the server; it fires ui-delete and ui-retry, and removing it from the page is up to you. edit: ready, with × to remove it. uploading: a spinner, or with progress the percentage, a bar and × to cancel. complete: a check mark; it can't be removed. invalid: a red outline with error-subject and error-body. Add retryable for an upload that failed: a retry button appears, and the title is \\"Upload failed\\" unless you set one. Refused files aren't retryable."],["File uploader","Files already on the server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#files-already-on-the-server","When a record already has files, put them in the uploader as <ui-file-uploader-item> children (FileUploaderItem in React + Tailwind). They show after the picked files. Their × fires ui-delete on the row itself: remove the row and the file on the server. The event passes through the uploader as it is, so listen on the row, not for the uploader's own ui-delete. saved and removeSaved stand for your own data and code."],["File uploader","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#disabled","disabled turns off the button or drop zone and every listed row, for example when a request is closed. A row on its own takes disabled too."],["File uploader","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#in-a-form","With a name, every valid file is submitted under that name, like <input type=\\"file\\" multiple>. Refused files are left out. required blocks the submit until there is at least one valid file; change the message with required-text. More in Forms and validation. A form reset empties the list. disabled, or a disabled fieldset, turns everything off. send stands for your own code."],["File uploader","Read the chosen files","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#read-the-chosen-files","ui-change tells you what changed (action) and gives the whole list (currentFiles), so it is the one event to keep your state in step with. Pick a few files below, then remove one."],["File uploader","Upload the files","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#upload-the-files","The uploader doesn't upload by itself: it lists the files and you send them. Update the list as each upload moves on: replace files with a new array, and each row follows its item's status. uploading shows a spinner. With a progress (0–100) it shows the percentage and a small bar instead, and × cancels the upload: the file is removed and ui-delete tells you to stop sending it. complete shows a check mark, and screen readers hear \\"Uploaded: contract.pdf\\". status on the uploader sets the state new files start in (edit by default, with ×). Pick some files below: each one uploads at once. The upload here is a stand-in that moves on a timer, and a file with \\"fail\\" in its name fails halfway, so you can retry it."],["File uploader","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#skeleton","While the page loads its data, show <ui-file-uploader-skeleton> in the uploader's place, as Carbon's FileUploaderSkeleton: bars for the title, the description and the button. It has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/file-uploader-skeleton, and is hidden from screen readers."],["File uploader","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#keyboard","Key What it does Enter or Space on the button or the drop zone Opens the file dialog Enter or Space on × Removes the file, or cancels its upload; focus moves to the next file's ×, else the previous one's, else the button Enter or Space on the retry button Fires ui-retry"],["File uploader","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#accessibility","The uploader is a group named by label-title, and the hidden file input is labelled by it too. The × and retry buttons are named with the file: \\"Remove file - contract.pdf\\", \\"Retry upload - contract.pdf\\". An error is an alert, read as soon as it appears. A finished upload is announced, since a spinner turning into a check mark is silent. The progress bar is a progressbar screen readers can query; the percentage isn't read on every change. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless File uploader."],["File uploader","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["File uploader","<ui-file-uploader> · React UiFileUploader","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#ui-file-uploader-react-uifileuploader","Attribute Property Type Default Description label-title labelTitle string '' label-description labelDescription string '' button-label buttonLabel string '' Button text; replaced by the file name / \\"N files\\" after a pick unless keep-label. button-kind buttonKind ButtonKind 'primary' size size FileUploaderSize 'md' Button and item sizes. drop drop boolean false Render the dashed drop zone instead of the button (Carbon FileUploaderDropContainer). drop-label dropLabel string '' accept accept string '' Comma-separated extensions / MIME types, e.g. \\".pdf,.jpg,image/png\\". multiple multiple boolean false max-file-size maxFileSize number 0 Bytes; larger files are added as invalid. max-files maxFiles number 0 Most valid files in the list; the ones past it are added as invalid (0 = no limit). max-total-size maxTotalSize number 0 Bytes the valid files may add up to; a file that would go over is added as invalid (0 = no limit). show-size showSize boolean false Show each file's size in its row (\\"1.2 MB\\", in the page language). name name string '' disabled disabled boolean false status status FileStatus 'edit' Status new items start in (Carbon filenameStatus). icon-label iconLabel string '' keep-label keepLabel boolean false required required boolean false At least one valid file must be chosen before the form submits. required-text requiredText string '' Validation message for required; defaults to the translation. invalid-type-text invalidTypeText string '' too-large-text tooLargeText string '' too-many-text tooManyText string '' total-too-large-text totalTooLargeText string '' invalid-body-text invalidBodyText string '' Property Type Description files FileItem[] The current list; replace it (new array) to update statuses or errors. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid until cleared with ''. browse() Open the file dialog. addFiles(files) Add files as if the user picked them. Event React Description ui-add onUiAdd detail: { addedFiles } right after the user picks files (invalid ones included) ui-delete onUiDelete detail: { deletedFile, remainingFiles } ui-change onUiChange detail: { addedFiles, removedFiles, currentFiles, action } change none (use a ref) Native-style, alongside ui-change ui-retry onUiRetry detail: { retriedFile } when the user retries a failed upload Slot Description (default) Extra <ui-file-uploader-item>s (e.g. files already on the server) Part Description title Label title description Label description trigger The button or drop zone drop-icon The drop zone's upload icon (hidden unless a design shows it) items The file list Custom property Default Description --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the drop zone (the field setting); --ui-file-drop-radius overrides it (Kanok: 12px) --ui-file-uploader-max-width Widest the drop zone and the file rows get (default Carbon's 320px; Kanok: none) --ui-file-drop-direction The drop zone's layout: flex-direction (default row), --ui-file-drop-align / -justify / -text-align / -gap (default flex-start, space-between, start, 0; Kanok: a centred column, 12px apart) --ui-file-drop-height block-size of the drop zone (default Carbon's 96px; Kanok: auto), --ui-file-drop-min-height (Kanok: 136px), --ui-file-drop-padding (default 16px; Kanok: 24px) --ui-file-drop-background Fill of the drop zone (default transparent; Kanok: the fields' fill); --ui-file-drop-hover-background while hovered or dragged over (Kanok: --ui-highlight) --ui-file-drop-hover-border-color Its dashed line while hovered or dragged over (default unchanged; Kanok: --ui-primary); --ui-file-drop-hover-outline the outline then (default --ui-focus; Kanok: transparent), --ui-file-drop-hover-decoration the text (default underline; Kanok: none) --ui-file-drop-icon-display The upload icon (default none; Kanok: grid, a 40px circle: --ui-file-drop-icon-background its fill, --ui-file-drop-icon-color the icon)"],["File uploader","<ui-file-uploader-item> · React UiFileUploaderItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/file-uploader/#ui-file-uploader-item-react-uifileuploaderitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description name name string '' uuid uuid string '' Identifies the file in ui-delete; defaults to name. status status FileStatus 'edit' invalid invalid boolean false error-subject errorSubject string '' error-body errorBody string '' size size FileUploaderSize 'md' disabled disabled boolean false icon-label iconLabel string '' Describes the state icon / remove button: \\"Remove file\\", \\"Uploading\\", \\"Uploaded\\" (Carbon iconDescription); with progress, the bar. progress progress number | undefined Upload progress 0–100, shown while status is uploading (percentage, bar, cancel button) instead of the spinner. retryable retryable boolean false On an invalid row: a retry button (ui-retry) for a failed upload. file-size fileSize number | undefined Bytes; shows the size in the row (\\"1.2 MB\\"). Property Type Description removable (read-only) The row has a remove button (edit, or uploading with progress) and isn't disabled. Method Description requestDelete() Ask the owner to remove this file (fires ui-delete). requestRetry() Ask the owner to upload this file again (fires ui-retry). Event React Description ui-delete onUiDelete detail: { uuid, name } when the user removes the file ui-retry onUiRetry detail: { uuid, name } when the user retries a failed upload Part Description base The row name File name size The file size (file-size) percent The upload percentage (progress) progress The <ui-progress-bar> under the row (progress) retry-button The retry button (retryable invalid row) delete-button The × button (edit status, or uploading with progress) error The error block (invalid) Custom property Default Description --ui-file-item-radius Corners of the row (default 0; Kanok: 6px); --ui-file-item-edge its box-shadow edge (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Modal","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/","A modal asks for the user's full attention: it opens over the page, the page behind it can't be used, and focus stays inside until it closes. Use it for a short task or a decision. For a long form or a flow with steps, use a Tearsheet; for details beside the page, a Side panel."],["Modal","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Modal","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#use-it","It is built on the native <dialog>: the browser puts it in the top layer, makes the page behind it inert and keeps Tab inside. Open it with the open attribute, show() or open = true; close it with close() or open = false. ui-close fires after it has closed, however that happened. The page doesn't scroll while it is open. React + Tailwind is controlled: onClose(reason) reports ×, Esc, an outside click or a <form method=\\"dialog\\"> inside; set open to false to close it, or leave it to keep it open."],["Modal","Passive modal","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#passive-modal","A modal with no footer buttons only shows information. It closes with ×, Esc or a click outside it."],["Modal","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#sizes","size: sm 480px, md 672px (the default), lg 1056px. It is never wider than the screen minus 16px a side, and never taller than 768px."],["Modal","Danger: confirm before you delete","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#danger-confirm-before-you-delete","alert is for a confirmation that interrupts, such as deleting something. The dialog gets role=\\"alertdialog\\", the body becomes its description, and focus starts on the safest footer button (the first one whose kind is neither primary nor a danger kind), so Enter doesn't delete by accident."],["Modal","A click outside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#a-click-outside","As in Carbon, a modal with footer buttons never closes on a click outside it, so nothing typed is lost. A passive modal does, unless it is persistent: then only ×, Esc or your own button close it."],["Modal","A form in a modal","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#a-form-in-a-modal","On open, focus goes to the first control in the body; with none, to the first footer button; else to ×. Put autofocus on another control to start there. The footer buttons sit outside your <form>, so the primary one calls requestSubmit(): the browser then checks the required fields first. Enter in a field submits too. In React + Tailwind the footer buttons are native <button>s, so form=\\"signer-form\\" connects the submit button to the form."],["Modal","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#ask-before-closing","×, Esc and a click outside first fire ui-request-close, cancelable, with the reason: close-button, escape or backdrop. Call preventDefault() to keep the modal open, for example while there are unsaved changes. Type a note below, then try to close the modal. ui-request-close and ui-close bubble, and a notification inside the modal fires them too: check that event.target is the modal. React's UiModal does that for you: onUiRequestClose and onUiClose get only the modal's own events. close() and open = false close without asking; requestClose(reason) asks first, as × does. Give feedback inside a modal with an inline Notification, as here: a toast would sit behind the inert page."],["Modal","Scrolling content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#scrolling-content","When the body is taller than the modal, only the body scrolls; the heading and the footer stay. The body then becomes a focusable region named by the heading, so keyboard users can scroll it."],["Modal","Header actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#header-actions","The header-actions slot puts controls at the top end of the header, beside ×. One 48px button fits. React + Tailwind takes them in headerActions."],["Modal","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#keyboard","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the controls inside the modal only Esc Asks to close (escape); focus goes back to what opened it Enter, Space Press the focused button"],["Modal","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#accessibility","The native modal <dialog> makes the rest of the page inert for the mouse, the keyboard and screen readers, and gives focus back to the control that opened it. The heading names the dialog. With no heading, the label slot names it; with neither, set label (React + Tailwind: aria-label). alert makes it an alertdialog described by its body; use it for confirmations only. The × button is named \\"Close\\" in the page language; close-label (closeLabel) changes it. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Modal."],["Modal","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Modal","<ui-modal> · React UiModal","/kanok-ui-docs/en/modal/#ui-modal-react-uimodal","Attribute Property Type Default Description open open boolean false heading heading string '' label label string '' Accessible name when there is no heading (Carbon aria-label); the label slot is used before it. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Dialog width (Carbon modal sizes): sm 480px, md 672px, lg 1056px — never wider than the viewport minus 16px a side. persistent persistent boolean false A passive modal (no footer) ignores outside clicks too; one with footer buttons always does (Carbon). close-label closeLabel string '' Accessible name for the close button. alert alert boolean false Interrupting confirmation: role=\\"alertdialog\\", focus starts on the safest action. Method Description requestClose(reason) Ask to close — fires cancelable ui-request-close first. focus(options) Focus inside the open dialog (the least destructive control, as on open). Event React Description ui-close onUiClose After the modal has closed ui-request-close onUiRequestClose Cancelable; detail: { reason }. preventDefault() keeps it open. Slot Description (default) Body content label Small label above the heading (the row renders only when slotted) footer Action buttons (laid out full-bleed, Carbon style) header-actions Controls at the top end of the header, beside the close button (one 48px button fits) Part Description dialog The native <dialog> panel header Header row header-actions Wrapper of the header-actions slot label The small label above the heading heading The heading close-button The × button body Scrollable body footer Footer holding the action buttons Custom property Default Description --ui-modal-radius Corner radius (default 0; Kanok: 12px) --ui-modal-shadow box-shadow of the box (default none) --ui-modal-scrim The overlay behind the box (default rgb(22 22 22 / 0.5)) --ui-overlay-background The box's surface, shared by every floating surface (default layer 1) --ui-overlay-border The box's border, shared by modal, side panel and tearsheet (default none) --ui-modal-footer-gap Gap between footer buttons (default none: they touch) --ui-modal-footer-height Footer min-height (default 64px) --ui-modal-footer-padding Footer padding (default 0: full-bleed buttons) --ui-modal-footer-border Border above the footer (default none) --ui-modal-button-flex flex of each footer button (default 0 1 50%: halves) --ui-modal-button-height Height of the footer buttons (default 64px) --ui-modal-button-align align-items of their content (default flex-start: text at the top) --ui-modal-button-padding-top Their top padding (default 14px) --ui-close-size Size of the × button (default 48px; Kanok: 32px) --ui-close-inset Margin that sets the × in from the corner (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of the ×, its hover fill and its ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of the ×'s focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside) --ui-modal-body-focus-radius Corners of the scrolling body's focus ring (default 0; Kanok: 6px)"],["Side panel","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/","A side panel slides in from the edge of the screen, under the 48px UI shell header, to show details or a short form while the page stays in view. It is Carbon for IBM Products' SidePanel. For a task that needs the whole screen, use a Tearsheet; for a short decision, a Modal. The panel is position: fixed. The live examples below sit in a box that holds it, with --ui-side-panel-top: 0px because the box has no header above it."],["Side panel","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Side panel","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#use-it","Set open to show it and back to false to hide it; it slides 320px in from its edge while fading in, and out the same way (150ms each, as Carbon), with no movement when the reader asks for reduced motion. heading is also the panel's accessible name. On open, focus goes to selector-initial-focus (a selector inside the panel), else to the first control. On close it goes back to what had it. ×, Esc and a click on the overlay ask to close first (see Ask before closing); ui-close fires after the panel has slid out. React + Tailwind is controlled: onRequestClose(reason) reports them, and you set open to false."],["Side panel","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#sizes","size: xs 16rem, sm 20rem, md 30rem (the default), lg 40rem, xl 65rem, 2xl 80rem. From medium screens up a panel is never wider than 75% of the screen, and never wider than its container."],["Side panel","From the left","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#from-the-left","placement=\\"left\\" slides the panel in from the start edge instead of the end."],["Side panel","Dim the page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#dim-the-page","include-overlay dims the page behind the panel and stops it scrolling. A click on the overlay asks to close (overlay), unless prevent-close-on-click-outside is set."],["Side panel","Push the page aside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#push-the-page-aside","slide-in makes room for the panel instead of covering the page: the element that selector-page-content points to gets a margin as wide as the panel. A slide-in panel doesn't take focus, keep Tab inside or close on Esc, so the page stays usable beside it."],["Side panel","Action buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#action-buttons","Up to four <ui-button slot=\\"actions\\"> sit at the foot of the panel, laid out as Carbon's ActionSet for the panel's size: side by side, or one per row in an xs or sm panel and in an md panel with more than two. They are 64px tall; condensed-actions makes them 48px. React + Tailwind takes them as data in actions."],["Side panel","Toolbar under the header","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#toolbar-under-the-header","slot=\\"action-toolbar\\" puts small buttons under the header: the first one with its label, the rest as icon buttons. React + Tailwind takes them in actionToolbar."],["Side panel","Heading that shrinks on scroll","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#heading-that-shrinks-on-scroll","With a label-text, a subtitle or a toolbar, and enough content to scroll, the label and subtitle fade as the content scrolls and the heading shrinks into a compact bar (Carbon's default). animate-title=\\"false\\" keeps the header still; reduced motion turns it off too. Scroll the panel below."],["Side panel","Steps","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#steps","A panel can hold a short flow. current-step above 0 shows a back button at the top; pressing it fires ui-navigate-back (React + Tailwind: onNavigationBack), and you change the step and the content. The content scrolls back to the top when the step changes. The back button is named \\"Back\\" in the page language; navigation-back-icon-description changes it."],["Side panel","Content above and below the title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#content-above-and-below-the-title","slot=\\"above-title\\" goes above the label and heading, slot=\\"below-title\\" under the subtitle: a status tag, a search field. React + Tailwind has neither: put the content at the start of the panel's children."],["Side panel","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#ask-before-closing","×, Esc and a click on the overlay fire ui-request-close, cancelable, with the reason: close-button, escape or overlay. Call preventDefault() to keep the panel open. requestClose(reason) asks the same way from your own button; setting open to false closes without asking. The panel below only closes with its Done button. ui-request-close and ui-close bubble, so a notification inside fires them on the panel too: check that event.target is the panel. React's UiSidePanel does that for you: onUiRequestClose and onUiClose get only the panel's own events. hide-close-button removes ×; then give the panel another way to close."],["Side panel","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#keyboard","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the panel's controls and wraps around inside it (not with slide-in) Esc Asks to close (escape; not with slide-in); focus goes back to what opened it"],["Side panel","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#accessibility","The panel is a complementary landmark named by its heading. × is named \\"Close\\" and the back button \\"Back\\", in the page language, with a tooltip; close-icon-description and navigation-back-icon-description change them. A slide-over panel keeps Tab inside, but the page behind it is not inert: screen reader users can still reach it with their reading keys. Use a Modal when the page must be out of reach. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Side panel."],["Side panel","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Side panel","<ui-side-panel> · React UiSidePanel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/side-panel/#ui-side-panel-react-uisidepanel","Attribute Property Type Default Description open open boolean false placement placement 'right' | 'left' 'right' size size SidePanelSize 'md' xs 16rem, sm 20rem, md 30rem, lg 40rem, xl 65rem, 2xl 80rem. heading heading string '' The heading (Carbon title); also the panel's accessible name. label-text labelText string '' A small label above the heading. slide-in slideIn boolean false Push the page aside (selector-page-content) instead of covering it; no focus trap, no Esc. include-overlay includeOverlay boolean false Dim the page; a click on it closes the panel (unless prevent-close-on-click-outside). prevent-close-on-click-outside preventCloseOnClickOutside boolean false selector-initial-focus selectorInitialFocus string '' What takes focus on open (a selector in the content), else the first control. selector-page-content selectorPageContent string '' The page element a slide-in panel pushes aside. hide-close-button hideCloseButton boolean false close-icon-description closeIconDescription string '' The × button's name and tooltip (default \\"Close\\", translated). close-icon-tooltip-alignment closeIconTooltipAlignment Placement 'left' navigation-back-icon-description navigationBackIconDescription string '' The back button's name and tooltip (default \\"Back\\", translated). current-step currentStep number 0 Above 0 shows the back button (a panel with steps). condensed-actions condensedActions boolean false 48px action buttons instead of 64px. animate-title animateTitle boolean true Shrink the heading as the content scrolls (Carbon's default). Method Description requestClose(reason) Asks to close (cancelable ui-request-close), then closes. Event React Description ui-close onUiClose After it closed ui-navigate-back onUiNavigateBack The back button (current-step > 0) was pressed ui-request-close onUiRequestClose Cancelable; detail: { reason: 'escape' | 'close-button' | 'overlay' } Slot Description (default) The content subtitle Text under the heading above-title Content above the label and heading below-title Content under the subtitle action-toolbar Small buttons under the header (the first one with its label) actions The action buttons Part Description panel The panel overlay The overlay of include-overlay header The header heading The heading body The content's box actions The row of action buttons Custom property Default Description --ui-side-panel-top Where the panel starts (default 3rem, under the UI shell header) --ui-side-panel-radius Corner radius of the edge facing the page (default 0; Kanok: 12px) --ui-actions-gap / --ui-actions-padding - Gap between the action buttons and padding round them (default none: full-bleed buttons that touch; Kanok: 8px / 16px 20px) --ui-actions-button-flex flex of each action button (default: Carbon's widths by count; Kanok: their own width) --ui-actions-button-align / --ui-actions-button-padding-top - Where a button's label sits (default: at the top, 16px in) --ui-actions-stacked-direction / --ui-actions-stacked-wrap / --ui-actions-stacked-width - Where Carbon stacks the actions (narrow): flex-direction, flex-wrap and each button's width (default column-reverse, nowrap, 100%; Kanok: one row that wraps)"],["Tearsheet","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/","A tearsheet is a large modal that rises from the bottom of the screen over the dimmed page. Use it for a task that needs room but keeps the user in the same place: creating a record, a form in several sections, a review with a side pane. It is Carbon for IBM Products' Tearsheet. For a short decision, use a Modal; to keep the page in view, a Side panel."],["Tearsheet","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tearsheet","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#use-it","Set open to show it and back to false to hide it. It is a native modal <dialog>: the page behind is inert and doesn't scroll, and Tab stays inside the sheet. On open, focus goes to selector-initial-focus (a selector inside the sheet), else to ×, else to the first control; on close it goes back to what had it. ui-close fires after the sheet has sunk back. The content has no padding of its own: put your own around it, as in these examples. React + Tailwind is controlled: onRequestClose(reason) reports ×, Esc and a click outside, and you set open to false."],["Tearsheet","Narrow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#narrow","width=\\"narrow\\" (the default) is Carbon's small modal width: 60%, 42% or 36% of the screen from medium, large and extra-large screens up. It starts 130px from the top; vertical-position=\\"normal\\" moves it up to 90px, as a wide one. The heading is a size smaller, and the content sits on the layer instead of the background. React + Tailwind also has TearsheetNarrow."],["Tearsheet","Header actions and tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#header-actions-and-tabs","A wide tearsheet can carry small buttons in the header (slot=\\"header-actions\\") and tabs under the header text (slot=\\"header-navigation\\"). Switch the content yourself on the tabs' ui-tab-change. React + Tailwind takes them in headerActions and navigation. Both slots show only in a wide tearsheet."],["Tearsheet","A side pane","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#a-side-pane","slot=\\"influencer\\" adds a pane beside the content of a wide tearsheet: a summary, the steps of a flow, a preview. It sits on the right; influencer-placement=\\"left\\" moves it. influencer-width is narrow (256px, the default) or wide (320px). It scrolls on its own. React + Tailwind calls the placement influencerPosition."],["Tearsheet","Actions and the close button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#actions-and-the-close-button","Up to four <ui-button slot=\\"actions\\"> sit at the foot, laid out as Carbon's ActionSet (64px tall; 80px in a wide tearsheet); any more are hidden. With actions, there is no × unless you set has-close-icon. With no actions, × always shows, so a sheet that only shows information still closes. × is named \\"Close\\" in the page language; close-icon-description changes it."],["Tearsheet","Rich label and description","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#rich-label-and-description","label and description take plain text. For markup, use slot=\\"label\\" and slot=\\"description\\" instead, for example a link in the description."],["Tearsheet","Stacked tearsheets","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#stacked-tearsheets","A tearsheet can open another one over it. The one underneath scales back (to 95%, then 90%) and the page dims less, up to three deep. Each closes on its own, newest first."],["Tearsheet","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#ask-before-closing","×, Esc and a click outside the sheet fire ui-request-close, cancelable, with the reason: close-button, escape or outside. Call preventDefault() to keep it open. prevent-close-on-click-outside turns the outside click off altogether, which suits a form people type into. Type something below, then press Esc. ui-request-close and ui-close bubble, so a notification inside fires them on the tearsheet too: check that event.target is the tearsheet. React's UiTearsheet does that for you: onUiRequestClose and onUiClose get only the tearsheet's own events. requestClose(reason) asks from your own button; setting open to false closes without asking."],["Tearsheet","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#keyboard","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the sheet's controls and wraps around inside it Esc Asks to close (escape); focus goes back to what opened it"],["Tearsheet","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#accessibility","It is a native modal <dialog>, named by its heading: the page behind it is inert for the mouse, the keyboard and screen readers. Give every tearsheet a heading; without one the dialog has no name. × is named \\"Close\\" in the page language; close-icon-description changes it. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Tearsheet."],["Tearsheet","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tearsheet","<ui-tearsheet> · React UiTearsheet","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tearsheet/#ui-tearsheet-react-uitearsheet","Attribute Property Type Default Description open open boolean false width width 'narrow' | 'wide' 'narrow' narrow: Carbon's small modal; wide: the whole screen but 64px each side. vertical-position verticalPosition 'normal' | 'lower' | undefined How far from the top the sheet starts: normal 90px, lower 130px (default lower for a narrow one). heading heading string '' label label string '' A small label above the heading. description description string '' influencer-placement influencerPlacement 'left' | 'right' 'right' influencer-width influencerWidth 'narrow' | 'wide' 'narrow' has-close-icon hasCloseIcon boolean false Show the × even with actions (it always shows without them). close-icon-description closeIconDescription string '' The ×'s name (default \\"Close\\", translated). prevent-close-on-click-outside preventCloseOnClickOutside boolean false selector-initial-focus selectorInitialFocus string '' What takes focus on open (a selector in the content), else × or the first control. Method Description placeInStack(position, depth) Called by the stack: this sheet's place among the open ones (position 1 = oldest) and how many show. requestClose(reason) Asks to close (cancelable ui-request-close), then closes. Event React Description ui-close onUiClose After it closed ui-request-close onUiRequestClose Cancelable; detail: { reason: 'escape' | 'close-button' | 'outside' } Slot Description (default) The content label Rich label (instead of label) description Rich description (instead of description), e.g. a <ui-truncated-text> header-actions Small buttons in the header (wide) header-navigation Tabs under the header text (wide) influencer A side pane beside the content (wide) actions Up to four action buttons Part Description dialog The full-screen dialog container The sheet header The header heading The heading close-button The × influencer The side pane content The content's box actions The row of action buttons Custom property Default Description --ui-tearsheet-radius Corner radius of the top corners (default 0; Kanok: 12px) --ui-actions-gap / --ui-actions-padding - Gap between the action buttons and padding round them (default none: full-bleed buttons that touch; Kanok: 8px / 16px 20px) --ui-actions-button-flex flex of each action button (default: Carbon's widths by count; Kanok: their own width) --ui-actions-button-align / --ui-actions-button-padding-top - Where a button's label sits (default: at the top, 16px in) --ui-actions-stacked-direction / --ui-actions-stacked-wrap / --ui-actions-stacked-width - Where Carbon stacks the actions (narrow): flex-direction, flex-wrap and each button's width (default column-reverse, nowrap, 100%; Kanok: one row that wraps) --ui-close-size Size of the × button (default 48px; Kanok: 32px) --ui-close-inset Margin that sets the × in from the corner (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of the ×, its hover fill and its ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of the ×'s focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Notification","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/","A notification tells the user about a change or a problem: a file that failed to upload, a draft that was restored, a policy that applies to the page. One element covers Carbon's inline, actionable, toast and callout notifications. For toasts that stack in the corner of the screen, see Toast."],["Notification","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Notification","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#use-it","heading is the bold title (title in React + Tailwind) and subtitle the text after it. The default kind is error, so always set it. An inline notification is 288px to 832px wide, depending on the screen."],["Notification","Kinds","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#kinds","kind sets the colour and the icon: error, success, info, info-square, warning and warning-alt."],["Notification","Low contrast","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#low-contrast","A notification is dark (the inverse surface) by default. low-contrast gives it a light tint of its kind with a thin border instead, which sits more quietly in a form."],["Notification","Links and other content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#links-and-other-content","When the title or subtitle needs markup, put it in slot=\\"title\\" or slot=\\"subtitle\\". Anything without a slot goes after the subtitle: a link, a short list. React + Tailwind takes markup in title and subtitle, and extra content as children."],["Notification","With an action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#with-an-action","action-label adds a button for one quick action, such as Undo or Retry (Carbon's actionable notification). Pressing it fires ui-action; it doesn't close the notification. An actionable notification becomes an alertdialog: when it appears, focus moves to the action button, Tab goes round its own controls, and Esc closes it while focus is inside it (as Carbon: an Esc meant for something else, such as a modal, leaves it open). Add no-autofocus when it is on the page from the start, as here, so it doesn't take focus from the page. close() closes it the way × does; it is described under Closing."],["Notification","Callout","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#callout","variant=\\"callout\\" is a static box of guidance that belongs to the page, not a message about something that just happened. It has no role, no close button and never takes focus. Its action button is described by the title."],["Notification","Toast look","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#toast-look","variant=\\"toast\\" is the 288px card with a shadow that Carbon uses for toasts: the text stacks, caption adds a small line (often the time), and the action becomes a tertiary button under the text. To show toasts in the corner of the screen and stack them, use the toaster: Toast."],["Notification","Close after a time","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#close-after-a-time","timeout closes the notification by itself after that many milliseconds (reason timeout). The countdown pauses while the pointer is over it or focus is inside it, and a notification with an action never closes by itself, so nobody loses a message they are reading. Hover the toast below to hold it. Setting open back to true shows it again and starts the countdown afresh."],["Notification","Full width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#full-width","full-width lets an inline notification or a callout fill its container instead of stopping at Carbon's widths: a banner across the top of a page or a card. A toast stays 288px."],["Notification","Closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#closing","×, Esc (on an actionable one) and the timeout fire ui-request-close, cancelable, with the reason: close-button, escape or timeout. Unless you call preventDefault(), the notification sets open to false (it stays in the page, hidden) and fires ui-close. If focus was inside it, focus goes back to where it was before. hide-close-button removes × when the message must stay until the problem is fixed. Without open, the React + Tailwind notification hides itself when it closes."],["Notification","Errors after a submit","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#errors-after-a-submit","A notification can sum up what blocks a form. It is a polite status by default; role=\\"alert\\" makes screen readers announce it at once, for an error the user must deal with now. Press Check below."],["Notification","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Reaches the content's links, the action button and × in order; in an actionable notification it goes round them Enter, Space Press the focused button Esc Closes an actionable notification while focus is inside it (close-on-escape=\\"false\\" turns it off)"],["Notification","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#accessibility","The role is status by default (announced politely), none for a callout, and alertdialog with an action, named by the title and described by the subtitle. role sets another, such as alert. Screen readers announce changes inside a live region; a notification added to the page together with its text may not be read. The toaster keeps one region in the page for its toasts, so every toast is announced. The icon is named after the kind (\\"error icon\\"); icon-label changes it. × is named \\"Close notification\\" in the page language; close-label changes it. Don't put a timeout on a message people need to act on. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Notification."],["Notification","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Notification","<ui-notification> · React UiNotification","/kanok-ui-docs/en/notification/#ui-notification-react-uinotification","Attribute Property Type Default Description title role variant variant NotificationVariant 'inline' Inline (default) or toast. kind kind NotificationKind 'error' Status kind; sets the colour and the icon. low-contrast lowContrast boolean false Tinted surface with primary text instead of the inverse surface. heading heading string '' Bold title; the title slot replaces it when markup is needed. (Before 0.5: the title attribute, still accepted.) subtitle subtitle string '' Body text; the subtitle slot replaces it when markup is needed. caption caption string '' Toast only: small text under the subtitle, e.g. the time. action-label actionLabel string '' Label of the action button; set it to get Carbon's actionable notification. timeout timeout number 0 Milliseconds after which the notification closes itself (toast); 0 = never. Paused on hover / focus; ignored with action-label. hide-close-button hideCloseButton boolean false close-on-escape closeOnEscape boolean true Esc closes an actionable notification while focus is inside it (Carbon closeOnEscape). no-autofocus noAutofocus boolean false Keep focus where it is instead of moving it to the action button (Carbon hasFocus={false}). full-width fullWidth boolean false Fills its container instead of Carbon's 288–832px cap (inline / callout; a toast stays 288px). close-label closeLabel string '' Accessible name of the close button. icon-label iconLabel string '' Accessible description of the status icon; defaults to \\"kind icon\\" (e.g. \\"error icon\\") like Carbon. open open boolean true False once closed (reflects open=\\"false\\"); set back to true to show it again. Property Type Description role NotificationRole | null ARIA role of the notification box; defaults to status, or alertdialog when there is an action button. A role attribute is read and moved inside. Method Description close(reason) Asks to close (ui-request-close, cancelable); hides and fires ui-close unless prevented. focus(options) Focus the action button, else the close button. Event React Description ui-close onUiClose After it closed ui-action onUiAction The action button was pressed ui-request-close onUiRequestClose Cancelable; detail: { reason: 'close-button' | 'escape' | 'timeout' } Slot Description (default) Extra content after the subtitle (links, details) title Title with markup; the heading attribute is the plain-text fallback subtitle Subtitle with markup; the subtitle attribute is the plain-text fallback Part Description base The notification box icon The status icon title The title subtitle The subtitle caption The toast caption action-button The action button close-button The close button Custom property Default Description --ui-notification-radius Corner radius (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-notification-bar-width Width of the status bar at the start (default 3px; Kanok: 0, the icon tells the kind) --ui-notification-frame-start Low contrast: the frame's start side (default 0, the bar is there; Kanok: 1px) --ui-notification-background / --ui-notification-ink / --ui-notification-edge - The high-contrast box: fill, text and an extra box-shadow (default Carbon's inverse block, none; Kanok: the raised floating surface) --ui-notification-link / --ui-notification-hover / --ui-notification-focus - On that box: links and the action, the action's hover and the focus ring (default link-inverse, inverse hover, inverse ink) --ui-toast-shadow A toast's shadow (default 0 2px 6px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2)) --ui-close-size Size of the × button (default 48px; Kanok: 32px) --ui-close-inset Margin that sets the × in from the corner (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of the ×, its hover fill and its ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of the ×'s focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Toast","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/","A toast is a short message that appears in the corner of the screen after something happened elsewhere on the page: a contract saved, an upload that failed in the background. Toasts stack, the newest nearest the corner, and the quiet ones go away by themselves. Carbon has no toast manager; ui-toaster and toast() are this library's. For a message that belongs in the page, use an inline Notification."],["Toast","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Toast","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#use-it","toast(options) creates a <ui-notification variant=\\"toast\\"> and adds it to the page's <ui-toaster>, which it creates at the end of <body> the first time. It returns { element, close }. The options are kind, title, subtitle, caption, timeout, actionLabel, onAction, lowContrast and id. The live examples on this page can't import a module, so they do what toast() does by hand: create the element and pass it to the toaster's add(). In your app, call toast(). React + Tailwind has its own toast() and a <Toaster> you mount once; it returns { close }, and toast.clear() removes every toast. The toaster is one polite live region named \\"Notifications\\", in the page before any toast, so screen readers announce each one. It sits in the top layer, 16px from the top end corner, or 16px under a ui-header."],["Toast","Kinds and how long they stay","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#kinds-and-how-long-they-stay","kind is info by default. Info and success toasts close after 5 seconds; error and warning toasts stay until they are closed, because they need reading. timeout sets another time in milliseconds, or 0 to stay. The countdown pauses while the pointer is over the toast or focus is inside it."],["Toast","Caption and low contrast","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#caption-and-low-contrast","caption adds a small line under the subtitle, usually the time. lowContrast gives the toast a light tint instead of the dark surface."],["Toast","With an action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#with-an-action","actionLabel adds a button for one quick action, and onAction runs when it is pressed. An actionable toast never closes by itself, takes focus when it appears and keeps Tab inside it until it is closed (Carbon's actionable notification). Use it only when the action is worth that interruption."],["Toast","Replace a toast","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#replace-a-toast","A toast with the same id as one that is still open replaces it instead of stacking a second one. Use it for a status that changes: \\"Syncing…\\", then \\"Synced\\"."],["Toast","Close from code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#close-from-code","toast() returns a handle: close() closes that toast, for example when the work it talks about is done. On the element, close() does the same."],["Toast","How many at once","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#how-many-at-once","The toaster shows at most max toasts (3 by default); a new one closes the oldest. Place a <ui-toaster> yourself to change it; toast() uses the first one in the page. Press the button a few times."],["Toast","Bottom corner","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#bottom-corner","placement=\\"bottom-end\\" stacks the toasts in the bottom end corner, the newest at the bottom. --ui-toaster-offset sets the distance from the edge (React + Tailwind: offset)."],["Toast","Toasts and modals","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#toasts-and-modals","A toast added while a Modal is open is drawn above it, but the page outside a modal is inert: nobody can click it and screen readers can't reach it. Give feedback inside a modal with an inline Notification instead (Carbon's guidance)."],["Toast","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#accessibility","Each toast is announced through the toaster's region; the toasts themselves have no live role. An actionable toast keeps the alertdialog role and takes focus. Closed toasts are removed from the page. Keep toasts short, and don't put anything in a toast that the user can only find there: once it is gone, it is gone. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Toast."],["Toast","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Toast","<ui-toaster> · React UiToaster","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toast/#ui-toaster-react-uitoaster","Attribute Property Type Default Description placement placement ToasterPlacement 'top-end' Corner: newest toast nearest the edge. max max number 3 Most toasts shown at once; a new one closes the oldest. Method Description add(toast) Adds toast, closes the oldest beyond max, and lifts the region above anything opened since. Slot Description (default) <ui-notification variant=\\"toast\\"> elements (added by toast()) Custom property Default Description --ui-toaster-offset Distance from the top (or bottom) edge (default 16px; 64px under a ui-header)"],["Tooltip","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/","A tooltip is a short line of plain text about the control it wraps. It opens when the pointer rests on the control or keyboard focus reaches it, and closes when they leave. Use it to name an icon or add a hint, never for content people must read or act on."],["Tooltip","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tooltip","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#use-it","Wrap one focusable element, such as a button or a link, and put the text in text."],["Tooltip","Tooltip, toggletip, definition tooltip or popover?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#tooltip-toggletip-definition-tooltip-or-popover","Component Use it when Tooltip A short plain-text hint or the name of an icon. It opens on hover and focus and holds nothing to click. Toggletip The explanation has a link or a button, or should stay open until the user closes it. It opens on a click. Definition tooltip A word in running text needs a definition. The word gets a dotted underline. Popover Your own content (filters, a small form) beside a trigger."],["Tooltip","Placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#placement","The bubble opens above the trigger (placement=\\"top\\"). bottom, left and right move it. When there is no room, it flips to the other side. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute."],["Tooltip","Start and end","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#start-and-end","Add -start or -end to line the bubble up with one edge of the trigger instead of its centre, for a trigger near the edge of the screen or a table. The caret still points at the trigger. In right-to-left pages, start and end swap sides."],["Tooltip","Name an icon-only button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#name-an-icon-only-button","A button with only an icon has no visible name. as-label (asLabel in React) makes the text the button's accessible name, and gives the bubble Carbon's icon-tooltip look: smaller padding and caret, 8px from the button. <ui-icon-button> does this for you with its label."],["Tooltip","Small","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#small","small gives the same compact look as as-label, but the text stays a description. Use it for a short hint on a control that already has a visible name."],["Tooltip","Any focusable trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#any-focusable-trigger","The trigger can be any element that takes focus: our buttons, a native <button>, a link. Wrap exactly one. The text joins the trigger's own descriptions (aria-describedby) and replaces none. A plain <span> or icon never gets keyboard focus, so keyboard users would never see its tooltip: wrap a button instead."],["Tooltip","Explain a disabled action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#explain-a-disabled-action","A disabled button can't take focus, so its tooltip never shows to keyboard users. Use disabled-focusable on the button instead: it looks and acts disabled but stays in the Tab order, and the tooltip says why."],["Tooltip","Longer text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#longer-text","The bubble grows to fit its text up to 288px wide, then wraps. Keep it to a sentence or two: nobody can scroll a tooltip, and it disappears when the pointer moves away. Longer help belongs in a toggletip or on the page."],["Tooltip","Inside a box that clips","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#inside-a-box-that-clips","The bubble opens in the browser's top layer, so a parent with overflow: hidden or a small height can't cut it off. Hover the button in the short box below."],["Tooltip","Keep it open: \\"Copied\\"","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#keep-it-open-copied","open shows the bubble. Together with pinned, it stays open whatever the pointer, focus, clicks and Esc do, until you clear open. Use it for a short confirmation, as Carbon's copy button does. Click the contract number below. copy and copied are the same in both React versions. React + Tailwind has no pinned: while open is set, hover and focus only report through onOpenChange."],["Tooltip","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#keyboard","Key What it does Tab Focus reaching the trigger opens the tooltip; focus leaving closes it Esc Closes the tooltip only. Focus stays on the trigger, and a surrounding modal stays open Enter, Space Activate the trigger and close the tooltip, so it doesn't cover the result A mouse click focuses the trigger without opening the tooltip a second time: the hover already showed it."],["Tooltip","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#accessibility","The bubble has role=\\"tooltip\\". Its text is the trigger's accessible description, or with as-label its accessible name. Screen readers read it without the bubble showing. It follows WCAG 1.4.13: the pointer can move onto the bubble without closing it, and Esc dismisses it. Never put links, buttons or anything else to click in a tooltip. Nobody can reach them. Use a toggletip or a popover. The text must not be the only place for information a user needs to finish a task. Touch screens have no hover. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Tooltip."],["Tooltip","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tooltip","<ui-tooltip> · React UiTooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tooltip/#ui-tooltip-react-uitooltip","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) text text string '' placement placement TooltipPlacement 'top' as-label asLabel boolean false Use the text as the trigger's accessible name instead of its description. small small boolean false The icon tooltip's look (as as-label: 8px off, 2px / 16px padding, 8×4 caret) without naming the trigger. open open boolean false Whether the bubble is showing. Hover / focus manage it; set it yourself together with pinned. pinned pinned boolean false Keep the bubble open regardless of hover, focus, clicks and Escape — for a confirmation such as \\"Copied!\\" (Carbon copy button). While pinned, only open closes it. Property Type Description anchor HTMLElement | null The element the bubble points at, listens to and names / describes, instead of the slotted trigger — for a focusable host that renders its tooltip in its own shadow root (an icon-only content switcher item). Method Description focus(options) Focus the slotted trigger (delegatesFocus does not reach slotted light DOM). Slot Description (default) The trigger (one focusable element, e.g. <ui-button>) Part Description bubble The tooltip bubble caret The arrow pointing at the trigger Custom property Default Description --ui-tooltip-radius Corner radius of the bubble (default --ui-radius-xs)"],["Definition tooltip","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/","A definition tooltip explains a word in running text. The word gets a dotted underline; a click, Enter or Space shows its definition in a dark bubble below it. Use it for terms readers may not know, such as legal or internal words."],["Definition tooltip","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Definition tooltip","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#use-it","Put the term inside the element and the explanation in definition. A tooltip explains a control; a definition tooltip explains a word. When the explanation needs a link, use a toggletip."],["Definition tooltip","Open on hover","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#open-on-hover","By default only a click, Enter, Space or keyboard focus opens the definition. open-on-hover (openOnHover in React) opens it when the pointer rests on the word too, as Carbon's openOnHover. However it opened, it closes 100ms after the pointer leaves the word and the bubble, so the pointer can move onto the bubble."],["Definition tooltip","Placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#placement","The definition opens below the word (placement=\\"bottom\\"). top, left and right move it, and -start / -end line it up with one edge of the word. It flips when there is no room. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute."],["Definition tooltip","Rich definition","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#rich-definition","For bold text or a line break, put the definition in the definition slot instead of the attribute. In React + Tailwind, definition takes any React node. Keep it short and with nothing to click: the bubble closes when focus leaves the word."],["Definition tooltip","In a table header","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#in-a-table-header","A column header with an abbreviation is a common place for a definition. The bubble opens in the top layer, so the table's own overflow can't clip it."],["Definition tooltip","Longer definitions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#longer-definitions","The bubble is at most 176px wide, so a longer definition wraps over several lines. Two short sentences is about the limit; beyond that, link to a glossary instead."],["Definition tooltip","Open state and events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#open-state-and-events","open is the state, and you can set it yourself. ui-toggle fires after the definition opens or closes, with detail.open. Use it, for example, to count which terms people look up. Open the term below a few times. React + Tailwind also takes open (controlled) and defaultOpen."],["Definition tooltip","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#keyboard","Key What it does Tab Focus reaching the word opens the definition; focus leaving closes it Enter, Space Open or close the definition Esc Closes the definition only; a surrounding modal stays open The word is a real <button> with tabindex=\\"0\\", so Tab reaches it in every browser, Safari included."],["Definition tooltip","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#accessibility","The word is a button with aria-expanded and aria-controls. The bubble has role=\\"tooltip\\". The definition is also the word's accessible description, so screen readers read it on focus without opening the bubble. The underline is dotted and turns blue on hover and focus, so it doesn't look like a link. Don't use it on words that go somewhere: use a link. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Definition tooltip."],["Definition tooltip","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Definition tooltip","<ui-definition-tooltip> · React UiDefinitionTooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/definition-tooltip/#ui-definition-tooltip-react-uidefinitiontooltip","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) definition definition string '' The explanation (plain text); use the definition slot for markup. placement placement Placement 'bottom' open open boolean false open-on-hover openOnHover boolean false Also open on pointer hover (Carbon openOnHover). Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) The term (inline text) definition Rich definition (overrides the definition attribute) Part Description trigger The term button bubble The popover caret The arrow Custom property Default Description --ui-tooltip-radius Corner radius of the bubble (default --ui-radius-xs; the tooltip setting)"],["Popover","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/","A popover is a floating box with your own content beside a trigger: a few filters, a short form, settings for a table. It is Carbon's Popover, the box behind tooltips, toggletips and menus. You decide when it opens; auto-close lets Esc and a click outside close it."],["Popover","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Popover","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#use-it","Put the trigger in the trigger slot and the content inside. The popover doesn't open by itself: toggle open when the trigger is clicked. show() and hide() on the element do the same as setting open. In React + Tailwind the trigger is the trigger prop: it gets aria-expanded and aria-controls."],["Popover","Popover, toggletip or modal?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#popover-toggletip-or-modal","Component Use it when Popover Your own content beside the trigger, and the page around it stays usable. Toggletip An explanation with a link or a button, behind an info icon. It is a popover with the trigger and closing rules built in. Menu A list of actions to pick from. Modal The user must finish or cancel a task before going back to the page."],["Popover","Close it yourself","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#close-it-yourself","Without auto-close, only your code closes the popover: Esc and clicks outside do nothing. Use it when the user must answer, for example a \\"what's new\\" hint with its own button. When your code closes the popover while focus is inside it, give focus back to the trigger yourself, as the demo does. With auto-close, Esc does that for you."],["Popover","Placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#placement","The box opens below the trigger (placement=\\"bottom\\"). top, left, right and the -start / -end forms move it; it flips when there is no room. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute."],["Popover","Caret and shadow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#caret-and-shadow","The caret (12×6px, 10px from the trigger) and the drop shadow are on by default. caret=\\"false\\" puts the box flush against the trigger with no arrow; drop-shadow=\\"false\\" removes the shadow, for a box on a layer that already stands out."],["Popover","High contrast","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#high-contrast","high-contrast (highContrast in React) gives the box the inverse colours of a tooltip: dark in the light theme, light in the dark one."],["Popover","Tab tip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#tab-tip","tab-tip (Carbon's isTabTip) makes a square box with no caret, flush under the trigger, as if the two were one piece. Use it for settings behind an icon button in a toolbar, usually with placement=\\"bottom-end\\"."],["Popover","A small form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#a-small-form","A popover can hold a short form, such as renaming a record in place. Prevent the submit, use the values, close the popover and give focus back to the trigger. save and name are the same in both React versions. In React, give focus back to the trigger after setOpen(false) (a ref on it) when focus was inside."],["Popover","Keep it open","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#keep-it-open","With auto-close, Esc and a click outside first fire ui-request-close with detail.reason (escape or outside). It is cancelable: preventDefault() keeps the box open, for example while a note isn't saved. ui-toggle fires after it opens or closes. Type a note below, then press Esc or click outside."],["Popover","Open on hover","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#open-on-hover","Beyond Carbon: open-on-hover (openOnHover) opens the popover while the pointer rests on its trigger (after 100ms) and closes it 300ms after the pointer leaves both the trigger and the popover, so the pointer can move onto the content. A keyboard user opens it by tabbing to the trigger; Esc closes it and keeps focus on the trigger. On a touch screen a tap opens and closes it. Use it for previews, such as a larger picture of a receipt; keep actions the user must reach in a popover that opens on click."],["Popover","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#keyboard","Key What it does Tab Moves through the trigger and the content in page order Esc With auto-close, from the trigger or the content: asks to close and gives focus back to the trigger. A control inside that uses Esc itself (an open dropdown) handles it first Enter, Space on the trigger Whatever your click handler does, usually toggles open"],["Popover","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#accessibility","The box has role=\\"group\\" named by label. Give it a label that says what the content is. The popover sets aria-expanded on the trigger (expanded on a <ui-button> or <ui-icon-button>). Focus doesn't move into the box when it opens. Keep the content short and right after the trigger, so a keyboard user reaches it with the next Tab. For a task the user must finish before going on, use a modal instead. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Popover."],["Popover","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Popover","<ui-popover> · React UiPopover","/kanok-ui-docs/en/popover/#ui-popover-react-uipopover","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) open open boolean false placement placement Placement 'bottom' caret caret boolean true On by default; caret=\\"false\\" hides it. drop-shadow dropShadow boolean true On by default; drop-shadow=\\"false\\" removes it. high-contrast highContrast boolean false tab-tip tabTip boolean false Carbon isTabTip: square box flush against the trigger (toolbar settings panels). auto-close autoClose boolean false Close on Escape and on clicks outside the trigger and the box. label label string '' Accessible name of the box (role=group). open-on-hover openOnHover boolean false Beyond Carbon (its Popover has no hover mode; the tooltip's timings): the popover opens and closes itself. A mouse resting on the trigger opens it after 100ms, and leaving the trigger and the box closes it after 300ms (the pointer can move onto the box, WCAG 1.4.13); keyboard focus on the trigger opens it at once, and focus leaving the trigger and the box closes it; a tap (touch, pen) on the trigger toggles it; Escape and a press outside close it. While focus is in the box, or on the trigger by keyboard, it stays open. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after it opens or closes ui-request-close onUiRequestClose cancelable; auto-close fires it before closing on Escape / outside click Slot Description trigger The element the box is positioned against (default) Box content Part Description content The floating box caret The arrow Custom property Default Description --ui-menu-border / --ui-menu-radius - Border and corners of the bubble (the menu settings)"],["Toggletip","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/","A toggletip is a small \\"i\\" button that opens an explanation when clicked. Unlike a tooltip, it stays open until the user closes it, and it may hold links and buttons. Put it next to a label or a heading that needs more context."],["Toggletip","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Toggletip","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#use-it","Put the explanation inside the element and name the button with label. React + Tailwind's Toggletip lives in the popover file, as both are built on the same parts."],["Toggletip","Toggletip or tooltip?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#toggletip-or-tooltip","Tooltip Toggletip Opens on Hover and keyboard focus A click, Enter or Space on the \\"i\\" button Closes on The pointer or focus leaving, Esc Another click, Esc, a click outside, focus leaving both the button and the bubble Content One line of plain text Text, links and buttons Trigger The control it explains Its own \\"i\\" button See the tooltip page for the definition tooltip and the popover too."],["Toggletip","Beside a heading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#beside-a-heading","The toggletip is an inline element that sits on the text's middle line. Put it right after the words it explains, so it reads as part of the same line."],["Toggletip","Links and buttons inside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#links-and-buttons-inside","The content follows the button in the Tab order, so a keyboard user reaches a link or a button inside with the next Tab. A link put directly inside takes the primary colour. When the bubble closes while focus is inside it (the \\"Got it\\" button, Esc), focus goes back to the \\"i\\" button."],["Toggletip","Placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#placement","The bubble opens below the button (placement=\\"bottom\\"). top, left, right and the -start / -end forms move it; it flips when there is no room. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute."],["Toggletip","Another icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#another-icon","The \\"i\\" is the default. Put another 16px icon in the trigger slot (icon in React + Tailwind), for example Carbon's Help (see Icons). It takes the button's colour."],["Toggletip","Open state and events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#open-state-and-events","open is the state; show() and hide() set it. ui-toggle fires after the bubble opens or closes, with detail.open. Leave open out in React + Tailwind and the toggletip keeps its own state."],["Toggletip","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#keyboard","Key What it does Enter, Space On the button: open or close the bubble Tab From the button into the content; leaving both closes the bubble Esc Closes the bubble and gives focus back to the button when it was inside A click outside the button and the bubble closes it too."],["Toggletip","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#accessibility","The trigger is a real <button> with aria-expanded and aria-controls. Its name is label, else \\"More information\\" in the page language (Thai or English). The bubble has role=\\"group\\" with the same name, so screen readers say what the content is about. Give label the topic (\\"About the deposit\\"), not \\"Info\\": a page with several toggletips needs a different name on each. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Popover, with closeOnFocusOut."],["Toggletip","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Toggletip","<ui-toggletip> · React UiToggletip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/toggletip/#ui-toggletip-react-uitoggletip","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) label label string '' Accessible name of the trigger, e.g. \\"More about retention\\". placement placement Placement 'bottom' open open boolean false Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open }, after it opens or closes Slot Description (default) Bubble content (text, links, buttons) trigger Custom trigger icon (default: an \\"i\\" information icon) Part Description trigger The info button bubble The popover content box caret The arrow pointing at the trigger Custom property Default Description --ui-menu-border / --ui-menu-radius - Border and corners of the bubble (the menu settings) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Menu","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/","A menu is a short list of actions that opens from a button. This page covers the three triggers Carbon ships (the menu button, the overflow menu \\"⋮\\" and the combo button), the items that go inside them, and the menu on its own."],["Menu","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Menu","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#use-it","Import the trigger you use; each brings the menu and its items with it. The combo button is its own file: @purpurabog/ui/combo-button, and @kanok-ui/tw-combo-button for React + Tailwind."],["Menu","Which trigger?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#which-trigger","Trigger Use it when Menu button (ui-menu-button) A labelled button groups several actions of the same kind (\\"Actions\\", \\"Export\\"). Overflow menu (ui-overflow-menu) Space is tight: secondary actions of a table row, a card or a toolbar, behind \\"⋮\\". Combo button (ui-combo-button) One action is the usual one and others are close variants (\\"Save\\", then \\"Save as draft\\"). Menu (ui-menu) None of these fit and you bring your own trigger."],["Menu","Menu button kinds","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#menu-button-kinds","kind is primary (the default), tertiary or ghost, as Carbon's MenuButton. Primary and tertiary buttons are at least 192px wide; ghost fits its label."],["Menu","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#sizes","size is sm 32px, md 40px or lg 48px (the default). The menu's rows take the same height as the button."],["Menu","Placement and width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#placement-and-width","The menu opens below the button. With placement=\\"bottom\\" (the default) or top, it is as wide as the button. bottom-start, bottom-end, top-start and top-end line it up with one edge and let it be as wide as its items. It flips when there is no room. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute."],["Menu","Overflow menu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#overflow-menu","<ui-overflow-menu> is a ghost icon button with \\"⋮\\" that opens the menu (Carbon's OverflowMenu). label names the button and shows in its tooltip; it defaults to \\"Options\\". In a table row, use placement=\\"bottom-end\\" so the menu stays inside the table. ui-select tells you which item was picked: detail has its value (else its label), label and checked. ui-select bubbles, so one listener on the table hears every row. Give each overflow menu a label that names its row: a screen reader hears \\"Actions for Lease, Silom office\\", not five times \\"Options\\"."],["Menu","Overflow menu sizes and icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#overflow-menu-sizes-and-icon","size is sm 32px, md 40px (the default) or lg 48px, for the button and the rows. tooltip-placement moves the tooltip (below by default). Another icon goes in the icon slot (icon in React + Tailwind), such as \\"⋯\\" for a horizontal toolbar."],["Menu","Combo button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#combo-button","<ui-combo-button> is a primary button for the usual action, joined to a chevron that opens the other actions (Carbon's ComboButton). The primary button fires ui-click; the items fire ui-select. The chevron is named \\"Additional actions\\" unless you set trigger-label. With placement=\\"bottom\\" (the default) the menu is as wide as the whole control. A plain click on the element also bubbles from the chevron and the items, so listen for ui-click to run the primary action only."],["Menu","Items: icons, shortcuts, disabled and danger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#items-icons-shortcuts-disabled-and-danger","An SVG in the item's icon slot (icon in React + Tailwind) shows a 16px icon. When one item has an icon, every row gets the icon column, so the labels line up. shortcut shows a key hint at the end of the row. It is only text: register the key yourself. disabled shows the item but skips it with the keys, and a click does nothing. kind=\\"danger\\" turns the row red on hover and focus. danger-description is read after the label, so screen reader users hear what will happen. <ui-menu-divider> draws a line between groups of items."],["Menu","Check boxes and radio groups","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#check-boxes-and-radio-groups","selectable makes an item an on / off choice (Carbon's MenuItemSelectable): a click flips checked and a check mark shows. <ui-menu-group selection=\\"single\\"> makes its items a radio group (Carbon's MenuItemRadioGroup): exactly one is checked, the one whose value is the group's value. It fires ui-change with detail.value when the choice changes. label on a group names it for screen readers. A group without selection only names its items. Picking an item closes the menu, check boxes and radios included."],["Menu","Submenus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#submenus","Put <ui-menu-item>s inside an item to give it a submenu: the item shows a chevron and opens them beside it, on hover, a click, Enter, Space or → (← in right-to-left pages). ← or Esc closes only that level. Picking a leaf closes every level and its ui-select bubbles out of the whole menu. In React + Tailwind, MenuItem children make the submenu. Keep submenus to one or two levels: each level is another hover target to hit."],["Menu","A menu with your own trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#a-menu-with-your-own-trigger","<ui-menu> is the list behind every trigger above. Use it on its own when you have a trigger of your own: show(anchor) opens it beside that element, hide() closes it. size sets the row height (xs 24, sm 32 by default, md 40, lg 48) and placement the side (bottom-start by default). You wire the trigger: aria-haspopup, aria-expanded from ui-toggle, and ↓ / ↑ if you want them. match-width (matchWidth) makes the menu as wide as the anchor."],["Menu","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#disabled","disabled on a trigger greys it out and keeps the menu closed. Prefer hiding actions the user can never take, and disabling those that are only unavailable for now."],["Menu","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#keyboard","Key On the trigger In the menu Enter, Space Open the menu on the first item Pick the focused item (or open its submenu) and close ↓ Open the menu on the first item Next item, wrapping to the first; disabled items are skipped ↑ Open the menu on the last item Previous item, wrapping to the last Home / End First / last item Letters Jump to the next item that starts with them → (← right-to-left) Open the focused item's submenu ← (→ right-to-left) In a submenu: close it and go back to its item Esc Close this level and give focus back (in a submenu, only the submenu) Tab Close the menu and give focus back to the trigger"],["Menu","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#accessibility","It follows the WAI-ARIA menu button pattern: the trigger has aria-haspopup and aria-expanded; the list has role=\\"menu\\" named by the trigger's label; items are menuitem, menuitemcheckbox or menuitemradio with aria-checked. Focus moves into the menu when it opens. It goes back to the trigger when a key or a picked item closes the menu. The overflow menu's button is named by label and shows it in a tooltip. Make each label unique on the page. A menu is for actions. To pick a value for a form field, use a Dropdown or a Select. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Menu."],["Menu","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Menu","<ui-menu-button> · React UiMenuButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-menu-button-react-uimenubutton","Attribute Property Type Default Description variant Same as kind, kept for teams used to variant (shadcn, MUI); kind is Carbon's name and the one in the docs align Carbon's name for placement (same values) label label string '' kind kind MenuButtonKind 'primary' Carbon kind: primary, tertiary or ghost. size size Exclude<ButtonSize, 'xl' | '2xl'> 'lg' sm 32 / md 40 / lg 48px (Carbon has no xl / 2xl here). placement placement MenuPlacement 'bottom' disabled disabled boolean false open open boolean false Property Type Description variant MenuButtonKind Same as kind (permanent alias for teams used to variant); a variant attribute works too. Event React Description ui-select onUiSelect bubbles from the activated item: detail { value, label, checked } ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) <ui-menu-item>, <ui-menu-divider>, <ui-menu-group> Part Description trigger The <ui-button> menu The <ui-menu>"],["Menu","<ui-overflow-menu> · React UiOverflowMenu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-overflow-menu-react-uioverflowmenu","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) label label string '' Accessible name of the trigger and the menu. size size OverflowMenuSize 'md' placement placement MenuPlacement 'bottom-start' tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement TooltipPlacement 'bottom' disabled disabled boolean false open open boolean false Event React Description ui-select onUiSelect bubbles from the activated item: detail { value, label, checked } ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) <ui-menu-item>, <ui-menu-divider>, <ui-menu-group> icon Replaces the \\"⋮\\" icon Part Description trigger The icon button menu The <ui-menu> Custom property Default Description --ui-button-radius Corner radius of the trigger (the button setting) --ui-overflow-open-background / --ui-overflow-open-shadow - The trigger while open (default: it joins the menu, Carbon's look) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Menu","<ui-combo-button> · React UiComboButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-combo-button-react-uicombobutton","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) label label string '' Primary action text. size size Exclude<ButtonSize, 'xl' | '2xl'> 'lg' sm 32 / md 40 / lg 48px (Carbon has no xl / 2xl here). placement placement MenuPlacement 'bottom' tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement TooltipPlacement 'bottom' trigger-label triggerLabel string '' Name of the chevron button; defaults to the translation (\\"Additional actions\\"). disabled disabled boolean false open open boolean false Event React Description ui-click onUiClick the primary button was activated (not the chevron or a menu item) ui-select onUiSelect bubbles from the activated item ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) <ui-menu-item> elements (secondary actions) Part Description primary The primary <ui-button> trigger The chevron <ui-icon-button> menu The <ui-menu>"],["Menu","<ui-menu> · React UiMenu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-menu-react-uimenu","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) open open boolean false label label string '' Accessible name of the menu (the trigger's label). size size MenuSize 'sm' placement placement MenuPlacement 'bottom-start' match-width matchWidth boolean false Make the menu as wide as the anchor (Carbon menu button with bottom / top). Property Type Description anchor Element | null What the menu is positioned against; show(anchor) sets it. Method Description show(anchor, focus) Open next to anchor; focus: 'last' starts on the last item (Up Arrow on a menu button), none leaves focus where it is (a submenu opened by hover). focusItem(which) Focus the first or last enabled item. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after it opens or closes Slot Description (default) <ui-menu-item>, <ui-menu-divider>, <ui-menu-group> Custom property Default Description --ui-menu-padding / --ui-menu-border / --ui-menu-radius / --ui-menu-shadow - The menu box, as the dropdown lists --ui-menu-item-radius / --ui-menu-item-ink - Its rows (on <ui-menu-item>) --ui-menu-min-width / --ui-menu-max-width - Width range (default 160px to 288px; Kanok: 180px to 320px) --ui-menu-item-height / --ui-menu-item-active-outline / --ui-menu-item-active-background - Every row's height and the focused row's ring or fill (on <ui-menu-item>)"],["Menu","<ui-menu-item> · React UiMenuItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-menu-item-react-uimenuitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' value value string '' Reported in ui-select; defaults to label. shortcut shortcut string '' kind kind MenuItemKind 'default' disabled disabled boolean false selectable selectable boolean false Carbon MenuItemSelectable: a menuitemcheckbox that toggles checked. checked checked boolean false danger-description dangerDescription string '' Property Type Description radio boolean Set by <ui-menu-group selection=\\"single\\">: this item is a menuitemradio. Method Description openSubmenu(focus) Open the submenu; focus picks the item that takes focus (none for hover). activate() What a click / Enter / Space does: opens the submenu, else toggles / selects and fires ui-select. Event React Description ui-select onUiSelect detail: { value, label, checked } when activated (not when disabled) Slot Description (default) Extra label content after label; <ui-menu-item> children move to the submenu submenu The submenu's items (children that are menu items get this slot automatically) icon 16px icon (shown when any item in the menu has one — Carbon renderIcon) Part Description icon Icon cell label Label cell shortcut Shortcut hint submenu The nested <ui-menu> submenu-icon The chevron of an item with a submenu Custom property Default Description --ui-menu-item-height Row height for every size (default 24 / 32 / 40 / 48px by size; Kanok: 32px) --ui-menu-item-active-outline / --ui-menu-item-active-background - The focused row: its ring and its fill (default focus, transparent) --ui-menu-item-pointer-outline The ring of a row focused by a mouse open or click, not the keyboard (default the focused row's ring, as Carbon; Kanok: none)"],["Menu","<ui-menu-group> · React UiMenuGroup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-menu-group-react-uimenugroup","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' selection selection 'none' | 'single' 'none' value value string '' The checked item's value in selection=\\"single\\". Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { value } when the checked radio item changes Slot Description (default) <ui-menu-item> elements"],["Menu","<ui-menu-divider> · React UiMenuDivider","/kanok-ui-docs/en/menu/#ui-menu-divider-react-uimenudivider",""],["Data table","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/","A data table shows rows of records in columns (Carbon DataTable). The web component follows Carbon web components (cds-table): you write the table as elements — <ui-table-head> with the header cells, <ui-table-body> with rows of cells — and it sorts, searches, selects, expands and pages the rows it holds. Beyond Carbon it can hide and pin columns, export CSV, edit cells in place and resize columns. The React + Tailwind DataTable is driven by data instead: you give it headers and rows. Coming from <ui-data-table> (before 1.0)? See Migrating to 1.0. headers and rows are the same data in every version: the HTML writes them out as elements, the React examples below map them with headerCells and cells(row) from above, and React + Tailwind takes them as props."],["Data table","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Data table","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#use-it","@purpurabog/ui/table defines every ui-table* element. <ui-table> holds a <ui-table-head> with one <ui-table-header-row> of <ui-table-header-cell>s and a <ui-table-body> with <ui-table-row>s of <ui-table-cell>s; a cell's column is its place in the row. The title, description and toolbar go in the table's title, description and toolbar slots. The table works on the rows it finds: add, remove or reorder rows and it follows. In React + Tailwind each header is { key, header } and each row needs a stable id."],["Data table","Custom cells","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#custom-cells","A cell shows whatever you put in it: a formatted number, a link, a tag. Sorting reads a cell's sort-value when it has one (give an amount shown as \\"1,250,000\\" its plain number) and CSV export its csv-value; both fall back to the cell's text. The search reads the text. React + Tailwind renders cells with renderCell(row, header), which returns React nodes, and align: 'end' on a header puts that column's cells at the end; sorting and search use the raw values."],["Data table","Sorting","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#sorting","is-sortable on the table gives every header a sort button; is-sortable on single headers makes only those sortable (the table's attribute sets every header). A click steps the header's sort-direction through its sort-cycle (default none → ascending → descending → none); the other headers go back to none and the table moves its rows into that order. Numbers sort by value, text by locale (default: the page's lang), and none restores the order the rows came in. A header with sort-direction in the markup sorts the rows on load. The header fires a cancelable ui-table-header-cell-sort with { oldSortDirection, sortDirection } before the rows move, and the table fires ui-table-sorted with { sortedHeader } after. The table sorts by moving its rows in the DOM. Rows a framework renders (React, Vue, Angular) belong to the framework, so there call preventDefault() on ui-table-header-cell-sort, sort the data yourself (or on the server), render the rows in that order and set the header's sort-direction (sortDirection), as the React tab does. Replace the comparison by assigning customSortRow(lhs, rhs, collator) on the table. React + Tailwind takes defaultSortKey / defaultSortDirection and sortRow(a, b, context); with manualSorting it keeps rows in your order and only shows the sort."],["Data table","Sizes and zebra stripes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#sizes-and-zebra-stripes","size sets the row height: xs 24px, sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (the default), xl 64px. use-zebra-styles shades every other row. use-static-width makes the table as wide as its content instead of its container. The toolbar follows the table's size (24px for xs, 32px for sm, 48px otherwise) and sizes the batch bar's buttons to it. In React + Tailwind, use size=\\"sm\\" buttons in the toolbar and batch bar of xs and sm tables."],["Data table","Selection and batch actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#selection-and-batch-actions","is-selectable adds a checkbox to every row and a select-all box to the header row. A row with disabled can't be chosen; selected on a row chooses it. A <ui-table-batch-actions> in the toolbar holds your buttons: while rows are chosen it covers the toolbar with the count and Cancel. The table fires ui-table-row-selected with { selectedRow, selectedRows } and, after select-all or Cancel, ui-table-row-all-selected with { selectedRows }; selectedRows on the table holds the chosen rows. React + Tailwind takes batchActions, selectedIds and onSelectionChange. Select-all follows Carbon: when any row is chosen, it releases them all; otherwise it chooses every enabled row the search shows. Before a row changes, the row fires a cancelable ui-table-row-change-selection (the header row ui-table-change-selection-all). For your own styles, chosen rows have selected, and so has the header row while any row is chosen."],["Data table","Pick one row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#pick-one-row","radio makes the selection a single choice with a radio on every row, for example to pick a template. Tab stops on the chosen row, and the arrow keys move and choose. There is no batch bar."],["Data table","Toolbar and search","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#toolbar-and-search","Put a <ui-table-toolbar slot=\\"toolbar\\"> on the table with a <ui-table-toolbar-content> for the controls: a <ui-table-toolbar-search>, an overflow menu, a primary button. The search stays a magnifier until pressed (Carbon's expandable search); persistent keeps it open. Typing leaves out the rows whose shown cells (and expanded row) don't contain the text, and the table fires ui-table-filtered with { unfilteredRows }. In React + Tailwind, searchable adds the search and the toolbar prop takes the other controls. filterRows(rowText, searchString) on the table replaces the test: return true to leave the row out (Carbon's way). To search on the server, set filterRows to () => false and listen for input on the search, whose value is the text. label and placeholder on the search replace its \\"Filter table\\". React + Tailwind has its own filterRows(row, text, headers) (true keeps the row), filterText, manualFiltering, and tells screen readers \\"3 of 12 rows\\" once typing pauses."],["Data table","Expandable rows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#expandable-rows","expandable on the table: a row followed by a <ui-table-expanded-row> gets a chevron that opens that full-width row of detail under it. batch-expansion adds a chevron to the header row that opens or closes every row, and expanded on a row opens it. The row fires a cancelable ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled, then ui-table-row-expando-toggled with { expanded }."],["Data table","Pages","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#pages","page-size adds a pagination bar under the table that shows that many of the rows the sort and search leave. page and page-sizes set the page and the choices, and ui-table-page-change fires with { page, pageSize }. Select-all then takes the page, and the batch bar offers \\"Select all (N)\\" for every row the search shows. Carbon has no paging on the table itself; it puts a Pagination under it. To page on the server, render one page of rows, put your own <ui-pagination> under the table, and sort and search on the server (cancel ui-table-header-cell-sort; filterRows that keeps every row, and the search's input). On <ui-table-batch-actions>, total-rows-count offers \\"Select all (N)\\" for rows the table doesn't hold (ui-table-batch-actions-select-all-clicked fires; choose them yourself), and setting selected-rows-count in your ui-table-row-selected listener counts a selection kept across pages. React + Tailwind does the same with manualSorting, manualFiltering, totalSelected, totalCount and onSelectAll."],["Data table","Show and hide columns","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#show-and-hide-columns","A <ui-table-column-settings> in the toolbar content adds a Columns button with a checkbox list of the columns. A header with hideable=\\"false\\" always shows, and one with column-hidden starts hidden; Reset goes back to the columns hidden in the markup. column names a column (default: its place, \\"0\\", \\"1\\" …). The table fires ui-table-columns-change with { hiddenColumns, column, hidden }; save hiddenColumns and restore it with column-hidden on the headers or setColumnHidden(column, hidden) on the table. Hidden columns leave the search and the CSV export too."],["Data table","Sticky header and pinned columns","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#sticky-header-and-pinned-columns","sticky-header keeps the header row in view while the body scrolls in a box up to --ui-table-max-height tall (300px, as Carbon). For wide tables, pinned=\\"start\\" on the first header keeps that column (and the chevron and checkbox columns before it) in view while the rest scrolls sideways, and pinned=\\"end\\" on the last header keeps row actions at the end. Pinning starts at 672px of window width. Change the box's height with CSS: ui-table { --ui-table-max-height: 480px; }. React + Tailwind's DataTable reads --ui-data-table-max-height."],["Data table","Export CSV","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#export-csv","A <ui-table-csv-export> in the toolbar content adds an Export CSV button: it downloads the columns shown and the rows the search shows (sorted, every page) as a CSV file for Excel, named after its file-name or the table's title. It fires a cancelable ui-table-csv-export first with { csv, rows, fileName }. A cell writes its csv-value, else its text. toCsv({ scope }) and downloadCsv({ scope, fileName }) on the table export 'shown', 'selected' or 'all' rows from your own buttons. This demo shows the CSV instead of downloading it. The file is UTF-8 with a byte order mark so Excel reads Thai correctly; every cell is quoted, and cells that start like a formula are made safe."],["Data table","Edit cells in place","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#edit-cells-in-place","Give a header editable=\\"text\\", \\"number\\" or \\"select\\" (with options, a list of { value, label } as a property or JSON in the attribute) and its cells can be edited: the table becomes a grid with one Tab stop, where the arrow keys move between cells. Enter, F2, a double click or typing opens the editor; Enter saves, Escape cancels, Tab saves and edits the next editable cell. A header's validate(value, cell) returns a message to keep the editor open. Saving fires a cancelable ui-table-cell-edit from the cell with { row, cell, column, value, previous }, then writes the value into the cell. Left alone, the table writes the saved value into the cell (its text, a select column's label). Rows a framework renders belong to it, so there call preventDefault() on ui-table-cell-edit and update your data, as the React tab does; to refuse an edit, cancel it and keep the data. React + Tailwind hands you the new rows in onCellEdit: set them, or keep yours to refuse the edit."],["Data table","Resize columns","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#resize-columns","resizable on the table puts a handle on the end edge of every column header, and resizable on single headers only on those: drag it, or Tab to it and use the arrow keys (Shift for 16px steps). width, min-width (default 50) and max-width in px on a header bound it. Each finished resize fires ui-table-column-resize with { column, width } from the header; columnWidths on the table holds every width. Save them and set width on the headers to restore them."],["Data table","Empty, loading and skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#empty-loading-and-skeleton","With no rows the table says \\"No data\\" under the headers; put your own message in the empty slot (emptyText in React + Tailwind). While a search finds nothing it says \\"No results found\\" (no-results slot, noResultsText). loading keeps the toolbar and headers and shows skeleton rows (loading-rows, default the rows shown) while the data reloads. Before the first data arrives, show <ui-table-skeleton> in the table's place. The skeleton is hidden from screen readers: put aria-busy and a status message on the region around it. It takes headers (a property: the column names) to show real column names, zebra, show-header=\\"false\\" and show-toolbar=\\"false\\". React + Tailwind's DataTableSkeleton takes headers, size, zebra, hideHeader and hideToolbar."],["Data table","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves through the toolbar, the sort buttons, the checkboxes and the controls in cells; a radio table and an editable grid are one Tab stop each Space Toggles a checkbox; picks the focused radio row Up / Down In a radio table, move to the previous / next row and choose it Arrow keys, Home / End, Ctrl + Home / End In an editable grid, move between cells Enter, F2 In an editable grid, edit the cell (or press the control in it) Escape Cancels an edit; clears the search"],["Data table","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#accessibility","The table has the roles of a table (table, rowgroup, row, columnheader, cell; grid once a column is editable), with aria-sort on sorted columns. Name it with aria-label on <ui-table>: as in Carbon, the title isn't tied to it. Each row's checkbox, radio and chevron is named with the row's first cell (\\"Select row, Service agreement\\"). A table that scrolls (sticky-header, or wider than its box) takes focus so keyboard users can scroll it, named by its aria-label or title. While loading, the table is aria-busy and a status says \\"Loading data\\". The batch bar's count is a status, so the new count is read when rows are chosen. React + Tailwind's DataTable also says \\"Sorted by Contract, ascending\\" after a sort and \\"3 of 12 rows\\" when typing in the search pauses. An editable grid follows the WAI-ARIA grid pattern: cells that can't be edited are aria-readonly, and editable cells say \\"Press Enter to edit\\". Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Data table."],["Data table","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Data table","<ui-table> · React UiTable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-react-uitable","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size TableSize 'lg' is-sortable isSortable boolean false Every header sorts the rows (Carbon is-sortable). use-zebra-styles useZebraStyles boolean false Stripe every second body row (Carbon use-zebra-styles). use-static-width useStaticWidth boolean false As wide as its content instead of its container (Carbon use-static-width). locale locale string '' The language text sorts in; empty: the page's lang. is-selectable isSelectable boolean false A checkbox on every row and select-all in the header row (Carbon is-selectable). radio radio boolean false One row at a time, with radios (Carbon radio). expandable expandable boolean false Rows followed by a <ui-table-expanded-row> open it with a chevron (Carbon expandable). batch-expansion batchExpansion boolean false An expand-all chevron in the header row (Carbon batch-expansion). with-header withHeader boolean false The title / description block shows (set from the title / description slots, as Carbon). resizable resizable boolean false A resize handle on every header (or resizable on single headers). page-size pageSize number 0 Rows per page: above 0 a <ui-pagination> pages the rows the sort and search leave. page page number 1 The page shown (from 1). page-sizes pageSizes string '10,25,50' The page sizes the pagination offers (comma-separated). loading loading boolean false Skeleton rows instead of the body while the data loads (the table is aria-busy). loading-rows loadingRows number 0 How many skeleton rows loading shows (default: the rows shown now, else the page size, else 5). sticky-header stickyHeader boolean false Keeps the header in view while the body scrolls inside a box (Carbon React stickyHeader; --ui-table-max-height, default 300px). Property Type Description filterRows (rowText: string, searchString: string) => boolean Whether the search leaves a row out: true hides it (Carbon filterRows; default: its text doesn't contain the search). columns UiTableHeaderCell[] (read-only) The column headers, in order (the column settings list them). hiddenColumns string[] (read-only) The keys of the hidden columns. contentWidth (read-only) Width of the horizontal scroll box (a resize stops a column there). selectedRows UiTableRow[] (read-only) The chosen rows. columnsChanged (read-only) Columns were shown or hidden since the markup (Reset has something to do). columnWidths Record<string, number> (read-only) The widths given or resized, by column. csvFileName (read-only) The file name a CSV download takes by default: the title's text. Method Description customSortRow(lhs, rhs, collator) Compares two cells' sort values (Carbon customSortRow) for ascending order: numbers by value, text with collator. Replace it on the element to sort another way. isColumnLocked(column) Whether column can't be hidden or shown now: not hideable, or the last one shown. setColumnHidden(column, hidden) Shows or hides a column (and its cells); false when it can't change (not hideable, or the last one shown). resetColumns() Back to the columns hidden in the markup. freezeColumns() The first resize freezes the automatic layout: every shown column keeps its width, a filler cell takes the rest of the row (none in a static-width table, which ends at its columns). csvRows(scope) The rows CSV takes: those the search shows (every page, in their order), the chosen ones, or all. toCsv({ scope = 'shown' }) The columns shown and the rows of scope as CSV (a cell writes its csv-value, else its text). downloadCsv({ scope = 'shown', fileName }) Downloads toCsv({ scope }) as fileName (default: the title, else \\"table\\"; .csv is added). focus(options) Focuses the table's first stop: the scroll box when it scrolls, else select-all, a sort button, the grid's Tab stop, or the first row's checkbox, radio or chevron. Event React Description ui-table-columns-change onUiTableColumnsChange detail: { hiddenColumns, column, hidden } after a column was shown or hidden (column is '' after Reset) ui-table-row-all-selected onUiTableRowAllSelected detail: { selectedRows } after select-all or Cancel ui-table-sorted onUiTableSorted detail: { sortedHeader } after the rows were sorted by a header click ui-table-row-selected onUiTableRowSelected detail: { selectedRow, selectedRows } after the user chose or released a row ui-table-filtered onUiTableFiltered detail: { unfilteredRows } after the search changed which rows show ui-table-page-change onUiTablePageChange detail: { page, pageSize } after the built-in pagination changed (page-size) ui-table-cell-edit onUiTableCellEdit from the cell, cancelable; detail: { row, cell, column, value, previous } before an edited value is written into the cell (preventDefault() to write it yourself) Slot Description (default) <ui-table-head> and <ui-table-body> title A <ui-table-header-title> description A <ui-table-header-description> toolbar A <ui-table-toolbar> empty Shown when there are no rows (default: \\"No data\\") no-results Shown when the search leaves no rows (default: \\"No results found. Try a different search.\\") Part Description header The title / description block content The horizontal scroll container table The box laid out as a table empty The message under the headers when there are no rows pagination The built-in <ui-pagination> (page-size) Custom property Default Description --ui-table-max-height Height of the scrolling box with sticky-header (default 300px) --ui-table-row-height Row height of the default size, lg (default 48px; Kanok: 40px) --ui-table-border / --ui-table-radius / --ui-table-overflow - A frame around the table (default none, 0, visible; Kanok: none, 12px, clip) --ui-table-background Fill of the table: its title, toolbar and rows (default transparent, rows --ui-surface-1; Kanok: the cards' fill) --ui-table-header-rule box-shadow under the header cells (default none; Kanok: a hairline)"],["Data table","<ui-table-head> · React UiTableHead","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-head-react-uitablehead","Slot Description (default) A <ui-table-header-row>"],["Data table","<ui-table-header-row> · React UiTableHeaderRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-header-row-react-uitableheaderrow","Attribute Property Type Default Description selected selected boolean false Chosen (Carbon selected); the table keeps the header's select-all and the batch actions in step. disabled disabled boolean false Can't be chosen. radio radio boolean false A single-choice radio instead of a checkbox (the table's radio sets it). hide-checkbox hideCheckbox boolean false No checkbox in the selection cell (the header row of a radio table). selection-name selectionName string '' Shows the selection cell: the checkbox's name (the table's is-selectable sets one). selection-value selectionValue string '' The checkbox's value. selection-label selectionLabel string '' The checkbox's accessible name; default \\"Select row\\" with the row's first cell. expandable expandable boolean false Has a <ui-table-expanded-row> after it (the table's expandable sets it). expanded expanded boolean false Its expanded row is open. batch-expansion batchExpansion boolean false The header row's chevron opens and closes every row (the table's batch-expansion sets it). filtered filtered boolean false Left out by the table's search. highlighted highlighted boolean false Hovered with its expanded row (the two tint together). paged-out pagedOut boolean false On another page of the table's pagination (the table sets it). Property Type Description expandColumn boolean The table has an expand column: every row gets the cell, expandable ones the chevron. indeterminate boolean The header's select-all is partly checked (some rows chosen); the table sets it. tabStop boolean The radio of a radio table that takes Tab (the chosen row, else the first); the table sets it. pinStart boolean The first column is pinned: the chevron and checkbox cells stick too (the table sets it). filler boolean A filler cell after the cells takes the rest of the row once the columns are resized (the table sets it). grid boolean The table is a grid (an editable column): grid cells, the body's cells and controls out of the Tab order (the table sets it). Method Description toggleExpanded(expanded) Opens or closes, unless the cancelable ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled is canceled. gridCells() The cells the grid's arrow keys move through: the chevron and checkbox cells, then the shown author cells. focusSelection() Focuses this row's selection control (a radio the arrow keys moved to). Event React Description ui-table-change-selection-all onUiTableChangeSelectionAll cancelable; detail: { selected } before every row is chosen or released ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled none (use a ref) ui-table-row-expando-toggled none (use a ref) Slot Description (default) The <ui-table-header-cell>s Part Description expand-cell The cell of the expand chevron expand-button The chevron button selection-cell The cell of the checkbox or radio"],["Data table","<ui-table-header-cell> · React UiTableHeaderCell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-header-cell-react-uitableheadercell","Attribute Property Type Default Description is-sortable isSortable boolean false Sortable on its own (the table's is-sortable sets every header). sort-active sortActive boolean false The column the rows are sorted by (set with the direction). sort-cycle sortCycle TableSortCycle | undefined The states each click steps through. sort-direction sortDirection TableSortDirection | undefined Sorted ascending, descending or not; a sortable header without one starts at none. column column string '' The column's name in events and the column settings (default: its place, \\"0\\", \\"1\\" …). column-hidden columnHidden boolean false Hidden with its cells (the column settings set it; set it in the markup to start hidden). hideable hideable boolean true Can be hidden from the column settings (hideable=\\"false\\" keeps it shown). pinned pinned 'start' | 'end' | undefined Stays in view while the table scrolls sideways: start on the first header, end on the last. resizable resizable boolean false A resize handle on its end edge (the table's resizable sets every header). width width number | undefined The column's width in px (a resize sets it). min-width minWidth number | undefined The narrowest a resize makes it (default 50). max-width maxWidth number | undefined The widest a resize makes it (default: the table's width). editable editable TableCellEditor | undefined Its cells can be edited in place, with this editor (no Carbon counterpart; the table becomes a grid). options options TableEditOption[] [] A select column's choices: the value saved and the label shown (JSON in the attribute). Property Type Description validate (value: string | number, cell: HTMLElement) => string | undefined Checks an edited value before it's saved: a message keeps the editor open and shows it. labelText (read-only) The label as text (the button's title, the screen reader hint, the column settings). columnKey (read-only) The column's key: column, else its place among the headers. Event React Description ui-table-header-cell-sort onUiTableHeaderCellSort cancelable; detail: { oldSortDirection, sortDirection } before the column sorts (preventDefault() keeps the rows and this header as they are: sort the data yourself and set sort-direction) Slot Description (default) The header's label Part Description content The box inside the header that holds its padding sort-button The button of a sortable header label-text The label sort-icon The sort arrow resizer The resize handle (an invisible range input over the end edge) Custom property Default Description --ui-table-header-background Fill of the header (default --ui-layer-accent; Kanok: the table's fill) --ui-table-header-ink Text colour of the header (default --ui-ink; Kanok: secondary text) --ui-table-sort-hover / --ui-table-sorted-background / --ui-table-sorted-icon - A sortable header: hover fill, the sorted column's fill and arrow (default layer-selected-hover, icon-primary; Kanok: the header fill, an --ui-icon-interactive arrow)"],["Data table","<ui-table-body> · React UiTableBody","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-body-react-uitablebody","Attribute Property Type Default Description use-zebra-styles useZebraStyles boolean false Stripe every second row (the table passes its use-zebra-styles). Method Description updateZebra() Marks the rows even / odd in document order (Carbon _updateZebra), counting only the rows shown (search, page). Event React Description ui-table-body-content-change onUiTableBodyContentChange its rows were added, removed or reordered (the table listens) Slot Description (default) The <ui-table-row>s"],["Data table","<ui-table-row> · React UiTableRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-row-react-uitablerow","Attribute Property Type Default Description even even boolean false A striped row (set by the body with use-zebra-styles). odd odd boolean false An unstriped row of a zebra table (set by the body). selected selected boolean false Chosen (Carbon selected); the table keeps the header's select-all and the batch actions in step. disabled disabled boolean false Can't be chosen. radio radio boolean false A single-choice radio instead of a checkbox (the table's radio sets it). hide-checkbox hideCheckbox boolean false No checkbox in the selection cell (the header row of a radio table). selection-name selectionName string '' Shows the selection cell: the checkbox's name (the table's is-selectable sets one). selection-value selectionValue string '' The checkbox's value. selection-label selectionLabel string '' The checkbox's accessible name; default \\"Select row\\" with the row's first cell. expandable expandable boolean false Has a <ui-table-expanded-row> after it (the table's expandable sets it). expanded expanded boolean false Its expanded row is open. batch-expansion batchExpansion boolean false The header row's chevron opens and closes every row (the table's batch-expansion sets it). filtered filtered boolean false Left out by the table's search. highlighted highlighted boolean false Hovered with its expanded row (the two tint together). paged-out pagedOut boolean false On another page of the table's pagination (the table sets it). Property Type Description expandColumn boolean The table has an expand column: every row gets the cell, expandable ones the chevron. indeterminate boolean The header's select-all is partly checked (some rows chosen); the table sets it. tabStop boolean The radio of a radio table that takes Tab (the chosen row, else the first); the table sets it. pinStart boolean The first column is pinned: the chevron and checkbox cells stick too (the table sets it). filler boolean A filler cell after the cells takes the rest of the row once the columns are resized (the table sets it). grid boolean The table is a grid (an editable column): grid cells, the body's cells and controls out of the Tab order (the table sets it). Method Description toggleExpanded(expanded) Opens or closes, unless the cancelable ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled is canceled. gridCells() The cells the grid's arrow keys move through: the chevron and checkbox cells, then the shown author cells. focusSelection() Focuses this row's selection control (a radio the arrow keys moved to). Event React Description ui-table-row-change-selection onUiTableRowChangeSelection cancelable; detail: { selected } before the row is chosen or released ui-table-row-expando-beingtoggled onUiTableRowExpandoBeingtoggled cancelable; detail: { expanded } before the row opens or closes ui-table-row-expando-toggled onUiTableRowExpandoToggled detail: { expanded } after the row opened or closed Slot Description (default) The row's <ui-table-cell>s Part Description expand-cell The cell of the expand chevron expand-button The chevron button selection-cell The cell of the checkbox or radio Custom property Default Description --ui-table-row-selected Fill of a chosen row (default --ui-layer-accent; Kanok: --ui-highlight) --ui-table-row-thread background-image of a chosen row's first cell, for a mark on its start edge (default none; Kanok: a 3px --ui-border-interactive mark) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Data table","<ui-table-cell> · React UiTableCell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-cell-react-uitablecell","Attribute Property Type Default Description column-hidden columnHidden boolean false Its column is hidden (the table follows the header's column-hidden). pinned pinned 'start' | 'end' | undefined Its column is pinned (the table follows the header's pinned). editable editable TableCellEditor | undefined Its column's editor (the table follows the header's editable). editing editing boolean false The editor is open (the table sets it). Property Type Description draft string The editor's text while editing (the table sets where it starts). editorLabel string The editor's name for screen readers: the column and the row (the table sets it). editorOptions TableEditOption[] A select editor's choices (the header's options). editorError string The header's validate message for the value in the editor. editorValue (read-only) What the editor holds now. Method Description focusEditor(select) Focuses the open editor; select selects a text editor's text (else the caret goes to the end). Slot Description (default) The cell's content Part Description content The box inside the cell that holds its padding edit-icon The pencil of an editable cell editor The input or select while editing error The validate message under the editor Custom property Default Description --ui-table-cell-ink Text colour of a row at rest (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink)"],["Data table","<ui-table-expanded-row> · React UiTableExpandedRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-expanded-row-react-uitableexpandedrow","Attribute Property Type Default Description colspan colSpan number 1 How many columns it spans (the table sets it). expanded expanded boolean false Shown (follows the row before it). filtered filtered boolean false Left out by the table's search, with its row. paged-out pagedOut boolean false On another page, with its row. highlighted highlighted boolean false Hovered with its row. selected selected boolean false Its row is chosen. Property Type Description grid boolean The table is a grid (an editable column): a grid cell (the table sets it). Slot Description (default) The content Part Description cell The full-width cell"],["Data table","<ui-table-header-title> · React UiTableHeaderTitle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-header-title-react-uitableheadertitle","Slot Description (default) The title"],["Data table","<ui-table-header-description> · React UiTableHeaderDescription","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-header-description-react-uitableheaderdescription","Slot Description (default) The description"],["Data table","<ui-table-toolbar> · React UiTableToolbar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-toolbar-react-uitabletoolbar","Slot Description (default) <ui-table-batch-actions> and <ui-table-toolbar-content>"],["Data table","<ui-table-toolbar-content> · React UiTableToolbarContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-toolbar-content-react-uitabletoolbarcontent","Attribute Property Type Default Description has-batch-actions hasBatchActions boolean false The batch actions are showing (rows are chosen). Slot Description (default) The controls"],["Data table","<ui-table-toolbar-search> · React UiTableToolbarSearch","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-toolbar-search-react-uitabletoolbarsearch","Attribute Property Type Default Description persistent persistent boolean false Always open (Carbon persistent). label label string '' Accessible name of the field (visually hidden, as in Carbon). placeholder placeholder string '' value value string '' name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. size size SearchSize 'md' Field height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (tokens --ui-field-height-*). disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. autocomplete autocomplete string 'off' inputmode inputmode string '' Passed to the text box: the virtual keyboard to show (numeric, decimal, email, tel, url, search…). enterkeyhint enterkeyhint string '' Passed to the text box: the label of the virtual keyboard's Enter key (search, send, next, done…). clear-label clearLabel string '' Accessible name of the clear button. required required boolean false Constraint validation like <input type=\\"search\\">: blocks submit and reports in the browser's bubble (Carbon Search has no error line). pattern pattern string '' minlength minlength number | undefined maxlength maxlength number | undefined readonly readonly boolean false Value can be selected and submitted but not changed; no clear button. fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidSearch: the label inside a 64px box. <ui-fluid-form> sets it for every field inside. expandable expandable boolean false Carbon ExpandableSearch: collapsed to its magnifier until opened. expanded expanded boolean false Whether an expandable search is open. Property Type Description willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid until cleared with ''. clear() Empties the field, keeps focus in it and announces the change (input, change, ui-clear). Event React Description change onChange When the value is committed (blur / Enter) or cleared ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } when an expandable search opens or collapses input onInput On every keystroke ui-clear onUiClear After the clear button or Esc emptied the field Part Description base The role=search wrapper input The native search input label The label (visually hidden, as in Carbon; shown inside the box when fluid) magnifier The search icon clear-button The clear button magnifier-button The magnifier of an expandable search Custom property Default Description --ui-field-open-background The box's fill while a search is under way (default the layer's field fill) --ui-field-border Border on every side of the box (default none: Carbon's underline only; Kanok: a 1px outline) --ui-field-disabled-border-color Border colour when disabled (default: the underline transparent) --ui-field-readonly-border-color Border colour when read-only (default: a hairline underline) --ui-field-radius Corner radius of the box (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-field-background Fill of the box (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent) --ui-label-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: 14px semibold) --ui-label-color Colour of the label (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Data table","<ui-table-batch-actions> · React UiTableBatchActions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-batch-actions-react-uitablebatchactions","Attribute Property Type Default Description active active boolean false Showing over the toolbar (rows are chosen). selected-rows-count selectedRowsCount number 0 How many rows are chosen (the table sets it; set it yourself for a selection kept across pages). total-rows-count totalRowsCount number 0 Every row there is (server paging): above the count, \\"Select all (N)\\" shows. size size 'xs' | 'sm' | 'lg' 'lg' The table's size, normalized to xs / sm / lg (the table sets it): sizes the action buttons. Property Type Description formatSelectedItemsCount (options: { count: number }) => string | undefined The count text (Carbon formatSelectedItemsCount); default: the translation. Event React Description ui-table-batch-actions-cancel-clicked onUiTableBatchActionsCancelClicked Cancel was clicked (the table releases every row) ui-table-batch-actions-select-all-clicked onUiTableBatchActionsSelectAllClicked \\"Select all (N)\\" was clicked Slot Description (default) The actions (<ui-button>s; the bar sizes them to the toolbar) cancel-button-content Cancel's text (default: the translation) select-all-button-content \\"Select all (N)\\"'s text Part Description batch-summary The selected-count text select-all-button \\"Select all (N)\\" cancel-button Cancel Custom property Default Description --ui-batch-background / --ui-batch-ink / --ui-batch-divider - The bar's fill, text and the rule before Cancel (default Carbon's brand bar: background-brand, text-on-color) --ui-batch-button / --ui-batch-button-ink / --ui-batch-button-hover / --ui-batch-button-active / --ui-batch-focus - Its buttons and their focus ring (default the primary button's colours, a layer-coloured ring)"],["Data table","<ui-table-column-settings> · React UiTableColumnSettings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-column-settings-react-uitablecolumnsettings","Part Description button The toolbar action panel The \\"Columns\\" list"],["Data table","<ui-table-csv-export> · React UiTableCsvExport","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-csv-export-react-uitablecsvexport","Attribute Property Type Default Description file-name fileName string '' The downloaded file's name (.csv is added); default: the table's title, else \\"table\\". Event React Description ui-table-csv-export onUiTableCsvExport cancelable; detail: { csv, rows, fileName } before the download Part Description button The toolbar action"],["Data table","<ui-table-skeleton> · React UiTableSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/data-table/#ui-table-skeleton-react-uitableskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description column-count columnCount number 5 row-count rowCount number 5 show-header showHeader boolean true The title / description bars (Carbon show-header; show-header=\\"false\\" hides them). show-toolbar showToolbar boolean true The toolbar bar (Carbon show-toolbar; show-toolbar=\\"false\\" hides it). zebra zebra boolean false Stripe every second row. Property Type Description headers string[] Header texts to show instead of bars (Carbon headers); their number sets the columns. Part Description table The <table>"],["Structured list","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/","A structured list shows a few rows of text in columns, for example to compare plans or to show the terms of a contract. It is lighter than a data table: no sorting, no toolbar. With selection, the user picks one row."],["Structured list","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Structured list","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#use-it",""],["Structured list","Structured list or data table?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#structured-list-or-data-table","Component Use it when Structured list A handful of rows to read or compare, or to pick one from. The cells wrap and hold any text. Data table Many rows: the user sorts, searches, selects several rows or pages through them. Contained list One column of items with an action each, in a panel or a tile."],["Structured list","A header row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#a-header-row","head on the first row makes its cells column headers (bold, columnheader). Leave it out for a list of label–value pairs where the first column already says what each row is."],["Structured list","Long text and nowrap","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#long-text-and-nowrap","Cells wrap their text, up to 576px wide each. nowrap keeps a cell on one line: use it on short cells such as names and amounts, so a long cell beside them wraps instead."],["Structured list","Condensed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#condensed","condensed halves the cell padding (Carbon's condensed list). Use it for many short rows, for example in a side panel."],["Structured list","Flush","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#flush","flush removes the padding before the first column, so the text lines up with the heading or the text above the list. It has no effect with selection, whose radio column needs the padding."],["Structured list","Pick one row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#pick-one-row","selection turns the body rows into a single choice: each row gets a radio in a leading cell. A click anywhere on the row, Space or the arrow keys select it. Give each row a value; the list's value holds the chosen one, and ui-change (onChange in React + Tailwind) fires when the user picks another row. React + Tailwind also takes defaultValue for an uncontrolled list. Without a value (or with one no row has), no row is selected and Tab stops on the first row."],["Structured list","Change the choice from your code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#change-the-choice-from-your-code","Set value to select a row from your own code, for example from a \\"Use the recommended plan\\" button. Setting it doesn't fire ui-change: that event is for the user's own picks."],["Structured list","Names for screen readers","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#names-for-screen-readers","label names the table (default: \\"Structured list section\\"). In a selection list, each row's radio is named by the row's text; when that text is long, give the row a short aria-label. selection-label (selectionLabel in React + Tailwind) names the radio column (default: \\"Select\\")."],["Structured list","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#skeleton","While the rows load, show ui-structured-list-skeleton: a header of three bars and rows empty rows (default 5). It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/structured-list-skeleton."],["Structured list","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#accessibility","The list is a role=\\"table\\" with row, cell and columnheader roles; React + Tailwind renders a real <table>. In a selection list, the rows' radios form one group: Tab reaches the selected row (else the first), and the arrow keys move and select, wrapping at the ends. Each radio says \\"1 of 3\\". The selected row is aria-selected. Focus draws a 2px outline around the whole row. A selection list isn't a form field: read value and send it yourself. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Structured list."],["Structured list","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Structured list","<ui-structured-list> · React UiStructuredList","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#ui-structured-list-react-uistructuredlist","Attribute Property Type Default Description selection selection boolean false condensed condensed boolean false flush flush boolean false value value string '' Selected row's value (selection lists). label label string '' selection-label selectionLabel string '' Screen-reader name of the radio column (selection lists). Method Description focus(options) Selection lists: focus the selected (or first) row's radio. Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { value } when the user selects another row Slot Description (default) <ui-structured-list-row> elements (first one usually head)"],["Structured list","<ui-structured-list-row> · React UiStructuredListRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#ui-structured-list-row-react-uistructuredlistrow","Attribute Property Type Default Description head head boolean false value value string '' Identifies the row in the list's value / ui-change. selected selected boolean false Set by the list. data-selection selection boolean false Set by the list: selection mode renders the radio cell. data-condensed condensed boolean false Set by the list. data-flush flush boolean false Set by the list. Property Type Description focusable boolean Set by the list: the hidden radio is the row's tab stop. selectionLabel string Set by the list: screen-reader name of the radio column header. position number Set by the list: position among the selectable rows and their count. Each radio sits in its own shadow root, so the browser would count \\"1 of 1\\". Method Description focus(options) Focus the row's radio (selection lists). Event React Description ui-row-select none (use a ref) Slot Description (default) <ui-structured-list-cell> elements Part Description radio-cell The leading cell with the radio icon (selection lists) Custom property Default Description --ui-structured-list-selected Fill of the chosen row of a selection list (default --ui-surface-2; Kanok: --ui-highlight)"],["Structured list","<ui-structured-list-cell> · React UiStructuredListCell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#ui-structured-list-cell-react-uistructuredlistcell","Attribute Property Type Default Description head head boolean false Set by the row: this cell is a column header. nowrap nowrap boolean false Slot Description (default) Cell content"],["Structured list","<ui-structured-list-skeleton> · React UiStructuredListSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/structured-list/#ui-structured-list-skeleton-react-uistructuredlistskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description rows rows number 5 Part Description header The header bars row Each empty row"],["Pagination","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/","Pagination splits a long list into pages: \\"Items per page\\", the range shown, a page select and previous / next buttons (Carbon Pagination). Put it under a table or a list. It only holds the page and the page size; showing the right rows is your code's."],["Pagination","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Pagination","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#use-it",""],["Pagination","Pagination or pagination nav?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#pagination-or-pagination-nav","Component Use it when Pagination Under a table or a list of data: the user picks the page size and jumps to any page. The total may be unknown. Pagination nav Page numbers as links, for search results or an article list, where each page has its own URL. A data table has this pagination built in: set its page-size."],["Pagination","Page and page size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#page-and-page-size","page (from 1) and page-size set where the bar starts; page-sizes lists the page-size choices (default 10,25,50). ui-change fires with { page, pageSize } after the user changes either. A new page size goes back to page 1, as in Carbon. React + Tailwind takes pageSizes as an array of numbers, and defaultPage / defaultPageSize when the bar keeps the state itself."],["Pagination","Show the rows of the page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#show-the-rows-of-the-page","Slice your rows with the page and the page size from ui-change. When the data comes from a server, ask it for that page instead and keep total-items at the server's count."],["Pagination","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. Match the rows of the table above it."],["Pagination","A fixed page size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#a-fixed-page-size","An empty page-sizes hides \\"Items per page\\" when the page size is fixed, for example in a narrow panel."],["Pagination","Total unknown","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#total-unknown","With pages-unknown the bar doesn't need total-items: the page select becomes plain text (\\"page 3\\") and the range has no total. Use it with cursor-based APIs that only say whether there is a next page. Set is-last-page when the server says there is none, so Next disables."],["Pagination","Texts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#texts","Every text can be replaced. The range and page texts are templates: {min}, {max}, {total} and {page} are filled in. Without them the bar uses its translation, in English or Thai from the page's lang. An empty text shows nothing, as in Carbon. item-text is the range while the total is unknown ({min}–{max} items)."],["Pagination","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#disabled","disabled turns off both selects and both buttons, for example while the next page loads."],["Pagination","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#accessibility","The page-size select has a visible label; the page select is named \\"Page number\\" (page-select-label). The arrows are named \\"Previous page\\" and \\"Next page\\" (previous-label, next-label). On the first or last page the pressed arrow disables, and focus moves to the other one instead of falling to the page. The selects are native, so the browser's own keys and the phone's picker work. Tell screen reader users that the rows changed, for example with a polite status line (\\"Showing 21–40 of 230\\"). Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Pagination."],["Pagination","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Pagination","<ui-pagination> · React UiPagination","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination/#ui-pagination-react-uipagination","Attribute Property Type Default Description page page number 1 1-based current page. page-size pageSize number 10 page-sizes pageSizes string '10,25,50' Choices for the page-size select, e.g. \\"10,25,50\\". Empty hides the select. total-items totalItems number 0 pages-unknown pagesUnknown boolean false Total unknown: no page select, next never disabled (Carbon pagesUnknown). is-last-page isLastPage boolean false With pages-unknown: this is the last page, so Next is disabled (Carbon isLastPage; cursor-based APIs). size size PaginationSize 'md' disabled disabled boolean false items-per-page-text itemsPerPageText string | undefined item-range-text itemRangeText string | undefined item-text itemText string | undefined Range text while the total is unknown. page-range-text pageRangeText string | undefined page-text pageText string | undefined Label of each page option and the page text while unknown. page-select-label pageSelectLabel string | undefined previous-label previousLabel string | undefined next-label nextLabel string | undefined Method Description focus(options) Focus the first control that shows (the page-size select; narrow, an arrow). Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { page, pageSize } after the user changed either Part Description base The bar page-size-select The items-per-page select range The item range text page-select The page select pages The \\"of N pages\\" text previous-button Previous page next-button Next page Custom property Default Description --ui-pagination-border / --ui-pagination-background / --ui-pagination-divider - The bar's top rule, fill and the rules between its parts (default hairline, the layer, hairline; Kanok: open, undivided) --ui-pagination-gap / --ui-pagination-range-ink - Space within each side and the range text colour (default none, ink) --ui-pagination-select-border / --ui-pagination-select-radius / --ui-pagination-button-radius - The selects' outline and corners, the arrows' corners (default none, 0, 0; Kanok: outlined 6px selects, round arrows) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Contained list","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/","A contained list is a titled list of rows separated by thin rules, for settings panels, side panels and tiles (Carbon ContainedList). A row can carry an icon and an action, or be a button itself."],["Contained list","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Contained list","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#use-it",""],["Contained list","On the page or in a layer","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#on-the-page-or-in-a-layer","kind=\\"on-page\\" (the default) has a 48px header in the heading style, on the page background. kind=\\"disclosed\\" has a small 32px label on the layer: use it inside a tile, a side panel or under a disclosure. On-page lists that follow each other sit 16px apart."],["Contained list","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#sizes","size sets the row height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (the default), xl 64px. An on-page header takes the same height."],["Contained list","Icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#icons","Put a 16px icon in a row's icon slot (icon in React + Tailwind). It sits before the text and takes Carbon's icon colour."],["Contained list","An action on each row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#an-action-on-each-row","The action slot (action in React + Tailwind) holds a control at the row's end, such as a small icon button. It stays a control of its own: pressing it doesn't press the row. Here Remove takes the row out. When a row goes away, move focus to a nearby row's control, as the demo does, so keyboard users don't land at the top of the page."],["Contained list","Tags and other trailing content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#tags-and-other-trailing-content","The action slot also takes non-interactive content, such as a status tag. Give it a small margin so it lines up with the text. React + Tailwind centres the action in the row by itself, so the tag only needs the end margin."],["Contained list","Clickable rows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#clickable-rows","clickable makes the whole row a button: it fires ui-click when pressed (onClick in React + Tailwind makes the row a button). disabled greys a clickable row out. A clickable row can still have an action: the action stays a separate button beside it."],["Contained list","Search in the header","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#search-in-the-header","The header's action slot also takes a search. An expandable search stays a magnifier until it is pressed. Filter the rows yourself as the user types."],["Contained list","Inset rules","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#inset-rules","inset stops the rules between rows at the row padding instead of running edge to edge (Carbon isInset). It reads lighter in a tile."],["Contained list","A rich label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#a-rich-label","For markup in the header, such as a count, put it in the label slot instead of the label attribute. React + Tailwind takes markup in label."],["Contained list","The current row and list","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#the-current-row-and-list","Beyond Carbon: current on a row marks the one the user is on, with the side nav's \\"you are here\\" look (a fill and a bar on the start edge, aria-current). current on a list marks it among several, such as the board on screen: its header takes the same fill and bar."],["Contained list","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#accessibility","The rows are a role=\\"list\\" of listitems, named by the header label (aria-labelledby). React + Tailwind renders a real <ul> and <li>s. A clickable row is a native <button>: Tab reaches it, Enter and Space press it. A disabled row is skipped. Name every icon-only action with its row, for example \\"Remove Appendix A.pdf\\", so the buttons differ for screen reader users. The header stays at the top while the list scrolls in a box (position: sticky)."],["Contained list","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Contained list","<ui-contained-list> · React UiContainedList","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#ui-contained-list-react-uicontainedlist","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' kind kind ContainedListKind 'on-page' size size ContainedListSize 'lg' inset inset boolean false Rules stop at the row padding instead of running edge to edge (Carbon isInset). current current boolean false Beyond Carbon: the list the user is on, among several (aria-current=\\"true\\" on the list, the side nav's fill and bar on the header). Slot Description (default) <ui-contained-list-item> elements label Rich label action Header action (search, icon button) Part Description header The sticky header row label The label action The header action wrapper list The role=list container Custom property Default Description --ui-nav-current-mark / --ui-nav-current-mark-width / --ui-nav-current-mark-inset / --ui-nav-current-mark-radius - The current list's header bar, the side nav's settings (default primary, 3px, 0, 0); --ui-nav-current-background its fill (default --ui-canvas-selected)"],["Contained list","<ui-contained-list-item> · React UiContainedListItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/contained-list/#ui-contained-list-item-react-uicontainedlistitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description clickable clickable boolean false Render the row as a button. disabled disabled boolean false current current boolean false Beyond Carbon: the row the user is on (aria-current=\\"true\\", the side nav's current-page look). Event React Description ui-click onUiClick Clickable rows, when activated Slot Description (default) Row content icon 16px icon action Trailing action Part Description content The row body (a button when clickable) action The action wrapper Custom property Default Description --ui-nav-current-background / --ui-nav-current-mark - The current row's fill and start bar, the side nav's settings (default canvas-selected, primary; Kanok: the highlight tint, no bar) --ui-nav-current-mark-width / --ui-nav-current-mark-inset / --ui-nav-current-mark-radius - The bar's width (3px), top and bottom inset (0) and corners (0)"],["Tree view","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/","A tree view shows nested items, such as folders, a chart of accounts or an organisation's departments (Carbon TreeView). Branches open and close; the user selects a node with a click or the keyboard."],["Tree view","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tree view","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#use-it","A node with child nodes is a branch. value identifies a node in the selection; without it the label does."],["Tree view","Icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#icons","Put a 16px icon in a node's icon slot (icon in React + Tailwind). Carbon uses a folder for branches and a document for leaves."],["Tree view","Rich labels and content at the end of the row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#rich-labels-and-content-at-the-end-of-the-row","Put markup in the label slot when the label needs more than text (React + Tailwind: label takes a node, as Carbon React's TreeNode); the label attribute stays the plain-text fallback. Beyond Carbon, the end slot (end prop) holds what belongs at the end of the row, such as an amount: it stays whole and lines up at the end while a long label is cut with an ellipsis. Screen readers read the label as the node's name and the end content as its description, and typing a letter still finds nodes by their label."],["Tree view","Selection and the active node","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#selection-and-the-active-node","A click, Space or Enter selects a node and makes it the active one (a 4px bar at its start). ui-select fires with { selected, value } after the selection changes, ui-activate with { active }. Set selected (a property: an array of values) and active to start with a node chosen; open its branches so it shows."],["Tree view","Select several nodes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#select-several-nodes","With multiselect, Ctrl / ⌘ + click and Space add a node to the selection or take it out, and Ctrl + A selects every node. A plain click still selects only that node."],["Tree view","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#sizes","size: sm 32px rows (the default) or xs 24px for dense trees."],["Tree view","Disabled nodes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#disabled-nodes","disabled shows a node but blocks it: it can't be selected or opened, and the arrow keys skip it."],["Tree view","Open and close branches from code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#open-and-close-branches-from-code","expanded opens a branch. Set it from your code, for example for an \\"Expand all\\" button; ui-toggle fires with { expanded, value } each time a branch opens or closes (onToggle on a React + Tailwind TreeNode). ui-toggle bubbles, so one listener on the tree hears every node."],["Tree view","Links","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#links","href turns a node's label into a link. Enter or a click follows it. In a single-page app, listen for ui-navigate (cancelable, { href }) and route yourself. React + Tailwind renders a plain <a>; route clicks with your router's own link handling."],["Tree view","Load children on demand","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#load-children-on-demand","lazy makes a node a branch before it has children. The first time it opens, a spinner replaces the caret and ui-lazy-load fires with its value: fetch the children and append them as <ui-tree-node>s. With nothing to add, set lazy = false and it becomes a leaf; after a failed load, set loading = false and it closes so the user can try again. TreeNodeElement is import type { UiTreeNode as TreeNodeElement } from '@purpurabog/ui'."],["Tree view","A hidden label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#a-hidden-label","hide-label (hideLabel in React + Tailwind) keeps the label for screen readers only, when a heading above the tree already names it."],["Tree view","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves into the tree and out of it: the tree is one Tab stop (the node focused last, else the selected one, else the first) Up / Down Previous / next visible node Home / End First / last visible node Right Opens a closed branch; on an open one, moves to its first child Left Closes an open branch; on a closed one or a leaf, moves to its parent Enter Opens or closes a branch, selects the node and follows its link Space Selects the node; in a multiselect tree, adds or removes it Ctrl / ⌘ + A Selects every node (multiselect) A letter Moves to the next visible node whose label starts with it"],["Tree view","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#accessibility","The tree is a role=\\"tree\\" of treeitems, with aria-expanded on branches and aria-selected on every node. Each branch's children are a group named by its row. label names the tree. The caret is hidden from screen readers: the keys above do its job. A loading node is aria-busy and says \\"Loading\\". Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Tree view."],["Tree view","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tree view","<ui-tree-view> · React UiTreeView","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#ui-tree-view-react-uitreeview","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' hide-label hideLabel boolean false size size TreeViewSize 'sm' multiselect multiselect boolean false active active string '' The node that was last activated (4px marker). Property Type Description selected string[] Selected node values. nodes UiTreeNode[] (read-only) Every node, document order. Event React Description ui-select onUiSelect detail: { selected: string[], value } after a selection change ui-activate onUiActivate detail: { active } when a node becomes the active one Slot Description (default) Top-level <ui-tree-node>s Part Description label The tree label tree The role=tree container Custom property Default Description --ui-tree-selected / --ui-tree-mark - The selected row's fill and mark (on <ui-tree-node>, with the other --ui-tree-* settings)"],["Tree view","<ui-tree-node> · React UiTreeNode","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tree-view/#ui-tree-node-react-uitreenode","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' value value string '' Identifies the node in selected / active; defaults to label. expanded expanded boolean false disabled disabled boolean false href href string '' lazy lazy boolean false A branch whose children aren't loaded yet: it shows a caret and fires ui-lazy-load when first expanded. loading loading boolean false The children are being fetched; set by the node when a lazy branch opens, cleared when children arrive. Property Type Description depth number Set by the tree. isBranch (read-only) Has child nodes, or is lazy and will have them. treeValue (read-only) What identifies the node in the tree's selected / active: value, else label, else the label slot's text. (Was nodeValue, which shadowed DOM Node.nodeValue.) labelText (read-only) The label as text, which type-ahead matches: the label slot's text when it is used, else label. childTreeNodes UiTreeNode[] (read-only) Direct child nodes. parentTreeNode UiTreeNode | null (read-only) The enclosing node, or null at the top level. Method Description toggle(expanded) Expand / collapse (branches only, including lazy ones). Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded, value } when the branch opens / closes ui-lazy-load onUiLazyLoad detail: { value } when a lazy node is expanded and its children should be fetched ui-navigate onUiNavigate detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Child nodes icon 16px icon before the label label Rich label (Carbon React's label node): replaces the label text, which stays the plain-text fallback end Beyond Carbon: content at the end of the row (an amount, a count, a badge), kept whole while the label truncates; it then describes the node, which the label alone names Part Description label The row toggle The caret button (branches) children The role=group container end The end content's wrapper (beyond Carbon) Custom property Default Description --ui-tree-background / --ui-tree-row-radius - Row fill and corners (default the layer, 0; Kanok: transparent, 6px) --ui-tree-selected / --ui-tree-selected-hover - The selected row's fill and its hover (default layer-selected, layer-selected-hover; Kanok: the highlight tint) --ui-tree-mark / --ui-tree-mark-width / --ui-tree-mark-inset / --ui-tree-mark-radius - The selected row's start mark (default interactive, 4px, full height, square; Kanok: none, the tint alone — forced colours still show it) --ui-tree-pointer-outline The ring of a node focused by a click, not the keyboard (default the focus ring, as Carbon; Kanok: none)"],["Tabs","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/","Tabs split related content into views on one page. One tab is selected at a time, and only its panel shows. A disabled tab stays in the strip but can't be chosen."],["Tabs","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tabs","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#use-it","Each <ui-tab panel> matches the name of a <ui-tab-panel>. Tabs and panels may come in any order in the markup: the tabs go into the strip by themselves. label names the strip for screen readers. In React + Tailwind, the Tabs sit in a TabList (it takes label), and a Tab and its TabPanel share a value."],["Tabs","Tabs, content switcher or accordion?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#tabs-content-switcher-or-accordion","Component Use it when Tabs The views are sections of one item (a contract's terms, parties, history) and the reader looks at one at a time. Content switcher The same content in another form or filter: table or grid, all requests or mine. Accordion A long page of sections the reader may open several of, or read top to bottom."],["Tabs","Starting tab and changes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#starting-tab-and-changes","value is the name of the panel that shows; left out, the first enabled tab is selected. ui-tab-change fires after the user selects another tab, with the panel's name in detail.name. React + Tailwind also takes defaultValue for an uncontrolled start."],["Tabs","Contained","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#contained","type=\\"contained\\" draws 48px tabs on a grey strip with dividers. The selected tab sits on the layer with a blue top edge, and the panels sit on the layer too. Use it where the tabs head a card or a section of their own."],["Tabs","Full width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#full-width","With type=\\"contained\\", full-width (fullWidth) shares the strip in equal columns. A label that doesn't fit ends in an ellipsis."],["Tabs","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the line default), lg 48px (the contained default), xl 64px (contained only; line tabs stop at 48px). The three strips above have no panels: tabs without a matching panel still select, they just show nothing."],["Tabs","Icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#icons","Put a 16px icon in a tab's icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind). It follows the label and takes its colour. The label still names the tab."],["Tabs","Secondary labels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#secondary-labels","On contained tabs, secondary-label (secondaryLabel) adds a second, smaller line, such as a count. One secondary label makes every tab in the strip 64px tall."],["Tabs","Icon only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#icon-only","icon-only (iconOnly) shows just the icon in a square tab. label is then required: it names the tab and shows as its tooltip on hover and on keyboard focus. With size=\\"lg\\" the icons grow to 20px."],["Tabs","Manual activation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#manual-activation","By default the arrow keys select as they move (activation=\\"automatic\\"). With activation=\\"manual\\", the arrows only move focus, and Enter or Space selects. Use it when a panel is slow to render or loads data."],["Tabs","An action at the end of the strip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#an-action-at-the-end-of-the-strip","The end slot (the end prop of TabList in React + Tailwind) puts content after the tabs, on the strip's line, for example a ghost button that adds a section."],["Tabs","Keep the current tab","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#keep-the-current-tab","ui-tab-before-change fires before the selection moves, with detail.name (the new tab) and detail.previous. Call preventDefault() to keep the current tab, for example while a form in it has unsaved changes. In React + Tailwind, keep value as it is in onValueChange."],["Tabs","Dismissable tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#dismissable-tabs","dismissable gives every tab a close button, and Delete closes the focused tab. The tab first fires a cancelable ui-request-close (detail.name); unless you prevent it, the tab is hidden and fires ui-close. A closed selected tab passes the selection to the first enabled tab, and focus moves to the tab now in its place. Not with vertical. In React + Tailwind, onTabCloseRequest gets the tab's value: remove that tab from your list to close it."],["Tabs","Vertical tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#vertical-tabs","vertical puts the tabs in a column beside the panels once the window is wider than 672px (42rem); on a narrower window they become contained tabs in a row. Labels wrap to two lines, then end in an ellipsis. height fixes the height: the tab list and the panels then scroll inside it. In the column, ↑ and ↓ move between the tabs, and the panels sit one layer up, so their fields keep their contrast."],["Tabs","Many tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#many-tabs","When the tabs don't fit, the strip scrolls. Previous and next buttons appear at its ends for the mouse; keyboard users have the arrow keys, so the buttons are no Tab stops and are hidden from screen readers."],["Tabs","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#skeleton","While the page loads, ui-tabs-skeleton stands in for the strip: tabs bars of 160 × 40px (5 by default). It is hidden from screen readers. On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/tabs-skeleton."],["Tabs","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#accessibility","The strip is a tablist named by label; each tab is a tab with aria-selected and aria-controls, and each panel a tabpanel labelled by its tab. One Tab stop: Tab reaches the selected tab, then moves into the panel. ← and → move between tabs and wrap (↑ and ↓ in a vertical column); Home and End jump to the first and last. Disabled tabs are skipped. A panel with nothing focusable inside becomes a Tab stop itself, so keyboard users can reach and scroll its text. Icon-only tabs need label: it is the tab's name and its tooltip. In dismissable tabs the close button is hidden from screen readers; each tab announces Delete as its shortcut (aria-keyshortcuts). Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Tabs."],["Tabs","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tabs","<ui-tabs> · React UiTabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#ui-tabs-react-uitabs","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' Name of the active panel. Defaults to the first enabled tab. label label string '' Accessible name for the tab strip, e.g. \\"Product details\\". activation activation TabsActivation 'automatic' automatic (Carbon's name; auto is still accepted) or manual. type type TabsType 'line' line (default) or contained (Carbon cds-tabs type=\\"contained\\"). size size TabsSize | undefined Tab height (Carbon size): sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px, xl 64px (contained only); unset = md for line, lg for contained. full-width fullWidth boolean false With type=\\"contained\\": the tabs share the full width in equal columns (Carbon full-width / fullWidth). vertical vertical boolean false Carbon TabsVertical: the tabs in a column beside the panels from md up (contained tabs in a row below). height height string '' A fixed height for vertical tabs (Carbon height), e.g. \\"400px\\": the tab list and the panels then scroll. dismissable dismissable boolean false A close button on every tab, and Delete closes the focused tab (Carbon dismissable); not with vertical. Method Description focus(options) Focus the active tab (the tablist's tab stop). Event React Description ui-tab-change onUiTabChange detail: { name } after the user selects a tab ui-tab-before-change onUiTabBeforeChange Cancelable; detail: { name, previous }. preventDefault() keeps the current tab (e.g. unsaved changes). ui-request-close onUiRequestClose From a <ui-tab> of dismissable tabs (close button or Delete); cancelable; detail: { name }. preventDefault() keeps the tab. ui-close onUiClose From a <ui-tab> after it closed (hidden); detail: { name } Slot Description nav <ui-tab> elements (assigned automatically) (default) <ui-tab-panel> elements end Content at the end of the strip, e.g. an action button Part Description base The strip holding the tab list and scroll buttons tablist The role=tablist container (tabs themselves are light-DOM <ui-tab>s: style the element) scroll-button The overflow scroll buttons end Wrapper of the end slot Custom property Default Description --ui-tabs-track box-shadow of the tab strip, for one line under every tab (default none; Kanok: a 1px hairline) --ui-tabs-gap Gap between line tabs (default 1px; Kanok: 4px) --ui-tabs-contained-height Tab height of type=\\"contained\\" (default 48px; Kanok: 32px) --ui-tabs-contained-track / --ui-tabs-contained-padding / --ui-tabs-contained-radius / --ui-tabs-contained-gap - The track behind contained tabs (default none: Carbon's full-width strip; Kanok: a grey rounded track) --ui-tabs-contained-flex flex of the contained strip (default 1, full width; Kanok: hugs the tabs) --ui-tab-vertical-background The vertical tab list's fill (default the layer; on <ui-tab> with the other --ui-tab-vertical-* settings)"],["Tabs","<ui-tab> · React UiTab","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#ui-tab-react-uitab","Attribute Property Type Default Description hidden panel panel string '' selected selected boolean false disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. secondary-label secondaryLabel string '' A second line under the label (Carbon secondaryLabel); contained tabs only. icon-only iconOnly boolean false Only the icon slot shows (Carbon IconTab); label names the tab and is its tooltip. label label string '' Accessible name and tooltip of an icon-only tab — required with it. Event React Description ui-request-close onUiRequestClose Dismissable tabs: its close button or Delete; cancelable; detail: { name } (its panel) ui-close onUiClose Dismissable tabs: after it closed (now hidden); detail: { name } Slot Description (default) Tab label icon A 16px icon (20px in icon-only tabs of size=\\"lg\\"), coloured like the label Part Description secondary-label The second line of a contained tab close-button The close button of a dismissable tab (no tab stop: Delete closes the focused tab) tooltip The <ui-tooltip> of an icon-only tab Custom property Default Description --ui-tab-line The underline of every tab (default 2px solid --ui-hairline; Kanok: transparent, the strip draws one line) --ui-tab-selected-line The selected tab's mark (default --ui-border-interactive, as in Kanok) --ui-tab-hover-line Underline colour on hover (default --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-tab-disabled-line Underline colour when disabled (default --ui-hairline) --ui-tab-background Fill of a line tab (default --ui-canvas; Kanok: transparent) --ui-tab-contained-background / --ui-tab-contained-hover / --ui-tab-contained-selected - Fills of a contained tab at rest, hovered and selected (Carbon: layer-accent, its hover, the layer) --ui-tab-contained-selected-shadow box-shadow of the selected contained tab (default: a 2px top bar in --ui-tab-selected-line) --ui-tab-contained-radius Corner radius of a contained tab (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-tab-contained-divider The 1px line between contained tabs (default --ui-hairline-strong; Kanok: none) --ui-tab-focus-radius Corner radius of the focus ring (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-tab-focus-offset / --ui-tab-contained-focus-offset - Where the focus ring sits, line and contained tabs (default -2px, over the selected underline; Kanok: -5px, clear of it, and 1px around the chip) --ui-tab-vertical-background / --ui-tab-vertical-selected / --ui-tab-vertical-bar / --ui-tab-vertical-hover-bar / --ui-tab-vertical-divider / --ui-tab-vertical-inset / --ui-tab-vertical-radius - Vertical tabs: fill, the chosen tab's fill, the side bars, the rule between tabs, inset and corners (default Carbon's layer fill with bars and rules; Kanok: inset rounded rows, the chosen one tinted) --ui-tab-vertical-mark The chosen vertical tab's 3px start bar (default --ui-tab-selected-line; Kanok: none, the tint alone) --ui-icon-control-radius Corners of its small icon buttons, their hover fill and ring (default 0; Kanok: round)"],["Tabs","<ui-tab-panel> · React UiTabPanel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#ui-tab-panel-react-uitabpanel","Attribute Property Type Default Description name name string '' Slot Description (default) Panel content"],["Tabs","<ui-tabs-skeleton> · React UiTabsSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tabs/#ui-tabs-skeleton-react-uitabsskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description tabs tabs number 5 Part Description tab Each tab"],["Breadcrumb","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/","A breadcrumb shows where the current page sits in the site's hierarchy, and links back up to each level above it. Put it at the top of the page, above the title."],["Breadcrumb","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Breadcrumb","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#use-it","<ui-breadcrumb> renders a <nav> landmark with an ordered list; each <ui-breadcrumb-item href> is one link in it."],["Breadcrumb","Current page and the trailing slash","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#current-page-and-the-trailing-slash","Every item is followed by a \\"/\\", the last one too, as in Carbon: a trail of links only, with the page title under it, reads as \\"you are inside Contracts\\". When the trail ends with the page the user is on, mark that item current (plain text with aria-current=\\"page\\") and drop the last slash with no-trailing-slash (noTrailingSlash)."],["Breadcrumb","A level without a page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#a-level-without-a-page","An item without href renders as plain text, for a level of the hierarchy that has no page of its own (a group in the menu, say). Unlike current, it doesn't claim to be the page the user is on."],["Breadcrumb","Small","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#small","size=\\"sm\\" uses the 12px label type and a 4px gap around the slashes. Use it in dense headers and side panels."],["Breadcrumb","Long trails wrap","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#long-trails-wrap","A trail that doesn't fit wraps onto the next line; each item stays on one line. To keep it on one line, set the CSS custom property --ui-breadcrumb-wrap: nowrap, or collapse it with overflow (next section)."],["Breadcrumb","Collapse a long trail","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#collapse-a-long-trail","overflow keeps the trail on one line: the crumbs that don't fit go, from the end, into a \\"…\\" menu just before the last crumb, which always stays. The first crumbs stay as long as they fit. Choosing a crumb in the menu follows its link. overflow-label (overflowLabel) names the menu button (default \\"More breadcrumbs\\"). Make the box narrower or wider to see the menu change."],["Breadcrumb","Route in a single-page app","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#route-in-a-single-page-app","A plain click on an item's link first fires a cancelable ui-navigate with detail.href, bubbling out of the breadcrumb. Call preventDefault() and hand the path to your router; Ctrl-, ⌘- and middle-clicks stay normal links. In React put onUiNavigate once on UiBreadcrumb (or on a single UiBreadcrumbItem). In React + Tailwind the items are plain <a>s: route in their onClick."],["Breadcrumb","Name the landmark","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#name-the-landmark","The <nav> is named \\"Breadcrumb\\" (translated with the page's language). When a page has two trails, or the default name doesn't fit, set label."],["Breadcrumb","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#skeleton","While the trail loads, ui-breadcrumb-skeleton shows items bars of 100 × 16px (3 by default), each followed by a slash. It takes size and no-trailing-slash like the breadcrumb, and is hidden from screen readers. On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/breadcrumb-skeleton."],["Breadcrumb","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#accessibility","The trail is a <nav> landmark named \\"Breadcrumb\\" (or label) holding an ordered list, so screen readers announce how many levels it has. The current page is text with aria-current=\\"page\\", not a link to itself. The slashes are drawn by CSS and aren't read out. Each link is a Tab stop. In a collapsed trail the \\"…\\" button is one more; its menu lists the hidden crumbs."],["Breadcrumb","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Breadcrumb","<ui-breadcrumb> · React UiBreadcrumb","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#ui-breadcrumb-react-uibreadcrumb","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Accessible name of the navigation landmark. no-trailing-slash noTrailingSlash boolean false size size BreadcrumbSize 'md' overflow overflow boolean false On one line, the crumbs that don't fit go into a \\"…\\" menu before the last one. overflow-label overflowLabel string '' The overflow menu's name (default: the translation's \\"More breadcrumbs\\"). Method Description focus(options) Focus the first crumb's link. Slot Description (default) <ui-breadcrumb-item> elements Part Description base The <nav> list The <ol> overflow The \\"…\\" item holding the overflow menu (overflow only) Custom property Default Description --ui-breadcrumb-wrap nowrap keeps the trail on one line (the page header's bar does)"],["Breadcrumb","<ui-breadcrumb-item> · React UiBreadcrumbItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#ui-breadcrumb-item-react-uibreadcrumbitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '' current current boolean false The page the user is on: plain text with aria-current=\\"page\\". Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) The item text Part Description base The link or the current-page text Custom property Default Description --ui-breadcrumb-trailing-slash display of the slash after the last item (default inline; Kanok: none)"],["Breadcrumb","<ui-breadcrumb-skeleton> · React UiBreadcrumbSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/breadcrumb/#ui-breadcrumb-skeleton-react-uibreadcrumbskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description items items number 3 no-trailing-slash noTrailingSlash boolean false size size 'sm' | 'md' 'md' Part Description item Each bar"],["Link","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/","A link takes the user to another page, another place on this page, or a file. It is blue, underlines on hover and focus, and has Carbon's focus ring."],["Link","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Link","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#use-it",""],["Link","Link or button?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#link-or-button","Component Use it when Link It goes somewhere: a page, a section of this page, a file. The browser's own link features work (open in a new tab, copy the address). Button It does something here: submits a form, opens a modal, starts an export. When an action must look like a button but go to a page, use a button with href; see Button."],["Link","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#sizes","size: sm 12px (helper text), md 14px (the default), lg 16px. Match the text around the link."],["Link","Inside a sentence","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#inside-a-sentence","inline underlines the link at rest, so it stands out in running text where colour alone isn't enough. An inline link shows no icon."],["Link","With an icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#with-an-icon","Put a 16px icon in the icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind): it sits 8px after the text, in the link's colour, and grows to 20px with size=\\"lg\\". Use it for standalone links, such as \\"View all\\" at the end of a list."],["Link","Open in a new tab","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#open-in-a-new-tab","target=\\"_blank\\" opens the page in a new tab, and the link adds rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\" unless you set rel. Say so in the text or with Carbon's Launch icon, so the new tab doesn't surprise anyone."],["Link","Download a file","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#download-a-file","download makes the link save its target instead of opening it; its value is the file name. Name the type and size in the text. (The docs site has no such file, so this demo builds one in the browser.)"],["Link","Visited links","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#visited-links","visited turns on Carbon's visited colour (purple) for links the browser has visited. Use it in lists the user works through, such as search results. Click the link, then look at it again."],["Link","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#disabled","disabled renders grey text with role=\\"link\\" and aria-disabled=\\"true\\": it isn't a link any more and takes no focus. Prefer leaving the link out, or explain next to it why it is unavailable."],["Link","Route in a single-page app","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#route-in-a-single-page-app","A plain click (main button, no modifier key, same tab, same site, not a download) first fires a cancelable ui-navigate with detail.href. Call preventDefault() and hand the path to your router; the browser then doesn't load the page. Ctrl-, ⌘- and middle-clicks stay normal links. The React + Tailwind Link is a plain <a>: route in its onClick, or wrap your router's link."],["Link","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#accessibility","The link is a real <a href>: Enter follows it, and the browser's menu (open in a new tab, copy the address) works. Write text that makes sense on its own (\\"Download the contract checklist\\", not \\"Click here\\"): screen reader users often move from link to link. Icons in the icon slot are decoration; give them aria-hidden=\\"true\\" and keep the meaning in the text. A disabled link is announced as a dimmed link but takes no focus, so keyboard users never reach it. Say why it is unavailable in nearby text. inline underlines links inside sentences, so they don't rely on colour alone."],["Link","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Link","<ui-link> · React UiLink","/kanok-ui-docs/en/link/#ui-link-react-uilink","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '' target target string '' rel rel string '' download download string '' size size LinkSize 'md' inline inline boolean false Underlined at rest, for links inside a sentence. visited visited boolean false Opt into Carbon's visited colour (browser :visited). disabled disabled boolean false Renders as inert text with aria-disabled. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Link text icon A 16px (lg: 20px) icon after the text (Carbon renderIcon; not shown when inline) Part Description base The anchor icon The icon wrapper Custom property Default Description --ui-link-focus-radius Corners of the focus ring (default 0; Kanok: 4px)"],["Pagination nav","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/","Pagination nav moves between numbered pages: Previous, the page numbers, and Next. The pages that don't fit fold into \\"…\\" menus at either end. page is 0-based, as in Carbon."],["Pagination nav","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Pagination nav","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#use-it","total-items is the number of pages (Carbon's name)."],["Pagination nav","Pagination or pagination nav?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#pagination-or-pagination-nav","Component Use it when Pagination Under a data table: the user picks how many rows a page shows and sees \\"1–10 of 240 items\\". Pagination nav Numbered pages of content that reads like a book: search results, a long report, the pages of a scanned contract."],["Pagination nav","Starting page and changes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#starting-page-and-changes","page is the current page, 0-based: page=\\"3\\" shows page 4. ui-change fires after the user chose another page, with the 0-based page in detail.page. React + Tailwind also takes defaultPage for an uncontrolled start."],["Pagination nav","Every page fits","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#every-page-fits","With as many pages as items-shown or fewer, every number shows and there are no \\"…\\" menus."],["Pagination nav","How many items show","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#how-many-items-show","items-shown (itemsShown) is how many page items the row holds, the \\"…\\" menus included: 10 by default, 4 at least. Lower it where the row has little room. On a window narrower than 320px, the row falls back to fewer items by itself."],["Pagination nav","Wrap around","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#wrap-around","With loop, Previous on the first page goes to the last one, and Next on the last page to the first. Without it, they are disabled at the ends."],["Pagination nav","Turn off the \\"…\\" menus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#turn-off-the-menus","disable-overflow (disableOverflow) keeps the \\"…\\" in the row but stops it from opening. The user then moves with Previous, Next and the numbers shown."],["Pagination nav","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px (the default). Previous and Next follow the same size."],["Pagination nav","Tooltip placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#tooltip-placement","Previous and Next are icon buttons: their name shows as a tooltip on hover and focus, below them by default. tooltip-placement (tooltipPlacement) moves it, for example above a row that sits at the bottom of the window."],["Pagination nav","Page through a list","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#page-through-a-list","The component only says which page to show; slicing the content is yours. Here 12 contracts show three per page."],["Pagination nav","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#accessibility","The row is a <nav> landmark named \\"Pagination\\" (translated), holding a list. Each page is a button that screen readers read as \\"Page 4\\"; the current one reads \\"Active, Page 4\\" and has aria-current=\\"page\\". Each \\"…\\" is a <select> named \\"Select page number\\": the keyboard and phones open it like any select. After a change, a polite live region says \\"Page 5 of 25\\". Previous and Next are icon buttons named \\"Previous\\" and \\"Next\\", with tooltips; they are disabled at the ends unless loop is on. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Pagination nav."],["Pagination nav","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Pagination nav","<ui-pagination-nav> · React UiPaginationNav","/kanok-ui-docs/en/pagination-nav/#ui-pagination-nav-react-uipaginationnav","Attribute Property Type Default Description page page number 0 The current page, 0-based (Carbon). total-items totalItems number 1 items-shown itemsShown number 10 Page items in the row (at least 4). loop loop boolean false Previous on the first page goes to the last, Next on the last to the first. disable-overflow disableOverflow boolean false The \\"…\\" selects can't be opened. size size NavSize 'lg' tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement TooltipPlacement 'bottom' Where Previous / Next show their tooltip. Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { page } (0-based) after the user chose a page Part Description base The <nav> page Each page button overflow Each \\"…\\" select Custom property Default Description --ui-button-radius Corner radius of the page buttons (the button setting) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside) --ui-pagination-nav-mark-height Height of the current page's underline (default 4px; Kanok: 2px)"],["Content switcher","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/","A content switcher shows the same content in another way: a filter (all requests or only mine) or a view (table or grid). Exactly one item is selected, and the switch happens at once."],["Content switcher","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Content switcher","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#use-it","Name the group with aria-label. The switcher fills the width it is given and shares it evenly between the items. When the items are different sections of one thing (a contract's terms, parties and history), use Tabs instead."],["Content switcher","Switch the content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#switch-the-content","The switcher only reports the choice: ui-change fires with detail.index and detail.name of the item the user selected. Showing the matching content is yours. Put that content right after the switcher."],["Content switcher","Starting item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#starting-item","selected-index (selectedIndex) is the selected item's position, from 0; the first item by default. The switcher updates it as the user chooses. React + Tailwind also takes defaultSelectedIndex for an uncontrolled start."],["Content switcher","With icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#with-icons","A 16px icon in the item's icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind) goes before the text, and takes the item's colours: grey at rest, white when selected."],["Content switcher","Icon only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#icon-only","With icon-only (iconOnly) on every item, each item is a square button and the switcher shrinks to fit them. label is then required: it names the item and shows as its tooltip on hover and keyboard focus. tooltip-placement (tooltipPlacement) moves the tooltip; it shows above by default."],["Content switcher","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#sizes","size: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. Icons grow to 20px in lg. Match the height of the fields and buttons beside it."],["Content switcher","Low contrast","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#low-contrast","low-contrast (lowContrast) is the quieter variant: a grey track, and the selected item a light pill with bold text instead of a dark fill. Use it where a dark selected item would draw too much attention."],["Content switcher","Disabled item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#disabled-item","disabled on an item greys it out; the arrow keys skip it and a click does nothing. While any item is disabled, the track's outline turns grey too, as in Carbon."],["Content switcher","Manual selection","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#manual-selection","By default the arrow keys select as they move (selection-mode=\\"automatic\\"). With selection-mode=\\"manual\\" (selectionMode), they only move focus, and Enter or Space selects. Use it when switching loads data."],["Content switcher","Long labels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#long-labels","Items share the width evenly. A label longer than its share ends in an ellipsis, so keep labels short: one or two words."],["Content switcher","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#accessibility","The switcher is a tablist and each item a tab with aria-selected; name the group with aria-label. One Tab stop: the selected item (or the first enabled one). ← and → move and wrap, skipping disabled items (mirrored right-to-left); Home and End jump to the ends. Enter and Space select in manual mode. The items control no panel (aria-controls): put the content they change right after the switcher, so it is the next thing a keyboard or screen reader user reaches. Icon-only items need label: it is their name and their tooltip. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Content switcher."],["Content switcher","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Content switcher","<ui-content-switcher> · React UiContentSwitcher","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#ui-content-switcher-react-uicontentswitcher","Attribute Property Type Default Description selected-index selectedIndex number 0 size size ContentSwitcherSize 'md' selection-mode selectionMode ContentSwitcherSelectionMode 'automatic' low-contrast lowContrast boolean false icon-only iconOnly boolean false Reflected by the switcher itself when every item is icon-only. Method Description focus(options) Focus the selected item (the tab stop). Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { index, name } after the user selects a different item Slot Description (default) <ui-content-switcher-item> elements Custom property Default Description --ui-content-switcher-border / --ui-content-switcher-selected-fill / --ui-content-switcher-selected-ink - Border, selected fill and selected text of the default kind (default: Carbon's inverse; Kanok: no border, a segment in the page colour with ink text) --ui-content-switcher-track / --ui-content-switcher-padding / --ui-content-switcher-radius / --ui-content-switcher-outline - The track around the items (default transparent, 0, 4px, border-inverse: Carbon's outlined group; Kanok: the contained tabs' segmented track) --ui-content-switcher-item-radius / --ui-content-switcher-item-size / --ui-content-switcher-item-grow / --ui-content-switcher-divider / --ui-content-switcher-selected-shadow - Its items (on <ui-content-switcher-item>)"],["Content switcher","<ui-content-switcher-item> · React UiContentSwitcherItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/content-switcher/#ui-content-switcher-item-react-uicontentswitcheritem","Attribute Property Type Default Description name name string '' Identifies the item in ui-change (Carbon name). label label string '' Accessible name — required with icon-only. selected selected boolean false Set by the switcher from its selected-index (it overwrites any value you set): read it or style on [selected]; select an item with the switcher's selected-index. disabled disabled boolean false icon-only iconOnly boolean false tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement TooltipPlacement 'top' Where the icon-only tooltip shows (Carbon align, default top). Property Type Description focusable boolean Set by the switcher: which item is the single tab stop (the selected one, or the first enabled one). Slot Description (default) Label text icon A 16px icon (20px in size=\\"lg\\") before the text, or alone with icon-only + label Part Description label The label wrapper tooltip The <ui-tooltip> of an icon-only item Custom property Default Description --ui-content-switcher-item-radius / --ui-content-switcher-item-size / --ui-content-switcher-item-grow - Corner radius, inline-size and flex-grow (default 4px, 100%, 0) --ui-content-switcher-divider / --ui-content-switcher-selected-shadow - The rule between items and the selected one's shadow (default hairline, none)"],["Accordion","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/","An accordion is a vertical list of headings. Each heading shows or hides the content under it, so a long page shows only the parts the reader asks for. Several items can be open at once."],["Accordion","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Accordion","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#use-it",""],["Accordion","Open items","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#open-items","open shows an item's content when the page loads (defaultOpen in React + Tailwind). Opening one item doesn't close the others: each item is on its own, as in Carbon."],["Accordion","Headings with markup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#headings-with-markup","heading is plain text. When the heading needs markup (a count, a status, bold text), put it in the title slot instead. In React + Tailwind, title takes any React node."],["Accordion","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#sizes","size sets the height of each heading: sm 32px, md 40px (the default), lg 48px. Set it on the accordion; every item follows."],["Accordion","Chevron at the start","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#chevron-at-the-start","align=\\"start\\" puts the chevron before the heading text. The content then lines up with the text, not with the chevron."],["Accordion","Flush","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#flush","flush removes the dividers at the outer edges and draws the lines between items 16px in from each side (Carbon's isFlush). Use it where the accordion sits inside a tile or a panel that already has an edge. It has no effect with align=\\"start\\"."],["Accordion","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#disabled","disabled on an item greys out its heading; it can't be opened or closed and Tab skips it. disabled on the accordion disables every item; removing it enables them again, except items that have their own disabled."],["Accordion","Know when an item opens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#know-when-an-item-opens","ui-toggle fires on the item after the user opens or closes it, with detail.open. It bubbles, so one listener on the accordion hears every item. Use it to load an item's content the first time it opens, or to remember which items were open. In React + Tailwind, onOpenChange on the item gets the new state."],["Accordion","Expand all, collapse all","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#expand-all-collapse-all","Set open on the items from your code to open or close them together (Carbon's \\"controlled\\" accordion). Setting open doesn't fire ui-toggle: the event is only for the user's own clicks. In React + Tailwind, hold each item's open in state. sections is the same in both React versions."],["Accordion","Fields inside an item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#fields-inside-an-item","An item's content can hold anything, fields included. A filter panel is a common case: each group of filters in its own item, so the list stays short."],["Accordion","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#skeleton","While the items load, show ui-accordion-skeleton: count headings (4 by default), the first one open with three lines. open set to false (in HTML, set the property) shows them all closed, and alignment=\\"start\\" puts the chevron first. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/accordion-skeleton."],["Accordion","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#keyboard","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves between the headings (and into an open item's content); disabled headings are skipped Enter, Space Opens or closes the focused item There are no arrow keys between headings, as in Carbon."],["Accordion","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#accessibility","Each heading is a <button> with aria-expanded and aria-controls pointing at its content. The content is a region named by its heading. The accordion is a list (role=\\"list\\") and each item a list item, as Carbon's <ul> / <li>. The heading button isn't inside an <h2>–<h6>. If the items are sections of the page outline, say so in the text around the accordion. Don't hide the only copy of something the user must read (an error, a required step) in a closed item. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Accordion."],["Accordion","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Accordion","<ui-accordion> · React UiAccordion","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#ui-accordion-react-uiaccordion","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size AccordionSize 'md' Heading height: sm 32px, md 40px (default), lg 48px. align align 'start' | 'end' 'end' Chevron before the title instead of after it. flush flush boolean false No outer dividers; an inset line between items (Carbon isFlush, ignored with align=\\"start\\"). disabled disabled boolean false Disables every item; removing it again leaves disabled only the items that have their own disabled. Method Description focus(options) Focus the first enabled item's heading. Slot Description (default) <ui-accordion-item> elements"],["Accordion","<ui-accordion-item> · React UiAccordionItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#ui-accordion-item-react-uiaccordionitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description title heading heading string '' Heading text; the title slot replaces it when markup is needed. (Before 0.5: the title attribute, still accepted.) open open boolean false disabled disabled boolean false Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } after the user opened or closed it Slot Description (default) Content title Heading text with markup; the heading attribute is the plain-text fallback Part Description heading The heading button arrow The chevron title The heading text content The content wrapper Custom property Default Description --ui-accordion-focus-radius Corners of the heading's focus ring (default 0; Kanok: 6px)"],["Accordion","<ui-accordion-skeleton> · React UiAccordionSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/accordion/#ui-accordion-skeleton-react-uiaccordionskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description count count number 4 open open boolean true The first item shows its content. alignment alignment 'start' | 'end' 'end' Part Description title Each title bar line Each line of the open item"],["Progress indicator","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/","A progress indicator shows where the user is in a task of several steps: which steps are done, which one is current and what comes next. Use it above a multi-step form or a wizard."],["Progress indicator","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Progress indicator","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#use-it",""],["Progress indicator","Step states","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#step-states","current-index (0-based) decides each step's state: the steps before it are complete (a check mark), the step at it is current (a half-filled circle), the steps after it are incomplete (an empty circle). Two flags on a step add to that: invalid shows a warning icon in red: the step has an error to fix. disabled greys the step out. It can't be clicked, even in an interactive indicator."],["Progress indicator","Secondary label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#secondary-label","secondary-label adds a smaller line under the label: \\"Optional\\", a date, a count."],["Progress indicator","Complete out of order","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#complete-out-of-order","complete on a step marks it done whatever current-index says. Use it when the user may fill the steps in any order: here the attachments are already in, while the user is still on the signers."],["Progress indicator","Let the user jump between steps","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#let-the-user-jump-between-steps","interactive makes the steps buttons: a click on a step (not the current one, not a disabled one) makes it current and fires ui-change with detail.index. In React + Tailwind, onChange gets the index. Use it when going back to an earlier step is safe, for example to correct the details before sending. React + Tailwind also takes defaultCurrentIndex when you don't need to hold the step yourself."],["Progress indicator","Back and Next buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#back-and-next-buttons","Most often the page moves through the steps itself: set current-index from your Back and Next buttons. The indicator only shows the position; it doesn't change it on its own unless it is interactive."],["Progress indicator","Vertical","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#vertical","vertical stacks the steps. Use it in a narrow column beside the form, or when the labels are long."],["Progress indicator","Space equally","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#space-equally","By default each step is 128px wide, and a longer label wraps at 88px (Carbon cuts it with an ellipsis; here no step name is hidden). space-equally stretches the steps to share the full width instead. It has no effect with vertical."],["Progress indicator","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#skeleton","While the steps load, show ui-progress-indicator-skeleton: steps empty steps (4 by default), in a row or stacked with vertical. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/progress-indicator-skeleton."],["Progress indicator","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#keyboard","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab With interactive: moves between the steps (disabled steps are skipped). Without it the steps aren't Tab stops. Enter, Space With interactive: makes the focused step current (nothing on the current step)"],["Progress indicator","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#accessibility","The indicator is a list and each step a list item, as Carbon's <ul> / <li>. The current step has aria-current=\\"step\\". After each label, screen readers hear the step's state: \\"Complete\\", \\"Current\\", \\"Incomplete\\" or \\"Invalid\\" (in Thai with lang=\\"th\\"). A disabled step's button is disabled and aria-disabled. The indicator shows progress; it doesn't name the task. Put a heading above it, and repeat the current step in text (as \\"Step 2 of 4\\" above) for people who don't see the icons. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Progress indicator."],["Progress indicator","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Progress indicator","<ui-progress-indicator> · React UiProgressIndicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#ui-progress-indicator-react-uiprogressindicator","Attribute Property Type Default Description current-index currentIndex number 0 Index of the current step (0-based). vertical vertical boolean false space-equally spaceEqually boolean false Stretch the steps to share the width (horizontal only). interactive interactive boolean false Let the user jump between steps (fires ui-change). Method Description focus(options) Interactive indicators: focus the current step. Event React Description ui-change onUiChange detail: { index } when the user picks another step Slot Description (default) <ui-progress-step> elements Part Description base The list"],["Progress indicator","<ui-progress-step> · React UiProgressStep","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#ui-progress-step-react-uiprogressstep","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' secondary-label secondaryLabel string '' Smaller text under the label (Carbon secondaryLabel). complete complete boolean false Marks the step done regardless of current-index. invalid invalid boolean false disabled disabled boolean false data-state state ProgressStepState 'incomplete' Set by the indicator: the resolved state. Property Type Description clickable boolean Set by the indicator: whether steps are clickable. index number Set by the indicator: this step's position. Event React Description ui-step-click none (use a ref) Slot Description (default) Nothing; use label and secondary-label Part Description button The clickable step icon The state icon label The label secondary-label The secondary label line The progress line Custom property Default Description --ui-progress-step-flex / --ui-progress-step-min-width - A horizontal step's flex and least width (default 0 1 auto, 112px: Carbon's 128px steps; Kanok: 1 1 0, 120px) --ui-progress-label-max-width / --ui-progress-label-gap - Its label's max-width and end margin (default 88px, 0) --ui-progress-label-white-space / --ui-progress-label-overflow / --ui-progress-label-text-overflow - Its label on one line (default normal, visible, clip: it wraps; Kanok: one line, an ellipsis)"],["Progress indicator","<ui-progress-indicator-skeleton> · React UiProgressIndicatorSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-indicator/#ui-progress-indicator-skeleton-react-uiprogressindicatorskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description steps steps number 4 vertical vertical boolean false Part Description step Each step label Each label bar"],["UI shell","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/","The UI shell is the frame of an application: a 48px header fixed at the top, a side navigation on the left and the content area beside them. The header holds the product name, the main menu bar and icon buttons for global actions; the side nav holds the sections of the product. This site is built with these elements: the header above this page and the side nav on its left are the live example. The examples below run in framed boxes of their own; Examples on this page says why. The …Icon components on this page are Carbon's icons from @carbon/icons-react, imported with an Icon suffix (see Icons). The header shows them at 20px and the side nav at 16px; in the React tabs they pass slot on to their <svg>."],["UI shell","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["UI shell","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#use-it","Put the header, the side nav and the content straight into <body>, in this order. A page has one shell. The web components wire themselves: the hamburger opens and closes the side nav in the same document with no code, and <ui-content> moves aside for the side nav. In React + Tailwind, hold the side nav's state yourself, as above."],["UI shell","Examples on this page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#examples-on-this-page","The header and the side nav are position: fixed: they stick to the window, and the hamburger and the content area look for the side nav in their document. This page already has a shell, so each live example below sits in a box whose transform keeps the fixed parts inside it, and runs in the box's own shadow root (a \\"micro app\\"), so the page's hamburger and the example's side nav don't drive each other. The demo script also cancels the links' ui-navigate, so a click in an example doesn't leave this page. None of that is needed in your app. The React tabs show the code as you would write it. The header's menu bar shows from Carbon's lg breakpoint, 1056px wide; below it the hamburger appears and the side nav slides over the page. The breakpoint is the window's width, not the box's: make the window narrower to see the small-screen layout."],["UI shell","Menu bar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#menu-bar","<ui-header-nav> is the main menu bar after the product name. It holds <ui-header-menu-item> links and <ui-header-menu> dropdowns of more links. current marks the page with a 3px bar. A closed menu shows the bar when one of its items is current; current on the menu shows it always. prefix on <ui-header-name> is the part of the name in regular weight (Carbon's \\"IBM\\"); the rest is semibold. A header menu is a disclosure, not an ARIA menu: its links stay links. Click, Enter or Space opens it; Esc or a click outside closes it and focus goes back to its title. Following one of its links closes it too."],["UI shell","Mega menu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#mega-menu","A <ui-header-mega-menu> opens a panel as wide as the header under it, with <ui-header-mega-group> columns of <ui-header-mega-item> links (a mega menu, as on Vercel's site). Put it in <ui-header-nav> next to plain links and <ui-header-menu>s. A group has a small heading; an item is a title, and may have an icon slot and a one-line description (the Products menu below). current on an item marks the page, and the closed menu shows the 3px bar. The panel opens in the browser's top layer, so a host app's own fixed bars can't cover it whatever their z-index: right for an app that sits inside another product's shell. With a mouse, resting on an entry opens its panel after 150ms, and while one is open, moving along the bar switches at once. Leaving the entry and its panel closes a panel the pointer opened after 300ms (enough for a diagonal path down to a link). A click holds it open; a finger opens it with a tap. Click, Enter or Space opens and closes it, ↓ opens it and moves to the first link, and Esc, a click outside, Tab out of it or following a link closes it. One panel is open at a time. Kanok draws the panel white over a hairline with a soft shadow, the links at 20px (as Vercel) and the group headings at 14px. The --ui-mega-* settings change these for any design."],["UI shell","Global actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#global-actions","<ui-header-global-bar> holds the icon buttons at the end of the header. Each <ui-header-global-action> is named by label, which also shows as its tooltip; tooltip-placement=\\"bottom-end\\" keeps the tooltip of the last button inside the window. active gives a button the pressed look (aria-pressed), for an action that turns something on or off."],["UI shell","Panels under the header","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#panels-under-the-header","<ui-header-panel> is a 256px panel that slides in under the header at the end side, for notifications, a profile or settings. Give it an id and put that id in the panel attribute of a global action: a click on the action opens and closes the panel, and the action shows as pressed while it is open (aria-expanded). Esc, a click outside or focus leaving the panel closes it. label names the panel as a region. In React + Tailwind the panel is controlled: expanded on the action makes it a disclosure, and onClose tells you why the panel asks to close ('escape', 'blur' or 'outside'). A click on the action whose aria-controls is the panel's id doesn't count as outside."],["UI shell","App switcher","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#app-switcher","<ui-switcher> in a header panel lists the other applications. <ui-switcher-item> is a link; selected marks the application you are in (aria-current=\\"page\\"). An <hr> between items draws a divider. Links to other sites take target and rel as on <a>."],["UI shell","Side nav: links, menus and icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#side-nav-links-menus-and-icons","<ui-side-nav> holds one <ui-side-nav-items> list of: <ui-side-nav-link>: a link; current marks the page with a 3px bar. <ui-side-nav-menu label>: a group that opens and closes, holding <ui-side-nav-menu-item> links. expanded opens it on load. Closed, it shows the bar when one of its items is current. <ui-side-nav-divider>: a line between groups. A 16px icon in the icon slot of a link or menu goes before the text; the menu's items then indent past it. large makes a row 48px tall. By default (no mode attribute) the side nav is open beside the content from 1056px. Below that it is closed: the hamburger opens it over the page with a dark overlay, and a click on the overlay, Esc or focus leaving it closes it again."],["UI shell","Rail","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#rail","rail makes the side nav a 48px strip of icons. It opens to 256px over the content while the pointer is on it or focus is inside, and the content keeps its 48px offset. Give every link and menu an icon."],["UI shell","Fixed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#fixed","fixed together with expanded keeps the side nav open at 256px at every width, and the content moves aside for it. There is no overlay. Use it for tools people work in all day, where the sections must always be in view. fixed without expanded slides the nav out of view while the content keeps its 256px offset, so set both."],["UI shell","Collapsible","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#collapsible","collapsible (Carbon's isPersistent={false}) keeps the side nav closed at every width, and the hamburger shows on large screens too. The nav opens over the content, which doesn't move; Esc or focus leaving the nav closes it. Use it when the content needs the whole width. The web component's hamburger finds the collapsible side nav and stays visible by itself. In React + Tailwind, set collapsible on HeaderMenuButton too."],["UI shell","Header links on small screens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#header-links-on-small-screens","Below 1056px the header's menu bar is hidden. Put a second <ui-header-nav> with the same links first inside <ui-side-nav>: it shows there as a column on small screens only (Carbon's HeaderSideNavItems), and it doesn't make a second navigation landmark. Make the window narrower than 1056px and open the hamburger to see it."],["UI shell","No side nav: collapse","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#no-side-nav-collapse","When the header has no side nav (an app inside another product, which keeps its own sidebar), the bar can't go there on small screens. collapse on <ui-header-nav> keeps it instead: below 1056px it becomes a menu button that opens the bar as a sheet under the header, down to the bottom of the window, and each mega menu is an accordion row. While the sheet is open, the page behind can't be reached with Tab and doesn't scroll; Esc or following a link closes it, and focus goes back to the button. Make the window narrower than 1056px to see it."],["UI shell","Route the links yourself","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#route-the-links-yourself","Every link of the shell (the name, menu items, side nav links, switcher items) is an <a> inside the element. On a plain click it first fires ui-navigate with detail.href; it bubbles and is cancelable. Cancel it and give the path to your router: the page doesn't reload. Ctrl / ⌘-click, middle click and target=\\"_blank\\" stay plain links. This docs site routes its own side nav this way. ui-navigate also bubbles up through <ui-header>, so one listener on a wrapper, or on the document, routes every link of the shell."],["UI shell","Events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#events","The shell reports what the user opens and closes with ui-toggle: Element detail When ui-header-menu-button { active } The user pressed the hamburger: the state asked for. Cancelable: preventDefault() stops the side nav following it, so you can open your own. ui-side-nav { expanded } The user opened or closed the side nav (the hamburger, Esc, the overlay, focus leaving) ui-side-nav-menu { expanded } A side nav menu opened or closed ui-header-menu { open } A header menu opened or closed ui-header-panel { expanded } A panel opened or closed Open and close things below; each event is listed. In React + Tailwind the state is yours: onToggle on HeaderMenuButton and SideNav asks for the new state, and nothing changes until you pass it back."],["UI shell","Skip to content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#skip-to-content","<ui-skip-to-content> goes first in the header. It is hidden until the first Tab on the page, then shows \\"Skip to main content\\" (in Thai with lang=\\"th\\") and jumps to href, #main-content by default: the id <ui-content> gives itself. Press Tab right after this page loads to see the site's own. Inside a shadow root (a micro app), the link finds its target there."],["UI shell","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#keyboard","Key Where Does Tab First stop on the page Shows the skip link Enter, Space Hamburger Opens or closes the side nav Enter, Space Header menu title Opens or closes the menu Esc Header menu Closes it, focus back on its title Esc Header panel Closes it, focus back on its global action Esc Side nav (opened by the hamburger) Closes it, focus back on the hamburger Tab Out of an open panel, header menu, or a side nav over the page Closes it Enter, Space Mega menu entry Opens or closes its panel ↓ Mega menu entry Opens the panel, focus on its first link Esc Mega menu panel Closes it, focus back on its entry Esc Collapsed bar's sheet Closes it, focus back on its menu button Enter Side nav menu title (a button) Opens or closes the menu"],["UI shell","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#accessibility","<ui-header> is the banner landmark, named by label. <ui-header-nav> is a navigation landmark (\\"Main navigation\\" unless label says otherwise), <ui-side-nav> another (\\"Side navigation\\"), and <ui-content> is main. current sets aria-current=\\"page\\" on the link; selected does the same on a switcher item. The hamburger is named \\"Open menu\\" / \\"Close menu\\" by its state (open-label / close-label change the words) and reports aria-expanded. A global action is named by label, through its tooltip. With panel it reports aria-expanded, else aria-pressed while active. A closed side nav (not a rail) is inert: its links leave the Tab order. Header menus and side nav menus are disclosures (aria-expanded, aria-controls), not ARIA menus: the links stay links, and Tab moves through them. A mega menu is a disclosure too (aria-expanded, aria-controls); each group is a list named by its heading. The collapsed bar's menu button is named \\"Open menu\\" / \\"Close menu\\" and reports aria-expanded; while its sheet is open the rest of the page is inert. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless UI shell."],["UI shell","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["UI shell","<ui-header> · React UiHeader","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-react-uiheader","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Accessible name of the banner, e.g. the product name. Slot Description (default) Header content Part Description base The <header>"],["UI shell","<ui-skip-to-content> · React UiSkipToContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-skip-to-content-react-uiskiptocontent","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#main-content' Slot Description (default) Link text (defaults to the translation)"],["UI shell","<ui-header-name> · React UiHeaderName","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-name-react-uiheadername","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '/' prefix prefix string '' target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Product name Part Description base The link"],["UI shell","<ui-header-menu-button> · React UiHeaderMenuButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-menu-button-react-uiheadermenubutton","Attribute Property Type Default Description active active boolean false collapsible collapsible boolean false Keep the button at every width (a collapsible, non-fixed side nav). open-label openLabel string '' close-label closeLabel string '' Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle cancelable; detail: { active } the state the user asked for Part Description base The button"],["UI shell","<ui-header-nav> · React UiHeaderNav","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-nav-react-uiheadernav","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' collapse collapse boolean false Below lg, a menu button and a full-screen sheet instead of hiding (a header with no side nav). Slot Description (default) Menu items Part Description base The <nav> list The menu bar list menu-button With collapse, below lg: the button that opens the sheet sheet With collapse, below lg: the sheet under the header"],["UI shell","<ui-header-menu-item> · React UiHeaderMenuItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-menu-item-react-uiheadermenuitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#' current current boolean false target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Link text Part Description base The link"],["UI shell","<ui-header-menu> · React UiHeaderMenu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-menu-react-uiheadermenu","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' open open boolean false current current boolean false Mark the menu as the current section even while open (Carbon isActive). Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) <ui-header-menu-item> elements Part Description trigger The title button menu The dropdown list"],["UI shell","<ui-header-mega-menu> · React UiHeaderMegaMenu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-mega-menu-react-uiheadermegamenu","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' open open boolean false current current boolean false Mark the menu as the current section even while open. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { open } Slot Description (default) <ui-header-mega-group> elements Part Description trigger The menu-bar entry panel The panel under the header content The grid of groups inside the panel Custom property Default Description --ui-mega-panel-background The panel's fill (default the overlay's, --ui-surface-1; Kanok: the page's white) --ui-mega-panel-shadow Its shadow (default Carbon's menu shadow; Kanok: a soft one) --ui-mega-panel-border Its bottom edge (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-mega-column-width The narrowest a group column gets (default 240px) --ui-mega-gap Between the columns (default 32px) --ui-mega-padding Around the columns (default 24px 32px 32px)"],["UI shell","<ui-header-mega-group> · React UiHeaderMegaGroup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-mega-group-react-uiheadermegagroup","Attribute Property Type Default Description heading heading string '' Slot Description (default) <ui-header-mega-item> elements Part Description heading The heading list The list of links Custom property Default Description --ui-mega-heading-font The heading's type (default Carbon's 12px caption; Kanok: 14px)"],["UI shell","<ui-header-mega-item> · React UiHeaderMegaItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-mega-item-react-uiheadermegaitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#' description description string '' A line under the title. current current boolean false target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) The title icon An icon before the title (20px) Part Description base The link description The line under the title Custom property Default Description --ui-mega-item-font The title's type (default Carbon's body 14px; Kanok: 20px, as Vercel) --ui-mega-item-ink The title's colour (default --ui-ink-muted; Kanok: --ui-ink); hovered or current it is --ui-ink --ui-mega-item-hover-background The row's fill while hovered (default --ui-layer-hover-1; Kanok: --ui-canvas-hover) --ui-mega-item-radius The row's corners (default 0; Kanok: 8px)"],["UI shell","<ui-header-global-bar> · React UiHeaderGlobalBar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-global-bar-react-uiheaderglobalbar","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Slot Description (default) Global actions"],["UI shell","<ui-header-global-action> · React UiHeaderGlobalAction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-global-action-react-uiheaderglobalaction","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' active active boolean false tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement 'bottom' | 'bottom-start' | 'bottom-end' 'bottom' panel panel string '' Id of the <ui-header-panel> this action opens. Clicking toggles the panel, active follows it, and the button reports aria-expanded (a disclosure) instead of aria-pressed (a toggle). The button has an explicit tabindex, as Carbon's (cds-button): Safari then focuses it on click and Tab reaches it. Slot Description (default) 20px icon Part Description base The button Custom property Default Description --ui-header-action-radius Corners of the button's hover fill and focus box (default 0; Kanok: 6px)"],["UI shell","<ui-header-panel> · React UiHeaderPanel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-header-panel-react-uiheaderpanel","Attribute Property Type Default Description expanded expanded boolean false label label string '' Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } Slot Description (default) Panel content (e.g. <ui-switcher>) Part Description base The panel"],["UI shell","<ui-switcher> · React UiSwitcher","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-switcher-react-uiswitcher","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Slot Description (default) <ui-switcher-item> and <hr> elements"],["UI shell","<ui-switcher-item> · React UiSwitcherItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-switcher-item-react-uiswitcheritem","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#' selected selected boolean false target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Link text"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav> · React UiSideNav","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-react-uisidenav","Attribute Property Type Default Description expanded expanded boolean false rail rail boolean false 48px icon rail that expands on hover / focus. fixed fixed boolean false With expanded: always 256px wide, pushing <ui-content> aside (no overlay). Set both — without expanded the nav slides out of view while <ui-content> keeps its 256px offset. collapsible collapsible boolean false Closed on large screens too until the hamburger opens it over the page (Carbon isPersistent={false}); <ui-content> isn't pushed aside. label label string '' Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } after a user action changed the state Slot Description (default) <ui-side-nav-items> Part Description base The <nav> overlay The page overlay (below lg)"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav-items> · React UiSideNavItems","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-items-react-uisidenavitems","Slot Description (default) <ui-side-nav-link>, <ui-side-nav-menu>, <ui-side-nav-divider>"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav-link> · React UiSideNavLink","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-link-react-uisidenavlink","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#' current current boolean false target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. large large boolean false 48px row. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Link text icon 16px icon Part Description base The link Custom property Default Description --ui-nav-item-inset Space each side of a row (default 0; Kanok: 8px) --ui-nav-item-radius Corner radius of a row (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-nav-current-background Fill of the current page's row (default --ui-canvas-selected) --ui-nav-current-mark Colour of its start-edge bar (default --ui-primary; Kanok: --ui-border-interactive) --ui-nav-current-mark-width / --ui-nav-current-mark-inset / --ui-nav-current-mark-radius - The bar's width (3px; Kanok: 0, the tinted row alone — forced colours still show it), top and bottom inset (0) and corners (0)"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav-menu> · React UiSideNavMenu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-menu-react-uisidenavmenu","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' expanded expanded boolean false large large boolean false Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } Slot Description (default) <ui-side-nav-menu-item> elements icon 16px icon Part Description trigger The title button menu The list of items Custom property Default Description --ui-nav-item-inset / --ui-nav-item-radius / --ui-nav-current-* - As on <ui-side-nav-link>"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav-menu-item> · React UiSideNavMenuItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-menu-item-react-uisidenavmenuitem","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '#' current current boolean false target target string '' Where the link opens (_blank for a new tab), as on <a>. rel rel string '' The link's relation (noopener, external …), as on <a>. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Link text Part Description base The link Custom property Default Description --ui-nav-item-inset / --ui-nav-item-radius / --ui-nav-current-* - As on <ui-side-nav-link>"],["UI shell","<ui-side-nav-divider> · React UiSideNavDivider","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-side-nav-divider-react-uisidenavdivider",""],["UI shell","<ui-content> · React UiContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/ui-shell/#ui-content-react-uicontent","Slot Description (default) Page content"],["Tag","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/","A tag labels and sorts things: a contract's status, the departments it belongs to, the filters on a list. It is read-only by default. It can also close (dismissible), turn on and off (selectable) or open something (operational)."],["Tag","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tag","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#use-it",""],["Tag","Which tag?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#which-tag","Carbon has four tags. Here they are one element with an attribute each. Tag Attribute Use it for Read-only none A status or a category to read. It isn't focusable. Dismissible dismissible A value the user can remove: a chosen filter, a recipient. Selectable selectable A filter the user turns on and off. selected holds the state. Operational operational A tag that opens something: the rest of a long list, the details of a category. For a status with an icon and a word (for example \\"Overdue\\" in a table), see Status indicator. For a count on an icon, see Badge indicator."],["Tag","Colours","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#colours","type picks one of 12 colours; gray is the default. The colours mean nothing by themselves: give each category one colour and keep it everywhere in the product. high-contrast and outline stand out on any background."],["Tag","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#sizes","size: sm 18px, md 24px (the default), lg 32px. Use sm in dense tables, lg next to 32px buttons or fields."],["Tag","With an icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#with-an-icon","A 16px icon goes before the text, in the icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind). It takes the tag's text colour. The icon is decoration: the text still has to say everything."],["Tag","Beside a title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#beside-a-title","A tag sits on the middle of the text line, so it can follow a heading or a name without extra layout. Use sm next to small text."],["Tag","Long text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#long-text","A tag is 208px wide at most. Longer text is cut with an ellipsis. As in Carbon web components, only a dismissible tag shows the full text as the browser's tooltip; when its text isn't the full name, give the full name in tag-title (tagTitle in React). React + Tailwind follows Carbon React: every tag shows it, and title sets it."],["Tag","Dismissible","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#dismissible","dismissible adds a close button. A press fires ui-dismiss (onDismiss in React + Tailwind); the tag stays until you remove it, so you can update your filters first. Removing a focused tag drops the focus: move it to the next tag, as the demo does. The close button is named \\"Dismiss {text}\\" in the page's language. Set your own with dismiss-label; {text} becomes the tag's text."],["Tag","Selectable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#selectable","selectable makes the tag a toggle button. A press flips selected and fires change. Selectable tags have one look of their own: type doesn't change them. Use them as quick filters above a list. React + Tailwind also takes defaultSelected for a tag you don't control."],["Tag","Operational","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#operational","operational makes the tag a bordered button in its colour, for a tag that opens something. Here \\"+3\\" opens the rest of a long list in a popover. When the text alone doesn't say what the button does, name it with label. Inside a ui-popover the tag gets aria-haspopup and aria-expanded by itself (through its expanded property). In React + Tailwind the operational tag is a plain <button>: name it with aria-label, and the popover's trigger prop adds aria-expanded."],["Tag","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#disabled","disabled greys out every kind. A dismissible tag's close button, a selectable tag and an operational tag stop responding."],["Tag","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#skeleton","While the tags load, show ui-tag-skeleton: a 60px pill at the tag's size. It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/tag-skeleton. More skeletons: Skeleton."],["Tag","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to a dismissible tag's close button, a selectable tag or an operational tag. A read-only tag isn't a tab stop. Enter, Space Presses the close button, flips a selectable tag, or presses an operational tag"],["Tag","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#accessibility","A read-only tag is text. Screen readers read it with the content around it, so the text must make sense there; the colour alone says nothing. The close button is named \\"Dismiss {text}\\" (translated), so each one is different. dismiss-label changes the words. A selectable tag is a button with aria-pressed. An operational tag is a button. Give it label when its text is only a number, such as \\"+3\\". el.focus() moves focus to the tag's own control: the close button, or the button of a selectable or operational tag. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Tag."],["Tag","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tag","<ui-tag> · React UiTag","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#ui-tag-react-uitag","Attribute Property Type Default Description type type TagType 'gray' Colour (Carbon type). size size TagSize 'md' sm 18px · md 24px (default) · lg 32px dismissible dismissible boolean false Shows a close button that fires ui-dismiss. selectable selectable boolean false A toggle button (aria-pressed); use selected for its state. selected selected boolean false operational operational boolean false A bordered button for tags that open or trigger something. disabled disabled boolean false tag-title tagTitle string '' A dismissible tag's full text for the browser tooltip (defaults to the text); other tags have none (Carbon WC). dismiss-label dismissLabel string '' Accessible name of the close button; {text} is replaced with the tag text. label label string '' An operational tag's accessible name, when its text alone doesn't say it (e.g. \\"+3\\": \\"3 more tags\\"). expanded expanded boolean | undefined An operational tag that opens a popup: whether it is open (aria-expanded, with aria-haspopup). Event React Description ui-dismiss onUiDismiss The dismiss button was pressed (the tag stays until you remove it) change onChange A selectable tag was toggled (selected already updated) Slot Description (default) The tag text icon A 16px icon before the text (Carbon renderIcon) Part Description base The tag box label The text dismiss-button The close button of a dismissible tag Custom property Default Description --ui-tag-radius Corner radius (default 16px: a pill) --ui-tag-selectable-border Outline of a selectable tag (default --ui-border-inverse; Kanok: --ui-hairline-strong) --ui-tag-selected Fill and outline of a chosen selectable tag (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: --ui-primary); its text --ui-tag-selected-ink (--ui-inverse-ink) --ui-tag-font Font of the label (default --ui-font-caption; Kanok: medium weight) --ui-tag-high-contrast / --ui-tag-high-contrast-ink / --ui-tag-high-contrast-hover / --ui-tag-high-contrast-border / --ui-tag-high-contrast-edge / --ui-tag-high-contrast-focus - The high-contrast type (default Carbon's inverse block; Kanok: an outlined ink tag) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Tag","<ui-tag-skeleton> · React UiTagSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tag/#ui-tag-skeleton-react-uitagskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Part Description bone The pill"],["Tile","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/","A tile is a plain box on the next layer colour: 16px padding, no border, no shadow. It groups content on a dashboard or a summary page. With href the whole tile becomes one link. Carbon has four more kinds; here they are ui-expandable-tile, ui-selectable-tile and ui-radio-tile."],["Tile","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Tile","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#use-it","Each kind has its own module: tile for ui-tile, expandable-tile, and selection-tiles for the selectable and radio tiles."],["Tile","Which tile?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#which-tile","Tile Element Use it for Tile ui-tile A box of content: a figure, a short summary. Clickable tile ui-tile href The whole tile goes to one page. Expandable tile ui-expandable-tile A summary that opens to show more. Selectable tile ui-selectable-tile A checkbox with room for a title and a description. More on the checkbox page. Radio tile ui-radio-tile A radio option with room for a title and a description. More on the radio page. For a box with a header, media and actions, use a Card."],["Tile","Content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#content","Put any content in a tile: headings, text, a small table. A tile is at least 64px tall and 128px wide and fills its column, so lay several out with CSS grid. The text inside is body-compact-01 unless you set another font."],["Tile","Clickable tile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#clickable-tile","With href the whole tile is one link and a single tab stop; the pointer turns its fill to the hover colour. Its text is the link's name, so keep it short, and don't put other buttons or links inside. As in Carbon, a linked tile has no icon until you give it one in the icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind): 20px, 12px from the bottom-end corner. target=\\"_blank\\" opens the link in a new tab; the tile then adds \\"(opens in a new tab)\\" for screen readers and rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"."],["Tile","Disabled clickable tile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#disabled-clickable-tile","disabled on a linked tile turns it into plain greyed text with no link (Carbon's disabled ClickableTile), for a page the user can't open right now. Say why in the tile."],["Tile","Route with your SPA router","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#route-with-your-spa-router","A plain click on a linked tile first fires a cancelable ui-navigate with { href }. Cancel it and let your router change the page; one listener on document covers every element, see Frameworks. The demo cancels it and shows the address instead."],["Tile","On a layer","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#on-a-layer","A tile draws itself in the layer colour it sits on. Inside a ui-layer it takes the next one, so it still stands out from a grey panel. More on layers: Layer."],["Tile","Expandable tile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#expandable-tile","ui-expandable-tile shows a summary and opens to show more. The summary (slot=\\"summary\\") sits inside the toggle button, so keep it to text; put links, fields and buttons in the revealed part. The chevron in the bottom-end corner turns when it opens."],["Tile","Open state and events","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#open-state-and-events","expanded opens the tile (start it open by setting it). After each toggle ui-toggle fires with detail.expanded. toggle() on the element opens or closes it from your code; toggle(true) only opens. React + Tailwind also takes defaultExpanded for a tile you don't control."],["Tile","Keep it open","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#keep-it-open","Before it changes, the tile fires a cancelable ui-before-toggle with the state it is about to take. Cancel it to keep the tile as it is, for example while a note inside isn't saved. In React + Tailwind, return false from onBeforeToggle. Type a note, then try to close the tile."],["Tile","Selectable tile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#selectable-tile","ui-selectable-tile is a checkbox drawn as a tile, with the same API as ui-checkbox: checked, name, value, change, and it submits with its form. Alone, each tile is one yes/no choice. Groups, required, read-only and errors are on the checkbox page."],["Tile","Radio tiles","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#radio-tiles","ui-radio-tile is one option of a ui-radio-group, drawn as a tile. The group gives the arrow keys, the value, change and the form; the check mark shows only on the chosen tile. Orientation, required, read-only and errors are on the radio page."],["Tile","The mark over the corner","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#the-mark-over-the-corner","A selectable or radio tile keeps 48px free at its end for the mark, as Carbon does, so in narrow columns the text wraps early. Set --ui-tile-mark-space (beyond Carbon) to 16px and the mark sits over the top-end corner instead, leaving the width to the content."],["Tile","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to a clickable tile, an expandable tile's toggle, a selectable tile, or the chosen radio tile. A plain tile isn't a tab stop. Enter Follows a clickable tile's link; opens or closes an expandable tile Space Opens or closes an expandable tile; checks or unchecks a selectable tile Arrow keys Move between radio tiles and choose"],["Tile","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#accessibility","A plain tile is a box with no role. Give its content real headings, so the page outline stays right. A clickable tile is one link, and its whole text is the link's name. Keep it short and put no other controls inside. An expandable tile's toggle is a button with aria-expanded and aria-controls. Its summary is part of the button's name, which is why it holds text only. A selectable tile is a real checkbox and a radio tile a real radio, so screen readers announce their state and the tile text is their name."],["Tile","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Tile","<ui-tile> · React UiTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#ui-tile-react-uitile","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '' Makes the whole tile a link. target target '_self' | '_blank' '_self' disabled disabled boolean false A linked tile that can't be followed right now (Carbon ClickableTile disabled): plain text, no link. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) Tile content icon A linked tile's icon (e.g. an arrow), 20px, 12px from the bottom-end corner Part Description base The container (<div> or <a>) Custom property Default Description --ui-card-radius Corner radius (default 0; Kanok: 12px) --ui-card-border Border (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Tile","<ui-expandable-tile> · React UiExpandableTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#ui-expandable-tile-react-uiexpandabletile","Attribute Property Type Default Description expanded expanded boolean false Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } ui-before-toggle onUiBeforeToggle Cancelable; detail: { expanded } — the state about to be applied Slot Description summary Always visible (text only) (default) Revealed content Part Description summary The always-visible button row chevron The arrow icon content The expandable body Custom property Default Description --ui-card-border / --ui-card-radius - Border and corners, as the cards (default none and square; Kanok: a hairline, 12px) --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Tile","<ui-selectable-tile> · React UiSelectableTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#ui-selectable-tile-react-uiselectabletile","Attribute Property Type Default Description checked checked boolean false indeterminate indeterminate boolean false Mixed state, e.g. a \\"select all\\" box with some children checked. Cleared on user toggle. disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. required required boolean false Blocks form submission while the field is empty. readonly readonly boolean false Shows and submits the value but blocks changes. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Keep the label text for screen readers but don't show it. name name string '' Reflected: form-associated elements submit under the name attribute. value value string 'on' helper-text helperText string '' Helper text under the field, shown while there is no error or warning. invalid-text invalidText string '' Error text shown while invalid or while the field fails validation. invalid invalid boolean false Forces the error state, e.g. after server-side validation. warn warn boolean false Non-blocking warning; shown when there is no error. warn-text warnText string '' Text of the warning shown while warn. Property Type Description groupDisabled boolean Set by ui-checkbox-group; kept apart from the author's own disabled / readonly. groupMessage string Error text of the owning ui-checkbox-group while the group is invalid. The group shows it once below the boxes; each box repeats it as its own accessible description and reports aria-invalid, so a screen reader landing on the first box hears why (an IDREF cannot cross the group's shadow root). willValidate (read-only) Whether the field takes part in constraint validation (not while disabled), as natively. labels (read-only) The <label>s that point at this field. Method Description setCustomValidity(message) Like <input>.setCustomValidity(): a non-empty message makes the field invalid (and is shown as its error once touched) until cleared with ''. Event React Description change none (use a ref) When the user toggles the box Slot Description (default) Tile content (title, description…) Part Description base The clickable row (label element) control The native checkbox input box The drawn 16px box label The text beside the box status-icon The error / warning icon helper-text The helper line warning-text The warning line warn-text Same line as warning-text (named after the warn-text attribute / slot) error-text The error line invalid-text Same line as error-text (named after the invalid-text attribute / slot) Custom property Default Description --ui-tile-border-color Border of an unchosen tile (default transparent; Kanok: a hairline); --ui-card-radius its corners --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-tile-selected-border Border of the chosen tile (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: primary blue); --ui-tile-selected-mark its check mark (default --ui-icon-primary) --ui-tile-selected-background Fill of the chosen tile (default --ui-card-background; Kanok: soft highlight wash) --ui-tile-mark-space End padding kept clear for the mark (default 48px, Carbon's); e.g. 16px lets the content run under the mark in the top-end corner (beyond Carbon) --ui-checkbox-border Border of the box (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-checkbox-checked Fill and border when checked or mixed (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary) --ui-checkbox-mark Check mark colour (default --ui-icon-inverse; Kanok: --ui-on-primary)"],["Tile","<ui-radio-tile> · React UiRadioTile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/tile/#ui-radio-tile-react-uiradiotile","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' checked checked boolean false disabled disabled boolean false Disables the control; a disabled <fieldset> ancestor does the same. label-position labelPosition RadioLabelPosition | undefined Carbon labelPosition: left puts the text before the circle; unset, the group's label-position applies. Slot Description (default) Tile content (title, description…) Part Description circle The drawn radio circle label The text beside it Custom property Default Description --ui-tile-border-color Border of an unchosen tile (default transparent; Kanok: a hairline); --ui-card-radius its corners --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-tile-selected-border Border of the chosen tile (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse; Kanok: primary blue); --ui-tile-selected-mark its check mark (default --ui-icon-primary) --ui-tile-selected-background Fill of the chosen tile (default --ui-card-background; Kanok: soft highlight wash) --ui-tile-mark-space End padding kept clear for the mark (default 48px, Carbon's); e.g. 16px lets the content run under the mark in the top-end corner (beyond Carbon) --ui-radio-border Ring colour (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-ink-subtle) --ui-radio-checked Ring and dot when chosen (default --ui-ink; Kanok: --ui-primary)"],["Card","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/","A card is a box built from parts: media, a header with a title and its actions, a body and a footer. Use it for a set of things the user browses or picks from: projects, reports, documents. It is Carbon's Card (a preview in Carbon): square, no border, no shadow, on the next layer colour."],["Card","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Card","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#use-it","All the parts load from one module. In React, import a wrapper for each element (UiCard, UiCardHeader, UiCardTitle …) from @purpurabog/ui/react."],["Card","Card, tile or product card?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#card-tile-or-product-card","Component Use it when Tile A plain box of content, or one link. No header or footer of its own. Card Content with a title, media and actions, built from parts. The choice for new work. Product card A screen must match IBM product UIs that use Carbon for IBM Products' ProductiveCard or ExpressiveCard."],["Card","The parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#the-parts","Every part is optional; put them in this order. Part Holds ui-card-media An image or video across the card, at ratio ui-card-header The header grid: ui-card-header-media, ui-card-title-media, ui-card-title, ui-card-actions ui-card-header-media A pictogram across the top of the header, at most 64px tall ui-card-title-media A logo before the title, 48–64px ui-card-title A label above, the title, a description below ui-card-actions Small buttons in the header's top-end corner ui-card-body The content, with 16px padding (none with is-flush) ui-card-footer Text, or a row of ui-card-actions ui-card-action One button in the footer or in ui-card-actions"],["Card","Media","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#media","ui-card-media fills the card's width at ratio: 16x9, 9x16, 2x1, 1x2, 4x3, 3x4, 3x2, 2x3 or 1x1. The image covers the box and is cropped to fit. Without ratio it keeps the image's own shape. Give the image alt=\\"\\" when it only decorates, and a real alt when it carries information the text doesn't."],["Card","Logo beside the title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#logo-beside-the-title","ui-card-title-media puts a logo or an avatar before the title; the title moves over to make room."],["Card","Title, label and description","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#title-label-and-description","ui-card-title holds the title text. label goes above it and description below, both in small muted text. For markup in them, use the label and description slots instead. Icons go before or after the title in the title-start and title-end slots (titleStart and titleEnd in React + Tailwind)."],["Card","Cut long text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#cut-long-text","Long titles wrap. title-truncate cuts the title instead: on its own to one line with an ellipsis, with a number to that many lines. label-truncate and description-truncate work the same. max-width limits how wide a cut title gets. On the element these are attributes whose presence means one line (in React pass \\"\\", or the number of lines as a string). React + Tailwind takes true or a number."],["Card","Header actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#header-actions","ui-card-actions puts small buttons in the header's top-end corner, in at most half its width. Put each ui-icon-button kind=\\"ghost\\" size=\\"sm\\" in a ui-card-action. Buttons that don't fit move into an overflow menu; choosing an item clicks that button. The narrow card shows it. An item in the overflow menu is named by the action's label, else by its button's label or text. overflow-menu-label names the menu button (\\"More actions\\" by default, translated)."],["Card","Footer actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#footer-actions","A ui-card-footer with ui-card-actions becomes a row of buttons across the card under a thin line: a ui-button stretches to share the row, a ui-icon-button keeps its size at the end. A footer with plain content just pads it."],["Card","Linked card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#linked-card","With href the whole card is one link and a single tab stop. Name it with label: the card's whole text would be a long link name. A linked card gets a border and the hover colour, and hides its footer: one link can't hold other controls, so leave out header actions too. They still show if you add them (as in Carbon, whose guidelines say a clickable card holds no interactive elements), inside the link. A plain click fires a cancelable ui-navigate first, for your SPA router. target=\\"_blank\\" opens a new tab; the card adds \\"(opens in a new tab)\\" for screen readers and rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"."],["Card","Clickable card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#clickable-card","clickable makes the whole card one button: a click, or Enter or Space while the card has focus, fires click. An arrow in the bottom-end corner shows it can be pressed; replace it with the footer-icon slot (footerIcon in React + Tailwind). Name the card with label, and put no other controls in it."],["Card","Selected card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#selected-card","Beyond Carbon (its card has no chosen state): selected on a clickable card says which one is chosen, for example the board the page shows. The card reports aria-pressed and takes the look of a checked selectable tile. It doesn't change by itself on a click: set it from your code, as the demo does."],["Card","Without the arrow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#without-the-arrow","Beyond Carbon: hide-footer-icon (hideFooterIcon in React + Tailwind) removes the clickable card's arrow and the row it takes, for small cards in a dense grid."],["Card","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#disabled","disabled greys the text and the arrow. A disabled clickable card fires no click and leaves the tab order; a disabled linked card is no longer a link. Say in the card why it can't be used."],["Card","Horizontal","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#horizontal","horizontal puts the media beside the content: at the start by default, at the end with media-position=\\"end\\". The media takes a third of the card; media-width on ui-card-media changes that."],["Card","Expressive","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#expressive","density=\\"expressive\\" sets the title in the larger heading-03 type, for marketing-like pages with few cards. The default productive suits dense product screens."],["Card","On a layer","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#on-a-layer","A card draws itself in the layer colour it sits on. Inside a ui-layer it takes the next one, so cards on a grey panel still stand out."],["Card","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to a linked or clickable card, or to the buttons in a plain card's header and footer Enter Follows a linked card; presses a clickable card Space Presses a clickable card"],["Card","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#accessibility","The title is not a heading element. When the cards form a list with headings on the page, wrap the title text in a heading of the right level, or name the list. A linked or clickable card is one control. Name it with label, since its whole text would make a long name, and don't put other controls inside. A clickable card is a role=\\"button\\"; a disabled one has aria-disabled and leaves the tab order. The arrow of a clickable card and the media are decorative. Give an image a real alt only when it carries information. The header actions are separate buttons, each with its own label; those in the overflow menu keep their names. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Card."],["Card","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Card","<ui-card> · React UiCard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-react-uicard","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '' Makes the whole card one link. target target '_self' | '_blank' '_self' clickable clickable boolean false Makes the whole card one button (listen for click). selected selected boolean | undefined A clickable card shown chosen, as a checked selectable tile, with aria-pressed (beyond Carbon; the app toggles it). hide-footer-icon hideFooterIcon boolean false Removes the clickable card's arrow footer (beyond Carbon). disabled disabled boolean false label label string '' The accessible name of a linked or clickable card (Carbon asks for one). density density CardDensity 'productive' horizontal horizontal boolean false media-position mediaPosition 'start' | 'end' 'start' Where a horizontal card's media goes. Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of a linked card; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) The parts media (filled for you) the media of a horizontal card footer-icon Replaces the clickable card's arrow Part Description base The card (<div>, or <a> with href) Custom property Default Description --ui-card-radius Corner radius (default 0; Kanok: 12px) --ui-card-border Border of every card, not only clickable ones (default none; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-card-clickable-border Border of a clickable card (default 1px --ui-border-tile-1; Kanok: none) --ui-card-overflow overflow of the card (default visible; Kanok: clip, so media follow the rounded corners) --ui-tile-selected-border Border of a selected card, as a checked tile's (default --ui-layer-selected-inverse); --ui-tile-selected-background / --ui-tile-selected-hover its fill"],["Card","<ui-card-media> · React UiCardMedia","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-media-react-uicardmedia","Attribute Property Type Default Description ratio ratio CardMediaRatio | '' '' media-width mediaWidth string '33.33%' A horizontal card's media width (Carbon's default 33.33%). Slot Description (default) An <img>, <video>, …"],["Card","<ui-card-header> · React UiCardHeader","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-header-react-uicardheader","Slot Description (default) <ui-card-header-media>, <ui-card-title-media>, <ui-card-title>, <ui-card-actions>"],["Card","<ui-card-header-media> · React UiCardHeaderMedia","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-header-media-react-uicardheadermedia","Slot Description (default) The media"],["Card","<ui-card-title-media> · React UiCardTitleMedia","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-title-media-react-uicardtitlemedia","Slot Description (default) The media"],["Card","<ui-card-title> · React UiCardTitle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-title-react-uicardtitle","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' description description string '' title-truncate titleTruncate string | null null label-truncate labelTruncate string | null null description-truncate descriptionTruncate string | null null max-width maxWidth string '100%' A truncated title's widest. Slot Description (default) The title text label Replaces label description Replaces description title-start An icon before the title title-end An icon after the title"],["Card","<ui-card-body> · React UiCardBody","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-body-react-uicardbody","Attribute Property Type Default Description is-flush isFlush boolean false Slot Description (default) The content"],["Card","<ui-card-footer> · React UiCardFooter","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-footer-react-uicardfooter","Slot Description (default) Content or <ui-card-action>s Custom property Default Description --ui-card-actions-padding / --ui-card-actions-gap - Around and between the footer's buttons (default 0 and 1px: full-bleed; Kanok: 8px and 8px)"],["Card","<ui-card-action> · React UiCardAction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-action-react-uicardaction","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Its name in the header's overflow menu (else the button's label or text). Slot Description (default) A <ui-button> or <ui-icon-button>"],["Card","<ui-card-actions> · React UiCardActions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/card/#ui-card-actions-react-uicardactions","Attribute Property Type Default Description overflow-menu-label overflowMenuLabel string '' The overflow menu's name (default: the translation's \\"More actions\\"). Slot Description (default) <ui-card-action>s, each with a small <ui-icon-button> (or <ui-button size=\\"sm\\">)"],["Product card","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/","ui-productive-card and ui-expressive-card are Carbon for IBM Products' ProductiveCard and ExpressiveCard: cards you configure with attributes, not with parts. They are IBM Products' legacy cards, kept for screens that must match IBM product UIs. For new work, use Card: Carbon's parts-based card, where both Carbon and IBM Products are heading."],["Product card","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Product card","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#use-it","Both cards load from one module. The title is heading on the element (title is every element's native tooltip) and title in React + Tailwind, as in Carbon."],["Product card","Productive, expressive or Card?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#productive-expressive-or-card","Component Use it when ui-productive-card Dense product screens that copy IBM Products: a compact title, small icon actions or an overflow menu, ghost buttons. ui-expressive-card Content cards that copy IBM Products: media, a pictogram, a larger title, primary and secondary buttons. Card Anything new. You build it from parts, and it is where Carbon is going."],["Product card","Action icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#action-icons","Icon buttons go in the actions slot (actionIcons in React + Tailwind); give each a label. The card makes them ghost buttons and sets their size: small at the top, medium at the bottom. They are separate tab stops."],["Product card","Overflow menu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#overflow-menu","A productive card can show its actions in an overflow menu instead: put ui-menu-items in the overflow slot (overflowActions in React + Tailwind). When there are menu items, they replace the icons. The menu button is named \\"Options\\" (translated); overflow-aria-label changes it. Choosing an item fires ui-select, which bubbles up to the card."],["Product card","Actions at the bottom","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#actions-at-the-bottom","actions-placement=\\"bottom\\" moves the icons (or the menu) into the footer, at medium size. With a primary button there too, the button goes at the start and the icons at the end."],["Product card","Buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#buttons","primary-button-text and secondary-button-text add buttons; on a productive card both are ghost buttons. They sit in the footer by default. primary-button-placement=\\"top\\" moves the primary one next to the top actions as a small ghost button; secondary-button-placement=\\"top\\" does the same for the secondary one, but only when there are other top actions, as in Carbon. A press fires ui-primary-button-click or ui-secondary-button-click. primary-button-disabled and secondary-button-disabled disable a button."],["Product card","Button links and icons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#button-links-and-icons","primary-button-href and secondary-button-href make a footer button a link (a primary button at the top takes no href, as in Carbon). A 16px icon after the text goes in the primary-button-icon or secondary-button-icon slot (primaryButtonIcon, secondaryButtonIcon in React + Tailwind)."],["Product card","Title size and heading level","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#title-size-and-heading-level","title-size=\\"large\\" sets a productive card's title in heading-03 instead of heading-compact-02. The title is an <h2>; set the level that fits your page with heading-level (h1 … h6; headingAs in React + Tailwind). For markup in the label, title or description, use the label, title and description slots."],["Product card","Clickable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#clickable","clickable turns one zone of the card into a button that fires ui-click on a click, Enter or Space (in React + Tailwind, passing onClick does it). click-zone picks the zone: one the whole card (default), two the header with the body, three the body. The zone's button lies under the card's own buttons, which stay separate tab stops and never fire ui-click. The title names the button and the description describes it."],["Product card","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#disabled","disabled only announces the card as disabled (aria-disabled) and stops ui-click; it doesn't grey anything out, as in Carbon. Disable the buttons with primary-button-disabled and secondary-button-disabled, and say in the card why it can't be used."],["Product card","Expressive card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#expressive-card","ui-expressive-card is for content. Media goes across the top (slot=\\"media\\", at its own size up to the card's width), a pictogram above the title (slot=\\"pictogram\\"), and the buttons in the footer: a primary and a secondary button by default. Action icons (slot=\\"actions\\") are small and sit at the end of the footer. primary-button-kind takes primary (default) or ghost, secondary-button-kind secondary (default) or ghost."],["Product card","Pictogram and media at the start","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#pictogram-and-media-at-the-start","A pictogram goes above the title, 16px in. media-position=\\"left\\" puts the media at the start, with the content beside it."],["Product card","Clickable expressive card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#clickable-expressive-card","On an expressive card clickable always makes the whole card the button. Its own buttons stay separate."],["Product card","Decorator and layers","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#decorator-and-layers","The decorator slot puts a small element 16px from the top-end corner, for example an AI label or a tag. Both cards draw themselves in the layer colour they sit on, so inside a ui-layer they take the next one."],["Product card","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves through the click zone and the card's own buttons and links, in page order Enter, Space Presses the click zone or the focused button"],["Product card","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#accessibility","The title is a real heading (<h2> by default). Set heading-level so the page outline stays right. The click zone is a <button> named by the title (else the label, else the body) and described by the description. disabled only sets aria-disabled: the card looks the same, so say why it can't be used. Each action icon needs a label; it is the button's name and tooltip. The media and pictogram are decorative unless you give them a real alt or name. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Product card."],["Product card","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Product card","<ui-productive-card> · React UiProductiveCard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#ui-productive-card-react-uiproductivecard","Attribute Property Type Default Description click-zone clickZone ProductCardClickZone 'one' Which zone clickable makes one button: one = the card, two = the header with the body, three = the body. actions-placement actionsPlacement ProductCardPlacement 'top' Where the action icons (or the overflow menu) go. title-size titleSize ProductCardTitleSize 'default' default: heading-compact-02; large: heading-03. overflow-aria-label overflowAriaLabel string '' The overflow menu's name and tooltip (default: the translation's \\"Options\\", as Carbon's iconDescription). primary-button-placement primaryButtonPlacement ProductCardPlacement 'bottom' At the top the primary button joins the top actions (a ghost sm button, without href). secondary-button-placement secondaryButtonPlacement ProductCardPlacement 'bottom' At the top the secondary button joins the top actions, only when there are other top actions (as Carbon). heading heading string '' The title (Carbon title; named heading because title is every element's native tooltip). heading-level headingLevel string 'h2' The title's element (h1 … h6; Carbon Heading in its Section, an <h2> at the top of a page). label label string '' Text above the title (label-01). description description string '' Text below the title (label-01). clickable clickable boolean false Makes the card's click zone one button (Carbon: an onClick); listen for ui-click. disabled disabled boolean false Announced as disabled (aria-disabled, as Carbon); a clickable zone then fires no ui-click. No other change, as Carbon. primary-button-text primaryButtonText string '' primary-button-href primaryButtonHref string '' Makes the primary button a link (in the footer; Carbon's button at the top takes no href). primary-button-disabled primaryButtonDisabled boolean false secondary-button-text secondaryButtonText string '' secondary-button-href secondaryButtonHref string '' Makes the secondary button a link. secondary-button-disabled secondaryButtonDisabled boolean false Event React Description ui-click none (use a ref) The click zone was activated (a click, Enter or Space); not while disabled ui-primary-button-click none (use a ref) The primary button was activated ui-secondary-button-click none (use a ref) The secondary button was activated Slot Description (default) The body (body-compact-01) label Replaces label title Replaces heading description Replaces description actions Icon buttons (<ui-icon-button label=\\"…\\">); the card sets their size overflow <ui-menu-item>s of the overflow menu, shown instead of the action icons primary-button-icon A 16px icon after the primary button's text (Carbon primaryButtonIcon) secondary-button-icon A 16px icon after the secondary button's text decorator E.g. an AI label, 16px from the top-end corner Part Description base The card click-zone The clickable zone's button (clickable only), covering the zone content The header, body and footer header The header label The label title The title (<h2> by default) description The description actions The action icons' (or overflow menu's) box, with the top buttons overflow The <ui-overflow-menu> body The body footer The footer primary-button The primary <ui-button> secondary-button The secondary <ui-button> decorator The decorator's box Custom property Default Description --ui-tile-border-color Its 1px border, as the selectable tiles (default transparent; Kanok: a hairline) --ui-card-background Its fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok paper: a cool grey that sets it apart from the page, no border) --ui-card-radius / --ui-card-overflow - Corners and clipping, as <ui-card> (default square, visible; Kanok: 12px, clipped)"],["Product card","<ui-expressive-card> · React UiExpressiveCard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/product-card/#ui-expressive-card-react-uiexpressivecard","Attribute Property Type Default Description media-position mediaPosition ProductCardMediaPosition 'top' Where the media goes: across the top, or at the start with the content beside it. primary-button-kind primaryButtonKind ProductCardPrimaryKind 'primary' secondary-button-kind secondaryButtonKind ProductCardSecondaryKind 'secondary' heading heading string '' The title (Carbon title; named heading because title is every element's native tooltip). heading-level headingLevel string 'h2' The title's element (h1 … h6; Carbon Heading in its Section, an <h2> at the top of a page). label label string '' Text above the title (label-01). description description string '' Text below the title (label-01). clickable clickable boolean false Makes the card's click zone one button (Carbon: an onClick); listen for ui-click. disabled disabled boolean false Announced as disabled (aria-disabled, as Carbon); a clickable zone then fires no ui-click. No other change, as Carbon. primary-button-text primaryButtonText string '' primary-button-href primaryButtonHref string '' Makes the primary button a link (in the footer; Carbon's button at the top takes no href). primary-button-disabled primaryButtonDisabled boolean false secondary-button-text secondaryButtonText string '' secondary-button-href secondaryButtonHref string '' Makes the secondary button a link. secondary-button-disabled secondaryButtonDisabled boolean false Event React Description ui-click none (use a ref) The card was activated (a click, Enter or Space); not while disabled ui-primary-button-click none (use a ref) The primary button was activated ui-secondary-button-click none (use a ref) The secondary button was activated Slot Description (default) The body (body-compact-01) label Replaces label title Replaces heading description Replaces description media An image or video across the top (or at the start), shown at its own size up to the card's width pictogram A pictogram above the title, 16px in actions Icon buttons (<ui-icon-button label=\\"…\\">, ghost); the card makes them sm primary-button-icon A 16px icon after the primary button's text (Carbon primaryButtonIcon) secondary-button-icon A 16px icon after the secondary button's text decorator E.g. an AI label, 16px from the top-end corner Part Description base The card click-zone The card's button (clickable only), covering the card media The media's box pictogram The pictogram's box content The header, body and footer header The header label The label title The title (<h2> by default) description The description actions The action icons' box body The body footer The footer primary-button The primary <ui-button> secondary-button The secondary <ui-button> decorator The decorator's box"],["Code snippet","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/","A code snippet shows code or a command that people copy: an install line, a config file, an ID inside a sentence. It has three types: single (one line), multi (a block that folds after 15 rows) and inline (a chip in running text). Every code sample on this site is a ui-code-snippet."],["Code snippet","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Code snippet","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#use-it",""],["Code snippet","Single line","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#single-line","type=\\"single\\" (the default) is one 40px line with the copy button at the end. A line longer than the box scrolls sideways; it never wraps. Use it for commands and one-line values."],["Code snippet","Multi-line","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#multi-line","type=\\"multi\\" shows a block with the copy button top-right. Up to 15 rows show at first; longer code gets a \\"Show more\\" button that opens the rest. As in <pre>, one line break right after the opening tag is dropped, so you can start the code on its own line. Write < as &lt; and & as &amp; when the code goes straight into HTML. In React, pass a string: JSX escapes it for you."],["Code snippet","Wrap long lines","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#wrap-long-lines","A multi-line snippet scrolls sideways by default, which keeps code aligned. wrap-text (wrapText in React) wraps long lines instead: use it for prose-like content such as log messages or SQL."],["Code snippet","Inline","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#inline","type=\\"inline\\" is a chip inside a sentence. The chip itself is the copy button: a click copies the code and its tooltip says \\"Copied!\\". Its name is the code, so screen readers read what they would copy."],["Code snippet","Without a copy button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#without-a-copy-button","hide-copy-button (hideCopyButton in React) shows the code only. An inline snippet then becomes a plain code chip that isn't a button. Use it for code people read but shouldn't paste, such as an example of output."],["Code snippet","Copy something else","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#copy-something-else","text is what gets copied instead of the code shown. Show a short or readable form, and copy the full one: here the snippet shows the request command with the token hidden, and copies it with the token."],["Code snippet","Copy labels and feedback","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#copy-labels-and-feedback","copy-label (copyLabel): the copy button's tooltip on a single or multi-line snippet (default \\"Copy to clipboard\\"). label: the accessible name of the code box (single and multi), or, on an inline chip, its tooltip and description. feedback: the tooltip after a copy (default \\"Copied!\\"), shown for feedback-timeout ms (2000). placement (or Carbon's align): the side of the tooltip, bottom by default."],["Code snippet","Rows shown","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#rows-shown","On a multi-line snippet, max-collapsed-rows (15) is how many 16px rows show before \\"Show more\\", and max-expanded-rows (0, no limit) caps the open block, which then scrolls. min-collapsed-rows (3) and min-expanded-rows (16) keep a minimum height. An open snippet whose code is no taller than min-expanded-rows folds back when the code is measured again, so lower that too when you lower the collapsed limit."],["Code snippet","Open or closed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#open-or-closed","expanded opens a multi-line snippet from the start; the element sets it as the user presses \\"Show more\\" and fires ui-toggle with detail.expanded. show-more-text and show-less-text change the button's words. In React + Tailwind, use defaultExpanded, or expanded with onToggle to hold the state yourself."],["Code snippet","Handle the copy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#handle-the-copy","Before copying, the snippet fires ui-copy with detail.text (cancelable). Listen to it to record the copy; call preventDefault() to put something else on the clipboard yourself, and the feedback still shows. In React + Tailwind, onCopy gets the text; return false to copy it yourself."],["Code snippet","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#disabled","disabled greys the code, disables the copy and \\"Show more\\" buttons, and takes the code box out of the Tab order. An inline chip stays focusable (aria-disabled) but copies nothing."],["Code snippet","Skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#skeleton","While the code loads, show ui-code-snippet-skeleton: a 56px box with one bar (single), or 98px with three lines (type=\\"multi\\"). It is hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). In React, use the UiCodeSnippetSkeleton wrapper. See Skeleton for the other placeholders. On the web component, import it from @purpurabog/ui/code-snippet-skeleton."],["Code snippet","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to the code box, then the copy button, then \\"Show more\\"; on an inline snippet, to the chip Arrow keys Scroll the focused code box when the code is wider or taller than it Enter, Space On the copy button or inline chip: copies. On \\"Show more\\": opens or closes the block"],["Code snippet","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#accessibility","The single and multi-line code box is a read-only textbox (role=\\"textbox\\", aria-readonly) that takes focus, so keyboard users can scroll it. Name it with label (default \\"Copy to clipboard\\"; \\"Webhook URL\\" is better). The copy button is named by its tooltip (copy-label). An inline chip is named by its code, and label becomes its description. After a copy, a polite live region says the feedback once. \\"Show more\\" has aria-expanded. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Code snippet."],["Code snippet","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Code snippet","<ui-code-snippet> · React UiCodeSnippet","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#ui-code-snippet-react-uicodesnippet","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) type type CodeSnippetType 'single' text text string '' Text to copy instead of the slotted content. label label string '' Accessible name of the read-only textbox (single / multi); inline: the copy button's tooltip and description (the button is named by its code, WCAG 2.5.3). copy-label copyLabel string '' Tooltip of the copy button (single / multi). feedback feedback string '' feedback-timeout feedbackTimeout number 2000 placement placement TooltipPlacement 'bottom' hide-copy-button hideCopyButton boolean false wrap-text wrapText boolean false disabled disabled boolean false expanded expanded boolean false show-more-text showMoreText string '' show-less-text showLessText string '' max-collapsed-rows maxCollapsedRows number 15 Rows (16px) visible while collapsed; 0 = no limit. max-expanded-rows maxExpandedRows number 0 Rows visible while expanded; 0 = no limit. min-collapsed-rows minCollapsedRows number 3 min-expanded-rows minExpandedRows number 16 Property Type Description copyText (read-only) What gets copied: text, else the slotted code. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } when \\"Show more / less\\" is used ui-copy onUiCopy detail: { text }; cancelable Slot Description (default) The code Part Description container Scrolling container (single) / <pre> wrapper (multi) code The <code> element copy-button The <ui-copy-button> (single / multi) expand-button The \\"Show more / less\\" button (multi) Custom property Default Description --ui-code-background Fill of the snippet (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: a light grey on its white surfaces) --ui-code-radius Corners of the single and multi-line snippets (default 0; Kanok: 8px; the inline chip keeps its 4px) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["Code snippet","<ui-code-snippet-skeleton> · React UiCodeSnippetSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/code-snippet/#ui-code-snippet-skeleton-react-uicodesnippetskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description type type 'single' | 'multi' 'single' Part Description base The box line Each bar"],["Copy button","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/","A copy button puts a value on the clipboard: a request number, a link, an API key. It is Carbon's 40px icon button: its tooltip names it (\\"Copy to clipboard\\"), and after a copy the tooltip says \\"Copied!\\" for two seconds."],["Copy button","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Copy button","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#use-it",""],["Copy button","Copy button or code snippet?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#copy-button-or-code-snippet","Component Use it when Copy button The value is shown somewhere else, in your own layout: a field, a table cell, a heading. Code snippet You show code or a command, and the copy button belongs to it. The snippet uses this button inside."],["Copy button","Next to the value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#next-to-the-value","Put the button right after the value it copies, so it is clear what it copies. text is exactly what goes on the clipboard."],["Copy button","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#sizes","size: md 40px (the default, next to 40px fields) or sm 32px (in table rows and dense lists). The icon stays 16px."],["Copy button","Label and feedback","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#label-and-feedback","label is the tooltip at rest and the button's accessible name (default \\"Copy to clipboard\\", in the page's language). feedback is the tooltip after a copy (default \\"Copied!\\"). Say what gets copied when there are several buttons on the screen."],["Copy button","Feedback time","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#feedback-time","feedback-timeout (feedbackTimeout in React) is how long the feedback shows, in ms (2000 by default). Pressing again starts the time over."],["Copy button","Tooltip side","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#tooltip-side","placement puts the tooltip on a side: top, bottom (the default), left, right, each with -start or -end. align is Carbon's name for the same attribute. Near the edge of the screen, the tooltip flips to the side with room."],["Copy button","Copy a value that changes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#copy-a-value-that-changes","text is read at the moment of the press, so set it whenever the value changes. Here the share link follows the expiry the user picks."],["Copy button","Copy it yourself","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#copy-it-yourself","Before it copies, the button fires ui-copy with detail.text. Call preventDefault() to put something else on the clipboard yourself; the feedback still shows. In React + Tailwind, onCopy gets the text; return false to copy it yourself. showFeedback() on the element shows the feedback at any time, for example after another control copied the value. If the browser refuses the copy (no permission, no secure page and no fallback), the button shows no feedback, so it never says \\"Copied!\\" for nothing."],["Copy button","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#disabled","disabled greys the icon and takes the button out of the Tab order. Use it while there is nothing to copy yet, for example before a number is issued."],["Copy button","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to the button; the tooltip shows its label Enter, Space Copies, and the tooltip shows the feedback Esc Hides the label tooltip (the feedback stays for its time)"],["Copy button","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#accessibility","The tooltip text is the button's accessible name, so the icon needs no other label. Give each button its own label when there are several (\\"Copy contract number\\", \\"Copy tax ID\\"). After a copy, a polite live region (role=\\"status\\") says the feedback once, so screen reader users hear \\"Copied!\\" too. Keep the copied value visible next to the button. The clipboard can't be seen, and users want to check what they took. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Copy button."],["Copy button","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Copy button","<ui-copy-button> · React UiCopyButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/copy-button/#ui-copy-button-react-uicopybutton","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) text text string '' What gets copied. label label string '' Accessible name / tooltip at rest. feedback feedback string '' Tooltip text after copying. feedback-timeout feedbackTimeout number 2000 placement placement TooltipPlacement 'bottom' size size 'sm' | 'md' 'md' disabled disabled boolean false data-copied copied boolean false True while the feedback is showing. Method Description showFeedback() Show the \\"Copied!\\" tooltip for feedback-timeout ms (Carbon Copy fade-in → fade-out). Event React Description ui-copy onUiCopy detail: { text }; cancelable Part Description button The native button Custom property Default Description --ui-copy-button-background Its fill at rest (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: transparent); --ui-copy-button-radius its corners (default 0; Kanok: 6px) --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["User avatar","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/","A user avatar is a round picture of a person: their photo, their initials, or a user icon. It comes from Carbon for IBM Products. Use it next to a name in approval chains, comments, owners of a record, and the header's account button."],["User avatar","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["User avatar","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#use-it",""],["User avatar","What it shows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#what-it-shows","The avatar shows the first of these it has: the photo (image), a custom icon (slot=\\"icon\\"), the initials of name, or the user icon."],["User avatar","Initials","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#initials","name gives the initials, as Carbon counts them: one word gives its first two letters (\\"Somchai\\" → \\"SO\\"), more words give the first letter of the first and of the last word (\\"Thomas J. Watson\\" → \\"TW\\"). Letters are upper-cased."],["User avatar","Thai names","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#thai-names","Thai words count their consonants only: a leading vowel (เ แ โ ใ ไ), a vowel or tone mark above or below, and a following vowel are skipped. So two words give the first consonant of each (\\"สมศรี มั่นคง\\" → \\"สม\\", \\"เกษม ใจดี\\" → \\"กจ\\"), and one word gives its first two consonants (\\"สุดา\\" → \\"สด\\"). Pass the full name; you don't need to work out the initials yourself."],["User avatar","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#sizes","size: sm 24px, md 32px (the default), lg 48px, xl 64px. The initials and the icon grow with it. Use sm in tables and lists, md next to body text, and lg or xl on a profile."],["User avatar","No name: the user icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#no-name-the-user-icon","Without name, image or an icon, the avatar shows Carbon's user icon: 16px in sm, then 20, 24 and 32px. Use it for an account that hasn't set a name yet."],["User avatar","Photo","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#photo","image is the photo's URL; it fills the circle instead of the initials. image-description (imageDescription) is its alt text: give the person's name, or leave it empty when the name is already written next to it. Keep name set too: if you remove image later (no photo, or it failed to load in your app), the initials come back."],["User avatar","Custom icon","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#custom-icon","Put an icon in the icon slot (the icon prop in React + Tailwind) for something that isn't one person: a service account, a team, a bot. It is sized like the user icon (16 / 20 / 24 / 32px) and drawn in the inverse icon colour."],["User avatar","Colours","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#colours","background-color (backgroundColor) picks one of Carbon's 12 avatar colours, order-1-cyan (the default) to order-12-teal: 1–6 are the strong grades, 7–12 the deep ones, and dark themes use lighter grades. Give each person a colour that stays the same, for example from their user id, so people learn to spot each other."],["User avatar","With a tooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#with-a-tooltip","tooltip-text (tooltipText) turns the avatar into a button named by that text, which shows it in a tooltip on hover and focus and takes a 2px focus ring. tooltip-alignment (tooltipAlignment) picks the side, bottom by default. Start the text with the initials, as Carbon does (\\"TW, Thomas J. Watson\\"), so the button's name includes what is seen. The button does nothing on click by itself. Use the tooltip where only the avatar is shown (a row of reviewers); when the name is written next to it, leave the tooltip out."],["User avatar","Next to a name","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#next-to-a-name","The common layout: the avatar, then the name and a second line. Here, the approvers of a contract. The written name says who it is, so the avatar needs no tooltip."],["User avatar","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#accessibility","Without a tooltip, the avatar is plain text (the initials) or an image with its image-description. Write the person's name next to it; initials alone don't say who it is. With tooltip-text, it is a button named by that text. Start the text with the initials so voice control users can say what they see. The colour carries no meaning, so it never needs a text equivalent. The icon slot is decoration: give the svg aria-hidden=\\"true\\"."],["User avatar","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["User avatar","<ui-user-avatar> · React UiUserAvatar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/user-avatar/#ui-user-avatar-react-uiuseravatar","Attribute Property Type Default Description name name string '' The person's name or initials; the avatar shows the initials. image image string '' A photo's URL, shown instead of the initials. image-description imageDescription string '' The photo's alt text. size size UserAvatarSize 'md' background-color backgroundColor UserAvatarColor 'order-1-cyan' One of Carbon's 12 avatar colours, order-1-cyan … order-12-teal. tooltip-text tooltipText string '' Shown in a tooltip and names the avatar, which becomes a button (e.g. \\"Thomas J. Watson\\"). tooltip-alignment tooltipAlignment Placement 'bottom' Slot Description icon A custom icon in place of the initials / user icon (sized 16 / 20 / 24 / 32px) Part Description avatar The circle image The photo trigger The button around the avatar when it has a tooltip"],["Truncated text","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/","Truncated text cuts a long text to a few lines with an ellipsis, and only when it doesn't fit, lets the user read the rest: in a tooltip, or with a \\"View more\\" toggle. It comes from Carbon for IBM Products. Use it for descriptions and notes in cards, tables and lists, where a long text would push everything else down."],["Truncated text","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Truncated text","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#use-it","The text goes in value, not in the element's content. The element fills its container's width, so the container decides where the lines break."],["Truncated text","Full text in a tooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#full-text-in-a-tooltip","type=\\"tooltip\\" is the default. When the text is cut, it becomes a button that shows the whole text in a tooltip on hover and keyboard focus. Use it where there is no room for a toggle, such as table cells."],["Truncated text","View more","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#view-more","type=\\"expand\\" adds a \\"View more\\" toggle under a cut text. It opens the rest with a short height animation (none with reduced motion), and becomes \\"View less\\". Use it for longer notes that people read in full."],["Truncated text","Only when it doesn't fit","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#only-when-it-doesn-t-fit","The element measures the text. A text that fits shows as it is, with no ellipsis, no tooltip button and no toggle; it measures again when the box resizes or value changes."],["Truncated text","Lines","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#lines","lines is how many lines show before the ellipsis: 2 by default. 0 shows the whole text."],["Truncated text","Toggle words","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#toggle-words","expand-label and collapse-label (expandLabel, collapseLabel) replace \\"View more\\" and \\"View less\\" (which follow the page's language). Keep them short and say what opens."],["Truncated text","Tooltip side","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#tooltip-side","placement sets the tooltip's side: top (the default), bottom, left, right, each with -start or -end. align is Carbon's name for it."],["Truncated text","Open from code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#open-from-code","expanded shows an expandable text in full; set it to open or close several texts at once. Set from code, it changes without the animation. ui-toggle fires with detail.expanded when the user presses the toggle. In React + Tailwind, hold it with expanded and onExpandedChange, or start with defaultExpanded."],["Truncated text","It follows its box","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#it-follows-its-box","The text is measured again whenever its box resizes, so the ellipsis, the tooltip button and the toggle come and go with the layout. Drag the corner of the box below to see it."],["Truncated text","Style a cut text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#style-a-cut-text","While the text doesn't fit its lines, the element has data-overflowing (kept while it is open). Style on it, for example to mark notes that have more to read. The text itself is the content part. In React + Tailwind the attribute is on the outer <div>, so use data-overflowing: classes."],["Truncated text","It takes the font around it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#it-takes-the-font-around-it","The text has no font of its own: it uses the font, size and colour of where it sits. Put it inside a heading, a caption or a table cell, and it looks like them."],["Truncated text","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#keyboard","Key Does Tab Moves to a cut tooltip text (its tooltip shows) or to the toggle Enter, Space On the toggle: opens or closes the text Esc Hides the tooltip"],["Truncated text","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#accessibility","A cut tooltip text is a button named by the whole text, so screen readers read all of it, not the cut part. The toggle has aria-expanded and aria-controls pointing at the text. A text that fits is plain text: no button, nothing extra to tab through. Don't cut text people must read to finish a task (an error, a legal condition they accept). Show it in full. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Truncated text."],["Truncated text","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Truncated text","<ui-truncated-text> · React UiTruncatedText","/kanok-ui-docs/en/truncated-text/#ui-truncated-text-react-uitruncatedtext","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (the tooltip's side) value value string '' The text. lines lines number 2 Lines shown before the ellipsis; 0 = all. type type TruncatedTextType 'tooltip' What a truncated text offers: the whole text in a tooltip, or a toggle that expands it. placement placement Placement 'top' The tooltip's side. expand-label expandLabel string '' The expand toggle's text (default \\"View more\\", translated). collapse-label collapseLabel string '' The collapse toggle's text (default \\"View less\\", translated). expanded expanded boolean false Whether an expandable text shows in full. Event React Description ui-toggle onUiToggle detail: { expanded } when the toggle opens or closes the text Part Description content The text trigger The button around the text of a truncated type=\\"tooltip\\" toggle The expand / collapse button Custom property Default Description --ui-focus-offset outline-offset of its focus ring (default -2px: inside; Kanok: 2px outside)"],["List","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/","Carbon's lists show related items in running content: steps to follow, conditions, documents to attach. ui-unordered-list marks each item with an en dash, ui-ordered-list numbers them, and ui-list-item is one item. A list inside an item is nested, and the elements notice that for you."],["List","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["List","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#use-it","The React + Tailwind components render real <ul>, <ol> and <li> elements. This list is for content; for a list people pick from or act on, see Contained list and Structured list."],["List","Unordered","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#unordered","Use an unordered list when the order doesn't matter. Each item gets an en dash 16px before the text, and the list is indented 16px."],["List","Ordered","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#ordered","Use an ordered list for steps that happen in order. The numbers (\\"1.\\") sit 24px before the text, outside the list's own box, as in Carbon: leave at least 24px of room on the start side (the demo box has it)."],["List","Nested unordered","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#nested-unordered","Put a list inside an item to nest it. The inner list is 32px in, and its items get a small square (▪) 12px before the text. You don't set nested: a list inside a ui-list-item (a ListItem in React + Tailwind) sets it itself."],["List","Nested ordered","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#nested-ordered","A nested ordered list counts with letters (a. b. c.), 32px in. Use it for sub-steps."],["List","Mixed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#mixed","The two kinds nest inside each other: steps with a list of things to bring, for example. Three levels is the most people can follow."],["List","Browser numbers","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#browser-numbers","native uses the browser's own decimal numbers instead of Carbon's counter. The browser lines them up on the dot once the list passes 9 items. In React + Tailwind, it also lets the <ol> attributes start and reversed work, which Carbon's counter ignores. Leave room on the start side here too."],["List","Expressive","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#expressive","is-expressive (isExpressive) sets the text in body-02 (16px / 24px) instead of body-01 (14px / 20px). Use it on reading pages, such as a policy or a help article. Nested lists take the size of their parent."],["List","Links and code in items","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#links-and-code-in-items","Items take any inline content: links, inline code, emphasis. Long items wrap under their own text, not under the marker."],["List","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#accessibility","Screen readers announce a list and its item count. ui-list-item gets role=\\"listitem\\" (unless you set a role), and the list's <ul> / <ol> sits in the element's shadow root around the items. Use an ordered list only when the order matters; the numbers are read out. The markers are drawn with CSS, so they aren't read; don't put meaning in them. Keep items short and parallel: start each one the same way (all nouns, or all verbs)."],["List","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["List","<ui-unordered-list> · React UiUnorderedList","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#ui-unordered-list-react-uiunorderedlist","Attribute Property Type Default Description nested nested boolean false Nested in another list's item (set for you when it sits in a <ui-list-item>). is-expressive isExpressive boolean false Body-02 type (16px) for expressive pages. Slot Description (default) <ui-list-item> elements Part Description list The <ul>"],["List","<ui-ordered-list> · React UiOrderedList","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#ui-ordered-list-react-uiorderedlist","Attribute Property Type Default Description nested nested boolean false Nested in another list's item (set for you when it sits in a <ui-list-item>). native native boolean false The browser's own markers (decimal) instead of Carbon's counter. is-expressive isExpressive boolean false Body-02 type (16px) for expressive pages. Slot Description (default) <ui-list-item> elements Part Description list The <ol>"],["List","<ui-list-item> · React UiListItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/list/#ui-list-item-react-uilistitem","Slot Description (default) The item's content, and a nested list"],["Loading","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/","A loading spinner says that a view or an area is waiting for data. Carbon's spinner is 88px; small is 16px with a grey track. It can cover the whole page (overlay) or one area (contained), and it can wait before it shows, so quick work never flashes a spinner."],["Loading","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Loading","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#use-it",""],["Loading","Loading, inline loading, progress bar or skeleton?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#loading-inline-loading-progress-bar-or-skeleton","Loading: a whole view or one area can't be used until the data arrives. Inline loading: a small status next to the thing that is saving or sending, which ends as \\"done\\" or \\"failed\\". Progress bar: the work has a known size, such as files uploaded out of five. Skeleton: the first load of a page, when you know the shape of the content to come. Inside a button, use the button's own loading; see Button."],["Loading","Small","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#small","small is the 16px spinner with a grey track, for tight places such as a card header or a table toolbar."],["Loading","Description","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#description","description names the spinner for screen readers and is announced when it shows. It defaults to \\"Loading\\", translated to the page language. Say what is loading."],["Loading","Start and stop","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#start-and-stop","The spinner is on by default. Set active to false to stop and hide it; the element stays in the page, ready for the next time. In HTML, write active=\\"false\\" to start it stopped. While it really shows, the element has a data-shown attribute."],["Loading","Over one area","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#over-one-area","contained wraps an area, such as a card or a table, instead of the page. While it is active, the overlay covers just that box, and the content under it is inert and aria-busy. The rest of the page stays usable. Carbon has no contained loading; this is our addition. refresh stands for your own code that sets refreshing while it works."],["Loading","Saving a form in place","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#saving-a-form-in-place","Put the form inside a contained loading while it saves. Focus that was inside the area waits on the spinner, then goes back where it was, so keyboard users keep their place. save stands for your own code that sets saving while it works."],["Loading","Wait before it shows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#wait-before-it-shows","delay (ms) shows the spinner only if the work is still going after that long. min-duration (ms, minDuration in React) keeps it up at least that long once shown, so it doesn't blink on and off. Both default to 0, as in Carbon. Try the quick check: it ends before the delay, and no spinner shows. delay and min-duration work with every kind of loading, not only contained."],["Loading","Over the whole page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#over-the-whole-page","overlay covers the page in the overlay colour while the spinner shows. It holds focus: Tab and clicks elsewhere come back to it. When it stops, focus goes back where it was. A modal dialog opened above it is left alone. Use it only while the whole view can't be used, and always set active from your own state. The overlay is position: fixed. In this demo it sits in a box with a transform, so it covers only the box; in your app it covers the window. generate stands for your own code that sets generating while it works."],["Loading","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#keyboard","Key Does Tab With overlay: stays on the spinner while it shows Esc doesn't close the overlay: it goes away when the work ends."],["Loading","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#accessibility","The spinner is an image named by description, inside an assertive live region while it shows, so screen readers announce it. With overlay, the spinner is a modal dialog named by description and takes focus. Focus goes back to where it was when it stops. With contained, the content is inert and aria-busy while it shows, and the spinner is a group named by description. Focus that was inside waits on the spinner, then goes back. Write the description as what is loading (\\"Loading the contract list\\"), not just \\"Loading\\". Under prefers-reduced-motion, the spinner turns more slowly. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Loading."],["Loading","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Loading","<ui-loading> · React UiLoading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/loading/#ui-loading-react-uiloading","Attribute Property Type Default Description active active boolean true On by default; active=\\"false\\" stops it. small small boolean false overlay overlay boolean false Cover the page and trap focus while active. description description string '' Accessible description; defaults to the translation (\\"Loading\\"). contained contained boolean false Cover just this element's content (the slot) instead of the page; the content is inert while active (no Carbon counterpart). delay delay number 0 Milliseconds active must last before the spinner shows (default 0, as Carbon). min-duration minDuration number 0 Once shown, the least milliseconds it stays (default 0). Slot Description (default) The area contained covers Part Description base The spinner wrapper (aria-live) overlay The page overlay (overlay), or the area's (contained) area The covered content (contained) spinner The <svg>"],["Inline loading","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/","Inline loading shows the progress of one action in place, such as saving or sending: a 16px spinner with a short text beside it. It moves from active to finished (a check mark) or error, and screen readers hear each change."],["Inline loading","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Inline loading","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#use-it",""],["Inline loading","Inline loading or loading?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#inline-loading-or-loading","Use inline loading next to the control that started the work, when the result ends as done or failed. When a whole view or area can't be used until the data arrives, use Loading. When the work has a known size, use a Progress bar. The headless Loading parts cover only a spinner with its timing, not these statuses."],["Inline loading","Statuses","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#statuses","status is one of: active (the default): the spinning icon. finished: a green check mark (it appears at once, as in Carbon). error: a red error icon. inactive: only the text. In HTML and React (UiInlineLoading) the spinner stops as in Carbon web components: it turns out and fades over 1.4s (at once with reduced motion). React + Tailwind follows Carbon React and shows no icon at once. The text in the element is the status text (Carbon's description). Change it with the status."],["Inline loading","In place of the submit button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#in-place-of-the-submit-button","Carbon's pattern: when the user submits, the submit button gives its place to an inline loading. When the work is done, the check mark shows, then ui-success puts the button back. send stands for your own code."],["Inline loading","After success","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#after-success","ui-success fires success-delay ms after status became finished (1500 by default, as Carbon's successDelay). Use it to close a dialog, clear the form or put a button back. In React the event prop is onUiSuccess; in React + Tailwind it is onSuccess."],["Inline loading","Error and try again","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#error-and-try-again","On failure, set status=\\"error\\" and say what failed in the text. Put a way to try again right next to it. retry stands for your own code."],["Inline loading","Checking a field","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#checking-a-field","Inline loading also fits under a field that the server checks, such as a tax ID. Show it when the check starts, and end with the result. check stands for your own code that asks the server and sets result (the status and the text)."],["Inline loading","Icon label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#icon-label","The icon is named by its status: \\"Loading\\", \\"Finished\\" or \\"Error\\", translated to the page language. icon-label (iconLabel in React) names it yourself when the status text needs a different word."],["Inline loading","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#accessibility","The whole element is a polite live region, so screen readers hear the icon's name and the text each time the status changes. Keep the text short and specific: \\"Submitting…\\", \\"Submitted\\", \\"Could not submit\\". Inline loading doesn't take focus. When it replaces the button that had focus, move focus somewhere useful afterwards, such as back to the button. Under prefers-reduced-motion, the spinner stops turning and the check mark shows at once."],["Inline loading","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Inline loading","<ui-inline-loading> · React UiInlineLoading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/inline-loading/#ui-inline-loading-react-uiinlineloading","Attribute Property Type Default Description status status InlineLoadingStatus 'active' success-delay successDelay number 1500 Milliseconds after finished before ui-success fires (Carbon successDelay). icon-label iconLabel string '' Accessible name of the icon; defaults to the status. Event React Description ui-success onUiSuccess success-delay ms after status became finished Slot Description (default) The status text (Carbon description) Part Description base The row icon The spinner / check / error icon text The description"],["Progress bar","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/","A progress bar shows how far a task has come, such as an upload or an import. The track fills to value / max; with no value a stripe sweeps across it while the length is unknown. A label names it, and helper text below says the details."],["Progress bar","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Progress bar","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#use-it",""],["Progress bar","Progress bar, progress indicator or loading?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#progress-bar-progress-indicator-or-loading","Progress bar: the system is doing one task and you can say how far it is. Progress indicator: the user goes through the steps of a form. Loading or Inline loading: something is busy and you can't say how far."],["Progress bar","Value and max","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#value-and-max","value is the progress and max the whole (100 by default). Use the units of the task when they mean something, such as files. A value below 0 or above max is held at the end."],["Progress bar","Indeterminate","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#indeterminate","Leave out value while you don't know the length yet. A stripe sweeps across the track until you set a value or a status."],["Progress bar","Live progress","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#live-progress","Set value as the work goes, and status=\\"finished\\" at the end. The track moves smoothly between values."],["Progress bar","Finished","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#finished","status=\\"finished\\" fills the track in green and puts a check mark beside the label, whatever the value."],["Progress bar","Error","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#error","status=\\"error\\" turns the track, the icon beside the label and the helper text red. Screen readers hear \\"Error\\" after the label. Say in the helper text what went wrong and what to do."],["Progress bar","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#sizes","size: md is an 8px track (Carbon's big, the default); sm is 4px (Carbon's small)."],["Progress bar","Inline","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#inline","type=\\"inline\\" puts the label and the track on one row, for tight places such as a table cell. The helper text is then read by screen readers only. When it is finished or fails, only the label and the icon show."],["Progress bar","Indented","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#indented","type=\\"indented\\" moves the label and the helper text 16px in, to line up with indented content such as the text of a tile or a list row. The track stays full width."],["Progress bar","Hidden label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#hidden-label","hide-label (hideLabel in React) hides the label from view when the text around already says what is progressing. It still names the bar for screen readers, so always write it."],["Progress bar","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#accessibility","The track is a progressbar named by the label and described by the helper text. It has aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax and aria-valuenow when it has a value, and none while indeterminate. It is aria-busy until it is finished. On error, screen readers hear \\"Error\\" after the label, translated to the page language. Always write a label, even with hide-label. Under prefers-reduced-motion, the indeterminate stripe moves more slowly."],["Progress bar","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Progress bar","<ui-progress-bar> · React UiProgressBar","/kanok-ui-docs/en/progress-bar/#ui-progress-bar-react-uiprogressbar","Attribute Property Type Default Description label label string '' Required. What is progressing; shown above (or beside) the track and read as the bar's name. hide-label hideLabel boolean false Visually hides the label (it still names the bar). helper-text helperText string '' value value number | undefined Current progress; leave unset for an indeterminate bar. max max number 100 size size ProgressBarSize 'md' status status ProgressBarStatus 'active' type type ProgressBarType 'default' Part Description base The wrapper label Label row (text + status icon) track The progressbar element bar The filled portion helper-text Helper text below the track Custom property Default Description --ui-progress-track The track's fill (default --ui-surface-1; Kanok: a hairline grey); --ui-progress-radius its corners (default square; Kanok: round)"],["Skeleton","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/","A skeleton is a grey placeholder in the shape of the content to come, shown while a page loads its data for the first time. <ui-skeleton> draws text lines, a heading, a field, a button or a block. Most components also have their own skeleton element; see the index at the end."],["Skeleton","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Skeleton","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#use-it",""],["Skeleton","Skeleton or loading?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#skeleton-or-loading","Use a skeleton for the first load of a page, when you know the layout of what is coming: the page appears at once and the content fills in. Use Loading or Inline loading when the user waits for an action, such as saving, and a skeleton would hide what they were working on."],["Skeleton","Text lines","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#text-lines","shape=\\"text\\" (the default) draws lines bars, 3 by default. The last of several lines is shorter, so it reads as a paragraph."],["Skeleton","Heading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#heading","shape=\\"heading\\" is one 24px bar, half the width by default."],["Skeleton","Field and button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#field-and-button","shape=\\"field\\" is a short label bar above a 48px field bar. shape=\\"button\\" is a 48px bar, 120px wide, that sits inline. For a real field or button, prefer its own skeleton element (see the index below), which matches its size."],["Skeleton","Placeholder block","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#placeholder-block","shape=\\"block\\" is one bar, 160px high by default, for an image, a chart or a whole card (Carbon's SkeletonPlaceholder). Set the height with the --ui-skeleton-height CSS property (height in React + Tailwind)."],["Skeleton","Width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#width","Every shape is full width by default (a heading half, a button 120px). Set the width with the --ui-skeleton-width CSS property (width in React + Tailwind), so the placeholder looks like the content to come. Give it with its unit (\\"200px\\", \\"70%\\"); width and height take strings, as Carbon's SkeletonText width. In React + Tailwind, give width and height with their unit, as strings: they set CSS properties, and a bare number has no unit there."],["Skeleton","Swap it for the content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#swap-it-for-the-content","Skeletons are hidden from screen readers. Tell them about the load on the container instead: aria-busy=\\"true\\" while it loads, and a short status message. When the data arrives, put the content in place and drop both. VendorCard stands for your own component."],["Skeleton","Component skeletons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#component-skeletons","Most components have a skeleton element in their own shape and size, as Carbon's TextInputSkeleton, DropdownSkeleton and so on. Each has its own import, @purpurabog/ui/<component>-skeleton. Each has a React wrapper named after it in @purpurabog/ui/react (UiTextInputSkeleton, UiDropdownSkeleton …). React + Tailwind has a …Skeleton component next to each component."],["Skeleton","Fluid field skeletons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#fluid-field-skeletons","The field skeletons take fluid for the skeleton of a fluid field: a 64px box with two bars. Inside <ui-fluid-form> (FluidForm in React + Tailwind) they are fluid without the attribute. The time picker skeleton is always fluid, as Carbon has only that one."],["Skeleton","Every component skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#every-component-skeleton","Each component page shows its skeleton with its options. The field skeletons (text input, number input, dropdown, select, date picker) also take size (sm, md, lg), hide-label and fluid. Element React + Tailwind Attributes Page ui-accordion-skeleton AccordionSkeleton count, open, alignment Accordion ui-big-number-skeleton BigNumberSkeleton size Big number ui-breadcrumb-skeleton BreadcrumbSkeleton items, no-trailing-slash, size Breadcrumb ui-button-skeleton ButtonSkeleton size Button ui-checkbox-skeleton CheckboxSkeleton Checkbox ui-code-snippet-skeleton CodeSnippetSkeleton type Code snippet ui-date-picker-skeleton DatePickerSkeleton range Date picker ui-dropdown-skeleton DropdownSkeleton Dropdown, also for combobox and multi-select ui-file-uploader-skeleton FileUploaderSkeleton File uploader ui-number-input-skeleton NumberInputSkeleton Number input ui-progress-indicator-skeleton ProgressIndicatorSkeleton steps, vertical Progress indicator ui-radio-skeleton RadioSkeleton Radio ui-search-skeleton SearchSkeleton size, fluid Search ui-select-skeleton SelectSkeleton Select ui-slider-skeleton SliderSkeleton hide-label, two-handles Slider ui-structured-list-skeleton StructuredListSkeleton rows Structured list ui-table-skeleton DataTableSkeleton row-count, column-count, zebra, show-header, show-toolbar Data table ui-tabs-skeleton TabsSkeleton tabs Tabs ui-tag-skeleton TagSkeleton size Tag ui-text-area-skeleton TextAreaSkeleton hide-label, fluid Text area ui-text-input-skeleton TextInputSkeleton Text input ui-time-picker-skeleton TimePickerSkeleton is-only-two Time picker ui-toggle-skeleton ToggleSkeleton Toggle ui-table-skeleton comes with @purpurabog/ui/table. Every element here has a React wrapper named after it: ui-accordion-skeleton is UiAccordionSkeleton, ui-table-skeleton is UiTableSkeleton, and so on; its props are the attributes in camelCase (hideLabel, noTrailingSlash). In React + Tailwind, import each …Skeleton from its component's file, for example TextInputSkeleton from @/components/ui/react-tw/text-input; RadioSkeleton comes from radio-group."],["Skeleton","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#accessibility","Every skeleton is hidden from screen readers (aria-hidden) and never takes focus. Say \\"loading\\" on the container: aria-busy=\\"true\\" and a short status message, such as a role=\\"status\\" \\"Loading contracts…\\". Drop both when the content arrives. The bars have Carbon's 3-second shimmer; under prefers-reduced-motion it stops."],["Skeleton","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Skeleton","<ui-skeleton> · React UiSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-skeleton-react-uiskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description shape shape SkeletonShape 'text' lines lines number 3 Number of lines for shape=\\"text\\". Part Description bone Each grey placeholder bar label The short label bar of shape=\\"field\\" Custom property Default Description --ui-skeleton-width Width (default: full width; buttons 120px) --ui-skeleton-height Height of shape=\\"block\\" (default 160px)"],["Skeleton","<ui-accordion-skeleton> · React UiAccordionSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-accordion-skeleton-react-uiaccordionskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description count count number 4 open open boolean true The first item shows its content. alignment alignment 'start' | 'end' 'end' Part Description title Each title bar line Each line of the open item"],["Skeleton","<ui-big-number-skeleton> · React UiBigNumberSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-big-number-skeleton-react-uibignumberskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size BigNumberSize 'default' Part Description label The label bar value The value bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-breadcrumb-skeleton> · React UiBreadcrumbSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-breadcrumb-skeleton-react-uibreadcrumbskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description items items number 3 no-trailing-slash noTrailingSlash boolean false size size 'sm' | 'md' 'md' Part Description item Each bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-button-skeleton> · React UiButtonSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-button-skeleton-react-uibuttonskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size ButtonSize 'lg' Part Description bone The bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-checkbox-skeleton> · React UiCheckboxSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-checkbox-skeleton-react-uicheckboxskeleton","Part Description box The empty box label The label bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-code-snippet-skeleton> · React UiCodeSnippetSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-code-snippet-skeleton-react-uicodesnippetskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description type type 'single' | 'multi' 'single' Part Description base The box line Each bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-date-picker-skeleton> · React UiDatePickerSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-date-picker-skeleton-react-uidatepickerskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description range range boolean false Start and end inputs. size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label Each label bar field Each field bar (fluid: the box)"],["Skeleton","<ui-dropdown-skeleton> · React UiDropdownSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-dropdown-skeleton-react-uidropdownskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label The label bar field The field bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-file-uploader-skeleton> · React UiFileUploaderSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-file-uploader-skeleton-react-uifileuploaderskeleton","Part Description title The title bar description The description bar button The button bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-number-input-skeleton> · React UiNumberInputSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-number-input-skeleton-react-uinumberinputskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label The label bar field The field bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-progress-indicator-skeleton> · React UiProgressIndicatorSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-progress-indicator-skeleton-react-uiprogressindicatorskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description steps steps number 4 vertical vertical boolean false Part Description step Each step label Each label bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-radio-skeleton> · React UiRadioSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-radio-skeleton-react-uiradioskeleton","Part Description label The label bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-search-skeleton> · React UiSearchSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-search-skeleton-react-uisearchskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' fluid fluid boolean false Carbon FluidSearchSkeleton. Part Description field The bar (fluid: the box) label Fluid: the 25% bar value Fluid: the 50% bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-select-skeleton> · React UiSelectSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-select-skeleton-react-uiselectskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label The label bar field The field bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-slider-skeleton> · React UiSliderSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-slider-skeleton-react-uisliderskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description hide-label hideLabel boolean false two-handles twoHandles boolean false The skeleton of a two-thumb slider (<ui-slider value-upper>). Part Description label The label bar range-label The min / max bars"],["Skeleton","<ui-structured-list-skeleton> · React UiStructuredListSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-structured-list-skeleton-react-uistructuredlistskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description rows rows number 5 Part Description header The header bars row Each empty row"],["Skeleton","<ui-table-skeleton> · React UiTableSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-table-skeleton-react-uitableskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description column-count columnCount number 5 row-count rowCount number 5 show-header showHeader boolean true The title / description bars (Carbon show-header; show-header=\\"false\\" hides them). show-toolbar showToolbar boolean true The toolbar bar (Carbon show-toolbar; show-toolbar=\\"false\\" hides it). zebra zebra boolean false Stripe every second row. Property Type Description headers string[] Header texts to show instead of bars (Carbon headers); their number sets the columns. Part Description table The <table>"],["Skeleton","<ui-tabs-skeleton> · React UiTabsSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-tabs-skeleton-react-uitabsskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description tabs tabs number 5 Part Description tab Each tab"],["Skeleton","<ui-tag-skeleton> · React UiTagSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-tag-skeleton-react-uitagskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' Part Description bone The pill"],["Skeleton","<ui-text-area-skeleton> · React UiTextAreaSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-text-area-skeleton-react-uitextareaskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label The label bar field The field bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-text-input-skeleton> · React UiTextInputSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-text-input-skeleton-react-uitextinputskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'md' The field's height: sm 32px, md 40px, lg 48px. hide-label hideLabel boolean false No label bar (the field had hide-label). fluid fluid boolean false The fluid field's skeleton (Carbon Fluid*Skeleton): a 64px box with two bars; <ui-fluid-form> sets it. Part Description label The label bar field The field bar"],["Skeleton","<ui-time-picker-skeleton> · React UiTimePickerSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-time-picker-skeleton-react-uitimepickerskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description is-only-two isOnlyTwo boolean false Two boxes (time and AM / PM), half each. Part Description field Each box"],["Skeleton","<ui-toggle-skeleton> · React UiToggleSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/skeleton/#ui-toggle-skeleton-react-uitoggleskeleton","Part Description circle The circle bar The bar"],["Badge indicator","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/","A badge indicator is the small red mark in the corner of a ghost icon button, for things that wait for the user, such as approvals or new messages. With a count it shows the number; without one it is a dot. It belongs on an icon button: <ui-icon-button badge-count> makes one for you. The icons are Carbon's, from @carbon/icons-react (see Icons)."],["Badge indicator","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Badge indicator","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#use-it","@purpurabog/ui/icon-button brings the badge indicator with it. Import @purpurabog/ui/badge-indicator on its own only when you place <ui-badge-indicator> yourself."],["Badge indicator","Count or dot","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#count-or-dot","badge-count (badgeCount in React) with a number above 0 shows the count in a 16px pill. 0 shows an 8px dot: something is new, but the number doesn't matter. Leave the attribute out for no badge."],["Badge indicator","Large counts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#large-counts","Past 999 the badge shows \\"999+\\", as in Carbon."],["Badge indicator","Small buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#small-buttons","Carbon designs the badge for the large (48px) ghost button. On a small button the dot sits 4px from the corner instead of 8px, so it stays on the button."],["Badge indicator","Your own badge element","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#your-own-badge-element","Instead of badge-count, put a <ui-badge-indicator count=\\"…\\"> inside the icon button. It takes the button's badge-indicator slot by itself, and the button still reads its count to screen readers. In React, UiBadgeIndicator works the same way. React + Tailwind has only badgeCount on IconButton for this; its BadgeIndicator is the part that IconButton draws."],["Badge indicator","Update the count","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#update-the-count","Set badgeCount as the number changes. To take the badge away, set the property to undefined (badgeCount={undefined} in React). Approve the requests one by one below: the last one removes the badge."],["Badge indicator","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#disabled","A disabled icon button hides its badge, and screen readers no longer hear the count."],["Badge indicator","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#accessibility","The badge itself is hidden from screen readers. The icon button reads the count as its description (Carbon's aria-describedby), so screen readers hear the count after the button's name. A dot has no count to read. Say it in the label instead, such as \\"Notifications, new\\". The label stays the button's name: write what the button opens (\\"Approvals\\"), not the count. In forced-colors mode the badge gets a border, so it stays visible."],["Badge indicator","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Badge indicator","<ui-badge-indicator> · React UiBadgeIndicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/badge-indicator/#ui-badge-indicator-react-uibadgeindicator","Attribute Property Type Default Description count count number | undefined The number shown; unset or 0 = a dot."],["Status indicator","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/","A status indicator shows the state of something with a small coloured icon and a label, such as a job that succeeded or an incident's severity. <ui-icon-indicator> uses Carbon's status icons; <ui-shape-indicator> uses simple shapes for severity and state. Both follow Carbon's status indicators, which Carbon still marks as preview."],["Status indicator","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Status indicator","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#use-it",""],["Status indicator","Icon or shape?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#icon-or-shape","Icon indicator: the state of a process or an item, such as a payment, an import or a server. Shape indicator: a level, such as the severity of an incident or a risk, and a few states (stable, draft, incomplete). For a label the user can click or remove, use a Tag instead. Each kind has its own icon and colour, so the state doesn't depend on colour alone. Always write a label."],["Status indicator","Icon indicator kinds","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#icon-indicator-kinds","kind picks the icon and its colour. There are 12 kinds; a kind that isn't one of them renders nothing."],["Status indicator","Icon size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#icon-size","size is 16 (the default, with 14px text) or 20 (with 16px text), for a bigger heading or a dashboard tile."],["Status indicator","Shape indicator kinds","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#shape-indicator-kinds","<ui-shape-indicator> has 11 kinds: the severities (failed, critical, high, medium, low, cautious) and the states (undefined, stable, informative, incomplete, draft). The shape is always 16px."],["Status indicator","Text size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#text-size","The shape indicator's text is 12px by default. text-size=\\"14\\" (textSize={14} in React) makes it 14px, to match body text around it."],["Status indicator","Compact","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#compact","compact shows only the icon or shape. The label moves into a tooltip that opens on hover and on keyboard focus. Screen readers hear the label, or icon-description / shape-description (iconDescription / shapeDescription in React) when you set one, for a longer text than the tooltip."],["Status indicator","Tooltip placement","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#tooltip-placement","placement sets where the compact tooltip opens: top, bottom, left or right (the default), each also with -start or -end. align is Carbon's name for it and takes the same values."],["Status indicator","In a list","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#in-a-list","Status indicators fit in a column of a list or a table, where each row has its own state."],["Status indicator","Severity","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#severity","Use the shape indicator for a level, such as the severity of incidents. Pair the shape with a word, so the order is clear without the colours."],["Status indicator","Change the status","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#change-the-status","Set kind and label as the state changes. The indicator is not a live region: when the change matters to the user, also announce it, for example in a role=\\"status\\" line."],["Status indicator","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#keyboard","Only the compact indicators take focus. Key Does Tab Moves to a compact icon and opens its tooltip; leaving closes it Enter, Space Open or close the tooltip Esc Closes the tooltip"],["Status indicator","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#accessibility","The icon or shape is hidden from screen readers; the label says the state. Write it as the state (\\"Signed\\"), not the colour. Compact: the icon is a button that opens a definition tooltip with the label, and screen readers read the label or the description. Status changes are not announced by themselves; add a status message when they matter."],["Status indicator","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Status indicator","<ui-icon-indicator> · React UiIconIndicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#ui-icon-indicator-react-uiiconindicator","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) kind kind IconIndicatorKind | undefined label label string '' size size 16 | 20 16 16 (body-compact-01) or 20 (body-compact-02). compact compact boolean false Only the icon; the label in a tooltip. icon-description iconDescription string | undefined Read by screen readers in compact mode instead of the label. placement placement Placement 'right' Where the compact tooltip opens. Part Description icon The icon label The label (not compact)"],["Status indicator","<ui-shape-indicator> · React UiShapeIndicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/status-indicator/#ui-shape-indicator-react-uishapeindicator","Attribute Property Type Default Description align Carbon's name for placement (same values) kind kind ShapeIndicatorKind | undefined label label string '' text-size textSize 12 | 14 12 12 (helper-text-01) or 14 (body-compact-01). compact compact boolean false Only the shape; the label in a tooltip. shape-description shapeDescription string | undefined Read by screen readers in compact mode instead of the label. placement placement Placement 'right' Where the compact tooltip opens. Part Description icon The shape label The label (not compact)"],["Grid","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/","The grid is Carbon's 2x Grid: 4 columns on small screens, 8 from 672px (md) and 16 from 1056px (lg), with 32px gutters. <ui-grid> holds <ui-column>s, and each column says how many columns it spans at each size. The tinted boxes on this page only show where the columns are. The sizes follow the width of the window, not of the box the grid sits in, as Carbon's media queries do. On this page the grid sits in a narrow column, so widen or narrow the window to see the columns move."],["Grid","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Grid","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#use-it","Size From Columns Grid margin sm 0 4 0 md 672px 8 16px lg 1056px 16 16px xlg 1312px 16 16px max 1584px 16 24px The grid is at most 1584px wide and centred. Each column is 16px in from the gutter on both sides, so text in neighbouring columns is 32px apart."],["Grid","Spans per size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#spans-per-size","sm, md, lg, xlg and max set the span from that size up: lg=\\"4\\" holds at lg, xlg and max until a larger size says otherwise. A column with no span takes one column. The web component and the React wrapper take the span as text (\\"4\\"); React + Tailwind takes a number."],["Grid","One span for every size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#one-span-for-every-size","span sets the same span at every size. Use it inside a subgrid, where the parent column already decides the width."],["Grid","Hide a column at a size","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#hide-a-column-at-a-size","A span of 0 hides the column from that size up. Here the help panel shows only from lg."],["Grid","Percent spans","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#percent-spans","25%, 50%, 75% and 100% take that share of the grid's columns at each size: 50% is 2 of 4, 4 of 8 and 8 of 16."],["Grid","Offset, start and end","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#offset-start-and-end","Write tokens to place a column: offset:N skips N columns, start:N and end:N are the grid lines it starts and ends at. In React + Tailwind, pass an object."],["Grid","Narrow and column hang","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#narrow-and-column-hang","narrow drops the gutter at the start of each column, so the text hangs on the gutter: Carbon uses it for type-heavy pages. Inside a narrow column, <ui-column-hang> pushes content in by 16px, so it lines up with the text of a wide grid above or below."],["Grid","Condensed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#condensed","condensed makes the gutters 1px, for tiles or images that sit edge to edge, such as a dashboard of cards. <ui-column-hang> pushes text in by 15.5px here."],["Grid","Space between rows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#space-between-rows","Columns that wrap to a new row touch by default. with-row-gap (withRowGap) spaces the rows like the columns: 32px, 16px in a narrow grid, 1px in a condensed one."],["Grid","Full width and alignment","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#full-width-and-alignment","The grid stops at 1584px and centres itself. full-width (fullWidth) lets it fill any screen; align=\\"start\\" or align=\\"end\\" pins the 1584px grid to one side. On this page the grid is narrower than 1584px, so the preview looks the same; the difference shows on a wide screen."],["Grid","Subgrids","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#subgrids","A <ui-grid> inside a <ui-column> becomes a subgrid: it has as many columns as its column spans, and its own columns line up with the outer grid. You don't mark it; nesting is enough. A subgrid decides once, when it is added to the page, whether it sits in a column. Moving a <ui-grid> in or out of a column later doesn't switch it."],["Grid","Mix gutter modes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#mix-gutter-modes","A subgrid can be narrow or condensed while the outer grid stays wide. Its <ui-column-hang>s still line up with the wide text around them. A percent span counts the columns of the size (4, 8 or 16), not the subgrid's. In a subgrid narrower than the grid, give numbers, as the condensed columns below do."],["Grid","Lay out a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#lay-out-a-form","Fields in columns: two side by side from md, one per row on a phone. The grid's 32px gutter separates them, so the fields need no margins of their own."],["Grid","Other elements as the grid or a column","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#other-elements-as-the-grid-or-a-column","In React + Tailwind, as renders the grid or a column as another element, for example a <main> grid with <section> columns. The web component is always <ui-grid>; put your landmark around it or inside a column."],["Grid","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#accessibility","The grid only places things. It has no role, and screen readers read the columns in the order they appear in the markup. Keep that order meaningful; don't use offsets to move content before something that comes earlier in the markup. A column hidden with a span of 0 is display: none at that size, so it is hidden from screen readers too. Use headings and landmarks for structure; the grid adds none."],["Grid","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Grid","<ui-grid> · React UiGrid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#ui-grid-react-uigrid","Attribute Property Type Default Description narrow narrow boolean false No start gutter: text hangs on the gutter (Carbon narrow). condensed condensed boolean false 1px gutters (Carbon condensed). full-width fullWidth boolean false No max width. align align 'start' | 'center' | 'end' | undefined Pin a max-width grid to a side (centred by default). with-row-gap withRowGap boolean false Rows spaced like columns. Slot Description (default) <ui-column> elements Part Description grid The grid Custom property Default Description --ui-grid-gutter The gutter (32px; 1px condensed)"],["Grid","<ui-column> · React UiColumn","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#ui-column-react-uicolumn","Attribute Property Type Default Description sm sm string | undefined md md string | undefined lg lg string | undefined xlg xlg string | undefined max max string | undefined span span string | undefined The span at every breakpoint (Carbon span). Slot Description (default) The column's content"],["Grid","<ui-column-hang> · React UiColumnHang","/kanok-ui-docs/en/grid/#ui-column-hang-react-uicolumnhang","Slot Description (default) The content"],["Heading","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/","<ui-heading> renders a heading at the right level without you counting: each <ui-section> around it goes one level deeper, so the same markup gives an <h2> on one page and an <h4> inside a nested panel. The type follows Carbon's productive scale for that level. The previews on this page start at level 3, because the page already has its own <h1> and <h2>s. The result above is <h3>, <h4>, <h5>, <h6>."],["Heading","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Heading","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#use-it","A <ui-heading> outside any section is an <h1>. The first section makes its headings <h2>, a section inside it <h3>, and so on down to <h6>. <ui-section> is a plain block with no role. The React + Tailwind Section renders a <section> element; change it with as (for example as=\\"div\\")."],["Heading","Set the level","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#set-the-level","level on a section sets the level of its headings, instead of one more than the section around it. Use it where a block starts below a heading that isn't a <ui-heading>, such as a page title from your layout. Sections inside it count on from there. Levels stop at 6."],["Heading","Type for each level","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#type-for-each-level","Level Carbon type Size <h1> heading-06 42px, light <h2> heading-05 32px <h3> heading-04 28px <h4> heading-03 20px <h5> heading-02 16px, semibold <h6> heading-01 14px, semibold Headings have no margins: space them with the layout around them, for example the gap of a flex box or a grid."],["Heading","The same block at any depth","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#the-same-block-at-any-depth","A block you reuse, such as a summary card, can hold a <ui-heading> and still be right wherever it goes: inside one section it is an <h4>, inside two it is an <h5>. The web component works out its level when it is added to the page. If you move a <ui-heading> to another section, it takes the new level then; changing a section's level later doesn't renumber the headings already inside."],["Heading","Style a heading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#style-a-heading","The web component shows its <h1>…<h6> as the heading part. In React + Tailwind, pass a className."],["Heading","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#accessibility","Screen reader users jump between headings and list them to find their way. Levels that follow the nesting make that list match the page. Keep one <h1> per page. Start a block at a deeper level when the page title comes from somewhere else. <ui-section> adds no landmark. If a part of the page needs one, wrap it in your own <section aria-labelledby> or <nav>."],["Heading","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Heading","<ui-heading> · React UiHeading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#ui-heading-react-uiheading","Property Type Description level HeadingLevel The level from the <ui-section> around it (1 outside any). Method Description syncLevel() Takes the level of the section around it (also called by a section whose level changed). Slot Description (default) The heading text Part Description heading The <h1>…<h6>"],["Heading","<ui-section> · React UiSection","/kanok-ui-docs/en/heading/#ui-section-react-uisection","Attribute Property Type Default Description level level number | undefined The heading level inside, instead of one more than the section around it. Method Description getCurrentLevel() The level its headings use (Carbon getCurrentLevel). syncLevel() Takes its level from level, else from the section around it (also called by an ancestor whose level changed). Slot Description (default) The section's content"],["Layer","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/","<ui-layer> is Carbon's Layer: everything inside it uses the theme's next layer set, so a field on a gray tile isn't the same gray as the tile. Fields, menus, borders, dividers and hover fills all follow it. The Themes and layers guide explains the layering model; this page shows the element."],["Layer","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Layer","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#use-it",""],["Layer","Levels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#levels","level is 0, 1 or 2. Level 0 is the page's own set, the same as outside any layer; 1 and 2 go deeper. Without level, the web component and the React wrapper start at 0 and a nested layer goes one deeper, as Carbon's cds-layer. The React + Tailwind Layer follows Carbon React instead: it starts at 1. Nesting deeper than level 2 stays at 2."],["Layer","Fields on a tile","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#fields-on-a-tile","A tile paints the current layer's color, but it doesn't change the layer of what is inside it. Put the fields in a layer one level up, so they stand out from the tile."],["Layer","With or without a background","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#with-or-without-a-background","A layer on its own only changes the tokens for what is inside it; it paints nothing. with-background (withBackground) paints it with Carbon's layer background, the surface its content sits on. Leave it off when your own box (a tile, a panel) already paints the surface."],["Layer","Menus, tables and other components","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#menus-tables-and-other-components","Everything that reads the layer tokens follows the layer: the list of a dropdown, the rows of a table, the dividers of a structured list, the hover fill of a ghost button."],["Layer","In a dark zone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#in-a-dark-zone","A layer works inside any theme zone: it moves along that theme's layer sets. See Make a zone dark for the zone itself."],["Layer","Read the level","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#read-the-level","The element's level property holds its level, worked out or set. In React + Tailwind, useLayerLevel() returns the level of the closest Layer (-1 outside any), for your own components that paint by layer. The web component works its level out when it is added to the page, through shadow roots too. Set level yourself if you move a layer somewhere else later."],["Layer","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#accessibility","A layer is only color. It has no role and adds nothing for screen readers. Layers keep fields visible against the surface under them, which helps everyone see where to type. Don't rely on the layer color alone to tell areas apart; use headings and labels too."],["Layer","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Layer","<ui-layer> · React UiLayer","/kanok-ui-docs/en/layer/#ui-layer-react-uilayer","Attribute Property Type Default Description level level 0, 1 or 2. Computed from the nearest ancestor layer when not set. with-background withBackground boolean false Paint the layer with Carbon's layer-background (withBackground): the colour its content sits on (white theme, level 1: #f4f4f4 under #ffffff fields). Method Description syncLevel() An automatic level follows the layer around it (also called by a layer whose level changed); a set one stays. Slot Description (default) Content Part Description base The wrapper Custom property Default Description --ui-layer-border / --ui-layer-radius - With with-background: its border and corner radius (default none, 0: Carbon's square, unbordered zone, Kanok too)"],["Action set","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/","An action set is the row of large buttons at the foot of a side panel or a tearsheet (Carbon for IBM Products ActionSet). The buttons are 64px tall with their text at the top, split by thin lines, and they share the width by rules that depend on how many there are and how wide the set is. In a narrow set they stack, the primary on top. Side panels and tearsheets lay out their own slot=\\"actions\\" buttons by these rules, so you don't need <ui-action-set> there. Use it for a panel or a page foot you build yourself."],["Action set","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Action set","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#use-it","The web component takes <ui-button>s as children. React + Tailwind takes the buttons as data in actions: each one is a Button's props plus a label."],["Action set","Action set or button set?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#action-set-or-button-set","Component Use it for Action set The foot of a side panel, a tearsheet or a full-width panel: 64px buttons that fill the width by Carbon's rules and stack when the panel is narrow. Button set Buttons at the end of a form: normal-height buttons side by side, each up to 196px wide."],["Action set","Size and stacking","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#size-and-stacking","size is the size of the panel the set sits in: sm, md (the default), lg, xl or 2xl (a side panel's xs counts as sm). A small set always stacks; a medium set stacks from three buttons. In a row, two buttons take half each, three or four take a quarter each (232px at most) in a large set, and in xl and 2xl sets every button takes a quarter. The max-widths only stand in for the panel widths in this preview."],["Action set","One, three or four buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#one-three-or-four-buttons","A lone button fills a medium set and takes half of a large one. Three buttons stack in a medium set and sit in quarters in a large one. Four is the most a set takes."],["Action set","Order of the buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#order-of-the-buttons","Carbon's order in a row is ghost, tertiary, secondary, danger, primary, so the primary action ends the row. A stack shows them the other way round, the primary on top. Web component and React wrapper: write the buttons in that order. The element keeps your order; a stack only reverses it on screen. React + Tailwind: ActionSet sorts actions into that order itself. Carbon allows one primary and one ghost per set. In a stacked set, Carbon also advises against a ghost next to other buttons. A set that breaks these rules, or has more buttons than its size takes, warns on the browser console as Carbon's ActionSet does, once until the buttons change; side panels and tearsheets check their actions too."],["Action set","A ghost takes what is left","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#a-ghost-takes-what-is-left","A ghost button in a row takes the width the others leave: 75% next to one button, 50% next to two, 25% next to three. Its text starts 16px in. Use it for Cancel in a wide panel."],["Action set","Condensed","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#condensed","condensed makes the buttons 48px tall, as Carbon's condensedActions on a side panel."],["Action set","Keep the buttons in a row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#keep-the-buttons-in-a-row","disable-stacking (disableStacking) keeps the buttons side by side even where Carbon would stack them. Use it only when the labels are short enough to fit."],["Action set","Handle the clicks","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#handle-the-clicks","The buttons are ordinary buttons: listen to each one's click. In React + Tailwind, give each action an onClick; disabled and loading work too, as on a Button."],["Action set","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#accessibility","The buttons are real buttons in the order you write them: Tab follows the markup, the same in a row and in a stack. In a stack, the web component shows them reversed, so the primary on top is the last one Tab reaches, as in Carbon. Give each button a label that says what happens (\\"Approve\\", not \\"OK\\"). The thin line between two buttons is left out next to the focused one, so the focus ring stays clear."],["Action set","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Action set","<ui-action-set> · React UiActionSet","/kanok-ui-docs/en/action-set/#ui-action-set-react-uiactionset","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size ActionSetSize 'md' The set's size (a side panel's size; xs counts as sm): how the buttons share the row, or stack. condensed condensed boolean false 48px buttons instead of 64px (Carbon condensedActions of a side panel). disable-stacking disableStacking boolean false Keep the buttons in a row even where Carbon would stack them. Property Type Description stacked (read-only) Whether the buttons stack, one per row. Slot Description (default) The buttons Part Description base The row of buttons Custom property Default Description --ui-actions-gap / --ui-actions-padding - Gap between the action buttons and padding round them (default none: full-bleed buttons that touch; Kanok: 8px / 16px 20px) --ui-actions-button-flex flex of each action button (default: Carbon's widths by count; Kanok: their own width) --ui-actions-button-align / --ui-actions-button-padding-top - Where a button's label sits (default: at the top, 16px in) --ui-actions-stacked-direction / --ui-actions-stacked-wrap / --ui-actions-stacked-width - Where Carbon stacks the actions (narrow): flex-direction, flex-wrap and each button's width (default column-reverse, nowrap, 100%; Kanok: one row that wraps)"],["Page header","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/","The page header is the top of a page in a product (Carbon PageHeader, from Carbon for IBM Products): a breadcrumb bar, the page title with its actions and a short text, and a tab bar. It sticks as the page scrolls: the title and text slide under the breadcrumb bar, which stays, the title appears as the last crumb, and the page's main action moves into the bar. Scroll the box below to see it. The header sticks inside the box that scrolls it: the page, or the nearest element with overflow: auto or scroll. Each preview on this page sits in its own scrolling box."],["Page header","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Page header","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#use-it","In React, import a wrapper for each element (UiPageHeader, UiPageHeaderBreadcrumb, UiPageHeaderContent …) from @purpurabog/ui/react, as in the React tabs here."],["Page header","The parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#the-parts","Web component React + Tailwind What it is <ui-page-header> PageHeader The header: a layer-01 surface with a line below. Holds the parts and makes them stick. <ui-page-header-breadcrumb> PageHeaderBreadcrumbBar The 40px bar on top: an icon, the breadcrumb trail, and actions at the end. It stays when the rest scrolls. <ui-page-header-title-breadcrumb> PageHeaderTitleBreadcrumb The page title as the last crumb. It shows once the title has scrolled away. <ui-page-header-content> PageHeaderContent The title row: an icon, the title, contextual actions next to it and page actions at the end. <ui-page-header-content-text> PageHeaderContentText A subtitle and a short text under the title, at most 640px wide. <ui-page-header-hero-image> PageHeaderHeroImage An image beside the content. <ui-page-header-tabs> PageHeaderTabBar The bar of tabs, with tags and the collapse button at the end. <ui-page-header-scroller> PageHeaderScrollButton The button that collapses or expands the header. <ui-page-header-actions> PageHeaderActions Page actions in a row; those that don't fit go into a \\"⋮\\" menu. <ui-page-header-tags> PageHeaderTags Tags in one line; those that don't fit go behind a \\"+N\\" tag. Use only the parts you need, in this order: breadcrumb bar, content, tab bar."],["Page header","Breadcrumb bar only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#breadcrumb-bar-only","A page without a title area, such as a list page, can have just the bar. Without a <ui-page-header-content>, the title crumb always shows."],["Page header","Title, subtitle and text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#title-subtitle-and-text","heading is the page title, in Carbon's heading-04 (28px), at most 640px wide and two lines; a longer title ends in \\"…\\" and shows whole in a tooltip. <ui-page-header-content-text> adds a subtitle and a short text under it. An icon goes in the content's icon slot. ReportIcon is Carbon's Report icon from @carbon/icons-react (see Icons); the content shows it at 32px."],["Page header","Contextual and page actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#contextual-and-page-actions","slot=\\"contextual-actions\\" sits right after the title: a status tag, for example. With it, the title keeps to one line. slot=\\"page-actions\\" sits at the end of the title row: the page's main buttons. When the page actions scroll under the bar, they fade out and the bar's slot=\\"content-actions\\" fades in, so put the same main action there too. The bar's content actions show only from 672px wide (md); on a phone, the bar keeps just the trail and its page actions."],["Page header","Actions that overflow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#actions-that-overflow","Put a page's icon buttons in <ui-page-header-actions>, in the bar's or the content's slot=\\"page-actions\\". The buttons that don't fit go, from the end, into a \\"⋮\\" menu; choosing one there clicks its button. Each button's label (else its text) names it in the menu. Narrow the box with the slider to see it. overflow-label (overflowLabel) names the \\"⋮\\" menu; it is \\"More actions\\" in the page language by default."],["Page header","Tabs and tags","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#tabs-and-tags","The tab bar holds a tabs strip, then slot=\\"tags\\" at its end, 40% wide. <ui-page-header-tags> takes its tags as data (a JSON attribute, or the property) and shows them on one line; the ones that don't fit go behind a \\"+N\\" tag that opens them in a popover. Past ten hidden tags, the popover offers \\"View all tags\\", a dialog with a search. A dismissible tag removes itself and fires ui-tag-dismiss with { tag, index }. React + Tailwind's PageHeaderTags doesn't remove a dismissed tag itself: onDismiss tells you, and you take it out of tags. The tab panels go below the header, in the page."],["Page header","Collapse and expand","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#collapse-and-expand","<ui-page-header-scroller> in the tab bar's slot=\\"scroller\\" is a ghost button with a chevron. It scrolls the page until the content sits just under the breadcrumb bar, or back to the top once it has. Its name and tooltip say \\"Collapse\\" or \\"Expand\\", in the page language; collapse-text and expand-text change them. ui-page-header-state fires on <ui-page-header> (it doesn't bubble) each time the header's state changes: fullyCollapsed, titleClipped, contentActionsClipped. React + Tailwind's PageHeader has onContentFullyCollapsed, onTitleClipped and onContentActionsClipped instead. disable-sticky-tab-bar (disableStickyTabBar) on the tab bar lets the whole header scroll away with the page, as Carbon's disableStickyTabBar: the breadcrumb bar is then fixed at the top of the window, full width, so use it for a header at the top of the page."],["Page header","Hero image","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#hero-image","<ui-page-header-hero-image> holds an <img> (or <picture>) beside the content, cropped to 3:2, or 2:1 from 1056px (lg). Carbon lays it out with a grid: the bar and the content in one half, the image in the other, which hides on a phone. object-fit=\\"contain\\" shows the whole image instead of cropping it. A decorative image takes alt=\\"\\". If the image says something the text doesn't, describe it in alt."],["Page header","Grid options","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#grid-options","The parts line up on Carbon's grid: at most 1584px wide and centred, with the grid's margin. narrow-grid (narrowGrid) hangs the text on the margin, without the half gutter; full-width-grid (fullWidthGrid) drops the 1584px cap. Match them to the grid of the page below."],["Page header","Rich title and heading levels","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#rich-title-and-heading-levels","The title is an <h1>. heading-level (headingAs in React + Tailwind) makes it another level, for a header inside a page that already has its <h1>; the subtitle is an <h2> and subtitle-level (subtitleAs) changes it. For a title with markup, put it in the content's slot=\\"title\\" instead of heading; in React + Tailwind, heading takes markup. A title in the slot isn't cut to two lines and gets no tooltip."],["Page header","Bar options","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#bar-options","On the breadcrumb bar: slot=\\"icon\\" (icon) puts a 16px icon before the trail; border=\\"false\\" (border={false}) drops the line under the bar; page-actions-flush (pageActionsFlush) lets the page actions reach the edge; content-actions-flush (contentActionsFlush) drops the 12px gap after the content actions. actions-aria-label (actionsAriaLabel) names the bar's toolbar (\\"Page header actions\\" by default, in the page language). A long trail can fold its middle crumbs into a menu with the breadcrumb's overflow."],["Page header","Under a fixed header","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#under-a-fixed-header","When the page has a fixed UI shell header above it, the page header measures how far it sits below the top of its scrolling box and sticks under the shell, not behind it. You set nothing. It measures again whenever its size changes."],["Page header","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#accessibility","The title is a real heading (<h1> by default); keep one <h1> per page. The title crumb is hidden from screen readers and out of the Tab order until it shows, so the trail isn't read twice. The page actions that fade out while scrolled away are hidden from everyone, and the bar's content actions show instead. Put the same actions in both places. The bar's actions are a toolbar with a name. The \\"+N\\" tag announces how many tags are hidden (\\"4 more tags\\"). With reduced motion, the title crumb fades in without moving."],["Page header","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Page header","<ui-page-header> · React UiPageHeader","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-react-uipageheader","Attribute Property Type Default Description full-width-grid fullWidthGrid boolean false No 1584px cap on the grid. narrow-grid narrowGrid boolean false Hang the text on the grid margin. Property Type Description state PageHeaderState The shared state; its parts read it. Method Description setState(next) Merge into the state and tell the parts. setStatic(on) A tab bar asks the header not to stick (Carbon disableStickyTabBar): the bar is fixed instead. Event React Description ui-page-header-state onUiPageHeaderState The state changed (state: fullyCollapsed, titleClipped, contentActionsClipped …); not bubbling Slot Description (default) The parts Custom property Default Description --ui-page-header-top Set by the header: how far up it sticks (minus the content's height) --ui-page-header-bar-top Set by the header: where the bar sticks (under a fixed UI shell)"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-breadcrumb> · React UiPageHeaderBreadcrumb","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-breadcrumb-react-uipageheaderbreadcrumb","Attribute Property Type Default Description border border boolean true The line under the bar. page-actions-flush pageActionsFlush boolean false The page actions reach the screen's edge. content-actions-flush contentActionsFlush boolean false No 12px gap after the content actions. actions-aria-label actionsAriaLabel string '' The toolbar's name (default \\"Page header actions\\", translated). Slot Description (default) The breadcrumb trail icon A 16px icon before the trail content-actions The content's page actions again, for when they have scrolled away page-actions Actions for the whole page (e.g. ghost icon buttons)"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-title-breadcrumb> · React UiPageHeaderTitleBreadcrumb","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-title-breadcrumb-react-uipageheadertitlebreadcrumb","Attribute Property Type Default Description href href string '' current current boolean false The page the user is on: plain text with aria-current=\\"page\\". Event React Description ui-navigate none (use a ref) detail: { href } (cancelable) on a plain click of the link; cancel it to route client-side (README: SPA router) Slot Description (default) The item text Part Description base The link or the current-page text Custom property Default Description --ui-breadcrumb-trailing-slash display of the slash after the last item (default inline; Kanok: none)"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-content> · React UiPageHeaderContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-content-react-uipageheadercontent","Attribute Property Type Default Description heading heading string '' The page's title (Carbon title, which would also be the element's native tooltip). heading-level headingLevel string 'h1' The title's element (h1 … h6). Slot Description (default) What follows the title (a <ui-page-header-content-text>) icon An icon before the title title Rich title instead of heading contextual-actions Next to the title page-actions At the end of the title row Part Description title The title heading"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-content-text> · React UiPageHeaderContentText","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-content-text-react-uipageheadercontenttext","Attribute Property Type Default Description subtitle subtitle string '' subtitle-level subtitleLevel string 'h2' The subtitle's element (h1 … h6). Slot Description (default) The text Part Description subtitle The subtitle heading"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-hero-image> · React UiPageHeaderHeroImage","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-hero-image-react-uipageheaderheroimage","Attribute Property Type Default Description object-fit objectFit 'cover' | 'contain' 'cover' Slot Description (default) The <img> (or <picture>)"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-tabs> · React UiPageHeaderTabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-tabs-react-uipageheadertabs","Attribute Property Type Default Description disable-sticky-tab-bar disableStickyTabBar boolean false Slot Description (default) The tabs tags Tags at the end scroller The collapse / expand button"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-scroller> · React UiPageHeaderScroller","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-scroller-react-uipageheaderscroller","Attribute Property Type Default Description collapse-text collapseText string '' expand-text expandText string ''"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-actions> · React UiPageHeaderActions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-actions-react-uipageheaderactions","Attribute Property Type Default Description overflow-label overflowLabel string '' The overflow menu's name (default: the translation's \\"More actions\\"). Slot Description (default) The buttons (<ui-icon-button>s, <ui-button>s), in order; each one's label (else its text) names it in the menu Part Description overflow The overflow menu"],["Page header","<ui-page-header-tags> · React UiPageHeaderTags","/kanok-ui-docs/en/page-header/#ui-page-header-tags-react-uipageheadertags","Attribute Property Type Default Description tags tags PageHeaderTag[] [] The tags, in order (Carbon tags-data; JSON as an attribute). Event React Description ui-tag-dismiss onUiTagDismiss detail: { tag, index } after a dismissible tag was dismissed (it is already gone from tags) Part Description more The \\"+N\\" tag popover The popover of hidden tags modal The \\"All tags\\" modal"],["Big number","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/","A big number shows one key figure large, under a small label: active contracts, money spent, uptime (Carbon for IBM Products BigNumber). It shortens long numbers (\\"12.3K\\"), can show the value against a total (\\"12.3K/50.0K\\"), a percentage, and an up arrow for a rising trend."],["Big number","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Big number","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#use-it",""],["Big number","Short or full numbers","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#short-or-full-numbers","By default the number is shortened with one decimal: 12,345 becomes \\"12.3K\\". fraction-digits (fractionDigits) sets the decimals. truncate=\\"false\\" (truncate={false}) writes the whole number with its separators, for figures people copy or check. Without a value, it shows \\"–\\"."],["Big number","Against a total","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#against-a-total","total adds \\"/total\\" after the value, smaller. It shows only when it is larger than the value and reads differently once shortened: 49,990 of 50,000 would both read \\"50.0K\\", so the total is left out. force-show-total (forceShowTotal) shows it anyway, and \\"Unknown\\" when there is no total. \\"Unknown\\" follows the page language."],["Big number","Percentage","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#percentage","percentage adds a small \\"%\\" after the value. A percentage never shows a total, unless forced."],["Big number","Trending","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#trending","trending puts an up arrow before the value. To show a different icon, such as a down arrow, put it in the trending-icon slot; in React + Tailwind, pass the icon to trending. The arrow is only a picture. Say what it means in the label or the text around it (\\"up 12% from last month\\"), so screen reader users get it too."],["Big number","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#sizes","size: the default (label 12px, value 28px), lg (value 42px) and xl (label 14px, value 54px). The total, the \\"%\\" and the arrow grow with it."],["Big number","Explain the number","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#explain-the-number","tooltip-description (tooltipDescription) adds a small info button after the label; hovering or focusing it shows the text in a tooltip. Its name is \\"More information\\", in the page language."],["Big number","Your own label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#your-own-label","When the label needs more than text, such as a toggletip with a link, put your markup in the label slot. In React + Tailwind, pass it to label."],["Big number","An action after the value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#an-action-after-the-value","The icon-button slot (iconButton in React + Tailwind) puts a small button after the value, for example to refresh it or open the report behind it."],["Big number","Number format of a locale","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#number-format-of-a-locale","locale writes the numbers the way a locale does, with Intl's short forms and separators. Without it, or with one the browser doesn't know, numbers are written as in en-US, as in Carbon. It doesn't follow the page language by itself."],["Big number","A row of key figures","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#a-row-of-key-figures","Put several big numbers side by side at the top of a dashboard. A grid or a flex row with a gap is enough; the element has no margins."],["Big number","Loading and skeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#loading-and-skeleton","While the number loads, set loading: the element shows its skeleton at the same size. ui-big-number-skeleton is the skeleton on its own, for a layout drawn before any data. Both are hidden from screen readers, so say \\"loading\\" on the container (for example aria-busy). On the web component, import the skeleton from @purpurabog/ui/big-number-skeleton; <ui-big-number> loads it itself."],["Big number","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#accessibility","The big number is a <figure> with its label as the <figcaption>, so the label names the figure. The shortened number is what screen readers read: \\"12.3K\\". When the exact figure matters, use truncate=\\"false\\" or give it in the text nearby. The trend arrow is hidden from screen readers. Put what it means in words. The info button of tooltip-description is a real button, reached with Tab."],["Big number","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Big number","<ui-big-number> · React UiBigNumber","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#ui-big-number-react-uibignumber","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value number | undefined The value (the numerator of a fraction). total total number | undefined The total after the slash; shown only when larger than value and different once abbreviated. label label string '' The label above the value. locale locale string '' How the numbers are written (Intl locale); en-US when empty or invalid. fraction-digits fractionDigits number 1 Fraction digits of an abbreviated number. truncate truncate boolean true Abbreviate the numbers (12,345 → 12.3K); truncate=\\"false\\" writes them in full. percentage percentage boolean false Add \\"%\\" after the value; the total never shows. trending trending boolean false An up arrow before the value. force-show-total forceShowTotal boolean false Show the total even when it would be hidden (\\"Unknown\\" without one). tooltip-description tooltipDescription string '' Text of an info button after the label, shown in a tooltip. size size BigNumberSize 'default' loading loading boolean false Show the skeleton instead. Slot Description label Replaces the label text (e.g. with your own info toggletip) trending-icon Replaces the up arrow of trending icon-button An icon button after the value Part Description figure The figure label The label value The value total The \\"/total\\" info The info button of tooltip-description"],["Big number","<ui-big-number-skeleton> · React UiBigNumberSkeleton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/big-number/#ui-big-number-skeleton-react-uibignumberskeleton","Attribute Property Type Default Description size size BigNumberSize 'default' Part Description label The label bar value The value bar"],["Edit in place","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/","Edit in place shows a value as plain text that people can edit right where it is, without opening a form (Carbon for IBM Products EditInPlace). Hovered, it gets the field fill and an \\"Edit\\" button. Clicked or tabbed into, it becomes a field with \\"Cancel\\" and \\"Save\\" buttons. Use it for one value on a page that is mostly read, such as a contract's title or a reference number."],["Edit in place","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#installation","npm gives you every component from the package. shadcn copies the source into your app instead: a copy pinned to this version that you can change. The shadcn commands need the @kanok-ui registry in your components.json once, see Installation."],["Edit in place","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#use-it","label is the field's accessible name; there is no visible label, so the text around the value has to say what it is."],["Edit in place","Save and cancel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#save-and-cancel","ui-save fires when a change is saved: with Save, with Enter, or when the focus leaves with a valid change. ui-cancel fires when the value is put back: with Cancel, with Escape, or when the focus leaves without a valid change. Both carry the value in detail.value. Save and Cancel are enabled only once the value has changed (spaces at the ends don't count). The input event fires on every keystroke, with value already updated. In React + Tailwind, onChange gets each new value, and the value put back on cancel."],["Edit in place","Save to your server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#save-to-your-server","Saving is your app's: send the value to the server in ui-save. The element keeps the edited value meanwhile; Cancel and Escape go back to the value last saved. A value you set while it isn't being edited becomes the new starting point. saveReference stands for your own call to the server. React + Tailwind's value is controlled: pair it with onChange."],["Edit in place","Sizes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#sizes","size: sm 40px (the default), md 48px, lg 64px. The buttons are squares of the same height."],["Edit in place","Show the Edit button all the time","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#show-the-edit-button-all-the-time","By default the Edit button shows on hover only. edit-always-visible (editAlwaysVisible) keeps it visible, so people on touch screens, or who don't hover, can see the value is editable."],["Edit in place","Placeholder","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#placeholder","placeholder shows in the empty field, for a value that hasn't been set yet."],["Edit in place","Invalid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#invalid","invalid draws a red border and a warning icon, and blocks saving: Save stays disabled, Enter doesn't save, and leaving the field puts the value back. invalid-text (invalidText) shows under it and describes the field. Check the value on input and set invalid yourself. Delete a digit to see the error. A cancel puts the value back without an input event, so check again on ui-cancel; React + Tailwind's onChange gets the value put back."],["Edit in place","Read-only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#read-only","readonly (readOnly) shows the value with an \\"Edit off\\" button instead of \\"Edit\\". A click on the field or the button opens a short note that it can't be edited. readonly-text (readOnlyText) says why, in your words."],["Edit in place","A heading you can edit","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#a-heading-you-can-edit","inherit-typography (inheritTypography) makes the field take the size and weight of the text around it, so a page title can be edited as it is. In a real page, put it inside the heading element itself (<h2>), so the heading keeps its level."],["Edit in place","Button names and tooltip places","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#button-names-and-tooltip-places","The buttons' names come from the page language (\\"Edit\\", \\"Save\\", \\"Cancel\\", \\"Edit off\\"). Change them with edit-label, save-label, cancel-label and readonly-label (editLabel, saveLabel, cancelLabel, readOnlyLabel in React + Tailwind). tooltip-placement moves the buttons' tooltips (top by default) and note-placement the read-only note (bottom by default)."],["Edit in place","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#style-it","The parts are base (the field box), input, actions (the buttons' box) and invalid-text. The host has data-editing while it is a field. className in React + Tailwind goes on the outer box, around the field and its error."],["Edit in place","Keyboard","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#keyboard","Key While editing Tab Moves into the field, which starts editing; then to Cancel and Save once they are enabled, then out (leaving saves a valid change, or puts the value back) Enter Saves a valid change and keeps editing. With nothing to save, stops editing; the focus stays in the field Escape Puts the value back and keeps editing"],["Edit in place","Accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#accessibility","The field is a text box named by label. Write a label that names the value (\\"Contract title\\"), since nothing visible does. invalid sets aria-invalid, and invalid-text is the field's description, so it is read with it. The buttons have names and tooltips. A press on Save or Cancel keeps the focus in the field. Leaving with a valid change saves it without a click. Tell people in your page's help if that could surprise them, or use a normal text input and a Save button for values with consequences. Unstyled React parts with the same behaviour: Headless Edit in place."],["Edit in place","API","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#api","Generated from the package. In React, pass a property as a prop of the same name; events are props too (the React column)."],["Edit in place","<ui-edit-in-place> · React UiEditInPlace","/kanok-ui-docs/en/edit-in-place/#ui-edit-in-place-react-uieditinplace","Attribute Property Type Default Description value value string '' The value (as <input>.value). label label string '' The field's accessible name (Carbon labelText; there is no visible label). placeholder placeholder string '' size size EditInPlaceSize 'sm' invalid invalid boolean false invalid-text invalidText string '' readonly readonly boolean false edit-always-visible editAlwaysVisible boolean false Show \\"Edit\\" without hovering. inherit-typography inheritTypography boolean false The field takes the surrounding type (a heading made editable). tooltip-placement tooltipPlacement Placement 'top' Where the buttons' tooltips go (Carbon tooltipAlignment). note-placement notePlacement Placement 'bottom' Where the read-only note goes (Carbon toggleTipAlignment). edit-label editLabel string '' The buttons' names and the read-only note (defaults: the translation's \\"Edit\\", \\"Save\\", \\"Cancel\\", \\"Edit off\\", …). save-label saveLabel string '' cancel-label cancelLabel string '' readonly-label readonlyLabel string '' readonly-text readonlyText string '' Event React Description type none (use a ref) input onInput On every keystroke (value already updated) ui-save onUiSave detail: { value } a change was saved (Save, Enter, leaving it) ui-cancel onUiCancel detail: { value } the value was put back (Cancel, Escape, leaving it without a valid change) Part Description base The field box input The <input> actions The buttons' box invalid-text The error message"],["Headless","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/","@purpurabog/ui/headless is the behaviour of the components without their look: React parts that bring Carbon's keyboard, focus, ARIA, popup placement and form submit, and render no class at all. The markup, the labels, the messages and every style are yours. The React + Tailwind components are built on these parts, so both behave the same."],["Headless","Headless or React + Tailwind?","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#headless-or-react-tailwind","Use When React + Tailwind You want Carbon's look and to change it line by line. You start from a finished field: label, helper text, errors and sizes included. Headless You have your own design system, or a layout Carbon's components don't fit. You build the field around the parts."],["Headless","Install","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#install","Import the parts from @purpurabog/ui/headless. Each component is a namespace of parts (Dropdown.Root, Dropdown.Trigger, …). There are no tokens to load: the parts have no colours of their own."],["Headless","Your first component","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#your-first-component","Root holds the state and submits name with the form. Trigger gets the keys, roles and aria-*. Popup opens in the top layer and flips when there is no room. Every popup, headless or not, is placed by one engine (@purpurabog/ui/core): it flips to the other side when there is no room and keeps that side while open (no jump back mid-scroll), shifts along its trigger to stay on screen but never leaves it, hides while its trigger is scrolled out of view, measures against the visible part of the screen (an on-screen keyboard, a zoom) and lands on whole pixels. A list or menu also gets --ui-available-height, the room left on its side. setAnchorPositioning(true) from @purpurabog/ui/core opts in to CSS anchor positioning where the browser has it: the popup's place is then written as anchor() offsets, so the browser itself keeps it on its trigger while a box around it scrolls. It is off by default, because inside a modal's scrolling body or a submenu Chromium still puts it a few pixels from the engine's place."],["Headless","Style on data-* attributes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#style-on-data-attributes","Each part shows its state as a data-* attribute: present when true, absent when not. Style it with Tailwind's data-*: variants or with [data-open] in CSS: Attribute Means data-open The popup, menu or panel is open (on the trigger and the popup) data-highlighted The row the keyboard points at in a list data-selected, data-checked, data-mixed Selected, checked, partly selected (Select all) data-disabled, data-readonly, data-invalid Field states data-placeholder No value chosen yet data-expanded, data-closing Expanded; sliding out (for a closing animation) data-side The side a popup ended up on after flipping: top, bottom, left, right Each component's page lists the attributes of every part."],["Headless","Build your own theme switcher","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#build-your-own-theme-switcher","There is no headless switcher. useThemeMode gives you what <ui-theme-switcher> keeps, so you can draw any control: it returns the mode (light, dark or system) and a function that shows, remembers and announces a new one. Every other switcher on the page, and in other tabs, follows. What it does is described in Themes. Option Values Default value light, dark, system: the mode your app owns (e.g. from a profile) none defaultValue the mode to start on when nothing is remembered what <html data-theme> shows, else light lightTheme white, g10 white darkTheme g90, g100 g100 storageKey any key; '' = don't remember ui-theme To save the choice to a user's profile, pass the profile's mode as value: the hook shows it and remembers it. On a server the hook returns defaultValue (or light). Put themeScript() in <head> so the first paint already has the remembered theme (Themes)."],["Headless","Components","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless/#components","The pages in this section cover the form fields. The package has more parts than these pages yet: Modal, Tabs, Accordion, ContentSwitcher, Menu, Popover, Tooltip, DefinitionTooltip, TreeView, StructuredList, SidePanel, Tearsheet, Notification, Toaster, Loading, Shell, Header, SideNav, DataTable, Pagination, PaginationNav, EditInPlace, Copy, CodeSnippet, TruncatedText, Tag, Card, ProductCard and ProgressIndicator. Until they have a page, each part's props and data-* attributes are described in its types (your editor shows them on hover)."],["Headless Text input","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/","TextInput is the behaviour of the styled Text input as unstyled React parts: an <input>, a button that shows or hides a password, and a mask that formats the value as the user types. You own the markup: the label, the helper and error text, a prefix or suffix, sizes and every style. The parts set data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Text input","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Text input","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#use-it","type, value, defaultValue and disabled go on Root, not on Input."],["Headless Text input","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#anatomy",""],["Headless Text input","Label and helper text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#label-and-helper-text","The label and the message line are your own elements. Tie them to the input with htmlFor and aria-describedby."],["Headless Text input","Passwords","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#passwords","With type=\\"password\\", PasswordToggle shows or hides the text. Name the button with what a press does next (\\"Show password\\", then \\"Hide password\\"); it has no aria-pressed. Read visible from useTextInputContext(). onVisibleChange runs on each press with the new state. For a controlled toggle, pass visible and update it in onVisibleChange."],["Headless Text input","Masks","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#masks","mask on Root formats the value as the user types: 0 is a digit, a a letter, * either, and any other character is a separator added for the user. \\\\ makes a pattern character a separator. The input and the submitted form get the formatted text (1-2345-67890-12-3). Input's onChange gets the value without separators (1234567890123) as its second argument, after the field has been reformatted. An edit is reformatted in place and the caret stays where it was. Nothing is reformatted while an input method is still composing. A value or defaultValue your code sets, raw or formatted, shows formatted. A mask of digits only sets inputMode=\\"numeric\\", unless you pass your own inputMode. TextInput has no character counter. Headless Text area's Counter part is the one to borrow."],["Headless Text input","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#style-it",""],["Headless Text input","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#parts",""],["Headless Text input","TextInput.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#textinput-root","Renders no element; it holds the state for the other parts. Prop Type Default type string 'text' The input's type. password hides the text until PasswordToggle shows it. value string | number | readonly string[] — The value (controlled). defaultValue string | number | readonly string[] — The starting value (uncontrolled). mask string — The format to type into. disabled boolean false Turns off the input and the toggle. visible boolean — Whether the password shows (controlled). defaultVisible boolean false Whether the password shows at first. onVisibleChange (visible: boolean, event) => void — Each press of PasswordToggle, with the new state."],["Headless Text input","TextInput.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#textinput-input","Renders an <input>. It takes every <input> prop except type, value, defaultValue and disabled, which come from Root. Prop Type Default onChange (event, raw: string) => void — The change, after the mask reformatted it. raw is the value without separators (the value itself without a mask). Attribute When data-visible The type is password and the password shows data-disabled Root is disabled"],["Headless Text input","TextInput.PasswordToggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#textinput-passwordtoggle","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\">. It adds no props. It is off while Root is disabled or you pass disabled. Attribute When data-visible The password shows data-disabled The button is off"],["Headless Text input","TextInput.useTextInputContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#textinput-usetextinputcontext","Returns the state of the enclosing Root: visible, value (as shown, formatted), type, mask and disabled. Call it in a component inside Root."],["Headless Text input","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-input/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Input is a native <input>: Enter submits its form. PasswordToggle is a native button, so Enter and Space press it. It has type=\\"button\\", so it never submits the form. You add the <label>, the aria-describedby to the helper or error text, and aria-invalid when the value is wrong. Give the toggle a name that says what the next press does, as text or aria-label. Write the mask's format in the helper text, so people know it before they type."],["Headless Text area","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/","TextArea is the behaviour of the styled Text area as unstyled React parts: a <textarea> that can grow with its text, and a soft character or word counter. An uncontrolled area, and its counter, go back to defaultValue when its form resets. You own the markup: the label, the helper and error text, the messages for a count that is near or over the limit, and every style. The parts set data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Text area","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Text area","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#use-it","value and defaultValue go on Root, not on Input."],["Headless Text area","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#anatomy",""],["Headless Text area","Label and helper text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#label-and-helper-text","The label and the message line are your own elements. Tie them to the text area with htmlFor and aria-describedby."],["Headless Text area","Height and auto-grow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#height-and-auto-grow","rows is the native attribute: the starting height in lines. autoGrow on Input starts at rows and grows a line at a time with the text. maxRows caps it; past that, the text area scrolls. It is fitted again after each render and when its width changes. autoGrow sets the height and overflow-y inline styles. The resize handle is yours: set resize: none if you don't want it. maxRows is measured from the computed line-height, so give the text area a line-height other than normal."],["Headless Text area","Count characters or words","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#count-characters-or-words","maxCount on Root turns the counter on. It's a soft limit: typing past it isn't blocked. Past the limit, Input and Counter get data-over; in the last 10% before it, Counter gets data-near. counterMode=\\"word\\" counts words instead. Words are counted by the browser's word segmenter for lang (en by default), so Thai words count whole. Numbers don't count as words. The counter only counts: the near and over messages, and what screen readers hear, are yours. For a hard limit that stops typing, use the native maxLength."],["Headless Text area","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#style-it",""],["Headless Text area","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#parts",""],["Headless Text area","TextArea.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#textarea-root","Renders no element; it holds the text for the counter. Prop Type Default value string | number | readonly string[] — The text (controlled). defaultValue string | number | readonly string[] — The starting text (uncontrolled). maxCount number — Soft limit of the counter. Without it, there is no counter. counterMode 'character' | 'word' 'character' What maxCount counts. lang string 'en' BCP 47 language the words are counted in."],["Headless Text area","TextArea.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#textarea-input","Renders a <textarea>. It takes every <textarea> prop except value and defaultValue, which come from Root. Prop Type Default autoGrow boolean false Grows with the text from rows. maxRows number — (no cap) The most lines autoGrow shows before it scrolls. Attribute When data-over The count is past maxCount"],["Headless Text area","TextArea.Counter","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#textarea-counter","Renders a <span> with length/maxCount (12/100), or your children instead. It renders nothing without maxCount. It adds no props. Attribute When data-over The count is past maxCount data-near The count is in the last 10% before maxCount, and not past it"],["Headless Text area","TextArea.useTextAreaContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#textarea-usetextareacontext","Returns the state of the enclosing Root: length, maxCount, over and near. Use it to write your own counter text or message."],["Headless Text area","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-text-area/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Input is a native <textarea>: Enter types a new line and never submits the form. You add the <label>, the aria-describedby to the helper or error text, and aria-invalid when the text is too long. Hide the counter from screen readers (aria-hidden=\\"true\\") and announce the limit yourself, for example once in a live region when near or over turns on, not on every keystroke."],["Headless Number input","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/","NumberInput is the behaviour of the styled Number input as unstyled React parts: an <input> with − and + buttons. ↑ / ↓ step from the field. A step stays within min and max and is rounded, and each button turns off at its end of the range. With type=\\"text\\", the field shows the number in a locale's format while the value stays a plain number. An uncontrolled field goes back to defaultValue when its form resets. You own the markup: the label, the button content and names, the helper and error text, a prefix or suffix, and every style. The parts set data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Number input","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Number input","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#use-it","The value is text, so the field can be empty: \\"12\\", \\"0.5\\", or \\"\\". onValueChange gets the new value as text, not an event. It runs after typing, a step, or a blur that rounded the value. name, min, max, step, disabled and readOnly go on Root, not on Input."],["Headless Number input","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#anatomy",""],["Headless Number input","Step, minimum and maximum","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#step-minimum-and-maximum","step (1 by default) is how far − / + and ↑ / ↓ move. A step stays within min and max, and the button at that end of the range turns off. From an empty field, the first step goes to stepStartValue if you set one; otherwise to min when only a minimum is set, else to 1 or −1, as in Carbon."],["Headless Number input","Decimals","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#decimals","A step rounds to the decimals of the value or of step, whichever has more, so 0.1 + 0.2 gives 0.3. With the default type=\\"number\\", step is also the precision the browser accepts."],["Headless Number input","Currency, units and number formats","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#currency-units-and-number-formats","type=\\"text\\" with formatOptions formats the number with Intl.NumberFormat: thousands separators, currency, percent, units. The text is free while the user types and is formatted on blur; text that isn't a number stays, marked invalid, for the user to correct. The value stays a plain number: ฿1,234.50 is 1234.5, and a percent style gives the fraction (0.5 for 50%). Without locale, type=\\"text\\" follows the page language (<html lang>, else the browser's). An invalid locale or formatOptions falls back to plain English and logs a console warning. A prefix or suffix (฿, kg) is your own markup next to the input."],["Headless Number input","Empty fields and errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#empty-fields-and-errors","There are no rules of their own for an empty field: check the value yourself. The browser's checks on the input (required, and min, max and step with type=\\"number\\") still run on submit, but its error bubble never shows. Instead the field gets data-touched, and the first invalid field of the form gets focus, so you can show your own message."],["Headless Number input","Steppers and the mouse wheel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#steppers-and-the-mouse-wheel","Leave out Decrement and Increment for a field without buttons; ↑ / ↓ still step. disableWheel on Input stops the mouse wheel from changing a focused field."],["Headless Number input","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#style-it",""],["Headless Number input","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#parts",""],["Headless Number input","NumberInput.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#numberinput-root","Renders no element; it holds the value and the limits. Prop Type Default value string | number — The value as plain number text ('' is empty). Controlled. defaultValue string | number — The starting value (uncontrolled). onValueChange (value: string) => void — The new value after typing, a step, or a blur that rounded it. min number — Lowest value a step reaches. max number — Highest value a step reaches. step number 1 Step of the buttons and ↑ / ↓; with type=\\"number\\" also the precision. stepStartValue number 0 Where a step from an empty field starts. 0 means ±1, or min when only a minimum is set. type 'number' | 'text' 'number' text formats the number for locale. locale string <html lang>, else the browser's BCP 47 locale of type=\\"text\\". formatOptions Intl.NumberFormatOptions — Format of type=\\"text\\". disabled boolean false Turns off the field and the buttons. readOnly boolean false Keeps the value; the buttons and ↑ / ↓ do nothing. name string — Submitted name: on Input with type=\\"number\\", on HiddenInput with type=\\"text\\"."],["Headless Number input","NumberInput.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#numberinput-input","Renders an <input> with inputMode=\\"decimal\\": a native number box with type=\\"number\\", a text box with type=\\"text\\". It takes every <input> prop except type, value, defaultValue, min, max, step and name, which come from Root. Your onBlur runs after the value settles. ↑ / ↓ don't step when your onKeyDown calls preventDefault(). Prop Type Default disableWheel boolean false Ignore the mouse wheel while focused. Attribute When data-disabled Root is disabled data-readonly Root is read-only data-touched The field was left or stepped, or a submit found it invalid"],["Headless Number input","NumberInput.Decrement and NumberInput.Increment","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#numberinput-decrement-and-numberinput-increment","Each renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that steps once down or up. They add no props. A button is off at its end of the range, while the field is disabled or read-only, and when you pass disabled. They are out of the Tab order unless you pass tabIndex. Attribute When data-disabled The button is off"],["Headless Number input","NumberInput.HiddenInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#numberinput-hiddeninput","Renders an <input type=\\"hidden\\"> with Root's name and the plain value, only with type=\\"text\\" and a name; otherwise nothing. It is disabled (not submitted) while Root is disabled."],["Headless Number input","NumberInput.useNumberInputContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#numberinput-usenumberinputcontext","Returns the state of the enclosing Root, such as value, number (NaN while empty), isEmpty, badText (type=\\"text\\" text that isn't a number), touched, atMin, atMax and stepBy(1 | -1)."],["Headless Number input","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-number-input/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key What it does ↑ / ↓ One step up or down, within min / max Enter Submits the form the field sits in, as a native input does The − / + buttons are out of the Tab order, as in Carbon: the arrow keys do the same from the field. They are real buttons with disabled at the end of the range. You add the <label>, names for the buttons (aria-label), the aria-describedby to the helper or error text, and aria-invalid with your own error message."],["Headless Search","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/","Search is the behaviour of the styled Search as unstyled React parts: a role=\\"search\\" landmark named by its label, an <input type=\\"search\\">, a clear button, and the magnifier button of an expandable search. The parts handle Esc, where focus goes after a clear, open or close, and when the clear button is in the Tab order. An uncontrolled field goes back to defaultValue when its form resets. You own the markup: the icons, how the label is hidden, the button names and every style. The parts set data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Search","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Search","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#use-it","value, defaultValue, disabled and readOnly go on Root, not on Input. Clearing empties the field with a real input event, so your onChange sees it; onClear runs after. Always render Label, even when you hide it: it names the landmark and the input."],["Headless Search","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#anatomy",""],["Headless Search","Clear the text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#clear-the-text","Clear empties the field and keeps focus in it. Esc in a filled field does the same. On an empty field Esc does nothing, so a dialog around the search can still close on Esc. While there is nothing to clear (the field is empty or read-only), Clear is out of the Tab order and has data-hidden; hide it with your CSS."],["Headless Search","Expandable search","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#expandable-search","expandable (Carbon's ExpandableSearch) collapses the search to its Trigger until someone clicks it or presses Enter or Space; then it opens and focus moves to the field. When focus leaves an empty open search for anywhere outside its Landmark, it collapses. Esc on an empty open search collapses it and focuses the Trigger. expanded controls the state; defaultExpanded sets where it starts. While collapsed, Landmark and Input have data-collapsed and the input is out of the Tab order. Hiding or narrowing the input is your CSS."],["Headless Search","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#style-it",""],["Headless Search","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#parts",""],["Headless Search","Search.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-root","Renders no element; it holds the text and the open state. Prop Type Default inputId string generated The input's id. The label's id is \${inputId}-label. value string | number | readonly string[] — The text (controlled; follow the input's onChange). defaultValue string | number | readonly string[] — The starting text (uncontrolled). disabled boolean false Turns off the input and the buttons. readOnly boolean false Keeps the text: nothing to clear. onClear () => void — After Clear or Esc emptied the field. expandable boolean false Collapsed to its Trigger until opened. expanded boolean — Whether an expandable search is open (controlled). defaultExpanded boolean false Whether it starts open. onExpandedChange (expanded: boolean) => void — Each open or close."],["Headless Search","Search.Landmark","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-landmark","Renders a <div role=\\"search\\"> named by Label (aria-labelledby). It adds no props. Attribute When data-empty The field has no text data-collapsed An expandable search is collapsed data-disabled Root is disabled data-readonly Root is read-only"],["Headless Search","Search.Label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-label","Renders a <label> for the input, with the id the landmark points to. You can't set its htmlFor or id."],["Headless Search","Search.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-input","Renders an <input type=\\"search\\" autoComplete=\\"off\\">. It takes every <input> prop except type, id, value, defaultValue, disabled and readOnly, which come from Root. It has the same data-* attributes as Landmark."],["Headless Search","Search.Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-clear","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\">. It adds no props, and takes no disabled (it follows Root). Its mousedown is cancelled, so focus stays in the field. Attribute When data-hidden Nothing to clear: the field is empty or read-only"],["Headless Search","Search.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-trigger","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded and aria-controls pointing at the input. It adds no props, and takes no disabled (it follows Root). It is a Tab stop only while the search is collapsed. Attribute When data-expanded The search is open (always, unless expandable)"],["Headless Search","Search.useSearchContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#search-usesearchcontext","Returns the state of the enclosing Root, such as empty, clearable, open, expandable, inputId and labelId."],["Headless Search","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-search/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key What it does Esc Clears the text and keeps focus in the field; on an empty open expandable search, collapses it and focuses the Trigger Enter Submits the form the search sits in, as a native input does Enter or Space on the Trigger Opens an expandable search; it doesn't submit the form Tab Moves to Clear only while there is text to clear Landmark is a role=\\"search\\" landmark named by Label, so screen reader users can jump to it. Carbon hides the label on screen. Hide it with a visually-hidden class, not display: none. You add names for Clear and Trigger (aria-label) and aria-hidden=\\"true\\" on their icons."],["Headless Select","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/","Select is the behaviour of the styled Select as one unstyled React part: a native <select> with your <option> and <optgroup> children, so the browser gives the list, the keyboard and the form. On top, it adds a placeholder option, a read-only mode, aria-invalid, and data-* attributes to style on. You own the markup: the label, the helper and error text, the arrow icon and every style. There are no sizes and no inline look: the height and layout are your CSS."],["Headless Select","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Select","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#use-it",""],["Headless Select","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#anatomy",""],["Headless Select","Label and helper text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#label-and-helper-text","The label and the message line are your own elements. Tie them to the select with htmlFor and aria-describedby."],["Headless Select","Placeholder and starting value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#placeholder-and-starting-value","placeholder adds a first, empty option (value=\\"\\"). It is the uncontrolled choice until the user picks another, and Root has data-placeholder while it shows. With required, the user has to pick something else before the form submits. Use value with onChange for a controlled select, or defaultValue for an uncontrolled one. onChange is React's own."],["Headless Select","Groups and disabled options","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#groups-and-disabled-options","The children are plain <option> and <optgroup> elements, so disabled on either works as in HTML."],["Headless Select","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps the value and sets aria-readonly: a press doesn't open the list, and no key changes or opens it, typed letters included. Tab and the ⌘ / Ctrl shortcuts still work. It still takes focus and submits. disabled is the native attribute: the select isn't submitted."],["Headless Select","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#style-it",""],["Headless Select","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#parts",""],["Headless Select","Select.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#select-root","Renders a <select>, with a first empty <option> when you set placeholder, then your children. It takes every <select> prop. Prop Type Default placeholder string — The text of a first, empty option (value=\\"\\"), chosen until the user picks another. readOnly boolean false Keeps the value: a press and the changing keys do nothing (aria-readonly). invalid boolean — Sets aria-invalid. Left out, there's no aria-invalid. Attribute When data-placeholder The empty placeholder option is the choice data-readonly readOnly is set data-disabled disabled is set data-invalid invalid is set"],["Headless Select","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-select/#keyboard-and-accessibility","The control is a native <select>: the browser's own keys open and change it, and phones show the system picker. You add the <label> (or aria-label), the aria-describedby to the helper or error text, and the error text itself. Give your arrow icon aria-hidden=\\"true\\" and pointer-events: none, so a click on it still reaches the select. Options can't hold markup or a second line. If you need that, use a Dropdown."],["Headless Dropdown","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/","The Dropdown parts give you the behaviour of the styled Dropdown with no styles: a button with role=\\"combobox\\" that opens a listbox in the top layer, the keyboard (arrows, Home / End, Page Up / Page Down, typing to jump), the highlight through aria-activedescendant, closing on a click outside, and a hidden input that submits the value. You own the markup, the label text, any helper or error message, the \\"Loading…\\" row and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Dropdown","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Dropdown","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#use-it","items on Root is the data: the keys move through it and typing searches its labels. The Options inside Popup are what people see and click. Render one Option for each option in items, with the same value."],["Headless Dropdown","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#anatomy",""],["Headless Dropdown","A second line","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#a-second-line","Put the second line inside the Option. Typing to jump only searches label, never description."],["Headless Dropdown","Groups and disabled options","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#groups-and-disabled-options","items takes options { value, label, description?, disabled? } and groups { label, options, disabled? }. A disabled option is shown but skipped by the keys and can't be picked; a disabled group disables its options. isGroup tells a group from an option, and flattenOptions returns every option in order."],["Headless Dropdown","Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#value","Hold the value yourself with value and onValueChange, or give a starting defaultValue and let Root keep it. onValueChange fires only when the user picks a different option. With name, a hidden input submits the value with the form. A form reset puts an uncontrolled value back to defaultValue; a controlled value is yours to set back."],["Headless Dropdown","Open above","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#open-above","The list opens below the trigger and is as wide as it. side=\\"top\\" on Popup prefers above. Either way it flips when there is no room, and data-side on the popup says where it went. There are no sizes: the height of the trigger and the rows is your CSS."],["Headless Dropdown","Load the options when the list opens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#load-the-options-when-the-list-opens","onOpenChange fires after the list opens or closes. While loading is true, the keys pick nothing and the popup has aria-busy. When loading ends with the list open, the highlight goes to the chosen option, else the first. Root draws no \\"Loading…\\" row and announces nothing: render the row and a status text yourself."],["Headless Dropdown","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly shows the value, but the list doesn't open and the keys do nothing. The trigger gets aria-readonly. disabled disables the trigger. A disabled field renders no hidden input, so it isn't submitted (as a disabled native control). required and invalid only set aria-required and aria-invalid (and data-invalid). There is no built-in message: check the value and show the error yourself (Forms and validation)."],["Headless Dropdown","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#style-it",""],["Headless Dropdown","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#parts",""],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, then the hidden input when name is set and disabled isn't. Prop Type Default items ListItem[] Options and groups { label, options }: what the keys move through and typing searches value string The chosen value (controlled) defaultValue string '' The starting value (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string) => void After the user picks another option onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After the list opens or closes disabled boolean false Disables the trigger readOnly boolean false The list doesn't open required boolean false aria-required on the trigger invalid boolean false aria-invalid and data-invalid on the trigger loading boolean false The keys pick nothing; the popup is aria-busy name string Submits the value with the form (a hidden input), unless disabled id string generated Base of the ids: <id>-label, <id>-value, <id>-list, <id>-opt-<n> Dropdown.useDropdownContext() returns the Root's state (open, value, selected, active, loading …) to any component inside it, for example to turn a chevron."],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-label","A <span> with the id <id>-label. It names the trigger (with Value) and the popup. Attribute When data-disabled Root is disabled"],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\" role=\\"combobox\\">. Its aria-labelledby is <id>-label <id>-value unless you pass your own. It takes every button prop except type, role and disabled. Attribute When data-open The list is open data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only data-invalid invalid is set data-placeholder Nothing is chosen"],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-value","A <span> with the id <id>-value: the chosen option's label, else placeholder. children replaces both. Prop Type Default placeholder ReactNode Shown while nothing is chosen Attribute When data-placeholder Nothing is chosen"],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-popup","A <ul role=\\"listbox\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer, as wide as the trigger. Its children render only while the list is open. A press inside it keeps focus on the trigger; a press outside closes it. Its aria-labelledby is <id>-label unless you pass your own. Prop Type Default side 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Where the list opens; it flips when there is no room Attribute When data-open The list is open data-side bottom or top: where the list went"],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Option","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-option","An <li role=\\"option\\"> with the id <id>-opt-<n>. A click on an enabled option picks it and closes the list. Prop Type Default value string The value of an option in items (required) Attribute When data-highlighted The keyboard highlight is on it data-selected It is the chosen option data-disabled The option (or its group) is disabled"],["Headless Dropdown","Dropdown.Group, GroupLabel, GroupOptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#dropdown-group-grouplabel-groupoptions","Group is a <div role=\\"group\\"> inside a presentational <li>, named by its GroupLabel (a <div>). GroupOptions is a presentational <ul> that holds the group's Options. They add no props and no data attributes."],["Headless Dropdown","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-dropdown/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key List closed List open ↓, Enter, Space Open on the chosen option (else the first) ↓ moves down; Enter and Space pick the highlighted option and close ↑ Does nothing Moves up (no wrap) Home / End Open on the first / last option First / last option Page Up / Page Down Move by 10 Letters Open on the next option that starts with them Jump to the next option that starts with them Alt+↑ Picks the highlighted option and closes Esc Closes without a change Tab Moves on Closes without a change and moves on The parts set role=\\"combobox\\", aria-haspopup, aria-expanded, aria-controls, aria-activedescendant, aria-readonly, aria-required and aria-invalid on the trigger, and role=\\"listbox\\", role=\\"option\\", aria-selected and aria-disabled on the list. Focus stays on the trigger the whole time. You add: The label text in Label, or your own aria-labelledby on the trigger and the popup. Helper and error text, linked with aria-describedby on the trigger. A role=\\"status\\" text for \\"Loading…\\", as in the example above."],["Headless Combobox","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/","The Combobox parts give you the behaviour of the styled Combobox with no styles: a text box with role=\\"combobox\\", a listbox in the top layer that typing narrows or only highlights, the keyboard, the rule for what leaving the field keeps, a clear button and a chevron that are not Tab stops, and a hidden input that submits the value. You own the markup, the <label>, any helper or error message, the \\"Searching…\\" and \\"No matching items\\" text, and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Combobox","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Combobox","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#use-it","items on Root is every option. Popup calls its children function with the items the typed text keeps (groups kept), so you render only those."],["Headless Combobox","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#anatomy",""],["Headless Combobox","How typing narrows the list","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#how-typing-narrows-the-list","Typing opens the list and highlights the first enabled option whose label contains the text. filter decides whether the other options stay: filter The list while typing none (default) Every option stays; only the highlight moves contains Only options whose label contains the text starts-with Only options whose label starts with the text While the text still equals the chosen option's label, the list shows every option."],["Headless Combobox","Free text or a listed option","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#free-text-or-a-listed-option","When the user leaves the field, text that exactly matches an enabled option's label picks that option. Other text snaps back to the option chosen before. With allowCustomValue, the typed text becomes the value instead."],["Headless Combobox","Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#value","Hold the value yourself with value and onValueChange, or give a starting defaultValue. onValueChange fires when the value changes: a pick, a committed text, a clear. When value changes from outside, the text box shows the new choice's label."],["Headless Combobox","Search on a server","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#search-on-a-server","onInputValueChange gets the text each time the user types. Fetch the matches, replace items, and set loading while the request runs: the popup then has aria-busy. Keep filter=\\"none\\" (the default), as the server has already filtered. The parts draw no \\"Searching…\\" or \\"No matching items\\" text. Combobox.useComboboxContext() gives you open, loading and listed (the options the text keeps) to render them: Here search() stands in for the server and answers after a short wait; in your app it fetches the matches, as on Combobox."],["Headless Combobox","Groups and descriptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#groups-and-descriptions","Groups are { label, options } in items, and options take description and disabled. Typing only searches the labels. isGroup tells a group from an option in the Popup function:"],["Headless Combobox","Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#clear","Combobox.Clear empties the text and the value and keeps focus in the input. Leave it out to have none. It is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only; the styled Combobox goes further and shows it only while the field can change and holds text: Esc on a closed list also clears."],["Headless Combobox","Open above, read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#open-above-read-only-and-disabled","side=\\"top\\" on Popup prefers opening above; it flips when there is no room. The list lines up with Anchor and is as wide as it (the Input when there is no Anchor). readOnly makes the input read-only: the keys and clicks don't open the list, and Toggle and Clear are disabled. disabled disables the input, Toggle and Clear. A disabled field renders no hidden input, so it isn't submitted (as a disabled native control). A form reset puts an uncontrolled value and its text back. required and invalid only set aria-required and aria-invalid (and data-invalid): check the value and show the error yourself (Forms and validation). There are no sizes; the height is your CSS."],["Headless Combobox","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#style-it",""],["Headless Combobox","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#parts",""],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, then the hidden input when name is set and disabled isn't. Prop Type Default items ListItem[] Options and groups { label, options } value string The chosen value (controlled) defaultValue string '' The starting value (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string) => void After the value changes: a pick, a committed text, a clear onInputValueChange (text: string) => void Each time the user types filter 'none' | 'contains' | 'starts-with' 'none' How typed text narrows the list allowCustomValue boolean false Keep text that matches no option as the value loading boolean false The popup is aria-busy onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After the list opens or closes disabled boolean false Disables the input, Toggle and Clear readOnly boolean false The text and the value can't change required boolean false aria-required on the input invalid boolean false aria-invalid and data-invalid on the input name string Submits the value with the form (a hidden input), unless disabled id string generated The input's id, and the base of the other ids: <id>-list, <id>-opt-<n>. The popup's aria-labelledby points at <id>-label, an id only your own <label> can carry (see Combobox.Popup) Combobox.useComboboxContext() returns the Root's state (text, value, open, listed, loading, interactive …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-input","An <input type=\\"text\\" role=\\"combobox\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\">. Its id is Root's id unless you pass one. It takes every input prop except type, role, value, defaultValue, disabled and readOnly, which come from Root. Attribute When data-open The list is open data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only data-invalid invalid is set"],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Anchor","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-anchor","A <div> around the input and its buttons. The popup lines up with it and matches its width. No props, no data attributes."],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-clear","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1} (pass your own to change it). A click empties the text and the value, closes the list and keeps focus in the input. It is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-toggle","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}, aria-expanded and aria-controls. A click opens or closes the list; focus stays in the input. It is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Give it an aria-label. Attribute When data-open The list is open"],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-popup","A <ul role=\\"listbox\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer. Its rows render only while the list is open. Its aria-labelledby is <id>-label unless you pass your own; there is no label part, so give it an aria-label or give your <label> that id. Prop Type Default children ReactNode | ((items: ListItem[]) => ReactNode) The rows, or a function of the items the typed text keeps side 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Where the list opens; it flips when there is no room Attribute When data-open The list is open data-side bottom or top: where the list went"],["Headless Combobox","Combobox.Option, Group, GroupLabel, GroupOptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#combobox-option-group-grouplabel-groupoptions","The same parts as in Headless Dropdown: Option is an <li role=\\"option\\"> with a required value and data-highlighted, data-selected and data-disabled. A click on an enabled option picks it, puts its label in the text box and closes the list."],["Headless Combobox","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-combobox/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Typing Opens the list and highlights the first option containing the text ↓ / ↑ Opens the list on the chosen option (else the first / last); then moves the highlight (no wrap) Alt+↓ Opens the list without a highlight Alt+↑ Picks the highlighted option and closes Enter Picks the highlighted option. With no highlight, picks the first option containing the text (or keeps the text with allowCustomValue) Esc Closes the list; on a closed list, clears the text and the value Tab Moves on without picking the highlight; the text is committed or snaps back The parts set role=\\"combobox\\", aria-autocomplete=\\"list\\", aria-expanded, aria-controls, aria-activedescendant, aria-required and aria-invalid on the input, and the listbox and option roles on the list. Focus stays in the input. You add: A <label htmlFor> for the input, and a name for the popup (aria-label, or a <label> with the id <id>-label). aria-label on Clear and Toggle. Helper and error text, linked with aria-describedby on the input. A role=\\"status\\" text for \\"Searching…\\" and \\"No matching items\\", as in the example above."],["Headless Multi-select","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/","The MultiSelect parts give you the behaviour of the styled Multi-select with no styles: a field that opens a listbox in the top layer and stays open while people toggle options, chosen options moving to the top, an optional \\"Select all\\" row, a filterable text box, the keyboard, and one hidden input per chosen value. You own the markup, the label text, the count, the check boxes in the rows, any helper or error message, the \\"Loading…\\" text and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Multi-select","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Multi-select","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#use-it","items on Root is every option. Popup calls its children function with the rows to show, in order: filtered by the typed text, chosen ones first, groups kept."],["Headless Multi-select","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#anatomy",""],["Headless Multi-select","The count, clear and descriptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#the-count-clear-and-descriptions","Value shows its children, else the placeholder: it doesn't count. Read count from MultiSelect.useMultiSelectContext() to show how many are chosen. Clear empties the choice and keeps focus in the field; it is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. The example below also leaves it out then, as the styled MultiSelect does."],["Headless Multi-select","Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#value","value is an array. Hold it yourself with value and onValueChange, or give a starting defaultValue. With name, Root renders one hidden input per chosen value, so read them with FormData.getAll()."],["Headless Multi-select","Select all","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#select-all","selectAll offers a \\"Select all\\" row. Put SelectAll first in the popup: it renders only while offered and something can be chosen. It chooses every enabled option shown, or none when all are chosen. While only some are, it has data-mixed and aria-checked=\\"mixed\\"."],["Headless Multi-select","Where chosen options go","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#where-chosen-options-go","selectionFeedback decides when chosen rows move to the top of the rows Popup hands you: selectionFeedback Chosen rows top-after-reopen (default) Move to the top the next time the list opens top Move to the top at once fixed Stay where they are With groups in items, nothing moves."],["Headless Multi-select","Filterable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#filterable","filterable makes the field a text box: use Input instead of Trigger and Value, and add ClearText and Toggle if you want them. filter is contains (the default) or starts-with. Choosing keeps the text and the list open; focus leaving Anchor or a press outside closes the list and empties the text. \\"Select all\\" then acts on the rows shown. For a server search, set filter=\\"none\\", get the typed text from onInputValueChange, replace items and set loading. Keep the chosen options in items so their rows stay. onText sets loading, searches (here a stand-in that answers after a short wait), and puts the result in rows together with the chosen options, as on Multi-select."],["Headless Multi-select","Load the options when the list opens","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#load-the-options-when-the-list-opens","onOpenChange fires after the list opens or closes. While loading is true, Popup hands you no rows, \\"Select all\\" is hidden, the keys pick nothing and the popup has aria-busy. Render a \\"Loading…\\" row and a role=\\"status\\" text yourself, as on Headless Dropdown."],["Headless Multi-select","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly shows the choice, but the list doesn't open and the keys do nothing. The field gets aria-readonly (or the input readOnly, filterable), and Toggle and Clear are disabled. disabled disables the field, Toggle and Clear. A disabled field renders no hidden inputs, so it isn't submitted (as a disabled native control). A form reset puts an uncontrolled choice back. required and invalid only set aria-required and aria-invalid (and data-invalid): check the value and show the error yourself (Forms and validation). There are no sizes; the height is your CSS."],["Headless Multi-select","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#style-it",""],["Headless Multi-select","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#parts",""],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, then one hidden input per chosen value when name is set and disabled isn't. Prop Type Default items ListItem[] Options and groups { label, options } value string[] The chosen values (controlled) defaultValue string[] [] The starting values (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string[]) => void After the choice changes onInputValueChange (text: string) => void Filterable: each change of the typed text selectionFeedback 'top-after-reopen' | 'top' | 'fixed' 'top-after-reopen' When chosen options move to the top selectAll boolean false Offer the SelectAll row filterable boolean false The field is a text box (Input) that narrows the list filter 'contains' | 'starts-with' | 'none' 'contains' How typed text narrows the list (filterable) loading boolean false No rows, the keys pick nothing, the popup is aria-busy onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After the list opens or closes disabled boolean false Disables the field, Toggle and Clear readOnly boolean false The choice can't change required boolean false aria-required on the field invalid boolean false aria-invalid and data-invalid on the field name string Submits each chosen value with the form (hidden inputs), unless disabled id string generated The input's id (filterable), and the base of the ids: <id>-label, <id>-value, <id>-list, <id>-opt-<n>, <id>-opt-all MultiSelect.useMultiSelectContext() returns the Root's state (value, count, open, text, rows, allState, interactive …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-label","A <span> with the id <id>-label. It names the field and the popup. Attribute When data-disabled Root is disabled"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Anchor","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-anchor","A <div> around the field, the count and the buttons. The popup lines up with it and matches its width. With filterable, focus leaving it closes the list and empties the text. No props, no data attributes."],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\" role=\\"combobox\\">, for a field that isn't filterable. Its aria-labelledby is <id>-label <id>-value unless you pass your own. It takes every button prop except type, role and disabled. Attribute When data-open The list is open data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only data-invalid invalid is set data-placeholder Nothing is chosen"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-value","A <span> with the id <id>-value: its children, else placeholder. Prop Type Default placeholder ReactNode Shown when there are no children Attribute When data-placeholder Nothing is chosen"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-input","Filterable: an <input type=\\"text\\" role=\\"combobox\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\"> that narrows the list. Its id is Root's id and its aria-labelledby is <id>-label, unless you pass your own. It takes every input prop except type, role, value, defaultValue, disabled and readOnly. It has the same data attributes as Trigger."],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-clear","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}. A click empties the choice and puts focus in the field. It is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.ClearText","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-cleartext","Filterable: a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}. A click empties the typed text and puts focus in the input. Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-toggle","Filterable: a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}, aria-expanded and aria-controls. A click opens or closes the list; focus stays in the input. It is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Give it an aria-label. Attribute When data-open The list is open"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-popup","A <ul role=\\"listbox\\" aria-multiselectable=\\"true\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer. Its rows render only while the list is open. A press outside closes it and empties the text. Prop Type Default children ReactNode | ((items: ListItem[]) => ReactNode) The rows, or a function of the rows to show side 'bottom' | 'top' 'bottom' Where the list opens; it flips when there is no room Attribute When data-open The list is open data-side bottom or top: where the list went"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.SelectAll","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-selectall","An <li role=\\"option\\"> with the id <id>-opt-all, rendered only while selectAll is set, nothing is loading and an enabled option is shown. A click chooses every enabled option shown, or none when all are chosen. Attribute When data-highlighted The keyboard highlight is on it data-selected Every shown option is chosen data-mixed Some are chosen"],["Headless Multi-select","MultiSelect.Option, Group, GroupLabel, GroupOptions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#multiselect-option-group-grouplabel-groupoptions","The same parts as in Headless Dropdown: Option is an <li role=\\"option\\"> with a required value and data-highlighted, data-selected and data-disabled. A click on an enabled option toggles it and keeps the list open."],["Headless Multi-select","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-multi-select/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key List closed List open ↓, Enter, Space Open the list Enter and Space toggle the highlighted row; the list stays open ↓ / ↑, Page Down / Page Up, Home / End ↑ does nothing; Home / End open on the first / last row Move the highlight Letters Open on the next option that starts with them Jump to the next option that starts with them Delete, Backspace, Esc Clear every choice Esc closes Tab Moves on Closes and moves on With filterable, letters, Space, Home, End, Delete and Backspace edit the text. ↓ or Enter open the list, Enter toggles the highlighted row (or closes with nothing highlighted), and Esc on a closed list clears the choices and the text. The parts set role=\\"combobox\\", aria-haspopup, aria-expanded, aria-controls, aria-activedescendant, aria-readonly, aria-required and aria-invalid on the field, and aria-multiselectable, aria-selected and aria-checked=\\"mixed\\" on the list. Focus stays on the field. You add: The label text in Label. aria-label on Clear, ClearText and Toggle. The count, if you show one, and a check box drawn in each row (hidden from screen readers; aria-selected already says it). Helper and error text, linked with aria-describedby on the field. A role=\\"status\\" text for \\"Loading…\\", \\"Searching…\\" and \\"No matching items\\"."],["Headless Checkbox","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/","Checkbox.Root is the native <input type=\\"checkbox\\"> with no styles, so form submission, required, Space, labels and screen readers come from the browser. On top of that it adds indeterminate as a prop, a read-only state, onCheckedChange, and data-* attributes for you to style on. You own the <label>, the box you draw, any group around the boxes, any helper or error message, and every style. For the styled version, see Checkbox."],["Headless Checkbox","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Checkbox","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#use-it","Hide the input over a box you draw beside it, and wrap both in a <label> so the whole row is clickable:"],["Headless Checkbox","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#anatomy",""],["Headless Checkbox","Checked state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#checked-state","Hold the state yourself with checked and onCheckedChange (or onChange), or give a starting defaultChecked. A checked box submits value (on by default) under name; an unchecked box submits nothing. A form reset puts an uncontrolled box back to defaultChecked, and data-checked follows."],["Headless Checkbox","A group of checkboxes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#a-group-of-checkboxes","There is no group part. Use a <fieldset> and <legend>, lay the boxes out yourself, and check \\"at least one\\" in your own validation. Each box submits its own name and value, so read them with FormData.getAll()."],["Headless Checkbox","Indeterminate","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#indeterminate","indeterminate shows the mixed state of a parent box whose children are partly checked. It is set as the DOM property, so screen readers hear \\"mixed\\". Keep the parent in step with its children in your code:"],["Headless Checkbox","No visible label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#no-visible-label","When the context already names the box, such as a checkbox in a table row, give it an aria-label instead of label text:"],["Headless Checkbox","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps the state and still submits it, but a click or Space changes nothing. The input gets aria-readonly. The click is blocked before your onClick runs, so your handler sees event.defaultPrevented. disabled is the native attribute: the box can't be used and isn't submitted. invalid sets aria-invalid and data-invalid. The error text is yours (Forms and validation)."],["Headless Checkbox","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#style-it",""],["Headless Checkbox","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#parts",""],["Headless Checkbox","Checkbox.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#checkbox-root","An <input type=\\"checkbox\\">. It takes every input prop except type. Prop Type Default indeterminate boolean false The mixed state, set as the DOM property readOnly boolean false Keeps the state: a click or Space changes nothing (aria-readonly) invalid boolean aria-invalid and data-invalid onCheckedChange (checked: boolean, event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => void After the user checks or unchecks it Attribute When data-checked Checked data-indeterminate indeterminate is set data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only data-invalid invalid is set"],["Headless Checkbox","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-checkbox/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Space Checks or unchecks the focused box Tab Moves to the next box: each checkbox is its own Tab stop The browser gives the role, the checked and mixed state, focus and Space. The part adds aria-readonly and aria-invalid. You add: A label: wrap the input in a <label>, or give it aria-label. A <fieldset> and <legend> around a group. Helper and error text, linked with aria-describedby. A visible focus style on the box you draw (the input itself is hidden)."],["Headless Radio button","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/","RadioGroup.Root is a role=\\"radiogroup\\" around native <input type=\\"radio\\"> items that share one name, so the browser gives the single Tab stop, the arrow keys and form submission. The parts add the group's value, a read-only state, onValueChange, and data-* attributes for you to style on. You own each item's <label>, the circle you draw, the group's label, any helper or error message, the layout and every style. For the styled version, see Radio button."],["Headless Radio button","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Radio button","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#use-it","Hide each input over a circle you draw beside it, and wrap both in a <label>: Give the group a name when it is in a form: without one, Root makes up a name so the items still form one group."],["Headless Radio button","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#anatomy",""],["Headless Radio button","Value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#value","Hold the value yourself with value and onValueChange, or give a starting defaultValue. With neither, nothing is checked; '' also checks none. The form submits the checked item's value under name."],["Headless Radio button","Orientation and label position","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#orientation-and-label-position","orientation only sets data-orientation: the browser's arrow keys go both ways, and the layout is your CSS. For the text before the circle, put it before the Item in its <label>."],["Headless Radio button","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#read-only-and-disabled","disabled on an Item disables that one; on Root, it disables every item, so none is submitted. readOnly keeps the value and still submits it. Clicks and arrow keys change nothing, but the arrows still move focus so people can read the options (as Carbon React). The group gets aria-readonly. required only sets aria-required on the group, and invalid sets aria-invalid on it and data-invalid on it and its items. Check the value and show the error yourself (Forms and validation). Give the message an id and put it in the group's aria-describedby: every item gets the same aria-describedby, so a screen reader hears it on the item it lands on."],["Headless Radio button","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#style-it",""],["Headless Radio button","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#parts",""],["Headless Radio button","RadioGroup.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#radiogroup-root","A <div role=\\"radiogroup\\">. It takes every div prop except defaultValue and role. Prop Type Default name string generated The submitted name, shared by every item value string The checked item's value (controlled); '' checks none defaultValue string '' The starting value (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string, event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => void After the user checks another item orientation 'vertical' | 'horizontal' 'vertical' Only sets data-orientation disabled boolean false Disables every item (aria-disabled on the group) readOnly boolean false Keeps the value: clicks and arrow keys change nothing (aria-readonly) required boolean aria-required on the group invalid boolean aria-invalid on the group; data-invalid on it and its items Attribute When data-orientation Always: vertical or horizontal data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only data-invalid invalid is set RadioGroup.useRadioGroupContext() returns the group's state (name, value, disabled, readOnly, invalid, select …), for building other kinds of item."],["Headless Radio button","RadioGroup.Item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#radiogroup-item","An <input type=\\"radio\\">, checked when its value is the group's. It takes every input prop except type, name, checked and defaultChecked. Its aria-describedby is the group's unless you pass your own. Prop Type Default value string This item's value (required) disabled boolean This item alone; a disabled group disables every item Attribute When data-checked Checked data-disabled This item or the group is disabled data-readonly The group is read-only data-invalid The group is invalid"],["Headless Radio button","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-radio/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Enters the group on the checked item (else the first), and leaves it on the next Tab ↓ / → Moves to the next item and checks it; wraps from the last to the first ↑ / ← Moves to the previous item and checks it; wraps from the first to the last Space Checks the focused item The browser gives the radio role, the checked state, the single Tab stop and the arrow keys; disabled items are skipped. The parts add role=\\"radiogroup\\", aria-required, aria-readonly, aria-disabled and aria-invalid on the group. You add: A name for the group: aria-label, or aria-labelledby pointing at your visible label. A <label> for each item. Helper and error text, linked with aria-describedby on Root. A visible focus style on the circle you draw (the input itself is hidden)."],["Headless Toggle","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/","The headless part is named Switch, as in Base UI, where \\"Toggle\\" means a pressed button. Switch.Root is a <button role=\\"switch\\"> with aria-checked, so Space and Enter flip it. A click focuses it in every browser, Safari included. It adds a read-only state, onCheckedChange, form submission through a hidden input, and data-* attributes for you to style on. You own the track and knob styles, the label, the \\"On\\" / \\"Off\\" text and every style. For the styled version, see Toggle."],["Headless Toggle","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Toggle","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#use-it",""],["Headless Toggle","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#anatomy",""],["Headless Toggle","On and off","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#on-and-off","Hold the state yourself with checked and onCheckedChange, or give a starting defaultChecked. onCheckedChange fires after the user flips it."],["Headless Toggle","Label and state text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#label-and-state-text","Switch draws no text. Name it with aria-label or aria-labelledby, and render the state text yourself. Screen readers hear \\"on\\" or \\"off\\" from the role, so hide the state text from them. A <label htmlFor> pointing at the switch's id also works: a click on the label clicks the switch."],["Headless Toggle","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#in-a-form","With a name, a checked switch submits value (on by default) through a hidden input after the button. Off or disabled, it submits nothing. A form reset puts an uncontrolled switch back to defaultChecked."],["Headless Toggle","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps the state and still submits it, but clicks, Space and Enter don't flip it. The switch gets aria-readonly. disabled is the button's own attribute: the switch can't be used and isn't submitted. There are no sizes: the track and the knob are your CSS."],["Headless Toggle","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#style-it",""],["Headless Toggle","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#parts",""],["Headless Toggle","Switch.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#switch-root","A <button type=\\"button\\" role=\\"switch\\">, then a hidden input when name is set and the switch is checked and enabled. It takes every button prop except type, role, value and defaultChecked. Prop Type Default checked boolean The state (controlled) defaultChecked boolean false The starting state (uncontrolled) onCheckedChange (checked: boolean, event: MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => void After the user flips it readOnly boolean false Keeps the state: a click, Space or Enter changes nothing (aria-readonly) name string A checked switch submits value with its form value string 'on' Submitted while checked Attribute When data-checked On data-disabled Disabled data-readonly Read-only Switch.useSwitchContext() returns checked, disabled and readOnly to any component inside Root."],["Headless Toggle","Switch.Thumb","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#switch-thumb","A <span aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> inside Root, for the knob. It has the same data-checked, data-disabled and data-readonly as Root."],["Headless Toggle","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toggle/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Space, Enter Flips the switch Tab Moves to the next control The part sets role=\\"switch\\", aria-checked and aria-readonly, and focuses the switch on a click. You add: A name: aria-label, aria-labelledby, or a <label htmlFor>. The state text, hidden from screen readers. A visible focus style. Write the label as the setting (\\"Email alerts\\"), not as an action (\\"Turn on email alerts\\")."],["Headless Date picker","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/","DatePicker and Calendar give you the date picker's behaviour with no classes. The parts read what users type (Thai digits too), open the calendar when the box gets focus, move focus between the box and the calendar, check the date against min, max and isDateDisabled, block the form while the date is wrong, and submit an ISO date. You own the markup, the label, the placeholder, the error text, the icons and every style. The parts render no text of their own apart from month and day names. The styled version is Date picker."],["Headless Date picker","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Date picker","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#use-it","Root calls onValueChange with the ISO string (yyyy-mm-dd, Gregorian year) whenever a committed date changes: a commit on blur or Enter (a full date typed is the value at once and is reported then), a pick, a clear. With name, a hidden input submits the same string. A Calendar.Root inside Popup takes the picker's state by itself."],["Headless Date picker","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#anatomy","Keep the boxes, Clear and Trigger inside Group: focus and presses there don't count as leaving the picker. A range adds a second <DatePicker.Input field=\\"end\\" />."],["Headless Date picker","Language, era and format","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#language-era-and-format","Root follows the page's language: without locale it uses <html lang>, else the browser's, so a Thai page gets Thai messages and month names. locale overrides it. For Thai, era defaults to be (พ.ศ.); set era=\\"ce\\" for ค.ศ. format sets the order users see and type; value stays ISO. The placeholder is yours: write the format in the page's language."],["Headless Date picker","Pick a range","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#pick-a-range","range gives two boxes sharing one calendar. The start box's id is Root's id, the end box's <id>-end; point each <label> at them. A pick for the start keeps the calendar open for the end, and the days in between get data-in-range. Picking an end before the start swaps the two."],["Headless Date picker","Limit the dates","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#limit-the-dates","Refused days get data-disabled and aria-disabled, and PrevButton / NextButton turn off at min / max. A refused date that is typed stays in the box with its problem, and the form won't submit."],["Headless Date picker","Clear button and Today","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#clear-button-and-today","Clear empties its box and keeps focus there without opening the calendar. Calendar.TodayButton picks today. firstDay on the calendar sets the first day of the week (0 Sunday … 6 Saturday). Clear is always rendered; hide it yourself while the box is empty if you want, as the example does with the context's state.text."],["Headless Date picker","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps and submits the value but blocks typing and the calendar. disabled disables the boxes and Trigger; nothing is submitted or validated. Clear and Trigger are disabled in both."],["Headless Date picker","Phones and tablets","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#phones-and-tablets","On a phone (a touch screen narrower than 42rem), picker=\\"auto\\" (the default) opens the calendar in a bottom sheet: Popup renders inside a modal <dialog data-sheet> (the page behind inert and held still, focus kept inside). Esc, a DatePicker.SheetClose, a swipe down on a DatePicker.SheetGrip or a tap on the scrim closes it, and focus alone doesn't open it, so the box can still be typed in. Style the dialog with sheetClassName (its scrim with backdrop:) and the box on data-sheet; keep its padding clear of env(safe-area-inset-*). SheetGrip and SheetClose render only in the sheet. picker=\\"custom\\" keeps the calendar under the box on phones, picker=\\"sheet\\" uses the sheet everywhere, and picker=\\"native\\" opens the OS date picker from a DatePicker.NativeInput: put one over each box, invisible and without pointer events. On a phone the example above opens the bottom sheet; elsewhere, the calendar under the box. The OS picker (picker=\\"native\\") can't grey out isDateDisabled days, so its pick is checked like typed text."],["Headless Date picker","The calendar on its own","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#the-calendar-on-its-own","Calendar.Root works outside a picker too. On its own it holds the month shown and the chosen day; pass value or focusDate (with onFocusDateChange) to control them. onPick hears every pick. A range (range, value, endValue, activeField) is yours to hold on a calendar on its own. Its era defaults to ce whatever the locale: set locale=\\"th\\" and era=\\"be\\" for Thai."],["Headless Date picker","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#style-it",""],["Headless Date picker","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#parts",""],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, plus an <input type=\\"hidden\\"> for name and one for endName (none while disabled). Prop Type Default value string The ISO date, controlled (the start in a range) defaultValue string '' onValueChange (value: string) => void After the date changes range boolean false Two boxes, one calendar endValue string The end, controlled defaultEndValue string '' onEndValueChange (value: string) => void name string Submits the (start) date endName string Submits the end date min, max string '' ISO dates isDateDisabled (date: Date) => boolean | string Refuses a day; a string is its message format 'dd/mm/yyyy' | 'mm/dd/yyyy' | 'yyyy-mm-dd' 'dd/mm/yyyy' era 'be' | 'ce' 'be' for a Thai locale, else 'ce' locale string <html lang>, else the browser's Language of the messages and the calendar's names disabled boolean false readOnly boolean false required boolean false invalid boolean false Forces the error state; the form won't submit invalidMessage string '' With invalid: the form's validity message picker 'auto' | 'custom' | 'sheet' | 'native' 'auto' auto: the calendar, in a bottom sheet on a phone; custom: under the box everywhere; sheet: the sheet everywhere; native: the OS picker id string generated The start box's id; the end box gets <id>-end, the popup <id>-calendar"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-group","Renders a <div> around the boxes. Attribute When data-open The calendar is open data-disabled disabled"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-input","Renders an <input type=\\"text\\" role=\\"combobox\\">. Its value, disabled, readOnly and required come from Root; its id from Root's id. Prop Type Default field 'start' | 'end' 'start' Which date the box holds Attribute When data-open The calendar is open and picks for this box data-invalid The box shows its error data-disabled disabled data-readonly readOnly"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.NativeInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-nativeinput","Renders an <input type=\\"date\\"> with tabIndex={-1} and aria-hidden=\\"true\\"; its value, min and max come from Root. Prop Type Default field 'start' | 'end' 'start' Which date it picks"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Clear","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-clear","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}, disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Prop Type Default field 'start' | 'end' 'start' Which box it empties"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-trigger","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1}, aria-haspopup=\\"dialog\\" and aria-expanded. It opens the calendar with focus in the grid, or closes it, and is disabled while Root is disabled or read-only. Attribute When data-open The calendar is open"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-popup","Renders a <div role=\\"dialog\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer, under the start box (above it when there's no room below). Its children render only while it is open. In the bottom sheet it renders the same <div>, without popover and role, inside a modal <dialog data-sheet> that takes aria-label. Prop Type sheetClassName, sheetStyle string, CSSProperties The bottom sheet's <dialog> Attribute When data-open Open data-side Where it ended up: bottom or top data-sheet In the bottom sheet (on the <dialog> and the box)"],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.SheetGrip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-sheetgrip","Renders a <div> with touch-action: none in the bottom sheet only: a swipe down on it closes the sheet (64px, or a flick), shorter it springs back. While a finger drags it, the dialog has data-dragging and a translate. Put a grip mark and a SheetClose in it."],["Headless Date picker","DatePicker.SheetClose","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#datepicker-sheetclose","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> in the bottom sheet only; it closes the sheet like Esc. Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-parts",""],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-root","Renders a <div>. Inside a DatePicker.Popup it takes the picker's value, range, focus, limits, locale and era; a prop you pass still wins. Prop Type Default value string The chosen day, ISO, controlled (the start in a range) defaultValue string '' The first chosen day (single date) endValue string '' The range's end range boolean false activeField 'start' | 'end' 'start' Which end a pick sets (drives the preview) focusDate Date The day with the tab stop, whose month shows (controlled) defaultFocusDate Date the value, else today onFocusDateChange (date: Date) => void onPick (date: Date) => void An available day was picked min, max string '' isDateDisabled (date: Date) => boolean | string locale string <html lang>, else the browser's BCP 47 locale for the names era 'be' | 'ce' 'be' for a Thai locale, else 'ce' firstDay number 0 0 Sunday … 6 Saturday months number 1 Months side by side, 1 to 12; put the grid in Months pageBy 'months' | 'single' 'months' How far ‹ › turn several months: the whole page, or one month today string the real today The day marked as today, ISO weekdayFormat 'narrow' | 'short' the translation's The weekday headings showWeekNumbers boolean false An ISO week number <th data-week-number> before each week showOutsideDays boolean false Other months' days fill six weeks (one month only). By default they are empty cells and a week without a day of the month is left out, as Cally onPageChange ({ start, end }) => void The months shown changed: the first and last day on show handle Ref<CalendarHandle> focusDay() moves focus to the tab-stop day Attribute When data-range range"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.PrevButton, Calendar.NextButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-prevbutton-calendar-nextbutton","Each renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that turns the page back or on: by one month, or with several months by the whole page (pageBy=\\"single\\": one month). Focus moves only when its day leaves the page. It is disabled when the first (or last) month on show reaches min (or max)."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.MonthName","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-monthname","Renders a <span aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> with the month's name; children replace it."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.Months, Calendar.MonthTitle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-months-calendar-monthtitle","With months above 1, Months calls its children function for each month on show; the MonthTitle, Grid and other parts inside stand in that month. MonthTitle renders a <div aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> with the month's name, and its year when that differs from the first month's (the header's YearInput shows the first month's year). With one month, Months renders children once. Prop Type Default children (Months) (month: Date) => ReactNode Renders one month, given its first day (required)"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.Heading","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-heading","Renders a <div aria-live=\\"polite\\"> with the month and year (with several months, the first one's). It names the grid, so keep it (hide it visually if you like); children replace the text."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.MonthSelect, Calendar.YearSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-monthselect-calendar-yearselect","Cally's heading selects. Each renders a <select>; give it an aria-label or a <label>. MonthSelect lists the months of the year shown, and a month wholly outside min / max is disabled. YearSelect lists maxYears years around the year shown, cut to min / max, in the calendar's era. A choice shows that month or year; focus stays on the select. With several months they show the first month. Use them instead of YearInput and YearStep, or next to them. Prop Type Default formatMonth (MonthSelect) 'long' | 'short' 'long' The month names maxYears (YearSelect) number 20 How many years to offer"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.YearInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-yearinput","Renders an <input type=\\"number\\"> with the year shown, in the calendar's era. A typed four-digit year shows that year; leaving the box puts the shown year back."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.YearStep","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-yearstep","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1} that steps the shown year. It is disabled past the years min / max allow. Prop Type Default delta number Years to step, e.g. 1 or -1 (required)"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.Grid","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-grid","Renders a <table role=\\"grid\\"> named by Heading (with several months, aria-label names it after its month and year). It handles the keys; in a right-to-left page ← and → swap."],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.GridHeader, Calendar.HeaderCell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-gridheader-calendar-headercell","GridHeader renders a <thead> with one row and calls its children function for each weekday. HeaderCell renders a <th scope=\\"col\\"> with the short weekday name and the full one as abbr. Prop Type Default children (GridHeader) (date: Date) => ReactNode Renders one weekday (required) date (HeaderCell) Date The weekday (required)"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.GridBody, Calendar.Cell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-gridbody-calendar-cell","GridBody renders a <tbody> with six weeks and calls its children function for each day. Cell renders a <td role=\\"gridcell\\" aria-selected>. Prop Type Default children (GridBody) (date: Date) => ReactNode Renders one day (required) date (Cell) Date The day (required)"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.Day","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-day","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with the day's number (children replace it). It goes inside a Cell. Only the tab-stop day has tabIndex={0}. Attribute When data-selected The chosen day (either end of a range) data-today Today data-outside-month A day of the month before or after data-disabled Refused: outside min / max, or by isDateDisabled data-in-range Between the range's start and its end (chosen or previewed) data-range-start The range's start data-range-end The range's end, chosen or previewed"],["Headless Date picker","Calendar.TodayButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#calendar-todaybutton","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that picks today. It is disabled when today is refused."],["Headless Date picker","Hooks","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#hooks","DatePicker.useDatePickerContext() inside Root gives the picker's state: state (text, values, open), problems, errors (the messages in locale's words) and showsError(field). Calendar.useCalendarContext() gives the month shown and its names; Calendar.useCellContext() inside a Cell gives that day's state as values."],["Headless Date picker","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-date-picker/#keyboard-and-accessibility","In the box: Key Does Typing Enters the date; Thai digits become 0–9 ↓ Opens the calendar and moves focus into it Tab Moves on to the next field (in a range, from the start to the end); what was typed is committed and the calendar closes once focus leaves the picker Shift + Tab From the start box: closes the calendar Enter Commits the typed text, closes the calendar; the form's own Enter submit follows Esc Closes the calendar In the calendar grid: Key Does ← / → Previous / next day ↑ / ↓ Same day of the previous / next week Home / End First / last day of the week Page Up / Page Down Previous / next month Shift + Page Up / Page Down Previous / next year Enter, Space Picks the day; in a picker the calendar closes (in a range, after the end) Esc Closes, focus back in the box Tab Goes round the calendar's own controls: ‹, the year, ›, the day (and Today), back to the first after the last; Esc or a pick leaves the calendar Shift + Tab The same, the other way round The parts handle: role=\\"combobox\\", aria-haspopup=\\"dialog\\", aria-expanded, aria-controls and aria-invalid on each box; role=\\"dialog\\" on Popup. A grid of day buttons with one roving tab stop. Each day is named by its full date, with aria-current=\\"date\\" on today, aria-pressed on chosen days and aria-disabled on refused ones. The month change, announced by Heading. The form's validation: the first wrong box carries the message, the browser's bubble is suppressed, and a blocked submit moves focus to that box. You add: A <label htmlFor> for each box, and an aria-label on Popup (\\"Choose date\\"), PrevButton, NextButton, YearInput, YearStep, Clear and Trigger. The error text and the format hint, linked to the box with aria-describedby:"],["Headless Time picker","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/","TimePicker gives you the time picker's behaviour with no classes: a short text box for hh:mm that takes part in the form's own validation through pattern, and native selects beside it for AM / PM or the time zone. Root passes disabled, readOnly and invalid to every part; a read-only select still takes focus but doesn't open or change. You own the label, the error text, the layout and every style. Validation is yours too, as in Carbon React: set invalid when your check fails. The styled version is Time picker."],["Headless Time picker","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Time picker","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#use-it","Each part submits on its own under its name: the time as typed, and each select's <option> value. Nothing is converted."],["Headless Time picker","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#anatomy","A Select also works on its own, outside a Root."],["Headless Time picker","12-hour or 24-hour","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#12-hour-or-24-hour","Input takes 12-hour time by default: h:mm or hh:mm, at most 5 characters (TimePicker.TWELVE_HOUR_PATTERN). For 24-hour time, set your own pattern and leave out the AM / PM select: maxLength changes the length limit."],["Headless Time picker","Errors","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#errors","pattern takes part in the form's validation, but no message shows by itself. Set invalid on Root when your check fails: the box gets aria-invalid and data-invalid. The message is your markup; link it with aria-describedby. There is no warning state; a warning is your markup too."],["Headless Time picker","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps every value and submits it: the box is read-only, and a select takes focus but doesn't open or change (aria-readonly). disabled disables the box and every select."],["Headless Time picker","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#style-it",""],["Headless Time picker","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#parts",""],["Headless Time picker","TimePicker.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#timepicker-root","Renders no element: it holds disabled, readOnly and invalid for its parts. Prop Type Default disabled boolean false Disables the box and every select readOnly boolean false Keeps every value invalid boolean false Marks the box aria-invalid and data-invalid"],["Headless Time picker","TimePicker.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#timepicker-input","Renders an <input type=\\"text\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\">. Its disabled and readOnly come from Root. Prop Type Default pattern string TWELVE_HOUR_PATTERN 12-hour h:mm / hh:mm, an optional space after maxLength number 5 Attribute When data-invalid invalid on Root data-disabled disabled on Root data-readonly readOnly on Root"],["Headless Time picker","TimePicker.Select","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#timepicker-select","Renders a native <select>. It is disabled with Root or by its own disabled. Attribute When data-disabled Disabled data-readonly readOnly on Root TimePicker.useTimePickerContext() inside Root gives disabled, readOnly and invalid."],["Headless Time picker","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-time-picker/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Enter (in the box) Submits the form it's in, as a native input does ↑ / ↓, Space, Enter (on a select) The browser's own select keys; ignored while read-only The parts handle: Native elements throughout: a text input and <select>s. aria-invalid on the box while invalid, and aria-readonly on a read-only select. A read-only select keeps focus on a mouse press without opening its list. You add: A <label htmlFor> for the box, and an aria-label for each select (nothing names them for you). The error text, linked to the box with aria-describedby."],["Headless Slider","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/","Slider gives you the slider's behaviour with no classes: one thumb, or two for a range. Each thumb is a role=\\"slider\\" Tab stop that moves with the arrow keys; a press on the track moves the nearer thumb and starts a drag that follows the pointer anywhere on the page. A number box beside the track applies typed numbers, and a hidden input submits each value. You own the markup, the end labels, the messages and every style, including where the thumbs sit: Control gives you the positions as CSS variables. The styled version is Slider."],["Headless Slider","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Slider","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#use-it","Values are arrays, one entry per thumb: [value], or [lower, upper]. onValueChange follows every change (dragging, keys, typing); onValueCommit hears the committed ones: the pointer released, a key handled, a number box committed. An entry of value left undefined keeps that thumb uncontrolled."],["Headless Slider","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#anatomy","With one thumb, leave out the parts with index={1}."],["Headless Slider","Scale and step","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#scale-and-step","min and max set the ends (0 and 100) and step the increment (1). Arrow keys move one step; with Shift they move stepMultiplier steps (4). The end labels are your markup. For a formatted value, give the thumb aria-valuetext (say, \\"10%\\"); screen readers read it instead of the number."],["Headless Slider","Two thumbs: a range","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#two-thumbs-a-range","Give two values and two thumbs. The thumbs never pass each other: each one's bounds stop at the other, and a press on the track moves the nearer one."],["Headless Slider","The number box","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#the-number-box","Input mirrors its thumb's value. A number within its bounds applies while typing, snapped to the nearest step. On blur or Enter, a number outside the bounds is clamped, and text that isn't a number makes the slider invalid. The context's corrected holds the typed number after a clamp, for you to announce: Without a number box, leave out Slider.Input. A value tooltip on the thumb, if you want one, is your markup:"],["Headless Slider","Errors and warnings","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#errors-and-warnings","invalid on Root shows the error: aria-invalid and data-invalid on the thumbs and the boxes, and data-invalid on Group, Control, Track and Indicator. A disabled or read-only slider shows no error. There is no warning state: a warning is your markup."],["Headless Slider","Read-only and disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#read-only-and-disabled","readOnly keeps the values and submits them; nothing moves and the boxes can't be edited. A read-only thumb leaves the Tab order unless you give it tabIndex={0}. disabled changes nothing either, and HiddenInput submits nothing. An uncontrolled slider goes back to defaultValue when its form is reset."],["Headless Slider","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#style-it","--slider-range-start is where the filled part starts (0 with one thumb) and --slider-range-end where it ends, as 0…1 of the track. Place the lower thumb at the start and the upper (or only) thumb at the end."],["Headless Slider","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#parts",""],["Headless Slider","Slider.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-root","Renders no element: it holds the values for its parts. Prop Type Default value readonly (number | undefined)[] One entry per thumb, controlled; an undefined entry keeps that thumb uncontrolled defaultValue readonly number[] [min] onValueChange (values: number[]) => void Every change onValueCommit (values: number[]) => void Committed changes: pointer released, a key, a box committed min number 0 max number 100 step number 1 stepMultiplier number 4 Shift + arrow moves step × stepMultiplier disabled boolean false readOnly boolean false Keeps the values; thumbs leave the Tab order invalid boolean false Shows the error"],["Headless Slider","Slider.Label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-label","Renders a <label> that names the group and the thumbs. A click on it focuses the first thumb. Its htmlFor defaults to the first thumb's id. Attribute When data-disabled disabled"],["Headless Slider","Slider.Group, Slider.Control, Slider.Track, Slider.Indicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-group-slider-control-slider-track-slider-indicator","Each renders a <div>. Group is a role=\\"group\\" named by Label, around the track, your end labels and the boxes. Control is the pointer area: a press there moves the nearer thumb (or the one pressed) and starts a drag. It sets --slider-range-start and --slider-range-end. Track is the rail and Indicator the filled part. Attribute When data-disabled disabled data-readonly readOnly data-invalid The error shows data-dragging A thumb is being dragged data-orientation Always horizontal (Group and Control only)"],["Headless Slider","Slider.Thumb","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-thumb","Renders a <div role=\\"slider\\"> with aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax and aria-valuenow, named by Label unless you give it aria-label or aria-labelledby. Prop Type Default index number 0 Which value it moves Attribute When data-index Always: its index data-disabled disabled data-readonly readOnly data-invalid The error shows data-dragging This thumb is being dragged"],["Headless Slider","Slider.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-input","Renders an <input type=\\"number\\"> whose min / max are the thumb's bounds and whose step is Root's. Prop Type Default index number 0 Which value it edits Attribute When data-index Always: its index data-disabled disabled data-readonly readOnly data-invalid The error shows"],["Headless Slider","Slider.HiddenInput","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#slider-hiddeninput","Renders an <input type=\\"hidden\\"> with the value; give it a name. It is disabled (submits nothing) while Root is disabled. Prop Type Default index number 0 Which value it submits Slider.useSliderContext() inside Root gives values, dragging, invalid, notANumber, corrected and the rest of the state."],["Headless Slider","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-slider/#keyboard-and-accessibility","On a thumb: Key Does ← / ↓ One step down → / ↑ One step up Shift + arrow stepMultiplier steps Home / End To min / max (in a range, as far as the other thumb allows) In a number box, Enter commits the typed number. The parts handle: role=\\"slider\\" with aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax and aria-valuenow on each thumb; in a range each thumb's bounds stop at the other. aria-disabled, aria-readonly and aria-invalid on the thumbs; aria-invalid on the boxes. A role=\\"group\\" named by Label; a click on the label focuses the first thumb. Focus moves to the thumb a press on the track moved. You add: An aria-label for each thumb in a range (\\"Lower bound\\", \\"Upper bound\\") and for each number box. aria-valuetext for a formatted value. The error message (link it with aria-describedby) and the announcement of a clamped number."],["Headless File uploader","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/","FileUploader gives you the file uploader's behaviour with no classes: a Trigger that opens the file dialog, a DropZone that takes dropped files (not folders), the limits on type, size and count, the list of chosen files, focus that moves on as rows go, and the valid files submitted with the form. You own the rows, the icons, the messages, the progress bar and every style. Nothing uploads by itself: you send the files and update their status. The styled version is File uploader."],["Headless File uploader","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless File uploader","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#use-it","Each file is a FileItem: uuid, name, the File itself, and its status, invalid, errorSubject, errorBody, progress and retryable. Root calls onAdd right after a pick (refused files included), before the list updates (as Carbon's onAddFiles), onChange with addedFiles, removedFiles, currentFiles and action (add, remove or clear), and onDelete when a file is removed. Without multiple, a new pick replaces the list."],["Headless File uploader","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#anatomy",""],["Headless File uploader","Button or drop zone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#button-or-drop-zone","DropZone takes files dropped on it; Trigger is your button, or the whole zone. openOnKeyDown opens the dialog on the Enter / Space key press itself, as Carbon's drop container does. Trigger's render prop renders your own button (a styled one, say) with the props it would put on its <button>. The context's picked holds the names of the last pick, if your button should show the file name or \\"3 files\\"."],["Headless File uploader","Limit the files","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#limit-the-files","accept, maxFileSize, maxFiles and maxTotalSize mark refused files invalid. A refused file stays in the list but isn't submitted. describeRejection gives its error text from the reason: 'invalid-type', 'too-large', 'too-many' or 'total-too-large'. Without it, a refused file has no error text. accept also filters the file dialog, and a dropped file is checked against it too."],["Headless File uploader","Upload the files","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#upload-the-files","Hold the list yourself with files and replace it as each upload moves on. Pass progress and retryable on to each Item. The example sends nothing: a timer stands in for the uploads, and a file over 1 MB fails once so you can retry it. status on Root sets the state new files start in (edit by default). An uploading item with a progress can be removed: that cancels the upload, and onDelete tells you to stop sending it. onRetry hears the retry of a failed upload (an invalid, retryable file). Refused files aren't retryable."],["Headless File uploader","File states","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#file-states","The state shows as data-status, data-invalid and data-removable on the Item. An Item also works on its own, for files already on the server: it calls onDelete and onRetry with its uuid (its name when you leave uuid out), and removing it is up to you. edit can be removed; uploading can be removed only with a progress; complete can't. Remove renders nothing on a row that can't be removed, and is disabled with the item. Retry renders only on an invalid, retryable row. ItemStatus shows its children once an upload goes from uploading to complete."],["Headless File uploader","In a form","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#in-a-form","With a name, FormValue submits every valid file under it, like <input type=\\"file\\" multiple>. Refused files are left out. required blocks the submit until there is a valid file, with requiredText as the message (without one, the English translation's: \\"Add at least one file.\\"). The browser's bubble doesn't show; focus goes to Trigger. The example shows its own message from Input's onInvalid. A form reset empties an uncontrolled list. disabled turns off Trigger, DropZone, Input, FormValue and every Item inside the Root."],["Headless File uploader","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#style-it",""],["Headless File uploader","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#parts",""],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-root","Renders no element: it holds the list, the limits and the focus rules. Prop Type Default accept string '' Extensions and MIME types, comma-separated multiple boolean false Without it, a pick replaces the list maxFileSize number 0 Bytes; larger files are added as invalid (0 = no limit) maxFiles number 0 Most valid files; the ones past it are invalid (0 = no limit) maxTotalSize number 0 Bytes the valid files may add up to (0 = no limit) describeRejection (rejection: Rejection) => { errorSubject?: string; errorBody?: string } The error text of a refused file name string Submitted name of FormValue disabled boolean false status 'edit' | 'uploading' | 'complete' 'edit' The state new files start in required boolean false At least one valid file before the form submits requiredText string '' The validity message while required and no valid file; empty: the English translation's files FileItem[] The list, controlled defaultFiles FileItem[] [] onAdd (addedFiles: FileItem[]) => void Right after a pick or drop onChange (change: FileChange) => void Every change of the list onDelete ({ deletedFile, remainingFiles }) => void A file was removed onRetry (retriedFile: FileItem) => void A failed upload was retried"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-group","Renders a <div role=\\"group\\">; name it with aria-label, or aria-labelledby with the context's titleId. Attribute When data-disabled disabled"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-title","Renders a <p> whose id is the context's titleId."],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.DropZone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-dropzone","Renders a <div> that takes dropped files. Folders are skipped. Attribute When data-drag-over Files are dragged over it data-disabled disabled"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-trigger","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that opens the file dialog; disabled while disabled. Focus comes back to it when the list empties under it. Prop Type Default openOnKeyDown boolean false Enter / Space open the dialog on key down render (props) => ReactElement Renders your own button with these props Attribute When data-drag-over Files are dragged over the drop zone data-disabled disabled"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Label, FileUploader.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-label-fileuploader-input","Label renders a <label> for Input; hide it visually. Input renders the <input type=\\"file\\"> that Trigger clicks, with tabIndex={-1}; its multiple, accept and disabled come from Root. Hide it."],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.FormValue","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-formvalue","With Root's name, renders a hidden <input type=\\"file\\" multiple> that holds every valid file. Renders nothing without a name."],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.List","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-list","Renders a <div> around the items; focus moves within it as rows go."],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-item","Renders a <div> for one file. Prop Type Default name string The file's name (required) uuid string name Identifies it in onDelete / onRetry status 'edit' | 'uploading' | 'complete' 'edit' invalid boolean false retryable boolean false On an invalid row: Retry shows disabled boolean false Also on while its Root is disabled progress number 0–100 while uploading; Remove then cancels onDelete (uuid: string) => void onRetry (uuid: string) => void Attribute When data-file-item Always data-status Always: edit, uploading or complete data-invalid invalid data-removable The file can be removed: edit, or uploading with a progress, and not disabled"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.ItemRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-itemrow","Renders a <div> with aria-disabled while the item is disabled. Focus lands on it when its last button goes with focus."],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Remove","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-remove","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that removes the file (onDelete), or cancels its upload; disabled with the item. Renders nothing on a complete row or one uploading without a progress. Attribute When data-file-remove Always"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.Retry","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-retry","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that retries a failed upload (onRetry), only on an invalid, retryable row; disabled with the item. Attribute When data-file-retry Always"],["Headless File uploader","FileUploader.ItemStatus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#fileuploader-itemstatus","Renders a <span role=\\"status\\">: its children show once the upload finished. FileUploader.useFileUploaderContext() inside Root gives files, picked, dragOver, titleId, remove, retry, browse and more. FileUploader.useItemContext() inside an Item gives its status, percent (the progress while uploading) and finished."],["Headless File uploader","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-file-uploader/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Enter or Space on Trigger Opens the file dialog Enter or Space on Remove Removes the file, or cancels its upload; focus moves to the next row's Remove, else the previous one's, else Trigger Enter or Space on Retry Calls onRetry; when the button goes away, focus stays on the row's Remove, else the row The parts handle: role=\\"group\\" and aria-disabled on Group; the file input labelled by Label and out of the Tab order. Focus after a row or a retry button goes, so it never falls to the page. required: the form's validity, with no browser bubble, and focus on Trigger when the submit is blocked. A polite live region in ItemStatus. You add: A name for Group and the text of Label. An aria-label on each Remove and Retry with the file's name: \\"Remove file - contract.pdf\\", \\"Retry upload - contract.pdf\\". The error text (an alert, as role=\\"alert\\"), the ItemStatus text, and a progress bar if you show one."],["Headless Tabs","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/","Tabs is the behaviour of the styled Tabs as unstyled React parts: one Tab stop on the strip (a roving tabindex), the arrow keys, Home and End, automatic or manual activation, Delete and close buttons for dismissable tabs, and the tablist / tab / tabpanel roles with their ids wired together. State shows as data-* attributes to style on. You own the markup and every style: the underline or the contained look, the sizes, the icons, the scroll buttons of a long strip, and the layout of a vertical column."],["Headless Tabs","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Tabs","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#use-it",""],["Headless Tabs","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#anatomy","A Tab and its Panel share a value. Close is only for dismissable tabs; put it beside its Tab, never inside it (a button can't hold a button)."],["Headless Tabs","Starting tab and changes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#starting-tab-and-changes","Without value or defaultValue, the first enabled Tab is selected. Root finds it among its children, inside List and fragments; when your tabs sit in other wrappers, set defaultValue. Use value with onValueChange for a controlled strip."],["Headless Tabs","Manual activation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#manual-activation","activation=\\"manual\\": the arrow keys only move focus, and Enter or Space selects. Use it when a panel is slow to render or loads data."],["Headless Tabs","Keep the current tab","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#keep-the-current-tab","onValueChange reports the tab the user chose. In a controlled strip, keep value as it is to stay on the current tab, for example while a form in it has unsaved changes."],["Headless Tabs","Vertical tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#vertical-tabs","orientation=\\"vertical\\" makes ↑ and ↓ the keys that move, sets aria-orientation=\\"vertical\\" on the list, and data-orientation=\\"vertical\\" on Root and List. The column layout is yours."],["Headless Tabs","Dismissable tabs","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#dismissable-tabs","With dismissable, Delete on a focused tab and a click on its Close call onTabCloseRequest with the tab's value. Remove the tab from your list to close it. A closed selected tab passes the selection to the first enabled tab (onValueChange), and focus moves to the tab now in its place, else the one before. These tabs sit in a wrapper with their Close, so Root gets a defaultValue."],["Headless Tabs","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#style-it","The contained look: tabs on the accent layer, the selected one on the layer with a blue top edge, and dividers that come from your CSS."],["Headless Tabs","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#parts",""],["Headless Tabs","Tabs.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#tabs-root","Renders a <div> that holds the state. It takes every <div> prop. Prop Type Default value string — The selected tab's value (controlled) defaultValue string the first enabled Tab The starting tab (uncontrolled). Found inside List and fragments only onValueChange (value: string) => void — After the user selects another tab, or a closed selected tab passed the selection on activation 'automatic' | 'manual' 'automatic' automatic selects as focus moves; manual selects on Enter or Space orientation 'horizontal' | 'vertical' 'horizontal' ← / → or ↑ / ↓ move dismissable boolean false Delete and Close ask to close a tab onTabCloseRequest (value: string) => void — A tab asked to close: drop it from your children to close it Attribute When data-orientation Always: horizontal or vertical"],["Headless Tabs","Tabs.List","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#tabs-list","Renders a <div role=\\"tablist\\"> (with aria-orientation=\\"vertical\\" in a vertical strip). It handles the keys and the clicks of its tabs, and takes every <div> prop; name it with aria-label or aria-labelledby. Attribute When data-orientation Always: horizontal or vertical"],["Headless Tabs","Tabs.Tab","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#tabs-tab","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\" role=\\"tab\\"> with aria-selected, aria-controls (its panel) and an id from Root. Only the tab stop has tabIndex={0}. Prop Type Default value string — Matches the value of its Panel (required) disabled boolean false aria-disabled: stays visible and announced, but can't be selected or reached with the arrows Attribute When data-selected It is the selected tab data-disabled disabled is set data-value Always: its value In dismissable tabs each enabled tab gets aria-keyshortcuts=\\"Delete\\", unless you pass your own."],["Headless Tabs","Tabs.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#tabs-close","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={-1} and aria-hidden=\\"true\\": Delete on the tab does the same for keyboard and screen reader users. Name it with title for the mouse. Prop Type Default value string — The tab it closes (required)"],["Headless Tabs","Tabs.Panel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#tabs-panel","Renders a <div role=\\"tabpanel\\">, labelled by its tab and hidden unless its tab is selected. It is a Tab stop (tabIndex={0}) only when nothing inside it can take focus. Prop Type Default value string — Matches the value of its Tab (required) Attribute When data-selected Its tab is selected Tabs.useTabsContext() gives the enclosing Root's state (value, orientation, activation, dismissable …) to your own parts, and Tabs.tabIds(id, value) the ids of a tab and its panel."],["Headless Tabs","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tabs/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does ← / → Previous / next enabled tab, wrapping (mirrored right-to-left); with automatic it also selects ↑ / ↓ The same with orientation=\\"vertical\\" Home / End First / last enabled tab Enter, Space Select the focused tab Delete Asks to close the focused tab (dismissable) Tab Leaves the strip; the next stop is the panel, or the first thing inside it The parts set the roles, aria-selected, aria-controls, aria-labelledby, aria-disabled, aria-orientation and the roving tabIndex. You add: A name for the strip: aria-label or aria-labelledby on List. aria-label on a tab that shows only an icon, and a tooltip for sighted users. Scroll buttons when the tabs overflow; keep them out of the Tab order, as the styled Tabs do."],["Headless Pagination nav","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/","PaginationNav is the behaviour of the styled Pagination nav as unstyled React parts. Root holds the page (0-based, as in Carbon) and lays out the row: which page numbers show, and which pages fold into the \\"…\\" menus at either end, following the current page as Carbon's do. Prev, Next, Page and Overflow move between pages, and Status announces the change. You own the markup and every style: the list, the icons, the underline of the current page, the \\"…\\" over each menu, and the words screen readers hear."],["Headless Pagination nav","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Pagination nav","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#use-it","Root doesn't render the row itself: read items from PaginationNav.usePaginationNavContext() in a component inside it, and render each item as a Page or an Overflow."],["Headless Pagination nav","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#anatomy","items (from usePaginationNavContext()) is the row in order: the first page, a front overflow, the pages around the current one, a back overflow and the last page. Each item is { kind: 'page', page, active } or { kind: 'overflow', from, count }."],["Headless Pagination nav","Controlled page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#controlled-page","Use page with onChange for a controlled row (both 0-based), or defaultPage for an uncontrolled one."],["Headless Pagination nav","Wrap around","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#wrap-around","With loop, Prev on the first page goes to the last, and Next on the last page to the first. Without it they are disabled at the ends (disabled and data-disabled)."],["Headless Pagination nav","Fewer items, or no menus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#fewer-items-or-no-menus","itemsShown is how many items the row holds, the overflows included (10 by default, at least 4); below 320px the row holds fewer by itself. disableOverflow keeps the overflows in the row but disables them."],["Headless Pagination nav","Name the hidden pages","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#name-the-hidden-pages","renderPage sets the text of each option in an Overflow (the 1-based number by default)."],["Headless Pagination nav","Your own row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#your-own-row","The parts don't need the \\"…\\" menus: render only the Page items, and text buttons for Prev and Next. Here a list of 12 contracts shows three per page."],["Headless Pagination nav","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#style-it","The current Page has data-current (and aria-current=\\"page\\"); Prev, Next and a disabled Overflow have data-disabled. Here they give round pages, the current one filled, and faded ends."],["Headless Pagination nav","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#parts",""],["Headless Pagination nav","PaginationNav.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#paginationnav-root","Renders a <nav>; name it with aria-label (\\"Pagination\\"). It takes every <nav> prop. Prop Type Default totalItems number — The number of pages (Carbon's name; required) page number — The current page, 0-based (controlled) defaultPage number 0 The starting page (uncontrolled) onChange (page: number) => void — After the user chose a page (0-based) itemsShown number 10 Items in the row, the overflows included (at least 4) loop boolean false Prev on the first page goes to the last, Next on the last to the first disableOverflow boolean false The overflows can't be opened size 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' 'lg' Only how many items fit on a window narrower than 320px (Carbon)"],["Headless Pagination nav","PaginationNav.Prev, PaginationNav.Next","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#paginationnav-prev-paginationnav-next","Each renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that moves one page back or forward; name it with aria-label. Disabled at the ends unless loop. Attribute When data-disabled It can't move (or you set disabled)"],["Headless Pagination nav","PaginationNav.Page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#paginationnav-page","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that goes to its page, with aria-current=\\"page\\" on the current one and tabIndex={0} (so Safari focuses it on click). Prop Type Default page number — Its page, 0-based (required) Attribute When data-current It is the current page data-page Always: its page, 1-based"],["Headless Pagination nav","PaginationNav.Overflow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#paginationnav-overflow","Renders a <select> of the hidden pages, with an empty, hidden first option, so it shows nothing: draw your \\"…\\" over it. Choosing an option goes to that page. Name it with aria-label. Prop Type Default from number — The first hidden page, 0-based (required) count number — How many pages it holds (required) renderPage (page: number) => ReactNode the 1-based number An option's text Attribute When data-disabled disableOverflow on Root, or you set disabled"],["Headless Pagination nav","PaginationNav.Status","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#paginationnav-status","Renders a <div aria-live=\\"polite\\" aria-atomic=\\"true\\">. Its text is yours: \\"Page 5 of 25\\", usually visually hidden."],["Headless Pagination nav","usePaginationNavContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#usepaginationnavcontext","Returns the state of the enclosing Root: page (0-based), total, items, loop, disableOverflow, go(page), step(-1 | 1) and stepDisabled(-1 | 1)."],["Headless Pagination nav","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination-nav/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Every page, Prev, Next and overflow is a native button or select, so Tab moves through them and Enter, Space and the select's own keys work. The parts set aria-current=\\"page\\", disabled at the ends, and the polite live region. You add: The landmark's name: aria-label on Root. Names for Prev, Next and each Overflow (aria-label), and the \\"…\\" drawn over each overflow with aria-hidden=\\"true\\" and pointer-events: none. Words before each number for screen readers (\\"Page 4\\"), as the visually hidden text in the examples, and the Status text."],["Headless Content switcher","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/","ContentSwitcher is the behaviour of the styled Content switcher as unstyled React parts: a tablist where exactly one item is selected, one Tab stop on the selected item, the arrow keys (wrapping and skipping disabled items), Home and End, and automatic or manual selection. State shows as data-* attributes to style on. You own the markup and every style: the track, the selected fill, the dividers, the icons and tooltips, and the content that changes."],["Headless Content switcher","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Content switcher","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#use-it",""],["Headless Content switcher","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#anatomy","Each direct child of Root is one item, by position. Root reads the name and disabled props of its children, so a component of your own that wraps an Item must take those two props too."],["Headless Content switcher","Switch the content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#switch-the-content","onChange gets { index, name } of the item the user selected. Showing the matching content is yours; put it right after the switcher."],["Headless Content switcher","Controlled selection","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#controlled-selection","Use selectedIndex with onChange for a controlled switcher, or defaultSelectedIndex (0 by default) for an uncontrolled one."],["Headless Content switcher","Disabled items and manual selection","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#disabled-items-and-manual-selection","A disabled item gets aria-disabled and data-disabled: the arrow keys skip it, and a click does nothing. With selectionMode=\\"manual\\" the arrow keys only move focus, and Enter or Space selects."],["Headless Content switcher","Icon only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#icon-only","An item that shows only an icon needs a name: aria-label on the Item. Add a tooltip for sighted users; here title stands in for one."],["Headless Content switcher","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#style-it","The low-contrast look: a grey track, and the selected item a light pill with bold text. The keyboard focus ring sits on the item with focus-visible."],["Headless Content switcher","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#parts",""],["Headless Content switcher","ContentSwitcher.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#contentswitcher-root","Renders a <div role=\\"tablist\\"> and wraps each child so it knows its position. It takes every <div> prop; name it with aria-label. Prop Type Default selectedIndex number — The selected item's position (controlled) defaultSelectedIndex number 0 The starting item (uncontrolled) onChange (change: { index: number; name: string }) => void — After the user selects another item; name is the item's name prop, or '' selectionMode 'automatic' | 'manual' 'automatic' automatic selects as the arrows move; manual selects on Enter or Space"],["Headless Content switcher","ContentSwitcher.Item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#contentswitcher-item","Renders a <div role=\\"tab\\"> with aria-selected. Only the Tab stop (the selected item, else the first enabled one) has tabIndex={0}. It takes every <div> prop. Prop Type Default name string — Reported in onChange (read by Root) disabled boolean false aria-disabled: stays visible and announced, but can't be selected or reached with the arrows Attribute When data-selected It is the selected item data-disabled disabled is set ContentSwitcher.useContentSwitcherContext() gives your own parts the state (selected, focusable, count, selectionMode, select(index)), and ContentSwitcher.useItemIndex() the position of the item it is called in."],["Headless Content switcher","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-content-switcher/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does ← / → Previous / next enabled item, wrapping (mirrored right-to-left); in automatic mode it also selects Home / End First / last enabled item Enter, Space Select the focused item Tab Leaves the switcher The parts set role=\\"tablist\\", role=\\"tab\\", aria-selected, aria-disabled and the roving tabIndex. You add: A name for the group: aria-label or aria-labelledby on Root. aria-label on items that show only an icon, and a tooltip. The content that changes, right after the switcher. The items control no panel, so there is no aria-controls."],["Headless Tooltip","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/","The Tooltip parts give you the behaviour of the styled Tooltip with no styles: a popup in the top layer beside the element it explains, opened on hover after a short delay and on keyboard focus, closed on blur, on activation and on Esc. The pointer can move onto the popup (WCAG 1.4.13). The text describes the element, or names it with label. You own the trigger element, the text, the caret and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Tooltip","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Tooltip","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#use-it","Trigger is a <span> around exactly one focusable element: it watches hover, focus and activation inside it, and gives that element its name or description. The popup sits beside the element, not beside the span."],["Headless Tooltip","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#anatomy",""],["Headless Tooltip","Describe or name","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#describe-or-name","Without label, the popup's text is the element's accessible description (aria-describedby), added to any description it already has. Use it for a hint on a control that has a visible name. With label, the text becomes the element's aria-label and the popup is aria-hidden: use it for icon-only buttons, as in \\"Use it\\"."],["Headless Tooltip","Placement and caret","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#placement-and-caret","placement takes top (the default), bottom, left, right, each with -start / -end. The popup flips when there is no room, and data-side says where it went. gap is the space to the element (8px by default). With caret, the popup gets --_caret-start: where a caret --_caret-w wide (12px if unset) must start along the edge to point at the element's centre. Draw the caret yourself, as below."],["Headless Tooltip","Delays","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#delays","The popup opens 100ms after the pointer arrives (delay) and closes 300ms after it leaves both the element and the popup (closeDelay, Carbon's leaveDelayMs). Keyboard focus opens it at once. Raise delay in a dense toolbar, so tooltips don't flash while the pointer crosses it."],["Headless Tooltip","Keep it open: \\"Copied\\"","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#keep-it-open-copied","Hold the state with open and onOpenChange. While your own flag is set the popup stays, whatever hover, focus, clicks and Esc report. Use it for a short confirmation. Click the number below. onOpenChange reports changes only, so a click on a closed tooltip reports nothing. disabled on Root is the opposite case: the popup never shows (for example while the text is still loading), and hover and focus still report."],["Headless Tooltip","Explain an unavailable action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#explain-an-unavailable-action","A disabled button takes no focus, so keyboard users would never see its tooltip. Use aria-disabled=\\"true\\" instead, ignore its clicks, and say why in the tooltip."],["Headless Tooltip","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#style-it",""],["Headless Tooltip","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#parts",""],["Headless Tooltip","Tooltip.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#tooltip-root","Renders no element of its own: it holds the open state and the hover timer, places the popup and closes it on Esc. Prop Type Default open boolean Shown (controlled); hover and focus then only report through onOpenChange defaultOpen boolean false Shown at first (uncontrolled) onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After hover, focus, activation or Esc would change it (changes only) label string The text as the element's accessible name instead of its description; the popup is then aria-hidden disabled boolean false Never shows; hover and focus still report placement Placement 'top' top, bottom, left, right, each with -start / -end gap number 8 Space between the element and the popup, in px caret boolean false Writes --_caret-start on the popup delay number 100 Hover time before it opens, in ms closeDelay number 300 Time after the pointer leaves before it closes, in ms Tooltip.useTooltipContext() returns the Root's state (open, popupId, label …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Tooltip","Tooltip.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#tooltip-trigger","A <span> around the one element the tooltip explains (its first child). It watches hover, keyboard focus (:focus-visible only: a mouse click already had its hover), clicks and Enter / Space inside it. It adds aria-describedby (or with label, aria-label) to that element, and the popup is placed beside it. It takes every span prop. Attribute When data-open The popup is showing"],["Headless Tooltip","Tooltip.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#tooltip-popup","A <span role=\\"tooltip\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer, with the id the element's aria-describedby points to. Its content stays rendered while closed. The pointer can rest on it. It takes every span prop except popover, id and role. Attribute When data-open Showing data-side top, bottom, left or right: where it went With caret on Root, it also gets the CSS variable --_caret-start."],["Headless Tooltip","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tooltip/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key What it does Tab Focus reaching the element opens the popup at once; focus leaving closes it Esc Closes the tooltip only (a surrounding dialog stays open); focus stays Enter, Space Activate the element and close the popup The parts set role=\\"tooltip\\" on the popup and aria-describedby or aria-label on the element. A click closes the popup too, so it doesn't cover the result. You add: A focusable element inside Trigger. A <span> or an icon on its own never gets keyboard focus. Nothing to click inside the popup: use Headless Popover for that."],["Headless Definition tooltip","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/","The DefinitionTooltip parts give you the behaviour of the styled Definition tooltip with no styles: a term that is a real button, and a popup in the top layer beside it. A click, Enter or Space toggle it; focus opens it; blur, the pointer leaving and Esc close it. The definition is also the term's description, so screen readers get it without opening. You own the underline, the popup's look, the caret and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Definition tooltip","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Definition tooltip","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#use-it",""],["Headless Definition tooltip","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#anatomy",""],["Headless Definition tooltip","Open on hover","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#open-on-hover","By default the pointer only opens the definition with a press. openOnHover opens it when the pointer rests on the term too. However it opened, it closes closeDelay (100ms) after the pointer leaves the term and the popup, so the pointer can move onto the popup."],["Headless Definition tooltip","Placement and caret","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#placement-and-caret","placement takes bottom (the default), top, left, right, each with -start / -end. The popup flips when there is no room; data-side says where it went. gap is the space to the term (8px by default). With caret, the popup gets --_caret-start, where a caret --_caret-w wide (12px if unset) starts so it points at the term's centre. The styled one uses gap={6}, the caret's height."],["Headless Definition tooltip","Open state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#open-state","Hold the state with open and onOpenChange, or give defaultOpen. onOpenChange reports changes only. Use it, for example, to count which terms people look up."],["Headless Definition tooltip","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#style-it",""],["Headless Definition tooltip","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#parts",""],["Headless Definition tooltip","DefinitionTooltip.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#definitiontooltip-root","Renders no element of its own: it holds the open state, places the popup and closes it on Esc. Prop Type Default open boolean Shown (controlled) defaultOpen boolean false Shown at first (uncontrolled) onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After it opens or closes (changes only) openOnHover boolean false The pointer resting on the term opens it too placement Placement 'bottom' top, bottom, left, right, each with -start / -end gap number 8 Space between the term and the popup, in px caret boolean false Writes --_caret-start on the popup closeDelay number 100 Time after the pointer leaves before it closes, in ms DefinitionTooltip.useDefinitionTooltipContext() returns the Root's state (open, popupId …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Definition tooltip","DefinitionTooltip.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#definitiontooltip-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={0} (yours wins), aria-controls, aria-expanded, and aria-describedby pointing at the popup next to any you pass. A press with the main button, Enter or Space toggle the popup; focus opens it, blur closes it. It takes every button prop except type. Attribute When data-open The popup is showing"],["Headless Definition tooltip","DefinitionTooltip.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#definitiontooltip-popup","A <span role=\\"tooltip\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer (a <span>, as Carbon's, so the term can sit in a <p>). Its content stays rendered while closed, so the term's description is always there. It takes every span prop except popover, id and role. Attribute When data-open Showing data-side top, bottom, left or right: where it went With caret on Root, it also gets the CSS variable --_caret-start."],["Headless Definition tooltip","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-definition-tooltip/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key What it does Tab Focus reaching the term opens the definition; focus leaving closes it Enter, Space Open or close the definition Esc Closes the definition only (a surrounding dialog stays open) The parts set aria-expanded, aria-controls and aria-describedby on the term and role=\\"tooltip\\" on the popup. You add: A look that tells the term apart from a link, such as a dotted underline. Nothing to click inside the popup: focus leaving the term closes it. Use Headless Popover for that."],["Headless Popover","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/","The Popover parts give you the behaviour of the styled Popover and Toggletip with no styles: your own content in a popup in the top layer beside a trigger, flipped when it doesn't fit and placed again on scroll. The trigger gets aria-expanded and aria-controls. Esc on the trigger or in the popup and a press outside close it, and after Esc focus goes back to the trigger. You own the trigger's look, the content, the caret and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Popover","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Popover","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#use-it","The popup's content stays rendered while it is closed, so the checkboxes keep their state. Name the popup with aria-label: it is a role=\\"group\\"."],["Headless Popover","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#anatomy",""],["Headless Popover","A form inside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#a-form-inside","Close is a button that closes the popup and gives focus back to the trigger. From your own code inside the popup, dismiss('close') from Popover.usePopoverContext() does the same: use it after a submit."],["Headless Popover","Placement and caret","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#placement-and-caret","placement takes bottom (the default), top, left, right, each with -start / -end. The popup flips when there is no room, and data-side says where it went. gap is the space to the trigger (8px by default; the styled one uses 10 with a caret, 0 without). With caret, the popup gets --_caret-start, where a caret --_caret-w wide (12px if unset) starts so it points at the trigger's centre."],["Headless Popover","A trigger of your own","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#a-trigger-of-your-own","When the trigger is your own component, wrap it in Anchor instead of using Trigger. The popup sits beside the anchor's first element, and a press anywhere inside the anchor doesn't count as outside. Give your trigger triggerProps (aria-expanded, aria-controls) and toggle with setOpen from Popover.usePopoverContext(). onOpenChange tells you why it changed. Popover.PopoverChangeReason is 'trigger', 'escape', 'outside', 'focus-out' or 'close'."],["Headless Popover","Close it yourself","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#close-it-yourself","dismissible={false} turns off Esc and the press outside: only the trigger, Close or your own open close the popup. Use it when the user must answer, such as a \\"what's new\\" hint."],["Headless Popover","Toggletip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#toggletip","A toggletip is a popover behind an \\"i\\" button, closed as soon as focus moves away. closeOnFocusOut adds that rule: focus leaving both the trigger and the popup closes it (focus-out). Put the popup right after the trigger so the next Tab reaches its links. Name both the trigger and the popup."],["Headless Popover","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#style-it",""],["Headless Popover","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#parts",""],["Headless Popover","Popover.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#popover-root","Renders no element of its own: it holds the open state, places the popup and closes it on Esc and on a press outside. Prop Type Default open boolean Shown (controlled) defaultOpen boolean false Shown at first (uncontrolled) onOpenChange (open: boolean, reason: PopoverChangeReason) => void After it opens or closes (changes only), with why dismissible boolean true Esc on the trigger or in the popup, and a press outside both, close it closeOnFocusOut boolean false Focus moving out of the trigger and the popup closes it (toggletip) placement Placement 'bottom' top, bottom, left, right, each with -start / -end gap number 8 Space between the trigger and the popup, in px caret boolean false Writes --_caret-start on the popup Popover.usePopoverContext() returns the Root's state to any component inside it: open, popupId, triggerProps, setOpen(open, reason) and dismiss(reason) (closes, and gives focus back to the trigger when it was inside, except after a press outside)."],["Headless Popover","Popover.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#popover-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that toggles the popup (reason trigger), with aria-expanded and aria-controls. The popup sits beside it. It takes every button prop except type. Attribute When data-open The popup is open"],["Headless Popover","Popover.Anchor","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#popover-anchor","A <span> around a trigger of your own, used in place of Trigger. The popup sits beside its first element child; a press anywhere inside it is not outside; after Esc focus goes back to that child (or the first focusable element in it). Attribute When data-open The popup is open"],["Headless Popover","Popover.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#popover-popup","A <div role=\\"group\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer, with the id the trigger's aria-controls points to. Your role wins. Its content stays rendered while closed. It takes every div prop except popover and id. Attribute When data-open Open data-side top, bottom, left or right: where it went With caret on Root, it also gets the CSS variable --_caret-start."],["Headless Popover","Popover.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#popover-close","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that closes the popup (reason close) and gives focus back to the trigger. It takes every button prop except type, and has no data attributes."],["Headless Popover","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-popover/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key What it does Enter, Space On the trigger: open or close Tab Moves through the trigger and the content in page order; with closeOnFocusOut, leaving both closes it Esc With dismissible, from the trigger or the popup: closes the popup, unless something else handled the key first (it checks defaultPrevented), and gives focus back to the trigger The parts set aria-expanded and aria-controls on the trigger and role=\\"group\\" on the popup. Focus doesn't move into the popup when it opens. You add: A name for the popup (aria-label or aria-labelledby), and for an icon-only trigger. The popup right after the trigger in the DOM, so the next Tab reaches its content. For a task the user must finish before going on, a modal instead."],["Headless Menu","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/","The Menu parts give you the behaviour of the styled Menu with no styles, in the WAI-ARIA menu button pattern: a trigger that opens a role=\\"menu\\" popup in the top layer, focus moved to the first item (or the last), ↑ / ↓ that wrap past disabled items, Home / End, typing to jump, and Esc, Tab, a press outside or a picked item closing it with focus given back. Items can be actions, check boxes or radios, and open submenus. You own the trigger's look, every row, the check marks and chevrons, and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes; the highlighted item is the focused one, so style it with focus:."],["Headless Menu","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Menu","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#use-it","The popup is named by the trigger (aria-labelledby) unless you give it an aria-label. onClick on an item runs on a click and on Enter or Space, then every level of the menu closes."],["Headless Menu","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#anatomy",""],["Headless Menu","Placement and width","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#placement-and-width","The popup opens below the trigger, lined up with its start edge (placement=\\"bottom-start\\" on Popup). Any placement works, and it flips when there is no room; data-side says where it went. matchWidth makes it as wide as the trigger, as Carbon's menu button with bottom."],["Headless Menu","Check boxes and radio groups","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#check-boxes-and-radio-groups","CheckboxItem is an on / off item (menuitemcheckbox): checked and onCheckedChange, or defaultChecked. RadioGroup holds RadioItems (menuitemradio), exactly one checked: value and onValueChange, or defaultValue. Both get aria-checked and data-checked to draw a check mark on. Menu.useMenuItemContext() gives checked to a component inside the item. Group with a GroupLabel names a set of items. RadioGroup is a Group too. Every item closes the menu when picked; closeOnClick={false} keeps it open, handy for check boxes."],["Headless Menu","Submenus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#submenus","A SubmenuRoot inside the popup holds a SubmenuTrigger, an item that opens the submenu's own Popup (put inside it) beside it: on hover after delay (150ms, focus stays), a click, Enter, Space or → (← right-to-left). ← or Esc closes only that level. Picking an item in a submenu closes every level. label on an item is the text typing matches (as data-label); give it when the item holds more than its name, such as a chevron or a shortcut."],["Headless Menu","A combo button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#a-combo-button","A trigger can be any button: render hands you the trigger's props and the open state to put on your own element. anchor on Popup places the menu beside another element, here the whole pair of buttons, and matchWidth makes it as wide."],["Headless Menu","Open state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#open-state","Hold the state with open and onOpenChange, or give defaultOpen. onOpenChange reports changes only, with why: trigger-press, trigger-hover (a submenu), item-press, escape-key, list-navigation (← out of a submenu), focus-out or outside-press. initialFocus on Root forces which item takes focus on open (first, last or none); left out, ↑ on the trigger starts on the last item and everything else on the first."],["Headless Menu","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#style-it",""],["Headless Menu","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#parts",""],["Headless Menu","Menu.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-root","Renders no element of its own: it holds the open state. Prop Type Default open boolean Open (controlled) defaultOpen boolean false Open at first (uncontrolled) onOpenChange (open: boolean, reason: OpenChangeReason) => void After it opens or closes (changes only), with why initialFocus 'first' | 'last' | 'none' Which item takes focus on open; left out, the trigger decides (↑ the last, else the first) id string generated Base of the ids: <id>-trigger, <id>-menu Menu.useMenuContext() returns the nearest Root's or SubmenuRoot's state (open, popupId, setOpen …), for example to turn a chevron. Menu.ownItems(popup) lists a popup's own items (not those of its submenus)."],["Headless Menu","Menu.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-haspopup=\\"menu\\" (yours wins), aria-expanded and aria-controls, and the id <id>-trigger, which names the popup. A click toggles the menu; ↓ opens it on the first item, ↑ on the last. Prop Type Default render (props, { open }) => ReactElement Render your own element with the trigger's props instead of a <button> Attribute When data-popup-open The menu is open"],["Headless Menu","Menu.Popup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-popup","A <div role=\\"menu\\" tabindex=\\"-1\\" popover=\\"manual\\"> in the top layer, with the id <id>-menu, named by the trigger unless you give aria-label or aria-labelledby. Its items are always rendered (hidden while closed). Inside a SubmenuTrigger it is that item's submenu, placed beside it at the inline end. Prop Type Default anchor RefObject<Element | null> the trigger What the menu sits beside placement Placement 'bottom-start' Where it opens beside the anchor (not for a submenu) matchWidth boolean false As wide as the anchor (not for a submenu) Attribute When data-open Open data-side top, bottom, left or right: where it went"],["Headless Menu","Menu.Item, CheckboxItem, RadioItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-item-checkboxitem-radioitem","A <div tabindex=\\"-1\\"> with role=\\"menuitem\\", \\"menuitemcheckbox\\" or \\"menuitemradio\\". A click, Enter or Space activates it: a CheckboxItem flips, a RadioItem becomes its group's value, then onClick runs and the menu closes. A disabled item stays visible and announced (aria-disabled) but the keys skip it and activating it does nothing. Prop Type Default onClick (event) => void On a click and on Enter / Space, before the menu closes (not when disabled) label string the item's text What typing matches, as data-label disabled boolean false Skipped by the keys; does nothing closeOnClick boolean true Activating it closes every level checked boolean CheckboxItem: on (controlled) defaultChecked boolean false CheckboxItem: on at first onCheckedChange (checked: boolean) => void CheckboxItem: after it flips value string RadioItem: what it stands for in its group (required) Attribute When data-disabled Disabled data-checked A checked CheckboxItem or RadioItem Menu.useMenuItemContext() returns { checked } of the enclosing item."],["Headless Menu","Menu.RadioGroup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-radiogroup","A Group of RadioItems, exactly one checked. Prop Type Default value string The checked item's value (controlled) defaultValue string '' The starting value (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string) => void After another item was picked"],["Headless Menu","Menu.Group, GroupLabel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-group-grouplabel","Group is a <div role=\\"group\\"> named by its GroupLabel (a <div>) unless you give it aria-labelledby. They add no props and no data attributes."],["Headless Menu","Menu.Separator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-separator","An <hr> between items."],["Headless Menu","Menu.SubmenuRoot, SubmenuTrigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#menu-submenuroot-submenutrigger","SubmenuRoot holds a submenu's state and takes the same props as Root. SubmenuTrigger is a <div role=\\"menuitem\\" aria-haspopup=\\"menu\\"> with aria-expanded; the submenu's Popup goes inside it. Prop Type Default label string the item's text What typing matches, as data-label disabled boolean false The submenu doesn't open delay number 150 Hover time in ms before the submenu opens or closes Attribute When data-popup-open Its submenu is open data-disabled Disabled"],["Headless Menu","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-menu/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key On the trigger In the menu Enter, Space Open on the first item Activate the focused item (or open its submenu) ↓ Open on the first item Next item, wrapping; disabled items are skipped ↑ Open on the last item Previous item, wrapping Home / End First / last item Letters Next item whose label (or text) starts with them → (← right-to-left) Open the focused item's submenu ← (→ right-to-left) In a submenu: close it, focus back on its item Esc Close this level and give focus back Tab Close the menu and give focus back to the trigger The parts set role=\\"menu\\", the item roles, aria-haspopup, aria-expanded, aria-controls, aria-checked and aria-disabled, and move focus in and out. You add: A name for an icon-only trigger (aria-label). A visible highlight on the focused item (focus:), and a check mark for data-checked. For a danger item, the consequence in words (for example a visually hidden \\"This cannot be undone\\")."],["Headless Accordion","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/","The Accordion parts give you the behaviour of the styled Accordion with no styles: a list of items, each a button that shows or hides its content, with aria-expanded, aria-controls and a content region named by its button. Several items can be open at once, as in Carbon. You own the markup inside the parts (the chevron, a heading level around the button), the text and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Accordion","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Accordion","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#use-it",""],["Headless Accordion","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#anatomy",""],["Headless Accordion","Open from your code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#open-from-your-code","Each Item is on its own: defaultOpen opens it on the first render, or hold it yourself with open and onOpenChange. Controlled items let a pair of buttons open and close them all at once. onOpenChange fires only for the user's own clicks."],["Headless Accordion","A heading around each button","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#a-heading-around-each-button","The styled accordion's heading is a plain button. With the parts you choose the markup: put each Trigger inside an <h3> (or the level that fits your page) and screen reader users can jump between the items by heading, as the WAI-ARIA accordion pattern suggests. The chevron sits before the text here (the styled align=\\"start\\"): the order is your markup."],["Headless Accordion","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#disabled","disabled on an Item disables its trigger button: it can't be clicked and Tab skips it. disabled on Root disables every item. Both set data-disabled on the item and its trigger."],["Headless Accordion","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#style-it","A closed Panel has the hidden attribute, so it needs no style to hide."],["Headless Accordion","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#parts",""],["Headless Accordion","Accordion.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#accordion-root","A <ul>. Put it in a list reset of your own (list-style: none, no padding). Prop Type Default disabled boolean false Disables every item Attribute When data-disabled disabled is set Accordion.useAccordionContext() returns { disabled } to a component inside Root."],["Headless Accordion","Accordion.Item","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#accordion-item","An <li>: one item, holding its Trigger and Panel. Prop Type Default open boolean Open (controlled) defaultOpen boolean false Open on the first render (uncontrolled) onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void After the user opened or closed it disabled boolean false Disables its trigger Attribute When data-open It is open data-disabled It, or the whole Root, is disabled Accordion.useItemContext() returns { open, disabled, toggle, triggerId, panelId } to a component inside the item, for example to turn a chevron that sits outside the trigger."],["Headless Accordion","Accordion.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#accordion-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded and aria-controls (its panel's id). A click (and Enter or Space, the button's own) opens or closes the item. It takes every button prop except type and disabled; its id is set by the item. Attribute When data-open The item is open data-disabled The item is disabled"],["Headless Accordion","Accordion.Panel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#accordion-panel","A <section> named by its trigger (aria-labelledby), so a region landmark. It has the hidden attribute while the item is closed. It takes every section prop except hidden. Attribute When data-open The item is open"],["Headless Accordion","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-accordion/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves between the triggers (and into an open panel); disabled triggers are skipped Enter, Space Opens or closes the focused item There are no arrow keys between the triggers, as in Carbon. The parts set aria-expanded and aria-controls on each trigger, and aria-labelledby and hidden on each panel. The list is a <ul> of <li> items. You add: The trigger's text. A heading element around the trigger when the items are sections of your page outline. Nothing else: the chevron is decoration, so give it aria-hidden=\\"true\\"."],["Headless Progress indicator","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/","The ProgressIndicator parts give you the behaviour of the styled Progress indicator with no styles: an ordered list of steps whose state (complete, current, incomplete) follows the current index, aria-current=\\"step\\" on the current one, and, when it is interactive, buttons that jump to a step. You own the markup inside each step (the icon, the label, a second line), the words a screen reader hears for each state, and every style. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on."],["Headless Progress indicator","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Progress indicator","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#use-it","Each direct child of Root is one step, by its position: the first is index 0. useStepContext() gives a component inside a step its state, so the icon and the screen-reader words can follow it."],["Headless Progress indicator","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#anatomy",""],["Headless Progress indicator","Invalid, disabled and complete steps","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#invalid-disabled-and-complete-steps","Three flags on a Step add to the state from the index: complete marks the step done whatever the current index says (data-complete). invalid sets data-invalid: show a warning in your style. disabled disables the step's button (data-disabled); it can't be clicked or focused."],["Headless Progress indicator","Let the user jump between steps","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#let-the-user-jump-between-steps","interactive puts the buttons in the Tab order. A click on a step that is not current and not disabled makes it current and calls onChange with its index (data-clickable marks those steps). Hold the index with currentIndex, or give defaultCurrentIndex and let Root keep it."],["Headless Progress indicator","Back and Next buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#back-and-next-buttons","Without interactive the steps don't react to clicks and stay out of the Tab order: your own buttons move through the task by changing currentIndex."],["Headless Progress indicator","Vertical","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#vertical","vertical sets data-orientation=\\"vertical\\" on the root, every step and every button (horizontal otherwise). The layout is yours: here the line runs down the start edge."],["Headless Progress indicator","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#style-it",""],["Headless Progress indicator","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#parts",""],["Headless Progress indicator","ProgressIndicator.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#progressindicator-root","An <ol>. Each direct child is one step, by position, so a component of your own that renders a Step works as a child. Prop Type Default currentIndex number The current step's index, 0-based (controlled) defaultCurrentIndex number 0 The starting index (uncontrolled) onChange (index: number) => void After the user jumped to another step interactive boolean false The steps' buttons take Tab and jump on a click vertical boolean false Sets data-orientation=\\"vertical\\" Attribute When data-orientation horizontal or vertical ProgressIndicator.useProgressIndicatorContext() returns { currentIndex, vertical, interactive, pick }. ProgressIndicator.stepState(index, currentIndex, complete?) returns the state a step at index would have."],["Headless Progress indicator","ProgressIndicator.Step","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#progressindicator-step","An <li>: one step. Prop Type Default complete boolean false Complete whatever the current index says invalid boolean false Sets data-invalid disabled boolean false Its button is disabled Attribute When data-complete / data-current / data-incomplete One of them: the step's state data-invalid invalid is set data-disabled disabled is set data-clickable A click on its button jumps here: interactive, not disabled, not current data-orientation horizontal or vertical ProgressIndicator.useStepContext() returns { index, state, invalid, disabled, vertical, interactive, clickable, pick } to a component inside the step."],["Headless Progress indicator","ProgressIndicator.StepButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#progressindicator-stepbutton","A <button type=\\"button\\">. The current step's has aria-current=\\"step\\". It is out of the Tab order (tabindex=\\"-1\\") unless the root is interactive, and disabled (with aria-disabled) when the step is. It takes every button prop except type, and has the same data attributes as its Step."],["Headless Progress indicator","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-progress-indicator/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab With interactive: moves between the step buttons (disabled ones are skipped). Without it the buttons aren't Tab stops. Enter, Space With interactive: jumps to the focused step (nothing on the current one) The parts set aria-current=\\"step\\", disabled and aria-disabled, and the Tab order. The list is an <ol> of <li> steps. You add: The label text inside each StepButton. The state in words for screen readers (\\"Complete\\", \\"Invalid\\" …), as the sr-only text in the first example: an icon alone says nothing. A heading that names the task, and the current step in text if the steps are small."],["Headless UI shell","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/","Three namespaces give you the behaviour of the styled UI shell with no styles: Shell: Shell.Root holds whether the side nav is open, so the hamburger and the side nav wire themselves to each other; Shell.Content is the <main> that tells how the side nav beside it lays out. Header: the <header>, the skip link, the hamburger, menus of links that open and close, icon buttons and the panel under the header, with Esc, clicks outside and focus return. SideNav: the <nav> with its modes (default, rail, fixed, collapsible), the overlay, links and menus, with Esc and focus leaving. You own every element's look and position: the 48px bar, the 256px nav, the offsets of the content, the icons and the words. The parts show their state as data-* attributes for you to style on. The examples sit in a box whose transform keeps their position: fixed parts inside it, and their links only change the example's state, so a click doesn't leave this page. In your app the header and the nav are fixed to the window."],["Headless UI shell","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless UI shell","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#use-it","Inside Shell.Root the MenuButton opens and closes the side nav with no props, and gets aria-expanded and aria-controls. The nav is open beside the content from Carbon's lg breakpoint, 1056px (data-open); below it, the hamburger opens it over the page with the overlay."],["Headless UI shell","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#anatomy","The product name link, the menu bar's <nav> and the group around the global actions have no behaviour: they are your own elements."],["Headless UI shell","Header menus","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menus","Header.Menu is an <li> holding a MenuTrigger button and a MenuPopup list of MenuItem links: a disclosure, not an ARIA menu. Click, Enter or Space toggle it; Esc closes it and focuses the trigger; a press outside or focus leaving closes it; following one of its links closes it and focuses the trigger. A closed menu has data-current when one of its items is current. current on a Menu shows the mark even while it is open (Carbon's isActive). The menu finds a current item by reading the props of the elements written inside it, so set current on the MenuItem itself, not on a wrapper component under another name."],["Headless UI shell","Global actions and a panel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#global-actions-and-a-panel","Header.GlobalAction is an icon button of two kinds: with active it is a toggle (aria-pressed); with expanded it is a disclosure (aria-expanded) for a panel. Header.Panel is controlled: it asks to close with onClose(reason) on Esc (focus goes back to what opened it), when focus leaves it, or on a press outside, but not on the action whose aria-controls is the panel's id, which toggles it. PanelContent is a <section>: named with aria-label, it is a region landmark. It has hidden while the panel is closed."],["Headless UI shell","Side nav modes","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#side-nav-modes","SideNav.Root takes the mode; Nav writes it in data-ui-side-nav, and Shell.Content copies it to its data-side-nav so you can offset the page: default: over the page below lg, beside it from lg (data-open from 1056px). rail: a strip of icons that is data-open while the pointer is on it or focus is inside (data-expanded too). fixed: always data-open, never an overlay. collapsible: closed at every width until the hamburger opens it over the page. Pick a mode, then point at the nav, use the hamburger and press Esc. Left without sideNav, Content looks for the first [data-ui-side-nav] in the document (and in its own shadow root) after each render. One shell per page, as in an app, needs no prop; this page holds several, so the examples after the first say it."],["Headless UI shell","Without Shell.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#without-shell-root","Leave out Shell.Root to hold the state yourself: active and onToggle on the MenuButton, expanded and onToggle on SideNav.Root. The side nav's onToggle asks to close on Esc, a click on the overlay, or focus leaving it while it is over the page; nothing changes until you pass the new state back."],["Headless UI shell","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#style-it",""],["Headless UI shell","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#parts",""],["Headless UI shell","Shell.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#shell-root","Renders no element: only its children. It holds the side nav's expanded state for a Header.MenuButton and a SideNav.Root inside it. Prop Type Default sideNavExpanded boolean The side nav is open (controlled) defaultSideNavExpanded boolean false Open on the first render (uncontrolled) onSideNavExpandedChange (expanded: boolean) => void The hamburger, Esc, the overlay or focus leaving asked for this state Shell.useShellContext() returns { sideNavExpanded, setSideNavExpanded, sideNavId }, or null outside a Shell.Root."],["Headless UI shell","Shell.Content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#shell-content","A <main> with the id main-content (the skip link's default target). Prop Type Default sideNav 'default' | 'rail' | 'fixed' | 'collapsible' | 'none' found on the page How the side nav beside it lays out id string 'main-content' The skip link's target Attribute When data-side-nav The mode: sideNav, else the first [data-ui-side-nav] in the document (or its shadow root), else none"],["Headless UI shell","Header.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-root","A <header>, the banner landmark: name it with aria-label. It sets data-ui-header, which a toaster uses to start below the header. No props of its own."],["Headless UI shell","Header.SkipToContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-skiptocontent","An <a> to the content; hide it until it has focus. Inside a shadow root (a micro app) a click moves focus to the target itself, which the browser can't find there. Prop Type Default href string '#main-content' The content's id as a fragment"],["Headless UI shell","Header.MenuButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menubutton","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded and aria-controls (the Shell.Root's side nav id unless you pass your own). Name it with aria-label, by its state if you like (\\"Open menu\\" / \\"Close menu\\"). Prop Type Default active boolean the shell's state, else false The side nav it controls is open onToggle (active: boolean) => void The user asked for the other state Attribute When data-active The side nav is open"],["Headless UI shell","Header.Menu","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menu","An <li> holding a MenuTrigger and a MenuPopup. Prop Type Default open boolean Open (controlled) defaultOpen boolean false Open on the first render onOpenChange (open: boolean) => void The user opened or closed it current boolean false Show the current-section mark even while open (Carbon isActive) Attribute When data-open It is open data-current current, or closed with a current item inside Header.useMenuContext() returns the menu's state; Header.useOptionalMenuContext() returns it or null in the menu bar."],["Headless UI shell","Header.MenuTrigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menutrigger","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded, aria-controls (its popup) and tabindex=\\"0\\" (so Safari focuses it on click and Tab reaches it). It has the same data-open and data-current as its menu."],["Headless UI shell","Header.MenuPopup","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menupopup","A <ul> with the menu's id: name it with aria-label (the trigger's text) and hide it while data-open is absent. Attribute When data-open The menu is open"],["Headless UI shell","Header.MenuItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-menuitem","An <a> of the menu bar or of a menu. Following it inside a menu closes the menu and focuses its trigger. It keeps target and rel. Prop Type Default current boolean false The current page (aria-current=\\"page\\") Attribute When data-current current is set"],["Headless UI shell","Header.GlobalAction","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-globalaction","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabindex=\\"0\\". Name it with aria-label (or a tooltip that labels it). Prop Type Default active boolean false Pressed: a toggle (aria-pressed) expanded boolean Its panel is open: a disclosure (aria-expanded); pair it with aria-controls = the panel's id Attribute When data-active Pressed, or its panel is open"],["Headless UI shell","Header.Panel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-panel","A <div>: the panel under the header. Give it the id its action's aria-controls names. Prop Type Default expanded boolean Open (required, controlled) onClose (reason: 'escape' | 'blur' | 'outside') => void Asks to close: Esc (focus goes back to what opened it), focus leaving, a press outside (not on its action) Attribute When data-open It is open"],["Headless UI shell","Header.PanelContent","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#header-panelcontent","A <section> inside the panel, hidden while it is closed. Name it (aria-label) to make it a region landmark. Attribute When data-open The panel is open"],["Headless UI shell","SideNav.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#sidenav-root","Renders no element: only its children. It holds the expanded, hover and breakpoint state. Prop Type Default expanded boolean the shell's state, else false Open (controlled) onToggle (expanded: boolean) => void Esc, the overlay or focus leaving asked for this state rail boolean false A strip of icons that opens on hover / focus fixed boolean false Always open beside the page collapsible boolean false Closed at every width until opened over the page SideNav.useSideNavContext() returns { expanded, hoverOpen, open, hidden, mode, rail, fixed, collapsible, large, … }."],["Headless UI shell","SideNav.Overlay","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#sidenav-overlay","A <div aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> that covers the page while the nav is expanded; a click on it asks to close. Show it below lg only. Attribute When data-open The nav is expanded and not fixed"],["Headless UI shell","SideNav.Nav","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#sidenav-nav","A <nav tabindex=\\"-1\\">: name it with aria-label. Its id is the shell's side nav id unless you pass one. Hover and focus open a rail; Esc asks to close and gives focus back to what opened it; over the page (below lg, or collapsible), focus leaving it asks to close. While neither shown nor a rail it is inert. Attribute When data-ui-side-nav The mode: default, rail, fixed or collapsible data-open Shown at full width: expanded, a hovered rail, fixed, or the default nav from lg data-expanded Asked open, or a rail under the pointer or holding focus data-collapsed Hidden and inert"],["Headless UI shell","SideNav.Link","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#sidenav-link","An <a>, out of the Tab order while the nav is hidden. It keeps target and rel. Prop Type Default current boolean false The current page (aria-current=\\"page\\") Attribute When data-current current is set"],["Headless UI shell","SideNav.Menu, MenuTrigger, MenuPopup, MenuItem","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#sidenav-menu-menutrigger-menupopup-menuitem","Menu is an <li>; MenuTrigger a <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded and aria-controls; MenuPopup a <ul> to hide while data-open is absent; MenuItem an <a> with current (aria-current=\\"page\\", data-current). Prop of Menu Type Default expanded boolean Open (controlled) defaultExpanded boolean false Open on the first render onExpandedChange (expanded: boolean) => void The user opened or closed it Attribute On When data-open Menu, MenuTrigger, MenuPopup The menu is open data-current Menu, MenuTrigger One of its items is current (open or closed) SideNav.useMenuContext() returns { expanded, current, menuId, toggle }."],["Headless UI shell","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-ui-shell/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Where Does Enter, Space MenuButton Opens or closes the side nav Enter, Space Header.MenuTrigger Opens or closes the menu Esc Open header menu Closes it, focus back on its trigger Esc Open panel Asks to close ('escape'), focus back on what opened it Esc Open side nav Asks to close, focus back on what opened it Tab Out of a header menu, a panel, or a side nav over the page Closes it (asks to) Enter, Space SideNav.MenuTrigger Opens or closes the menu The parts set aria-expanded, aria-controls, aria-pressed, aria-current=\\"page\\", inert on a hidden nav and tabindex=\\"-1\\" on its links, and aria-hidden on the overlay. You add: The names: aria-label on Header.Root, the menu bar's <nav>, SideNav.Nav, MenuButton, each GlobalAction and MenuPopup. The skip link's text and a style that shows it on focus. The icons, with aria-hidden=\\"true\\"."],["Headless Modal","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/","The Modal parts give you the behaviour of the styled Modal with no styles: a native <dialog> opened with showModal() (the top layer, an inert page behind, Tab kept inside, focus back to the opener on close), Esc and a click outside that ask to close, Carbon's first focus, a body that becomes a focusable region when it overflows, and a page that doesn't scroll while it is open. You own the markup, the heading text, the buttons and every style. Root is controlled: it reports why it wants to close, and closes only when you set open to false."],["Headless Modal","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Modal","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#use-it","onClose(reason) gets 'close-button', 'escape', 'backdrop' or 'api' (a <form method=\\"dialog\\"> inside closed the dialog). The preflight of most CSS resets removes the dialog's margin: auto, so put it back (m-auto) to centre it."],["Headless Modal","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#anatomy",""],["Headless Modal","Confirm before you delete","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#confirm-before-you-delete","alert gives the dialog role=\\"alertdialog\\" and makes Body its description. Focus then starts on the least destructive action in Footer: the first one whose data-kind is neither primary nor a danger kind. Put data-kind on every footer button. There is no Close here, so Esc is the keyboard's way out."],["Headless Modal","A form, and a click outside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#a-form-and-a-click-outside","On open, focus goes to an autoFocus control, else the first control in Body, else the first in Footer, else Close. A click on the backdrop asks to close ('backdrop') by default; Carbon allows that only for a passive modal, so pass closeOnOutsideClick={false} when there are footer actions. A <form method=\\"dialog\\"> closes the dialog when it is submitted, after the browser has checked the required fields; onClose then gets 'api'."],["Headless Modal","Long content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#long-content","When Body is taller than the room it has, it gets tabIndex={0} and data-scrollable, and the Title names it, so keyboard users can scroll it. Give the dialog a maximum height and let Body scroll. Body watches its first child for size changes, so wrap the content in one element, as here."],["Headless Modal","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#ask-before-closing","onClose only reports. To keep the modal open, don't set open to false: here a first attempt with unsaved text shows a warning, and a second one closes."],["Headless Modal","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#style-it","ui-modal-motion (React + Tailwind theme) gives it Carbon's motion: the box drops 24px in while it and the overlay fade, and fades back out after closing. A closing dialog stays on screen while it fades, so put the layout (flex-col) on the dialog itself and only display under data-open."],["Headless Modal","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#parts",""],["Headless Modal","Modal.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#modal-root","A <dialog>, opened with showModal() while open is true. It takes every dialog prop except open, onClose and role. While open, the page (<html>) doesn't scroll. Prop Type Default open boolean Shows the modal (required) onClose (reason: Modal.ModalCloseReason) => void Esc, Close, a click outside or a <form method=\\"dialog\\"> asked to close: 'escape', 'close-button', 'backdrop', 'api' alert boolean false role=\\"alertdialog\\"; Body describes it; focus starts on the least destructive footer action closeOnOutsideClick boolean true A press and release on the backdrop asks to close ('backdrop') Its aria-labelledby is the Title's id, and with alert its aria-describedby is the Body's, unless you pass your own. Attribute When data-open open is true"],["Headless Modal","Modal.Title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#modal-title","An <h2> with an id (yours or <id>-title) that names the dialog."],["Headless Modal","Modal.Body","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#modal-body","A <section> for the content. While it overflows, it gets tabIndex={0} and an aria-labelledby pointing at the Title, so it is a named region the keyboard can scroll. First focus looks for a control in it first. Attribute When data-scrollable The content is taller than the body"],["Headless Modal","Modal.Footer","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#modal-footer","A <footer> for the action buttons. First focus looks here after Body; with alert, it reads the data-kind of its buttons (primary, secondary, danger, …) to start on the least destructive one."],["Headless Modal","Modal.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#modal-close","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that asks to close ('close-button'). It is a Tab stop even in Safari (tabIndex={0}). Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Modal","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-modal/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the controls inside the dialog only (the native modal dialog) Esc Calls onClose('escape'); the dialog stays open until you set open to false The native modal dialog makes the rest of the page inert and gives focus back to the element that had it when the dialog closes. The parts add the name from Title, alertdialog and its description, and the focusable scrolling Body. You add: A Title, or an aria-label on Root when there is no visible heading. An aria-label on Close. data-kind on the footer buttons of an alert modal."],["Headless Side panel","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/","The SidePanel parts give you the behaviour of the styled Side panel with no styles: a panel that slides in from the right or the left and slides out again before it unmounts, Tab kept inside it, Esc and a click on the overlay that ask to close, first focus inside and focus back on close, and a \\"slide-in\\" mode that pushes the page aside instead of covering it. You own the markup, the heading, the buttons, where the panel sits and every style. Root is controlled: it reports why it wants to close, and closes only when you set open to false. The panel is yours to position: fixed under your app's header, or absolute inside a box, as in these examples."],["Headless Side panel","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Side panel","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#use-it","onRequestClose(reason) gets 'close-button', 'escape' or 'overlay'. On open, focus goes to selectorInitialFocus (a selector inside the panel), else to the panel's first control; on close it goes back to what had it. Name the panel with aria-label or aria-labelledby."],["Headless Side panel","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#anatomy",""],["Headless Side panel","From the left","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#from-the-left","placement=\\"left\\" makes the panel slide in from the left; Panel gets data-placement=\\"left\\" for you to place it. Without an Overlay the page stays clickable beside the panel, but Tab still stays inside it."],["Headless Side panel","Push the page aside","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#push-the-page-aside","slideIn gives the element that selectorPageContent points to a margin as wide as the panel, with a transition, instead of covering it. A slide-in panel takes no focus, doesn't keep Tab inside and ignores Esc, so the page stays usable beside it."],["Headless Side panel","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#ask-before-closing","onRequestClose only reports: the panel closes when you set open to false. closeOnOverlayClick={false} stops a click on the overlay from asking at all. This panel only closes with its Done button and shows what asked."],["Headless Side panel","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#style-it","The panel slides 320px and fades with the Web Animations API (150ms in and out, as Carbon); there is nothing to animate in CSS. data-closing marks the panel and the overlay while they slide out, for example to stop clicks on them."],["Headless Side panel","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#parts",""],["Headless Side panel","SidePanel.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#sidepanel-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, while the panel is open and while it slides out. Prop Type Default open boolean Shows the panel (required) onRequestClose (reason: SidePanel.SidePanelCloseReason) => void Esc, Close or a click on the Overlay asked to close: 'escape', 'close-button', 'overlay' placement 'right' | 'left' 'right' The side it slides in from slideIn boolean false Push the page aside instead of covering it: no focus trap, no Esc, no first focus closeOnOverlayClick boolean true A click on the Overlay asks to close selectorInitialFocus string What takes focus on open (a selector inside the panel), else the first control selectorPageContent string The page element a slideIn panel pushes aside layerClassName string Class of the <dialog> the panel goes into when it opens from a modal (over it, in the top layer); give its ::backdrop no colour (backdrop:bg-transparent) A slide-over panel joins the page's overlay stack with the modals and tearsheets: one Esc closes only the topmost (a modal opened from the panel closes first, and focus goes back into the panel), and a panel opened from a modal goes over it so it can be used. SidePanel.useSidePanelContext() returns the Root's state (open, closing, placement, slideIn, requestClose …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Side panel","SidePanel.Panel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#sidepanel-panel","An <aside> (a complementary landmark): what slides, and where Tab stays unless slideIn. Name it with aria-label or aria-labelledby. Attribute When data-open open is true data-closing It is sliding out data-placement right or left"],["Headless Side panel","SidePanel.Overlay","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#sidepanel-overlay","A <div aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> that dims the page: while it is open, the page doesn't scroll (the one scroll lock the overlays share, on <html>: it lets go when the last overlay closes), and a click on it asks to close ('overlay', unless closeOnOverlayClick is false). Leave it out for a panel that doesn't dim the page. Attribute When data-open open is true data-closing It is fading out"],["Headless Side panel","SidePanel.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#sidepanel-close","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that asks to close ('close-button'). Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Side panel","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-side-panel/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the panel's controls and wraps around inside it (not with slideIn) Esc Calls onRequestClose('escape') (not with slideIn) The parts move focus into the panel on open and back on close, and keep Tab inside a slide-over panel. The page behind is not made inert: screen reader users can still reach it. You add: The panel's name (aria-label, or aria-labelledby pointing at your heading). An aria-label on Close, and on any back button you add for steps. The panel's position and size, and a top offset under your header."],["Headless Tearsheet","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/","The Tearsheet parts give you the behaviour of the styled Tearsheet with no styles: a native <dialog> opened with showModal() (the top layer, an inert page behind) whose sheet rises from below on open and sinks back before it unmounts, Tab kept inside the sheet, Esc, the close button and a click outside the sheet that ask to close, first focus and focus back, a page that doesn't scroll, and Carbon's stacking of tearsheets opened over each other. You own the markup, the header, the action buttons and every style. Root is controlled: it reports why it wants to close, and closes only when you set open to false."],["Headless Tearsheet","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Tearsheet","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#use-it","onRequestClose(reason) gets 'close-button', 'escape' or 'outside'. First focus goes to selectorInitialFocus, else Close, else the sheet's first control; on close it goes back to what had it. Dialog fills the screen and Sheet is the visible part: what rises, where Tab stays, and what a click counts as outside of."],["Headless Tearsheet","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#anatomy",""],["Headless Tearsheet","Stacked tearsheets","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#stacked-tearsheets","A tearsheet opened over another one stacks on it. While more than one is open, data-stack on Dialog and Sheet says where each sits: 1-of-2, 2-of-2, 1-of-3 … up to three deep. Scale the ones underneath back and dim the page less, as Carbon does."],["Headless Tearsheet","Ask before closing","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#ask-before-closing","onRequestClose only reports: the tearsheet closes when you set open to false. closeOnOutsideClick={false} stops a click outside the sheet from asking at all, which suits a form people type into. Type a memo, then press Esc."],["Headless Tearsheet","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#style-it","The sheet rises with the Web Animations API (240ms) and sinks back on close; the backdrop fades with it. There is nothing to animate in CSS. Style the stack with data-stack."],["Headless Tearsheet","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#parts",""],["Headless Tearsheet","Tearsheet.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#tearsheet-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, while the tearsheet is open and while it sinks back. Prop Type Default open boolean Shows the tearsheet (required) onRequestClose (reason: Tearsheet.TearsheetCloseReason) => void Esc, Close or a click outside the sheet asked to close: 'escape', 'close-button', 'outside' closeOnOutsideClick boolean true A press and release outside the Sheet asks to close selectorInitialFocus string What takes focus on open (a selector inside the dialog), else Close, else the sheet's first control Tearsheet.useTearsheetContext() returns the Root's state (open, closing, stackPlace, requestClose …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Tearsheet","Tearsheet.Dialog","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#tearsheet-dialog","A <dialog>, opened with showModal(): style it to fill the screen, with the dim on its ::backdrop. It takes every dialog prop except open and onClose. Its aria-labelledby is the Title's id unless you pass your own. While a tearsheet is open, the page (<html>) doesn't scroll. Attribute When data-open open is true data-closing It is sinking back data-stack 1-of-2, 2-of-2, 1-of-3, 2-of-3 or 3-of-3 while more than one is open"],["Headless Tearsheet","Tearsheet.Sheet","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#tearsheet-sheet","A <div>: the visible sheet. It rises and sinks, Tab stays inside it, and a click outside it asks to close. Attribute When data-open open is true data-closing It is sinking back data-stack As on Dialog"],["Headless Tearsheet","Tearsheet.Title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#tearsheet-title","An <h2> with an id (yours or <id>-title) that names the dialog."],["Headless Tearsheet","Tearsheet.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#tearsheet-close","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that asks to close ('close-button'). It takes first focus unless selectorInitialFocus says otherwise. Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Tearsheet","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tearsheet/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab Moves through the sheet's controls and wraps around inside it Esc Calls onRequestClose('escape'); the tearsheet stays open until you set open to false The native modal dialog makes the rest of the page inert. The parts name it from Title, keep Tab inside the sheet, and move focus in on open and back on close. You add: A Title, or an aria-label on Dialog. An aria-label on Close. The action buttons, header actions, tabs and any side pane: they are plain markup inside Sheet."],["Headless Notification","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/","The Notification parts give you the behaviour of the styled Notification with no styles: the right role (status, none for a callout, alertdialog with an action), focus moved to the action of an actionable one and Tab kept going round it, Esc that closes it while focus is inside, a timeout that pauses while it is hovered or holds focus, and focus sent back when it closes itself. You own the markup, the icon, the text and every style. Root renders nothing while the notification is closed."],["Headless Notification","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Notification","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#use-it","Without open, Root hides the notification itself when it closes. Box carries the role: status here, so screen readers read changes politely."],["Headless Notification","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#anatomy",""],["Headless Notification","With an action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#with-an-action","actionable (with an Action inside) makes the Box an alertdialog, named by Title and described by Subtitle. When it appears, focus moves to Action (autoFocus={false} keeps it where it is); Tab and Shift+Tab go round its controls; Esc closes it while focus is inside it (closeOnEscape={false} turns that off). When it closes through Close, Esc, the timeout or requestClose with focus inside, focus goes back to where it was; setting open to false yourself doesn't move focus (nor does Carbon). Action doesn't close the notification: in its onClick, call requestClose from Notification.useNotificationContext(), which closes it the way Close does and sends focus back."],["Headless Notification","Callout","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#callout","variant=\\"callout\\" gives the Box no role: it is guidance that belongs to the page. Its Action is described by the Title. Leave out Close and actionable: a callout stays."],["Headless Notification","Close after a time","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#close-after-a-time","timeout closes it after that many milliseconds ('timeout'). The countdown pauses while the pointer is over the Box or focus is inside it, and an actionable one never closes by itself. Hover the card to hold it. Each time it shows again, the countdown starts afresh."],["Headless Notification","Keep it open","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#keep-it-open","onClose(reason) runs for Close, Esc and the timeout ('close-button', 'escape', 'timeout'). Return false to keep the notification open; with open, it closes only when you set open to false."],["Headless Notification","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#style-it","The parts set no data-* attributes: the kind and the look are yours. Put the kind on the Box yourself, as data-kind here, and style on it."],["Headless Notification","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#parts",""],["Headless Notification","Notification.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#notification-root","Renders no element of its own: its children, while the notification is open. It holds the open state, moves focus, listens for Esc and runs the timeout. Prop Type Default open boolean Controlled visibility; without it the notification hides itself when it closes onClose (reason: Notification.NotificationCloseReason) => boolean | void Close, Esc or the timeout: 'close-button', 'escape', 'timeout'. Return false to keep it open variant 'inline' | 'toast' | 'callout' 'inline' A callout has no role role 'status' | 'alert' | 'log' | 'alertdialog' | 'none' The Box's role, in place of the one picked for you actionable boolean false It has an Action: an alertdialog that never closes by itself timeout number 0 Milliseconds before it closes itself; 0 = never closeOnEscape boolean true Esc closes an alertdialog one while focus is inside it autoFocus boolean true An alertdialog one moves focus to its Action when it appears Notification.useNotificationContext() returns the Root's state (open, variant, role, requestClose …) to any component inside it."],["Headless Notification","Notification.Box","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#notification-box","A <div> with the role: status by default, none for a callout, alertdialog when actionable, or the role you set (none gives no role). An alertdialog one is named by Title, described by Subtitle, and keeps Tab going round its links and buttons. The timeout pauses while it is hovered or holds focus."],["Headless Notification","Notification.Title, Notification.Subtitle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#notification-title-notification-subtitle","<span>s with ids (yours or <id>-title, <id>-subtitle). Title names an alertdialog one and describes a callout's Action; Subtitle describes an alertdialog one."],["Headless Notification","Notification.Action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#notification-action","A <button type=\\"button\\">: the first focus of an alertdialog one, and a Tab stop even in Safari (tabIndex={0}). In a callout, the Title describes it. It doesn't close the notification."],["Headless Notification","Notification.Close","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#notification-close","A <button type=\\"button\\"> that asks to close ('close-button'). Give it an aria-label."],["Headless Notification","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-notification/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab / Shift+Tab In an alertdialog one, goes round its links and buttons; otherwise the page's normal order Esc Closes an alertdialog one while focus is inside it (closeOnEscape) The parts set the role and, for an alertdialog, aria-labelledby and aria-describedby. You add: The status icon with a name (role=\\"img\\" and aria-label, such as \\"error icon\\"), or text that says the kind. An aria-label on Close. A live region that exists before the message, for messages that must be announced: render the Root in the page and change its text, or use the Toast region."],["Headless Toast","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/","The Toaster parts give you the behaviour of the styled Toast region with no styles: a queue of toasts (at most max, a new one closes the oldest, the same id replaces an open one), one polite live region that is in the page before any toast so each one is announced, placed in the top layer from the start and lifted above a modal dialog when a toast arrives while one is open. You own the markup of each toast (usually the Notification parts), where the region sits and every style."],["Headless Toast","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Toast","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#use-it","Each toast is a Notification with role=\\"none\\", because the region announces it; remove it from the queue in its onClose. Root is a popover, so it sits in the top layer: place it with fixed and reset the popover's inset, margin and background, as here."],["Headless Toast","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#anatomy",""],["Headless Toast","Kinds and how long they stay","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#kinds-and-how-long-they-stay","Toaster.toastTimeout(kind, timeout?) is the rule the styled toaster uses: the timeout you give, else 5 seconds for info and success and 0 (stays until closed) for error and warning."],["Headless Toast","Replace, and how many at once","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#replace-and-how-many-at-once","queue.add(data, id) replaces an open toast with the same id instead of stacking another: \\"Syncing…\\", then \\"Synced\\". queue.max (3 by default) is how many show at once; a new toast drops the oldest. queue.remove(key) and queue.clear() take toasts away. queue.add returns the toast's key. A new key each time also gives the Notification a fresh start, so a replaced toast's timeout starts again."],["Headless Toast","With an action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#with-an-action","Leave out role=\\"none\\" and pass actionable for a toast with an action: it keeps its alertdialog role, takes focus, keeps Tab inside and never closes by itself. Use it only when the action is worth that interruption."],["Headless Toast","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#style-it","Where the region sits is your CSS: the top end corner under the header (newest at the top, flex-col-reverse), or the bottom end corner (newest at the bottom). Toaster.ToasterPlacement ('top-end' | 'bottom-end') is the type the styled toaster uses for it."],["Headless Toast","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#parts",""],["Headless Toast","Toaster.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#toaster-root","A <section popover=\\"manual\\" aria-live=\\"polite\\" aria-relevant=\\"additions\\">, shown in the top layer as soon as it mounts. It takes every section prop except popover. When a toast is added while a modal dialog is open, it shows itself again so it is drawn above the modal. Prop Type Default queue Toaster.ToastQueue<T> The toasts this region shows (required); render them as its children Give it an aria-label, such as \\"Notifications\\"."],["Headless Toast","Toaster.ToastQueue","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#toaster-toastqueue","A class: new Toaster.ToastQueue<T>() holds the open toasts, oldest first. Member add(data, id?) Adds a toast and returns its key; replaces an open one with the same id; drops the oldest beyond max remove(key) Removes one toast clear() Removes every toast max How many toasts at once (default 3) toasts The open toasts: { key, id?, data }[] subscribe(listener) Calls listener on every change; returns the unsubscribe function"],["Headless Toast","Toaster.useToasts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#toaster-usetoasts","Toaster.useToasts(queue) returns the queue's toasts and re-renders when they change."],["Headless Toast","Toaster.toastTimeout","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#toaster-toasttimeout","Toaster.toastTimeout(kind, timeout?) returns timeout when given, else 5000 for info and success, 0 for error, warning and warning-alt."],["Headless Toast","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-toast/#keyboard-and-accessibility","The region announces each toast politely. The toasts have no role of their own (role=\\"none\\"), except an actionable one, which is an alertdialog that takes focus and keeps Tab inside until it closes. The keys inside a toast are the Notification's. You add: An aria-label on Root. role=\\"none\\" on toasts without an action. Feedback inside a modal as an inline notification: the page outside a modal dialog is inert, so a toast drawn above it can't be clicked or read by screen readers."],["Headless Data table","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/","DataTable is the behaviour of the styled Data table without a single class, in the style of TanStack Table: the useDataTable(options) hook holds the state — sort, search, pages, selection, open rows, hidden columns, column widths and the editable grid — and hands back the rows to show, actions and prop getters. You write the <table>; the parts add the keyboard, focus and ARIA rules where they are needed. You own the markup: every cell, the header, the toolbar, the icons, the empty state and every style. State shows as data-* attributes on the parts."],["Headless Data table","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Data table","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#use-it",""],["Headless Data table","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#anatomy","Use only the parts you need: a read-only table is Root, Table, Body, Row and Cell, or even plain <tr> and <td> around table.pageRows."],["Headless Data table","Search and pages","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#search-and-pages","table.setFilterText(text) filters the rows (any cell shown contains the text, case-insensitive) and goes back to page 1. With pageSize (or defaultPageSize), table.pageRows is one page; drive it with the headless Pagination or your own buttons through table.setPagination. filterRows(row, text, headers) replaces the test, and manualFiltering keeps every row while you filter on the server. filterText / onFilterChange and page / onPageChange make both controlled."],["Headless Data table","Expandable rows","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#expandable-rows","With expandable, each row's ExpandToggle opens it; render an ExpandedRow under every open row (table.isExpanded(id)). ExpandAll opens every row shown, or closes them all once all are open. The toggles get aria-expanded and aria-controls pointing at the open row. Return the rows as one flat list (as here with flatMap), so opening a row doesn't remount it."],["Headless Data table","Pick one row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#pick-one-row","With radio, SelectRow is a radio: the radios are one Tab stop (the chosen row, else the first enabled one), and the arrow keys move to the next enabled row and select it, wrapping. SelectAll renders nothing. A row with disabled: true can't be chosen."],["Headless Data table","Show and hide columns","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#show-and-hide-columns","table.columns is the columns shown; table.headers is all of them. toggleColumn(key, show) shows or hides one, isColumnLocked(key) says it can't be hidden (hideable: false, or the last one shown), and resetColumns() goes back to the headers' hidden. columnsChanged says the choice differs from that. Hidden columns leave the search too. hiddenColumns / onColumnsChange make the choice controlled, so you can save it."],["Headless Data table","Edit cells in place","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#edit-cells-in-place","A column with editable: 'text' | 'number' | 'select' makes the table an APG grid: Table gets role=\\"grid\\", one body cell is the Tab stop, and the arrow keys, Home / End and Ctrl + Home / End move it. Enter, F2, a double click, a click on a data-edit-icon element or typing opens the editor. Render CellInput or CellSelect while the cell is edited (useCellContext().editing), and CellError for validate's message. onCellEdit hands you the new rows. In the editor, Enter saves, Escape cancels, Tab / Shift + Tab save and edit the next / previous editable cell, and leaving the cell saves. Controls inside cells (links, buttons) leave the Tab order in a grid; Enter or Space on their cell presses them."],["Headless Data table","Resize columns","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#resize-columns","resizable (or a column's resizable) gives ResizeHandle something to do: a native range input on the header's edge — drag it, or arrows 2px, Shift / Page Up / Down 16px, Home / End narrowest / widest. The first resize freezes the automatic layout into fixed widths (table.resize.fixed); Filler then takes the rest of the row. Attach table.boxRef to the scroll box, so the widest a column gets is the box's width. columnWidths / onColumnResize make the widths controlled, so you can save and restore them. Columns take width, minWidth (default 50) and maxWidth."],["Headless Data table","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#style-it","Draw the checkboxes yourself from data-checked and data-indeterminate, turn the sort arrow from data-direction, and shade selected and striped rows."],["Headless Data table","The hook","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#the-hook",""],["Headless Data table","DataTable.useDataTable(options)","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-usedatatable-options","Holds the state. Every piece of state can be controlled (sortKey, selectedIds …) or left to the hook (default…). Option Type Default headers DataTableColumn[] The columns: { key, header } plus the column options below (required) rows R[] The rows: { id, …cells }, disabled to block selection (required) id string generated Base of the ids the parts give their elements sortable boolean false Every column sorts unless its header sets sortable: false sortKey, sortDirection string, SortDirection The sort (controlled) defaultSortKey, defaultSortDirection string, SortDirection '', 'none' The starting sort onSortChange (sort: { key, direction }) => void After a sort button was pressed manualSorting boolean false Keep rows in your order (sort on the server); the headers still show the sort sortRow (a, b, context) => number Replaces the comparison locale string 'en' Orders the sort selectable boolean false Checkboxes with select-all radio boolean false One choice with a radio per row selectedIds, defaultSelectedIds string[] [] The selected rows onSelectionChange (ids: string[], rows: R[]) => void After the selection changed filterText, defaultFilterText string '' The search text onFilterChange (value: string) => void After setFilterText filterRows (row, text, headers) => boolean Replaces the search's row test manualFiltering boolean false Keep every row (filter on the server) expandable boolean false Rows open and close expandedIds, defaultExpandedIds string[] [] The open rows onExpandChange (change: { expandedIds, expanded, id? }) => void After a row (or, without id, every row) opened or closed pageSize, defaultPageSize number 0 Rows per page (0: one page of every row) page, defaultPage number 1 The page, from 1 onPageChange (change: { page, pageSize }) => void After setPagination, or a new search on a later page hiddenColumns, defaultHiddenColumns string[] headers marked hidden Keys of the columns not shown onColumnsChange (change: { hiddenColumns, key, hidden }) => void After a column was shown or hidden (key '' after a reset) resizable boolean false Every column gets a resize handle columnWidths, defaultColumnWidths Record<string, number> {} Column widths in px by key onColumnResize (change: { key, width, widths }) => void After a resize (once per drag or key press) staticWidth boolean false A resized table is as wide as its columns, not its box onCellEdit (edit: { rowId, key, value, previous, row, rows }) => void An edited cell was saved: set rows to edit.rows Column options on each header: sortable, editable ('text' \\\\| 'number' \\\\| 'select'), options ({ value, label }[] for a select), validate(value, row), resizable, width, minWidth, maxWidth, hideable, hidden, pinned ('start' \\\\| 'end'). What it returns, by topic: Rows rows, filteredRows (search kept), sortedRows, pageRows (the rows to render), rowById Columns headers (all), columns (shown), hiddenColumns, toggleColumn(key, show), resetColumns(), isColumnLocked(key), columnsChanged, pins Sort sortKey, sortDirection, sortDirectionOf(key), isSortable(column), sortBy(key) Search filterText, setFilterText(text) Pages paged, page, pageSize, pageCount, setPagination({ page, pageSize }) Selection selectable, radio, selectedIds, isSelected(id), setSelectedIds(ids), toggleRow(row, checked), toggleAll(), selectAll(), allSelected, someSelected, radioStop, getSelectAllProps(), getSelectRowProps(row) Open rows expandable, expandedIds, isExpanded(id), allExpanded, toggleExpanded(id), toggleAllExpanded(), expandedRowId(id) Widths and grid columnWidths, resize (fixed, hasFiller, tableStyle, widthOf(column) …), grid (enabled …), tableRef, boxRef, id DataTable.useDataTableContext() returns the same object to any component inside Root."],["Headless Data table","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#parts",""],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-root","Renders nothing of its own: it gives its children the hook's table. Prop Type Default table what useDataTable returned Required"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Table","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-table","Renders a <table> with the hook's tableRef; role=\\"grid\\" once a column is editable. It takes every <table> prop."],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Body","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-body","Renders a <tbody>. In a grid it handles the cells' keys, clicks, double clicks and focus."],["Headless Data table","DataTable.ColumnHeader","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-columnheader","Renders a <th scope=\\"col\\"> with aria-sort on a sortable column, data-key, and its resized width. It takes every <th> prop. Prop Type Default column string The column's key (required) Attribute When data-sortable The column sorts data-resizing Its handle is being dragged"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.SortButton","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-sortbutton","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that steps its column's sort: none → ascending → descending → none; a new column starts ascending. Describe the next step with aria-describedby if you like. Attribute When data-direction Always: none, ascending or descending"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.ResizeHandle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-resizehandle","Renders an <input type=\\"range\\"> (nothing for a column that doesn't resize). Name it (\\"Resize Name column\\"). It takes every input prop except type, value, min, max and step. Prop Type Default valueText (width: number) => string The width as words for assistive tech (\\"120 pixels\\")"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-row","Renders a <tr> with data-row-id, which the grid and the radios find it by. Prop Type Default rowId string The row's id (required) Attribute When data-selected The row is selected data-expanded The row is open"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Cell","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-cell","Renders a <td>. In a grid one body cell is the Tab stop and the others are tabIndex={-1}; cells that can't be edited are aria-readonly. Prop Type Default index number The cell's place in its row, from 0, counting every cell (expand, select, data) (required) column string The column's key, for a data cell; an editable column makes the cell editable Attribute When data-editable The cell can be edited data-editing The cell is being edited data-key The column's key, on an editable cell DataTable.useCellContext() returns the cell's rowId, column and editing ({ draft, error } while edited, else null)."],["Headless Data table","DataTable.CellValue, DataTable.EditHint","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-cellvalue-datatable-edithint","CellValue renders a <span> around an editable cell's value: a click on it focuses the cell. EditHint renders a <span> with the text that describes every editable cell (\\"Press Enter to edit\\"); only in a grid. Hide it visually."],["Headless Data table","DataTable.CellInput, DataTable.CellSelect, DataTable.CellError","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-cellinput-datatable-cellselect-datatable-cellerror","The editor while a cell is edited: CellInput an <input> (text, or number with inputMode=\\"decimal\\"), CellSelect a <select> of the column's options (or your own <option> children). Both are aria-invalid and described by the error while validate refuses the value. CellError renders a <span role=\\"alert\\"> with the message, and nothing while the value is valid."],["Headless Data table","DataTable.SelectAll","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-selectall","Renders a native checkbox (the headless Checkbox): checked when every row in scope is selected, mixed when some are. A press clears the selection when any row is selected, else selects every enabled row shown (Carbon). Nothing in a radio table. Attribute When data-checked Every row in scope is selected data-indeterminate Some are"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.SelectRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-selectrow","Renders a native checkbox for its row, or a radio in a radio table. A disabled row's box is disabled. Attribute When data-checked The row is selected"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.ExpandToggle, DataTable.ExpandAll","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-expandtoggle-datatable-expandall","Each renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded; aria-controls points at the open row(s). ExpandToggle opens or closes its row; ExpandAll opens every row shown, or closes them all once all are open. Name them with aria-label. Attribute When data-expanded Its row is open (every row, for ExpandAll)"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.ExpandedRow","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-expandedrow","Renders the <tr> under an open row, with the id its toggle controls. Prop Type Default rowId string The open row's id (required)"],["Headless Data table","DataTable.Filler","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#datatable-filler","Renders an empty <td aria-hidden=\\"true\\"> that takes the rest of a row of resized columns — only then."],["Headless Data table","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-data-table/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Without editable columns, the parts are native: sort buttons, checkboxes and expand buttons are each in the Tab order. A radio table's radios are one Tab stop, and the arrow keys move and select, wrapping. With an editable column, the table is a WAI-ARIA grid: one Tab stop among the body cells, the arrow keys, Home / End and Ctrl + Home / End move it, and Enter or Space press a control in a cell. You add the table's name (aria-label, or aria-labelledby to your heading), names for the select and expand controls (say the row: \\"Select row, NDA\\"), a screen-reader name for the radio column, and the \\"Press Enter to edit\\" text. Announce what changed yourself: after a sort (\\"Sorted by Contract, ascending\\") and once typing in a search pauses (\\"3 of 12 rows\\"), with a polite status. Set aria-busy on the table while it reloads."],["Headless Structured list","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/","StructuredList is the row selection of the styled Structured list as unstyled React parts. The rest of a structured list is plain table markup (thead, tbody, th, td), so the parts are only what selection needs: the <table> (Root), a selectable row (Row with a value: a click anywhere on it selects it) and its Radio (the keyboard: one Tab stop, the arrow keys move and select). You own the markup: the cells, the header row, the radio icon and every style. State shows as data-* attributes to style on."],["Headless Structured list","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Structured list","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#use-it",""],["Headless Structured list","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#anatomy",""],["Headless Structured list","A list without selection","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#a-list-without-selection","Without selection you need no parts at all: write the table. Root and Row without a value render a plain <table> and <tr>, which helps when one list switches selection on and off."],["Headless Structured list","Controlled value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#controlled-value","Pass value and onValueChange to hold the choice yourself, or defaultValue to let Root keep it. values lists the selectable rows in order: it sets the radios' \\"1 of 3\\" and which row takes Tab when none is selected. A value not in values selects nothing. onValueChange runs only when the user picks a row, not when you change value."],["Headless Structured list","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#style-it","Hide the native radio and draw Carbon's radio icon from the row's data-selected. A group class on the row lets the icon read it."],["Headless Structured list","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#parts",""],["Headless Structured list","StructuredList.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#structuredlist-root","Renders a <table>. It takes every <table> prop. Prop Type Default values readonly string[] [] The selectable rows' values, in order: the radio group's size and its first Tab stop value string The selected row's value (controlled); one not in values selects none defaultValue string '' The starting value (uncontrolled) onValueChange (value: string) => void After the user selected another row StructuredList.useStructuredListContext() returns value, focusValue (the row whose radio takes Tab), values and select(value) to any component inside Root."],["Headless Structured list","StructuredList.Row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#structuredlist-row","Renders a <tr>. With a value it is selectable: a click anywhere on it selects it, and it gets aria-selected. Without one it is a plain row (for the header or a read-only list). Prop Type Default value string Makes the row selectable and identifies it in Root's value Attribute When data-selectable The row has a value data-selected The row is the selected one StructuredList.useRowContext() returns the row's value and selected to any component inside a selectable Row."],["Headless Structured list","StructuredList.Radio","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#structuredlist-radio","Renders an <input type=\\"radio\\"> checked when its row is selected. It goes inside a selectable Row. It takes every input prop except type, value, checked and defaultChecked; name it with aria-label. Attribute When data-selected Its row is selected"],["Headless Structured list","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-structured-list/#keyboard-and-accessibility","The radios form one Tab stop: the selected row's radio, else the first row's. Up, Down, Left and Right move focus and the selection to the previous or next row, wrapping at the ends. Space selects the focused row. Each radio has aria-posinset and aria-setsize from values, so screen readers say \\"2 of 3\\". You add the table's name (aria-label on Root), a name for each radio (the row's main text) and a screen-reader name for the radio column's header cell. Keep the radio in the accessibility tree when you hide it: use sr-only, not display: none."],["Headless Pagination","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/","Pagination is the behaviour of the styled Pagination as unstyled React parts. Root holds the page, the page size and the total; inside it go a PageSizeSelect (a new size goes back to page 1, as in Carbon), a PageSelect (one option per page) and Prev / Next buttons that disable at the ends and hand focus to each other. You own the markup: the labels, the range text (\\"1–10 of 95 items\\"), the icons and every style. usePaginationContext() gives you the numbers for the texts."],["Headless Pagination","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Pagination","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#use-it",""],["Headless Pagination","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#anatomy","Every part is optional: a bar with only Prev and Next works too."],["Headless Pagination","The texts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#the-texts","usePaginationContext() returns min and max (the first and last item the page shows), totalItems, page, pageSize and pageCount. Write them in your own words and language. PageSelect takes renderPage for the text of each option."],["Headless Pagination","Show the rows of the page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#show-the-rows-of-the-page","Hold page and pageSize yourself with onChange, and slice your rows with them (or ask the server for that page)."],["Headless Pagination","Total unknown","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#total-unknown","With pagesUnknown, Root doesn't need totalItems and has no last page: render no PageSelect, and set isLastPage when your cursor-based API says there is no next page. Here the \\"server\\" has four pages: isLastPage turns true on page 4."],["Headless Pagination","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#style-it","Every part has data-disabled while it can't be used: Prev on the first page, Next on the last, and all of them when Root is disabled."],["Headless Pagination","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#parts",""],["Headless Pagination","Pagination.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#pagination-root","Renders a <div> around the parts and gives them its state. It takes every <div> prop. Prop Type Default page number The page, from 1 (controlled) defaultPage number 1 The starting page (uncontrolled) pageSize number Items per page (controlled) defaultPageSize number 10 The starting page size (uncontrolled) totalItems number 0 Items across every page pagesUnknown boolean false No page count: Next stops only with isLastPage isLastPage boolean false With pagesUnknown: this is the last page disabled boolean false Disables every select and button onChange (change: { page, pageSize }) => void After the user changed the page or the page size Attribute When data-disabled disabled is set Pagination.usePaginationContext() returns page, pageSize, totalItems, pageCount, min, max, atFirst, atLast, pagesUnknown, disabled, and goTo(page), setPageSize(size), step(1 | -1) to any component inside Root."],["Headless Pagination","Pagination.PageSizeSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#pagination-pagesizeselect","Renders a <select> of page sizes; give it a <label>. A new size goes back to page 1. It takes every <select> prop except value and defaultValue. Prop Type Default pageSizes readonly number[] [] The choices, one <option> each (unless you pass your own <option> children) Attribute When data-disabled Root or the select is disabled"],["Headless Pagination","Pagination.PageSelect","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#pagination-pageselect","Renders a <select> with one option per page; name it with aria-label. It takes every <select> prop except value, defaultValue and children. Prop Type Default renderPage (page: number) => ReactNode String The text of each page's option Attribute When data-disabled Root or the select is disabled"],["Headless Pagination","Pagination.Prev, Pagination.Next","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#pagination-prev-pagination-next","Each renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that steps one page. Name icon-only buttons with aria-label. Attribute When data-disabled On the first page (Prev), on the last page (Next), or Root is disabled"],["Headless Pagination","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-pagination/#keyboard-and-accessibility","The selects are native: the browser's keys and the phone's picker work. Prev and Next are buttons in the Tab order (tabIndex={0}, as Carbon, so Safari focuses them on click). When the pressed arrow disables at the first or last page, focus moves to the other arrow. You add the page-size <label>, the aria-label of the page select and of icon-only arrows, and the range text. Tell screen reader users that the rows changed, for example with a polite status line."],["Headless Tree view","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/","TreeView is the behaviour of the styled Tree view as unstyled React parts, following the WAI-ARIA tree pattern: a role=\\"tree\\" of nested Nodes, one Tab stop, the arrow keys, Home / End, typing to jump, single or multiple selection, an active node, and children loaded on demand. You own the markup: each node's Row (caret, icon, label), the indent, and every style. State shows as data-* attributes on the node and its row; useNodeContext() gives a node's depth for the indent."],["Headless Tree view","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Tree view","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#use-it",""],["Headless Tree view","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#anatomy","hasChildren tells a Node it is a branch. The tree finds the nodes in the DOM, so they can come from any component, at any depth."],["Headless Tree view","Selection and the active node","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#selection-and-the-active-node","A click, Space or Enter selects a node and makes it the active one. Hold both with selected / onSelect and active / onActivate, or start them with defaultSelected / defaultActive. With multiselect, Ctrl / ⌘ + click and Space toggle a node, and Ctrl / ⌘ + A selects every enabled node. A disabled node can't be selected or opened, and the arrow keys skip it."],["Headless Tree view","Open and close branches","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#open-and-close-branches","Each Node keeps its own open state (defaultExpanded), or takes expanded with onToggle when you hold it, for example for an \\"Expand all\\" button. Right opens a branch and Left closes it; the Toggle caret does the same with the mouse."],["Headless Tree view","Load children on demand","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#load-children-on-demand","lazy makes a node a branch before it has children. The first time it opens, it gets data-loading and aria-busy and calls onLazyLoad(value): render the children when they arrive. A returned promise that resolves while there are still no children makes the node a leaf; one that rejects closes it, so opening it again retries."],["Headless Tree view","Links","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#links","Put an <a> in a node's Row. Enter follows the node's own link (after selecting it); keep the link out of the Tab order with tabIndex={-1}, since the node takes the keyboard."],["Headless Tree view","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#style-it",""],["Headless Tree view","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#parts",""],["Headless Tree view","TreeView.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#treeview-root","Renders a <div role=\\"tree\\"> and handles the keys, clicks and the one Tab stop for every node inside. It takes every <div> prop except role. Prop Type Default multiselect boolean false Ctrl / ⌘ + click and Space toggle nodes; Ctrl / ⌘ + A selects all (aria-multiselectable) selected readonly string[] Selected node values (controlled) defaultSelected readonly string[] [] The starting selection (uncontrolled) onSelect (selected: string[], value: string) => void After the user changed the selection; value is the node that did it active string The node last activated (controlled) defaultActive string '' The starting active node (uncontrolled) onActivate (value: string) => void After a node became the active one Attribute When data-multiselect multiselect is set TreeView.useTreeViewContext() returns multiselect, selected, active and tabStop to any component inside Root."],["Headless Tree view","TreeView.Node","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#treeview-node","Renders a <div role=\\"treeitem\\"> with aria-expanded (branches), aria-selected, aria-disabled and aria-busy. Put its Row and, for a branch, its Group inside. It takes every <div> prop except role. Prop Type Default value string Identifies the node in selected and active (required) label string value The text typing matches hasChildren boolean false The node has child nodes in its Group: a branch disabled boolean false Can't be selected or opened; the keys skip it expanded boolean Open (controlled) defaultExpanded boolean false Open at first (uncontrolled) onToggle (expanded: boolean) => void After the branch opened or closed lazy boolean false A branch whose children aren't loaded yet onLazyLoad (value: string) => void | Promise<void> Called the first time a lazy node opens Attribute When data-selected The node is selected data-active The node is the active one data-disabled disabled is set data-branch It has children, or is lazy and may get some data-expanded A branch that is open data-loading A lazy node waiting for its children TreeView.useNodeContext() returns the node's value, branch, expanded, loading, selected, active, disabled, depth (0 at the top level), rowId and toggle(expanded)."],["Headless Tree view","TreeView.Row","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#treeview-row","Renders a <div>: what the user sees and clicks. Its id names the node's Group. It has the same data-* attributes as its Node."],["Headless Tree view","TreeView.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#treeview-toggle","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\"> that opens and closes the branch; a click on the rest of the row selects instead. It is out of the Tab order and hidden from assistive tech (aria-hidden), since the node takes the keyboard. Attribute When data-expanded The branch is open"],["Headless Tree view","TreeView.Group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#treeview-group","Renders a <div role=\\"group\\"> holding the child nodes, named by the row (aria-labelledby) and hidden while the branch is closed. Each Group adds one to the depth of the nodes inside. Attribute When data-expanded The branch is open"],["Headless Tree view","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tree-view/#keyboard-and-accessibility","One Tab stop for the whole tree: the node focused last, else the selected one, else the first visible one. Up / Down move through the visible nodes, Home / End jump to the first / last. Right opens a branch or moves to its first child; Left closes it or moves to the parent. Enter opens or closes a branch, selects the node and follows the node's own link. Space selects (toggles in a multiselect tree). Typing a letter moves to the next node whose label starts with it. You add the tree's name (aria-label or aria-labelledby on Root), the indent, the caret and a visible focus style on the row. Say \\"loading\\" for a loading node in its row (for example a visually hidden text), as the styled tree does."],["Headless Code snippet","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/","CodeSnippet is the behaviour of the styled Code snippet as unstyled React parts. Code is the <code> whose text, read back after each render, is what gets copied (unless you give text). For a multi-line snippet, Content holds the code between Carbon's row limits (16px rows, 15 shown while collapsed) and measures it as it resizes, and Toggle (\\"Show more / Show less\\") is there only while the code is taller than the collapsed limit. The copy itself is the headless Copy button: pass the context's copyText to a Copy.Root. You own the box, the copy icon, the tooltip, the button words and every style."],["Headless Code snippet","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Code snippet","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#use-it","Root renders only its children. The read-only textbox around the code (role=\\"textbox\\", aria-readonly, tabIndex={0}) is yours, as in Carbon: it lets keyboard users reach and scroll the code."],["Headless Code snippet","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#anatomy","A single-line or inline snippet needs only Root and Code."],["Headless Code snippet","Multi-line with Show more","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#multi-line-with-show-more","Wrap the code in Content: it sets its own max-height and min-height from the row limits, so give it overflow-y-auto. Toggle appears once the code is taller than 15 rows; give the code a 16px line height (type-code) so the rows line up."],["Headless Code snippet","Hold the open state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#hold-the-open-state","expanded with onExpandedChange holds the state yourself; defaultExpanded only sets the start. onExpandedChange fires on each press of Toggle, and when an open snippet folds back by itself (its code got no taller than minExpandedRows)."],["Headless Code snippet","Row limits","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#row-limits","maxCollapsedRows (15) and maxExpandedRows (0, no limit) cap the height in 16px rows; minCollapsedRows (3) and minExpandedRows (16) set a minimum. Toggle shows only when the code is taller than the collapsed limit and expanding would show more. Lower minExpandedRows with the collapsed limit, or an open snippet of short code folds back when it is measured again. Here Toggle hides itself once open (data-expanded:hidden): the open block scrolls after 8 rows."],["Headless Code snippet","Copy something else","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#copy-something-else","text on Root replaces the code as copyText: show a short or safe form, copy the full one."],["Headless Code snippet","Inline chip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#inline-chip","For an inline snippet, the code is the copy button: put Code inside Copy.Trigger. The button is then named by its code, so people hear what they would copy."],["Headless Code snippet","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#style-it",""],["Headless Code snippet","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#parts",""],["Headless Code snippet","CodeSnippet.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#codesnippet-root","Renders only its children: it holds the expanded state, the row limits and the code's text. Prop Type Default text string '' What gets copied instead of the code shown expanded boolean Showing every row (controlled) defaultExpanded boolean false The start state (uncontrolled) onExpandedChange (expanded: boolean) => void Each press of Toggle, and the fold back maxCollapsedRows number 15 16px rows shown while collapsed; 0 = no limit maxExpandedRows number 0 Rows shown while expanded; 0 = no limit minCollapsedRows number 3 Minimum rows while collapsed minExpandedRows number 16 Minimum rows while expanded; an open snippet whose code is no taller folds back CodeSnippet.useCodeSnippetContext() returns, among others, copyText (text, else the code's text with one leading line break dropped, as <pre> does), expanded, canExpand (the Toggle shows) and setExpanded()."],["Headless Code snippet","CodeSnippet.Code","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#codesnippet-code","A <code>. Its text is read back after every render, so its children can be any elements (for example syntax colours); that text is the copyText. It takes every <code> prop."],["Headless Code snippet","CodeSnippet.Content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#codesnippet-content","A <div> around the code of a multi-line snippet. It sets max-height / min-height from the row limits (your style is merged after them), measures the code as it resizes, and folds an open snippet back when the code fits. Attribute When data-expanded Expanded"],["Headless Code snippet","CodeSnippet.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#codesnippet-toggle","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded, rendered only while the code is taller than the collapsed limit (canExpand). A press expands or collapses. It takes every button prop except type; give it the words. Attribute When data-expanded Expanded"],["Headless Code snippet","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-code-snippet/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Moves to your code box (with tabIndex={0}), the copy button, then Toggle Enter, Space On Toggle: opens or closes; on the copy trigger: copies Arrow keys Scroll the focused code box The parts set aria-expanded on Toggle. The copy parts give a button and a polite live region. You add: The read-only textbox around the code: role=\\"textbox\\", aria-readonly=\\"true\\" (and aria-multiline for a block), tabIndex={0} and a name (aria-label). A name for an icon-only copy button, and the feedback words in Copy.Status. The \\"Show more\\" / \\"Show less\\" words, and a visible focus style everywhere."],["Headless Copy button","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/","Copy is the behaviour of the styled Copy button as unstyled React parts. Root holds the text and the feedback timer, Trigger puts the text on the clipboard and then reports copied for two seconds, and Status is a polite live region that announces your feedback during that moment. A copy that failed shows no feedback. Copy.useCopy gives you the same behaviour as a hook, for a control of your own. You own the icon, the tooltip, the feedback words and every style. The styled Code snippet uses the same parts for its inline chip."],["Headless Copy button","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Copy button","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#use-it","Trigger is a <button type=\\"button\\"> with no name of its own: an icon-only trigger needs aria-label (or a tooltip that names it, below)."],["Headless Copy button","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#anatomy",""],["Headless Copy button","Show the feedback","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#show-the-feedback","For the feedback moment, Trigger has data-copied. Swap the icon for a check mark with group-data-copied:, or read copied from Copy.useCopyContext() in a component inside Root."],["Headless Copy button","Feedback in a tooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#feedback-in-a-tooltip","Carbon shows the label and the feedback in the button's tooltip. Combine Copy with the headless Tooltip: the tooltip's label names the icon button, and open keeps it up while copied is true."],["Headless Copy button","Feedback time","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#feedback-time","feedbackTimeout on Root is how long copied stays true, in ms (2000). A second press starts the time over. The Status here is visible: its text is there only during the moment, so it doubles as the visible feedback."],["Headless Copy button","Copy it yourself","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#copy-it-yourself","onCopy on Root runs before the copy with the text. Return false to copy something else yourself; the feedback still shows. Return nothing to let the part copy as usual (use it to record the copy)."],["Headless Copy button","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#disabled","disabled on Trigger disables the button: no focus, no copy. With focusableWhenDisabled it stays a Tab stop with aria-disabled and copies nothing, as Carbon's inline code snippet does, so people can still reach it and read why. Both set data-disabled."],["Headless Copy button","Just the hook","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#just-the-hook","Copy.useCopy(text, { onCopy, feedbackTimeout }) returns { copied, copy } without any part. Use it when the copy control is something else: a menu item, a link-styled button, a keyboard shortcut. Add your own live region."],["Headless Copy button","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#style-it",""],["Headless Copy button","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#parts",""],["Headless Copy button","Copy.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#copy-root","Renders only its children: it holds the text and the feedback timer, which stops with the component. Prop Type Default text string What gets copied (required) onCopy (text: string) => boolean | void Before copying; return false to copy it yourself (the feedback still shows) feedbackTimeout number 2000 How long copied stays true, in ms Copy.useCopyContext() returns text, copied and copy() to any component inside Root."],["Headless Copy button","Copy.Trigger","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#copy-trigger","A <button type=\\"button\\">; a press copies unless it is disabled. It takes every button prop except type. Prop Type Default disabled boolean false Copies nothing; the native disabled unless focusableWhenDisabled focusableWhenDisabled boolean false Disabled but still a Tab stop, with aria-disabled Attribute When data-copied In the feedback moment after a copy data-disabled Disabled"],["Headless Copy button","Copy.Status","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#copy-status","A <span role=\\"status\\">, a polite live region. Its children (your feedback) render only during the moment after a copy, so screen readers announce them once. Hide it with sr-only, or let it be the visible feedback."],["Headless Copy button","Copy.useCopy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#copy-usecopy","useCopy(text, { onCopy?, feedbackTimeout? }) returns { copied, copy }: copy() copies (unless onCopy returns false) and sets copied for feedbackTimeout ms. Root uses it."],["Headless Copy button","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-copy-button/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Enter, Space On Trigger: copies Tab Moves to the next control (a focusableWhenDisabled trigger stays in the order) The parts give you a real button and a polite live region that speaks only after a successful copy. The copy falls back to document.execCommand('copy') where the Clipboard API isn't available (a plain-http intranet page). You add: A name for an icon-only Trigger: aria-label, or the headless Tooltip's label. The feedback words inside Status (\\"Copied!\\", \\"Link copied\\"). A visible feedback for sighted users: the data-copied style, a tooltip, or a visible Status. A visible focus style."],["Headless Truncated text","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/","TruncatedText is the behaviour of the styled Truncated text as unstyled React parts. Root measures whether the text in Content is cut at lines lines (again whenever the box resizes or the text changes), and Toggle (\\"View more / View less\\") opens the rest with a short height animation. Content gets a CSS variable for your line clamp, and the state shows as data-* attributes. You own the clamp itself (one class), the ellipsis, the tooltip for cut text, the toggle's words and every style."],["Headless Truncated text","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Truncated text","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#use-it","Content sets --truncated-text-lines to the lines to show, or none while open. Tailwind's line-clamp-(--truncated-text-lines) turns it into the clamp and the ellipsis."],["Headless Truncated text","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#anatomy",""],["Headless Truncated text","Full text in a tooltip","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#full-text-in-a-tooltip","Carbon's other choice: no toggle, and the whole text in a tooltip when it is cut. Read overflowing from the context and wrap the text in a button with the headless Tooltip only then; the tooltip's label names the button with the whole text."],["Headless Truncated text","Lines","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#lines","lines (2) is how many lines show before the cut; 0 shows everything and never counts as cut. A text that fits isn't overflowing, and Toggle renders nothing."],["Headless Truncated text","Hold the open state","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#hold-the-open-state","expanded with onExpandedChange holds the state yourself; defaultExpanded only sets the start. onExpandedChange fires on a press of Toggle. Changing expanded yourself opens or closes without the animation, which plays only on a press."],["Headless Truncated text","Your own content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#your-own-content","Content shows value unless you give it children. Give children to add markup (a bold label, a link) while value stays the plain text, for the tooltip and for measuring again when it changes."],["Headless Truncated text","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#style-it",""],["Headless Truncated text","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#parts",""],["Headless Truncated text","TruncatedText.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#truncatedtext-root","A <div>: it holds the state and measures whether the text is cut as the box resizes. It takes every <div> prop. Prop Type Default value string The text (required; measured again when it changes) lines number 2 Lines shown before the cut; 0 = all expanded boolean Whether the text shows in full (controlled) defaultExpanded boolean false The start state (uncontrolled) onExpandedChange (expanded: boolean) => void On a press of Toggle Attribute When data-overflowing The text is cut (kept while open) data-expanded Open TruncatedText.useTruncatedTextContext() returns value, overflowing, expanded, closing (a collapse is animating), clamp and toggle() to any component inside Root."],["Headless Truncated text","TruncatedText.Content","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#truncatedtext-content","A <div> with the text: value, or your children. It gets the id that Toggle points at, and the style --truncated-text-lines: the lines, or none while open, while a collapse animates, or with lines 0. The height animation runs on it (--ui-duration-moderate, 110ms; none when that is 0, as with reduced motion)."],["Headless Truncated text","TruncatedText.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#truncatedtext-toggle","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-expanded and aria-controls (the Content), rendered only while the text is cut or open. A press opens or closes. It takes every button prop except type; give it the words. Attribute When data-expanded Open"],["Headless Truncated text","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-truncated-text/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Moves to Toggle (or to your tooltip button) Enter, Space On Toggle: opens or closes the text The parts set aria-expanded and aria-controls on Toggle, and keep the toggle out of the page while the text fits. You add: The clamp on Content (line-clamp-(--truncated-text-lines) with overflow-hidden). The toggle's words (\\"View more\\" / \\"View less\\"). For the tooltip pattern: a button named by the whole text, only while it is cut, so screen readers read all of it. A visible focus style."],["Headless Loading","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/","Loading is the behaviour of the styled Loading without a single class. Loading.Root decides when the spinner shows: while active, after delay ms, and once shown for at least minDuration ms, so quick work never flashes a spinner. Spinner makes your graphic an assertive live region while it shows. Indicator holds focus: as a modal dialog over the page with modal, or as the waiting spot of a busy Area, and focus goes back where it was afterwards. You own the spinner graphic, the overlay, hiding the parts while they don't show, and every style. Each part has data-shown while the spinner shows."],["Headless Loading","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Loading","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#use-it",""],["Headless Loading","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#anatomy","Area and Indicator are optional: a plain spinner needs only Root and Spinner."],["Headless Loading","Start, stop and wait","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#start-stop-and-wait","active starts and stops it (on by default). delay waits before showing, and minDuration keeps it up once shown. useLoadingContext().shown tells any component inside Root whether it shows now. The parts don't hide themselves: hide the spinner while it has no data-shown. Try the quick check: it ends before the 300 ms delay, so nothing shows."],["Headless Loading","Over one area","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#over-one-area","Wrap the content in Area and put the Indicator over it. While it shows, the area is inert and aria-busy, and the indicator is a group named by its aria-label. Focus that was inside the area waits on the indicator, then goes back: press Refresh with the keyboard and focus returns to it."],["Headless Loading","Over the whole page","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#over-the-whole-page","With modal, the Indicator is a modal dialog while it shows. It takes focus, and Tab and focus moving elsewhere come back to it; a modal dialog opened above it is left alone. When it stops, focus goes back where it was. It is no <dialog>, so Esc can't close it. The overlay is position: fixed. In this demo it sits in a box with a transform, so it covers only the box."],["Headless Loading","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#style-it","Every part has data-shown while the spinner shows. Hide the indicator and the spinner without it, and fade or blur the area with it."],["Headless Loading","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#parts",""],["Headless Loading","Loading.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#loading-root","Renders only its children. It holds whether the spinner shows and moves focus while it does. Prop Type Default active boolean true Starts and stops it; false hides it delay number 0 Milliseconds active must last before it shows minDuration number 0 Once shown, the least milliseconds it stays modal boolean false A page overlay: the Indicator is a modal dialog that holds focus while shown Loading.useLoadingContext() returns shown and modal (plus the refs of the area and the indicator) to any component inside Root."],["Headless Loading","Loading.Area","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#loading-area","A <div> around the content that a contained loading covers. While shown it is inert and has aria-busy=\\"true\\". Attribute When data-shown The spinner shows"],["Headless Loading","Loading.Indicator","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#loading-indicator","A <div> that holds focus while it shows. It takes every div prop except role and tabIndex; name it with aria-label. While shown it has tabIndex={-1}, role=\\"dialog\\" with aria-modal=\\"true\\" when Root is modal, or else role=\\"group\\", and its aria-label. While hidden it has no role and no name. Attribute When data-shown The spinner shows"],["Headless Loading","Loading.Spinner","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#loading-spinner","A <div> around your spinner graphic, with aria-atomic=\\"true\\". While shown it is an assertive live region (aria-live=\\"assertive\\"), so the graphic's name is announced; while hidden, aria-live=\\"off\\". Attribute When data-shown The spinner shows"],["Headless Loading","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-loading/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab With modal: stays on the indicator while it shows The parts: move focus to the Indicator when a modal loading shows, or when focus was inside the Area, and give it back afterwards; set role, aria-modal, aria-label and tabIndex on the Indicator while it shows; make the Area inert and aria-busy; make the Spinner an assertive live region while it shows. You add: The spinner graphic with an accessible name (role=\\"img\\" and aria-label on the <svg>) and the aria-label of the Indicator. Say what is loading. Hiding the parts while they have no data-shown, and the overlay colour. A slower or still spinner under prefers-reduced-motion."],["Headless Tag","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/","Tag is the behaviour of the styled Tag as three unstyled React parts. Tag.Root is a read-only or dismissible tag (a <span>). Tag.Dismiss is its close button: a press calls onDismiss and doesn't reach a click handler around the tag. Tag.Toggle is a selectable tag: a <button aria-pressed> that flips on a press, Space or Enter. An operational tag is a plain <button>, so it needs no part. You own the markup and every style: the colours, the size, the icon, the ellipsis. The tag stays until you remove it from your state."],["Headless Tag","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Tag","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#use-it",""],["Headless Tag","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#anatomy",""],["Headless Tag","Dismissible","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#dismissible","Put Tag.Dismiss inside Tag.Root and remove the tag in onDismiss. Name the button with aria-label, different for each tag. When the removed tag had focus, move focus to the next tag yourself."],["Headless Tag","Selectable","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#selectable","Tag.Toggle keeps its own state with defaultSelected, or follows selected when you control it. onSelectedChange gets the new state after each press."],["Headless Tag","Operational","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#operational","An operational tag is your own <button type=\\"button\\"> drawn as a tag. When it shows or hides something, give it aria-expanded (and aria-controls); when its text is only a number, name it with aria-label."],["Headless Tag","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#disabled","disabled on Tag.Root disables its Tag.Dismiss too (a disabled of its own on Dismiss wins). Tag.Toggle takes disabled like any button. Each part then has data-disabled."],["Headless Tag","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#style-it",""],["Headless Tag","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#parts",""],["Headless Tag","Tag.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#tag-root","A <span>, the tag itself. It takes every <span> prop. Prop Type Default disabled boolean false Disables its Tag.Dismiss too Attribute When data-disabled disabled is set"],["Headless Tag","Tag.Dismiss","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#tag-dismiss","A <button type=\\"button\\">, the close button. It takes every button prop except type. Its press stops there: a click handler around the tag doesn't see it. Prop Type Default onDismiss () => void — After a press, not while disabled disabled boolean the root's Its own state; left out, it follows Tag.Root Attribute When data-disabled Disabled, by itself or through Tag.Root"],["Headless Tag","Tag.Toggle","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#tag-toggle","A <button type=\\"button\\"> with aria-pressed, the selectable tag. It takes every button prop except type and aria-pressed. Prop Type Default selected boolean — The state (controlled) defaultSelected boolean false The starting state (uncontrolled) onSelectedChange (selected: boolean, event: MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => void — After the user flips it Attribute When data-selected On data-disabled disabled is set"],["Headless Tag","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-tag/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Moves to a close button or a selectable tag. Tag.Root itself isn't a tab stop. Enter, Space Presses the close button, or flips a selectable tag The parts set type=\\"button\\", aria-pressed on Tag.Toggle, and the native disabled. You add: A name on each Tag.Dismiss, for example aria-label=\\"Remove filter Legal\\". Focus after a removal: the removed button takes the focus with it. aria-label on an operational tag whose text is only a number, and aria-expanded when it shows or hides something. The full text in title when you cut a long tag with an ellipsis. A visible focus style."],["Headless Card","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/","Card is the behaviour of the styled Card as two unstyled React parts. Card.Root is the card: with href one link (<a>), with clickable one button (a <div role=\\"button\\">, since a card holds block content a <button> may not), else a plain box (<div>). A click, or Enter or Space on the card itself, calls onClick. Card.Actions marks the card's own small buttons: a click or key that starts inside it belongs to that button, not to the card. You own everything else: the media, the header, the title, the body, the footer and every style. The styled card's other parts (media, header, title, body, footer) are layout, so here they are your own elements."],["Headless Card","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Card","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#use-it",""],["Headless Card","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#anatomy",""],["Headless Card","Linked card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#linked-card","With href the whole card is one <a> (with tabIndex={0}, so Safari focuses it on a click and stops on it with Tab). target=\\"_blank\\" adds rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\". onClick runs too, so a single-page app can route the click; the example prevents the navigation and shows the address. Name the link with aria-label, as its whole text would make a long name."],["Headless Card","Clickable card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#clickable-card","With clickable the card is a <div role=\\"button\\" tabIndex={0}>: a click, or Enter or Space while the card itself has focus, calls onClick. Name it with aria-label."],["Headless Card","Buttons inside a card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#buttons-inside-a-card","Carbon's guideline keeps other controls out of a link or clickable card: put buttons in a plain card, or use a Headless Product card with click zones. If a button must sit inside one anyway, wrap it in Card.Actions (a <div data-card-actions>). A click inside it is that button's: the card's onClick doesn't run. Enter and Space on a focused button never press the card either, as the card only answers keys while it has focus itself. Screen readers handle controls inside a role=\\"button\\" poorly, which is why Carbon advises against it."],["Headless Card","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#disabled","disabled stops onClick. A disabled linked card becomes a plain box (or the button, when it is also clickable); a disabled clickable card keeps its role, gets aria-disabled and leaves the tab order (tabIndex={-1}). The box and the button have data-disabled."],["Headless Card","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#style-it",""],["Headless Card","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#parts",""],["Headless Card","Card.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#card-root","An <a> with href (unless disabled), a <div role=\\"button\\"> with clickable, else a <div>. It takes every <div> prop; ref points at whichever element it renders. Prop Type Default href string — Makes the whole card one link target '_self' | '_blank' '_self' _blank adds rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\" clickable boolean false Makes the whole card one button (tabIndex 0, Enter and Space) onClick (event: MouseEvent<HTMLElement> | KeyboardEvent<HTMLElement>) => void — The card was pressed: a linked or clickable card only, not from inside Card.Actions, not while disabled disabled boolean false No onClick; a link falls back to the box or the button Attribute When data-link It renders the link data-clickable It renders the button data-disabled disabled is set, on the box or the button"],["Headless Card","Card.Actions","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#card-actions","A <div data-card-actions> for a button that must sit inside a link or clickable card (Carbon advises against it). It takes every <div> prop. A click that starts inside it doesn't call the card's onClick."],["Headless Card","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-card/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Moves to a linked or clickable card, then to the buttons inside it Enter Follows a linked card; presses a clickable card that has focus itself Space Presses a clickable card that has focus itself The part sets role=\\"button\\", tabIndex, aria-disabled and rel. You add: A name on a linked or clickable card: aria-label, since its whole text would be read as the name. Headings for the titles, at the level the page needs. alt text for media that carries information, alt=\\"\\" for decoration. A visible focus style on the card and its buttons. A sentence in a disabled card saying why it can't be used."],["Headless Product card","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/","ProductCard is the behaviour of the styled Product card (Carbon for IBM Products' legacy ProductiveCard and ExpressiveCard) as unstyled React parts. For new work, use Headless Card instead. What the parts give you is a clickable zone that never swallows the card's own controls. ProductCard.ClickZone is an empty <button> that you lay over the zone (position: absolute; inset: 0), with the card's buttons stacked above it. The buttons stay siblings of the zone's button: separate tab stops whose clicks never press the card. The zone's button is named by ProductCard.Title (else Label, else Body) and described by Description; a click, Enter or Space on it calls the root's onClick. You own the layout, the buttons and every style."],["Headless Product card","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Product card","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#use-it",""],["Headless Product card","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#anatomy",""],["Headless Product card","Clickable card","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#clickable-card","Give Root an onClick and position: relative, put ClickZone in it with position: absolute; inset: 0, and lift the card's own buttons above it with position: relative; z-index: 1. Here a click on the card opens the project, and the edit button only edits."],["Headless Product card","A smaller zone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#a-smaller-zone","Carbon's productive card can make only part of the card clickable: the header with the body, or the body alone. Put ClickZone inside that part and make the part position: relative. The footer button below stays outside the zone."],["Headless Product card","What names the zone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#what-names-the-zone","ClickZone points aria-labelledby at the Title, or at the Label when there is no title, or at the Body when there is neither. aria-describedby points at the Description. Pass your own aria-labelledby or aria-describedby on ClickZone to change them. The parts make their own ids; an id you pass is used instead."],["Headless Product card","Disabled","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#disabled","disabled on Root stops onClick and sets aria-disabled on the card and the zone's button, as Carbon does. The button stays focusable, so screen readers still find it and hear that it's disabled. Nothing else changes: grey it out yourself with data-disabled, and say why."],["Headless Product card","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#style-it",""],["Headless Product card","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#parts",""],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-root","A <div>, the card. It takes every <div> prop except onClick, which here means the click zone. Prop Type Default onClick (event: MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>) => void — The click zone was pressed (a click, Enter or Space on ClickZone); never while disabled disabled boolean false Sets aria-disabled; the zone then calls no onClick Attribute When data-disabled disabled is set"],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.ClickZone","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-clickzone","An empty <button type=\\"button\\"> with tabIndex={0}, to lay over the zone. It takes every button prop except type and children; your own onClick runs before the root's. Attribute When data-click-zone Always (to leave it out of rules such as [&>button]:relative) data-disabled The root is disabled"],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.Title","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-title","A heading, <h2> by default. It takes every heading prop. It names the click zone. Prop Type Default as 'h1' | 'h2' | 'h3' | 'h4' | 'h5' | 'h6' 'h2' The heading level"],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.Label","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-label","A <p>, the text above the title. It names the click zone when there is no title."],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.Description","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-description","A <p>, the text below the title. It describes the click zone."],["Headless Product card","ProductCard.Body","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#productcard-body","A <div>, the content. It names the click zone when there is neither title nor label. Every part except Root throws when it isn't inside a ProductCard.Root."],["Headless Product card","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-product-card/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Key Does Tab Moves to the zone's button and, separately, to each of the card's own controls Enter, Space Presses the zone's button (calls onClick) or the focused control The parts set the zone's aria-labelledby, aria-describedby and aria-disabled, and give each named part an id. You add: The positioning: the zone's button over its part, the card's own controls above it. A visible focus style on the zone's button; it covers the zone, so an outline on it outlines the zone. Names for icon-only buttons. A disabled look, if you want one; the parts only announce it."],["Headless Edit in place","","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/","EditInPlace is the behaviour of the styled Edit in place as unstyled React parts: a value shown in a text field that is edited where it is, with Edit, Cancel and Save buttons. The parts hold the value and the value editing started from, start editing on focus or typing, save on Enter, put the value back on Escape, and save or put back when the focus leaves. Each button shows only when it applies, and a press on one keeps the focus in the field. You own the markup and every style: the icons, the hover fill, the focus line, the error text and the read-only note. State shows as data-* attributes to style on."],["Headless Edit in place","Installation","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#installation","The headless parts come with the package (there is no shadcn item; the React + Tailwind items are built on them):"],["Headless Edit in place","Use it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#use-it",""],["Headless Edit in place","Anatomy","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#anatomy","Root renders nothing of its own. Group is the box that hears the focus move between the field and its buttons; put every part that takes focus inside it."],["Headless Edit in place","Save and cancel","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#save-and-cancel","onSave gets the value when a change is saved: with Save, with Enter, or when the focus leaves the group with a valid change. onCancel gets the value put back: with Cancel, with Escape, or when the focus leaves without a valid change. Save and Cancel are enabled only once the value has changed (spaces at the ends don't count)."],["Headless Edit in place","Controlled value","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#controlled-value","Hold the value with value and onValueChange. onValueChange gets every keystroke, and the value put back on cancel. Send the value to your server in onSave."],["Headless Edit in place","Invalid, with an error text","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#invalid-with-an-error-text","invalid blocks saving: Save is disabled, Enter doesn't save, and leaving puts the value back. It sets aria-invalid on the field and data-invalid on the group and the field. Put the error text in InvalidText: it shows only while invalid and describes the field (aria-describedby)."],["Headless Edit in place","Read-only","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#read-only","readOnly keeps the value: the field is readonly, no button shows, and a click on the field sets noteOpen in the context. Show your note with it, for example in a Headless Popover, and close it with setNoteOpen(false). The Actions show in their own mode only: edit at rest, cancel and save while editing, none when read-only. For an \\"Edit off\\" button beside a read-only field, render your own button that calls setNoteOpen."],["Headless Edit in place","Your own buttons","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#your-own-buttons","render on an Action renders your component with the action's props (type, disabled, data-disabled, onMouseDown, onClick and your own), for example a styled icon button with a tooltip. Spread them all onto your button, so the press keeps the focus in the field."],["Headless Edit in place","Style it","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#style-it","The same in plain CSS, with your own class names on the parts:"],["Headless Edit in place","Parts","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#parts",""],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.Root","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-root","Holds the value, the editing state and the value editing started from. Renders only its children. Prop Type Default value string — The value, controlled (pair with onValueChange) defaultValue string '' The first value, uncontrolled onValueChange (value: string) => void — Every keystroke, and the value put back on cancel onSave (value: string) => void — A change was saved (Save, Enter, leaving the group) onCancel (value: string) => void — The value was put back (Cancel, Escape, leaving without a valid change) invalid boolean false Blocks saving; aria-invalid on the field readOnly boolean false Shown, not edited"],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.Group","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-group","Renders a <div>. A focus coming in starts editing; a focus leaving all of it saves a valid change or puts the value back. It takes every <div> prop. Attribute When data-editing While editing data-invalid invalid is set data-readonly readOnly is set"],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.Input","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-input","Renders an <input type=\\"text\\"> with the value. Enter saves, or stops editing when there is nothing to save (the focus stays); Escape puts the value back. A click starts editing, or opens the note when read-only. It takes every <input> prop except value, defaultValue, type and readOnly, which come from Root. Its id is yours when you give one, else \${id}input; its aria-describedby is yours when you give one, else the InvalidText shown. Attribute When data-editing While editing data-invalid invalid is set data-readonly readOnly is set"],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.InvalidText","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-invalidtext","Renders a <p> with your error text while Root is invalid, and nothing otherwise; while it shows, it describes the field. Its id is yours when you give one, else \${id}error. It takes every <p> prop."],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.Action","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-action","Renders a <button type=\\"button\\">, only in its mode. Its mousedown is cancelled, so a press keeps the focus in the field. It takes every <button> prop except type. Prop Type Default action 'edit' | 'cancel' | 'save' — edit at rest: focuses the field. cancel while editing, once the value changed: puts it back. save while editing, once it changed and is valid: saves render (props) => ReactElement — Renders your own button with these props Attribute When data-disabled disabled is set, or the action can't run yet (cancel without a change, save without a valid change)"],["Headless Edit in place","EditInPlace.useEditInPlaceContext()","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#editinplace-useeditinplacecontext","Reads the state of the enclosing Root from any component inside it: id (the field is \${id}input and the error text \${id}error unless you give them ids), value, editing, mode ('rest', 'editing' or 'readonly'), canSave, canCancel, invalid, readOnly, noteOpen and setNoteOpen, and the actions begin, save, cancel and refocus. Outside a Root it throws."],["Headless Edit in place","Keyboard and accessibility","/kanok-ui-docs/en/headless-edit-in-place/#keyboard-and-accessibility","Tab into the field starts editing. Tab then reaches Cancel and Save once they are enabled; leaving the group saves a valid change or puts the value back. Enter saves a valid change and keeps editing; with nothing to save it stops editing, the focus staying in the field. Escape puts the value back and keeps editing. After Save, Cancel or Escape, the focus goes back to the field with the caret at the end. The field sets aria-invalid when invalid. InvalidText describes it while it shows. You add its name (aria-label, or a <label> for its id) and names for the buttons, whose content is often only an icon. A read-only field is readonly: it still takes focus and is read. Your note should say why it can't be edited. The styled Edit in place is built on these parts."]]`);export{e as default};